window.QUIZ_CONFIG={"title": "國中會考文法歷屆試題｜全部主題綜合", "mode": "mcq", "questions": [{"id": 1, "question": "It was very windy this morning. Some of the shirts on the balcony were blown away ______ in the pond.", "options": ["fell", "and fell", "fallen", "and fallen"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜對等連接 V1 and V2 時態一致", "explanation": "【句型】S + V1 + and + V2:對等連接的兩個動詞時態須一致。\n【分析】前面 were blown away 是過去式,後面「掉進池塘」也要用過去式 fell,且兩個動詞之間要用 and 連接 → and fell。\n【其他選項】(A) fell 缺連接詞 and,一句不能有兩個動詞直接相連;(C)(D) fallen 是過去分詞,不能單獨當動詞。\n【例句】The vase fell off the table and broke.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 2, "question": "Last Sunday, Kevin went to the night market ______ a bowl of beef noodles.", "options": ["eats", "and ate", "eating", "and eaten"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "前面 went 為過去式,用 and 連接同為過去式的 ate。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 3, "question": "Every morning, my grandma gets up early and ______ in the park near our house.", "options": ["walks", "walked", "walking", "to walk"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "and 連接 gets up,兩動詞都用現在簡單式第三人稱單數 walks。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 4, "question": "The little boy dropped his ice cream on the ground ______ to cry.", "options": ["starts", "started", "and started", "and starting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "dropped 為過去式,用 and 連接過去式 started。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 5, "question": "David looked out of the balcony window and saw a woman get in his car ______ away.", "options": ["drive", "drove", "and drive", "and drove"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 saw + O + V1 and V2(原形)", "explanation": "【句型】感官動詞 see/hear/watch + O + 原形V(或Ving);兩個受詞補語用 and 連接,形式要一致。\n【分析】saw a woman get in his car 中 get 是原形,第二個動作「把車開走」也用原形 drive,並以 and 連接 → and drive。\n【其他選項】(A) drive 缺 and;(B)(D) drove 是過去式,感官動詞後的受詞補語不可用過去式。\n【例句】I saw him open the door and walk in.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 6, "question": "Amy heard her brother ______ the door and run out of the house.", "options": ["opens", "opened", "open", "to open"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "感官動詞 heard + O + 原形 open,與後面的 run 形式一致。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 7, "question": "We watched the dancers come onto the stage ______ a bow.", "options": ["and take", "took", "and took", "taking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "感官動詞後受詞補語用原形,come 與 take 以 and 連接 → and take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 8, "question": "Mr. Lin saw a thief climb over the wall ______ into his neighbor's house.", "options": ["got", "and got", "gets", "and get"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "saw + O + 原形 climb ... and get,兩動作都用原形並以 and 連接。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 9, "question": "I can't tell you what I think of the movie because I ______ it. I'll probably watch it this Saturday.", "options": ["am not seeing", "don't see", "haven't seen", "won't see"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 haven't p.p.(尚未做)", "explanation": "【句型】S + have/has not + p.p. (yet):表「到目前為止還沒做」。\n【分析】後句 I'll probably watch it this Saturday 表示這週六才要看,所以「到現在還沒看過」,用 haven't seen。\n【其他選項】(A) am not seeing 表此刻沒在看,與「無法評論」的理由不符;(B) don't see 現在簡單式表習慣,語意不通;(D) won't see 與後句「週六會看」矛盾。\n【例句】I haven't read the book yet, but I plan to.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 10, "question": "Jenny can't join us for dinner because she ______ her homework. She has to finish it first.", "options": ["didn't finish", "hasn't finished", "won't finish", "doesn't finish"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "還沒寫完、現在必須先完成 → 現在完成式否定 hasn't finished。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 11, "question": "I don't know how the new teacher looks because I ______ her yet.", "options": ["haven't met", "don't meet", "won't meet", "am not meeting"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "句尾 yet 表「至今尚未」,用 haven't met。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 12, "question": "Ben: Is the new coffee shop good?\nTina: I don't know. I ______ there. Let's go together tomorrow.", "options": ["didn't go", "won't go", "don't go", "haven't been"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "到目前為止沒去過 → 現在完成式 haven't been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 13, "question": "Christmas ______ and I want to visit my aunt abroad. Do you have any plans yet?", "options": ["came", "comes", "is coming", "was coming"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在進行式表近未來(來去動詞 come)", "explanation": "【句型】來去動詞(come/go/leave/arrive)+ 現在進行式,可表示即將發生的未來。\n【分析】後面 I want to visit my aunt、Do you have any plans yet? 都表示在計畫未來,所以「聖誕節快到了」用 is coming。\n【其他選項】(A)(D) 過去式不合計畫未來的語境;(B) comes 表一般事實,不能表達「即將到來」。\n【例句】We are leaving for Tokyo next Friday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 14, "question": "Hurry up! The train ______ in five minutes.", "options": ["left", "is leaving", "was leaving", "has left"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "來去動詞 leave 用現在進行式表即將發生。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 15, "question": "Summer vacation ______. Have you decided where to go?", "options": ["is coming", "came", "was coming", "has come"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "暑假即將來臨,come 用進行式表近未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 16, "question": "My cousin ______ to Taipei next week, so I'm going to show him around.", "options": ["came", "comes", "is coming", "was coming"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "next week 為近期未來的安排,來去動詞用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 17, "question": "Mom: Linda, you've been playing computer games all evening! Have you finished your report?\nLinda: Well, ______ most of it this afternoon, and I'll finish it by Friday.", "options": ["I would do", "I did", "I was doing", "I'll do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式(this afternoon 已過去)", "explanation": "【句型】過去明確時間 + 過去簡單式。\n【分析】現在已是晚上(all evening),this afternoon 已經過去,「下午完成了大部分」用過去式 I did;後句 I'll finish it by Friday 才是未來。\n【其他選項】(A) would do 為過去未來式,不合;(C) was doing 只表當時正在做,不能表示「做完大部分」;(D) I'll do 是未來,與 this afternoon(已過)矛盾。\n【例句】I did my homework this morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 18, "question": "Dad: Did you clean your room?\nTom: Yes, I ______ it this morning before lunch.", "options": ["clean", "cleaned", "will clean", "am cleaning"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "this morning 在午餐前已過去,用過去式 cleaned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 19, "question": "It's 9 p.m. now. Mia ______ two hours on her science project this afternoon.", "options": ["spent", "spends", "will spend", "is spending"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "現在是晚上,this afternoon 已過 → 過去式 spent。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 20, "question": "Teacher: Where is your homework, Leo?\nLeo: Sorry, I ______ it at home this morning. I'll bring it tomorrow.", "options": ["leave", "am leaving", "left", "will leave"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "今早已發生的事用過去式 left;明天的事才用 will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 21, "question": "Listen! The baby ______ in the bedroom. Why don't you go in and take a look?", "options": ["cried", "cries", "is crying", "will cry"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在進行式(Listen! 此刻正在發生)", "explanation": "【句型】Listen! / Look! + S + is/are + Ving:表此刻正在發生的動作。\n【分析】Listen! 提示「現在聽到」,寶寶此刻正在哭,所以用 is crying,後面才叫對方進去看看。\n【其他選項】(A) cried 過去式不合當下;(B) cries 表習慣;(D) will cry 表未來,與 Listen! 不符。\n【例句】Look! The cat is climbing the tree.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 22, "question": "Look! Some students ______ basketball on the playground.", "options": ["play", "are playing", "played", "will play"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Look! 表此刻正在發生 → are playing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 23, "question": "Be quiet! Grandpa ______ in the living room.", "options": ["is sleeping", "sleeps", "slept", "has slept"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Be quiet! 表此刻爺爺正在睡,用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 24, "question": "Listen! Someone ______ at the door. Can you open it?", "options": ["knocked", "knocks", "will knock", "is knocking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Listen! 表當下聽到有人正在敲門 → is knocking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 25, "question": "Paul misses his parents a lot. He ______ them since he came to work in Taiwan a year ago.", "options": ["didn't see", "doesn't see", "hasn't seen", "won't see"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 since + 過去時間", "explanation": "【句型】S + have/has + p.p. + since + S + 過去式:從過去某時持續到現在。\n【分析】since he came to work in Taiwan a year ago 表示「從一年前來台至今」,所以主句用現在完成式 hasn't seen,說明一直沒見到父母(所以很想念)。\n【其他選項】(A) didn't see 過去式不能與 since 子句搭配表持續;(B) doesn't see 表習慣;(D) won't see 未來式不合。\n【例句】She has lived here since she was ten.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 26, "question": "My uncle ______ in Kaohsiung since he got a job there in 2020.", "options": ["lived", "has lived", "lives", "will live"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間點,主句用現在完成式 has lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 27, "question": "Annie ______ any junk food since she started her diet last month.", "options": ["hasn't eaten", "doesn't eat", "didn't eat", "won't eat"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "since 從上個月開始到現在都沒吃 → hasn't eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 28, "question": "We are good friends. We ______ each other since we were in elementary school.", "options": ["knew", "know", "will know", "have known"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去子句,主句用 have known 表持續至今。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 29, "question": "Tina ______ hamburgers for lunch every day last week.", "options": ["has", "had", "has had", "was having"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式(last week 過去習慣)", "explanation": "【句型】明確過去時間(last week)→ 過去簡單式。\n【分析】every day last week 描述上週每天重複的動作,是過去的習慣,用過去式 had。\n【其他選項】(A) has 現在式與 last week 不符;(C) has had 現在完成式不可與明確過去時間連用;(D) was having 表當時正在吃,不能表示每天的習慣。\n【例句】I went swimming every weekend last summer.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 30, "question": "Jason ______ to school by bike every day last semester.", "options": ["goes", "has gone", "went", "is going"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "last semester 明確過去時間 → 過去式 went。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 31, "question": "My parents ______ TV every night when they were young.", "options": ["watched", "watch", "have watched", "are watching"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "when they were young 表過去習慣 → watched。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 32, "question": "It ______ a lot in Taipei last month, so we stayed home most of the time.", "options": ["rains", "has rained", "is raining", "rained"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "last month 為過去時間 → 過去式 rained。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 33, "question": "My brother doesn't live with us. He ______ out after he got married.", "options": ["has moved", "will move", "was moving", "moved"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜after + 過去式,主句過去式", "explanation": "【句型】主句 + after + S + 過去式:兩件都是過去發生的事,用過去簡單式。\n【分析】after he got married 是過去發生的事,「結婚後搬出去」也是過去已完成的動作,用 moved。\n【其他選項】(A) has moved 現在完成式不與過去時間子句 after he got married 連用;(B) will move 未來式與「已不住在一起」矛盾;(C) was moving 表當時正在搬,語意不合。\n【例句】He left the company after he found a better job.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 34, "question": "Lisa ______ the dishes after she finished dinner last night.", "options": ["washes", "washed", "has washed", "will wash"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "last night 及 after 子句皆為過去 → washed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 35, "question": "After the movie ended, we ______ home by MRT.", "options": ["went", "go", "have gone", "will go"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "After 子句 ended 為過去式,主句也用過去式 went。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 36, "question": "Mr. Huang doesn't teach here anymore. He ______ after he turned sixty-five.", "options": ["retires", "will retire", "is retiring", "retired"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "after he turned 65 是過去的事 → retired。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 37, "question": "My sister is coming to my home today. She ______ with me for a week.", "options": ["stays", "stayed", "has stayed", "will stay"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜未來式 will + V", "explanation": "【句型】未來將發生的動作 → will + 原形V / be going to + V。\n【分析】姊姊今天才要來(is coming today),「住一週」是之後才會發生的事,用 will stay。\n【其他選項】(A) stays 表習慣;(B) stayed 過去式不合;(C) has stayed 表已住了一段時間,但她還沒到。\n【例句】My cousin is arriving tonight and will stay with us for a month.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 38, "question": "Our new classmate is arriving tomorrow. He ______ next to you.", "options": ["sat", "will sit", "has sat", "sits"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "新同學明天才到,之後才會坐在你旁邊 → will sit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 39, "question": "Grandma is flying back to Tainan tomorrow. I ______ her at the airport.", "options": ["will meet", "met", "have met", "meet"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "明天才發生的事 → will meet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 40, "question": "The typhoon is coming tonight. Schools ______ closed tomorrow.", "options": ["were", "are", "have been", "will be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow 未來時間 → will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 41, "question": "For the past twenty years, my father ______ in a school library. But he'll leave the job next month.", "options": ["worked", "has worked", "is working", "works"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 For the past + 時間", "explanation": "【句型】For the past + 一段時間 → 現在完成式 have/has + p.p.。\n【分析】For the past twenty years 表「過去二十年到現在」,且 he'll leave the job next month 表示他現在仍在工作,所以用 has worked。\n【其他選項】(A) worked 表已結束,但他下個月才離職;(C) is working 只表此刻;(D) works 現在簡單式無法表達「持續了多久」。\n【例句】For the past five years, she has taught English.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 42, "question": "For the past three months, Andy ______ English every night. His grades are getting better.", "options": ["studied", "studies", "has studied", "is studying"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "For the past three months 持續到現在 → has studied。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 43, "question": "Ms. Chang ______ at this school for ten years. She is going to retire this summer.", "options": ["has taught", "taught", "teaches", "will teach"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "for ten years 且仍在任教 → 現在完成式 has taught。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 44, "question": "My family ______ in this apartment for the past six years, but we'll move next year.", "options": ["lived", "live", "will live", "have lived"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "For the past six years 到現在仍住 → have lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 45, "question": "At first, my bookstore's business ______ not very good. But now it is doing quite well.", "options": ["is", "does", "was", "did"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去式 vs. 現在式對比(At first … But now)", "explanation": "【句型】At first + 過去式 …, But now + 現在式:對比過去與現在。\n【分析】At first「起初」指過去,後面 not very good 是形容詞補語,需要 be 動詞;主詞 business 為單數 → was。\n【其他選項】(A) is 現在式與 At first 不合;(B)(D) does/did 是助動詞,後面不能直接接形容詞 good,且缺主要動詞。\n【例句】At first, I was shy, but now I'm outgoing.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 46, "question": "At first, the new student ______ very quiet. But now she talks with everyone.", "options": ["is", "was", "does", "did"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "At first 表過去,後接形容詞用 be 動詞過去式 was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 47, "question": "Ten years ago, this town ______ only one convenience store. Now it has five.", "options": ["had", "has", "have", "is having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "Ten years ago 為過去,have 表擁有 → had。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 48, "question": "When I was little, I ______ afraid of dogs. But now I have two of them.", "options": ["am", "did", "do", "was"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "When I was little 表過去,afraid 為形容詞 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 49, "question": "Mozart ______ his first music when he was only six years old.", "options": ["is writing", "has written", "will write", "wrote"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式(when he was six)", "explanation": "【句型】明確過去時間 → 過去簡單式。\n【分析】when he was only six years old 是過去明確時間點,莫札特六歲時寫下第一首曲子,用 wrote。\n【其他選項】(A) is writing 現在進行式不合;(B) has written 現在完成式不可與明確過去時間連用;(C) will write 未來式不合。\n【例句】Edison invented the light bulb in 1879.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 50, "question": "My grandfather ______ to Taipei when he was eighteen.", "options": ["moves", "has moved", "moved", "will move"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "when he was eighteen 為明確過去時間 → moved。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 51, "question": "Jolin ______ her first song when she was in junior high school.", "options": ["sang", "sings", "has sung", "is singing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "when she was in junior high 為過去 → sang。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 52, "question": "I ______ how to ride a bike when I was five years old.", "options": ["learn", "have learned", "will learn", "learned"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "when I was five 明確過去時間 → learned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 53, "question": "We were so sure that Jerry ______ well on the difficult job. His past experience in other work showed he was the right guy for it. So when he failed, no one believed it.", "options": ["had done", "did", "has done", "would do"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去未來式 would + V(were sure that …)", "explanation": "【句型】主句過去式 + that + S + would + 原形V:表「從過去的角度看將會發生的事」(過去未來式)。\n【分析】主句 were sure 是過去式,當時我們確信 Jerry「將會」把工作做好(那時還沒做),所以用 would do;後面 when he failed 才說明結果。\n【其他選項】(A) had done 表當時已完成;(B) did 表事實已發生,但他其實失敗了;(C) has done 與主句過去時態不一致。\n【例句】She told me she would come back next week.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 54, "question": "Mandy thought it ______ rain, so she brought an umbrella.", "options": ["will", "would", "is going to", "has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "主句 thought 為過去式,子句用過去未來式 would。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 55, "question": "Last night, Dad promised that he ______ me to the zoo this Sunday.", "options": ["would take", "takes", "took", "has taken"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "過去答應「將會」帶我去 → would take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 56, "question": "Everyone believed our team ______ the game, but we lost in the end.", "options": ["wins", "has won", "will win", "would win"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "believed 為過去式,當時認為將會贏 → would win。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 57, "question": "Stella is a baseball fan. She ______ more than one hundred pictures of famous baseball players.", "options": ["has", "has been", "is", "is having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜have 表擁有(狀態動詞不用進行式)", "explanation": "【句型】have/has 表「擁有」是狀態動詞,用現在簡單式,不用進行式。\n【分析】「她擁有一百多張棒球明星照片」,主詞 She 單數 → has。\n【其他選項】(B) has been 後面不接名詞當受詞;(C) is 是 be 動詞,不能表示「擁有」;(D) is having 指「正在吃/正在進行」,不能表擁有。\n【例句】I have three cats.(不可說 I am having three cats.)", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 58, "question": "Kevin loves music. He ______ a guitar, a piano, and two violins.", "options": ["is having", "has", "is", "have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "have 表擁有用現在簡單式,主詞單數 → has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 59, "question": "Shhh! We ______ a meeting now. Please come back later.", "options": ["are having", "have", "had", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "have a meeting 表「舉行」為動作,可用進行式;Shhh!/now 表此刻正在進行。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 60, "question": "My aunt ______ a big house with a beautiful garden in Yilan.", "options": ["is having", "have", "is", "has"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "表擁有的 have 不用進行式,主詞單數 → has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 61, "question": "______ that last piece of pie? If not, can I have it? I didn't eat much this morning.", "options": ["Had you eaten", "Were you eating", "Do you eat", "Are you going to eat"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜be going to 問打算(未來計畫)", "explanation": "【句型】Are you going to + V? 詢問對方「是否打算做某事」。\n【分析】後句 If not, can I have it? 表示派還在,說話者想先確認對方打不打算吃,用 Are you going to eat。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去完成式不合;(B) 問過去某時是否正在吃,不合;(C) Do you eat 問習慣,與「最後一塊派」不搭。\n【例句】Are you going to watch the game tonight?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 62, "question": "______ the old bike? If not, I'd like to buy it from you.", "options": ["Did you use", "Were you using", "Are you going to keep", "Have you kept"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問對方打不打算留下這台車 → Are you going to keep。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 63, "question": "______ this weekend? We can go hiking together if you're free.", "options": ["What are you going to do", "What did you do", "What were you doing", "What have you done"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問週末計畫 → be going to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 64, "question": "Mom: ______ your old toys? If not, we can give them to the children's home.", "options": ["Did you play with", "Were you playing with", "Had you played with", "Are you going to play with"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問未來是否還要玩 → Are you going to play with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 65, "question": "When the baby cried, Mr. Wu ______ in the kitchen and did not hear it.", "options": ["cooked", "was cooking", "has cooked", "is going to cook"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式 When + 過去式, S + was/were + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】When + S + 過去簡單式, S + was/were + Ving:過去某個短動作發生時,另一個長動作正在進行。\n【分析】寶寶哭的時候,吳先生「正在」廚房煮飯,所以沒聽到 → was cooking。\n【其他選項】(A) cooked 只表做過,無法說明「同時正在做所以沒聽到」;(C) 現在完成式、(D) 未來式皆不合過去情境。\n【例句】When the phone rang, I was taking a shower.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 66, "question": "When the earthquake happened, we ______ dinner.", "options": ["have", "were having", "had had", "are having"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "地震發生時正在吃飯 → were having。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 67, "question": "When Dad came home, my sister ______ the piano in her room.", "options": ["was practicing", "practices", "has practiced", "will practice"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "爸爸回家時姊姊正在練琴 → was practicing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 68, "question": "Jeff didn't answer your call because he ______ a shower when you called.", "options": ["takes", "has taken", "took", "was taking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "你打電話時他正在洗澡,所以沒接 → was taking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 69, "question": "Aunt Gina has lived in this town for more than sixty years, so she ______ it very well.", "options": ["will know", "knew", "knows", "was going to know"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 + so + 現在簡單式(結果)", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式(持續至今), so + 現在簡單式(現在的結果/狀態)。\n【分析】Gina 阿姨在這個鎮住了六十多年(到現在),所以「現在」很熟悉 → knows;know 是狀態動詞,用現在簡單式。\n【其他選項】(A) will know 未來式不合;(B) knew 表過去熟悉,與現在仍住在此不合;(D) 過去未來式不合。\n【例句】She has worked here for 20 years, so she knows everyone.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 70, "question": "Ray has studied Japanese for five years, so he ______ it quite well.", "options": ["spoke", "speaks", "will speak", "was speaking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "學了五年到現在,現在會說 → speaks。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 71, "question": "Our team has practiced hard for months, so we ______ ready for the game now.", "options": ["are", "were", "will be", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "now 表現在的狀態 → are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 72, "question": "Mrs. Lin has taught here since 2005, so she ______ almost every teacher in the school.", "options": ["knew", "will know", "is knowing", "knows"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "know 為狀態動詞,表現在的結果用 knows。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 73, "question": "I don't have any money with me because I ______ my wallet this morning.", "options": ["had lost", "would lose", "lost", "was losing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式(this morning 已過去)", "explanation": "【句型】明確過去時間 → 過去簡單式。\n【分析】this morning 是已過去的明確時間,今天早上弄丟錢包,所以現在身上沒錢 → lost。\n【其他選項】(A) had lost 過去完成式需要另一個過去時間當參考點;(B) would lose 過去未來式不合;(D) was losing 表正在丟,語意不通。\n【例句】I missed the bus this morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 74, "question": "I'm really tired now because I ______ only four hours last night.", "options": ["sleep", "slept", "have slept", "will sleep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "last night 明確過去時間 → slept。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 75, "question": "Jim can't play basketball today because he ______ his leg yesterday.", "options": ["hurt", "hurts", "will hurt", "was hurting"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "yesterday 過去時間 → hurt(過去式同形)。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 76, "question": "Our classroom is so clean! The students ______ it this afternoon.", "options": ["clean", "will clean", "have cleaned", "cleaned"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "this afternoon 已過去的明確時間 → cleaned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 77, "question": "Lisa: What ______ this morning?\nTina: Well, it's Sunday. I think I'll go to church with my father.", "options": ["have you done", "are you going to do", "did you do", "were you doing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜be going to 問未來計畫(看答句時態)", "explanation": "【句型】What + are you going to + V? 詢問未來計畫。\n【分析】Tina 回答 I think I'll go to church(未來式),表示今天早上還沒到/還沒過,Lisa 問的是「今天早上打算做什麼」→ are you going to do。注意不要只看 this morning 就選過去式,要看回答的時態。\n【其他選項】(A) have you done 問已做了什麼;(C) did you do 問過去;(D) were you doing 問過去某時正在做什麼,皆與答句的未來式不合。\n【例句】A: What are you going to do tonight? B: I'll watch a movie.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 78, "question": "Amy: What ______ this evening?\nBen: I'll probably stay home and read.", "options": ["did you do", "have you done", "are you going to do", "were you doing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "答句用 I'll → 問未來計畫 are you going to do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 79, "question": "Dad: Where ______ this afternoon?\nKai: I went to the library with Eric.", "options": ["did you go", "are you going", "will you go", "do you go"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "答句用過去式 went → 問句用 did you go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 80, "question": "Ken: How ______ to Kenting this weekend?\nMay: We'll take the bus.", "options": ["did you get", "have you got", "were you getting", "are you going to get"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "答句 We'll take → 問未來 are you going to get。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 81, "question": "She ______ to the department store and bought two new sweaters for her husband.", "options": ["has gone", "is going", "went", "goes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜對等連接 V1 and V2 時態一致(went and bought)", "explanation": "【句型】S + V1 + and + V2:and 連接的兩個動詞時態須一致。\n【分析】後面 bought 是過去式,前面「去百貨公司」也要用過去式 went。\n【其他選項】(A) has gone 現在完成式與 bought 不對等;(B) is going 進行式不對等;(D) goes 現在式不對等。\n【例句】She went to the store and bought some milk.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 82, "question": "Yesterday Peter ______ his room and did his homework.", "options": ["cleans", "cleaned", "has cleaned", "is cleaning"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "and 後 did 為過去式,前面也用過去式 cleaned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 83, "question": "Every weekend, Ella goes to the market and ______ fresh fruit.", "options": ["buys", "bought", "buying", "to buy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "and 連接 goes,同為現在簡單式第三人稱單數 buys。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 84, "question": "Last night my dad ______ home late and went to bed right away.", "options": ["comes", "has come", "is coming", "came"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "went 為過去式,前面對等用 came。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 85, "question": "Excuse me. I really need to go now. My kids ______ for me at school.", "options": ["are waiting", "were waiting", "wait", "waited"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在進行式(此刻正在進行)", "explanation": "【句型】S + am/is/are + Ving:表說話當下正在進行的動作。\n【分析】I really need to go now 是說話當下,孩子「此刻正在」學校等我,所以我得走了 → are waiting。\n【其他選項】(B) were waiting 過去進行式不合當下;(C) wait 表習慣;(D) waited 過去式不合。\n【例句】Sorry, I can't talk now. I'm driving.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 86, "question": "Sorry, I can't talk now. I ______ for my math test tomorrow.", "options": ["studied", "am studying", "study", "was studying"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "now 表當下正在準備 → am studying。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 87, "question": "Turn off the TV, please. Your brother ______ to sleep in the next room.", "options": ["is trying", "tried", "tries", "has tried"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "弟弟此刻正在試著睡覺 → is trying。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 88, "question": "Hurry up! Everyone ______ for us in front of the school bus.", "options": ["waited", "waits", "was waiting", "is waiting"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "Hurry up! 表此刻大家正在等 → is waiting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 89, "question": "The weather ______ rainy and cloudy in the last few days. I hope the sun will come out soon.", "options": ["has been", "had been", "will be", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 in the last few days", "explanation": "【句型】in the last/past few days → 現在完成式,表從過去持續到現在。\n【分析】in the last few days「最近幾天(到現在)」天氣一直陰雨,所以希望太陽快出來 → has been。\n【其他選項】(B) had been 過去完成式需要過去的參考時間點;(C) will be 未來式不合;(D) would be 過去未來式不合。\n【例句】He has been busy in the past two weeks.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 90, "question": "I ______ very busy in the past few weeks, so I haven't called you.", "options": ["was", "have been", "had been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "in the past few weeks 持續至今 → have been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 91, "question": "Prices ______ a lot in the last two years. Everything is so expensive now.", "options": ["have gone up", "went up", "will go up", "go up"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "in the last two years 到現在 → 現在完成式 have gone up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 92, "question": "Ivy ______ three books in the last few days. She really loves reading.", "options": ["reads", "will read", "had read", "has read"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "in the last few days → has read。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 93, "question": "Have you got anything for Joe ______? He'd be happy to get your gift on his birthday.", "options": ["almost", "either", "soon", "yet"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式疑問句 + yet", "explanation": "【句型】Have/Has + S + p.p. ... yet?「(到目前為止)已經…了嗎?」\n【分析】Have you got ...? 是現在完成式問句,問「你已經幫 Joe 準備好禮物了嗎」,句尾用 yet。\n【其他選項】(A) almost「幾乎」不放句尾修飾此問句;(B) either 用在否定句尾表「也」;(C) soon「很快」不與現在完成式問句搭配。\n【例句】Have you finished your homework yet?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 94, "question": "Have you cleaned your room ______? Grandma is coming in ten minutes.", "options": ["already", "yet", "ever", "soon"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "現在完成式疑問句句尾用 yet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 95, "question": "I haven't decided what to buy for Mom's birthday ______.", "options": ["yet", "already", "too", "either"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "現在完成式否定句句尾用 yet 表「還沒」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 96, "question": "Don't worry. I've ______ bought the tickets for the concert.", "options": ["yet", "either", "ever", "already"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "肯定句表「已經」用 already,放在 have 與 p.p. 之間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 97, "question": "On Children's Day, Ms. Lee, a famous storybook writer, ______ to Molly's Bookstore to talk about her new book. My two little kids just can't wait to see her.", "options": ["came", "was coming", "has come", "is going to come"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜be going to + V(未來計畫)", "explanation": "【句型】be going to + 原形V:表未來的計畫或安排。\n【分析】後句 My two little kids just can't wait to see her「等不及要見她」,表示活動還沒發生 → is going to come。\n【其他選項】(A) came 表已來過;(B) was coming 過去進行式不合;(C) has come 表已經來了,都與「等不及要見她」矛盾。\n【例句】She is going to give a speech tomorrow.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 98, "question": "Jay Chou ______ a concert in Taichung next month. My sister can't wait to buy a ticket.", "options": ["held", "is going to hold", "has held", "was holding"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "next month 且「等不及買票」→ 未來 is going to hold。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 99, "question": "The school ______ a sports day this Friday. All the students are excited about it.", "options": ["is going to have", "had", "has had", "was having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "this Friday 尚未發生 → is going to have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 100, "question": "A famous baseball player ______ our school next week. Everyone is looking forward to meeting him.", "options": ["visited", "has visited", "was visiting", "is going to visit"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "next week 未來 → is going to visit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 101, "question": "Betty ______ fake watches when the police came.", "options": ["sells", "is selling", "was selling", "has sold"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式 when + 過去式", "explanation": "【句型】S + was/were + Ving + when + S + 過去簡單式:過去某事發生時,另一動作正在進行。\n【分析】when the police came 是過去的短動作,當時 Betty「正在」賣假錶 → was selling。\n【其他選項】(A) sells、(B) is selling 現在時態與 came 不合;(D) has sold 現在完成式不合。\n【例句】I was reading when the doorbell rang.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 102, "question": "Steve ______ a video game when his mom walked into his room.", "options": ["plays", "was playing", "has played", "is playing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "媽媽進房時正在玩 → was playing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 103, "question": "The students ______ loudly when the teacher came in.", "options": ["were talking", "talk", "have talked", "are talking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "老師進來時學生正在聊天 → were talking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 104, "question": "We ______ along the beach when it started to rain.", "options": ["walk", "have walked", "are walking", "were walking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "開始下雨時正在散步 → were walking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 105, "question": "Betty ______ TV when her little brother fell off the chair.", "options": ["watched", "was watching", "has watched", "is going to watch"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式 when + 過去式", "explanation": "【句型】S + was/were + Ving + when + S + 過去簡單式。\n【分析】弟弟從椅子上摔下來(過去短動作)時,Betty「正在」看電視(進行中的動作)→ was watching。\n【其他選項】(A) watched 只表完成的動作,無法表示「同時正在進行」;(C) has watched、(D) is going to watch 時態不合過去情境。\n【例句】I was doing my homework when the lights went out.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 106, "question": "Grandpa ______ in the garden when he heard a strange sound.", "options": ["works", "was working", "has worked", "will work"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "聽到聲音時正在花園工作 → was working。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 107, "question": "When I called Nina last night, she ______ dinner with her family.", "options": ["was having", "has", "has had", "is having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "我打電話時她正在吃晚餐 → was having。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 108, "question": "My mom ______ the floor when the cat jumped onto the table.", "options": ["cleans", "is cleaning", "has cleaned", "was cleaning"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "貓跳上桌時媽媽正在拖地 → was cleaning。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 109, "question": "Christine: Dad, I'm hungry. Do we have anything to eat?\nMr. Chen: You can have some bread I ______ from the supermarket. It's on the table.", "options": ["am buying", "to buy", "bought", "will buy"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜關係子句中的時態(省略關代 that 的子句用過去式)", "explanation": "【句型】N + (that/which) + S + V:關係子句(省略關代)中的動詞依實際時間決定時態。\n【分析】bread (that) I ______ from the supermarket 修飾 bread;It's on the table 表示麵包已經買回來了,所以「買」是過去的動作 → bought。\n【其他選項】(A) am buying 表正在買,但麵包已在桌上;(B) to buy 不是主要動詞,子句缺動詞;(D) will buy 表還沒買,與「在桌上」矛盾。\n【例句】The cake my mom made yesterday was delicious.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 110, "question": "The shoes Mandy ______ last week are too small for her now.", "options": ["buys", "bought", "will buy", "is buying"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "last week 已買 → 關係子句用過去式 bought。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 111, "question": "The movie we ______ last night was really scary.", "options": ["saw", "see", "will see", "are seeing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "last night → 子句用過去式 saw。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 112, "question": "You can borrow the comic books my uncle ______ me for my birthday. They're on my desk.", "options": ["gives", "will give", "is giving", "gave"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "書已在桌上,送書是過去的事 → gave。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 113, "question": "B&J Café ______ known as the tallest building in town. However, O&G Restaurant became the tallest building in 2010.", "options": ["has been", "had been", "is", "would be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去完成式 had been(過去某時之前的狀態)", "explanation": "【句型】S + had + p.p.:過去完成式,表在過去某時間點「之前」一直持續的狀態。\n【分析】O&G Restaurant 在 2010 年(過去)成為最高建築,表示 B&J Café 是在 2010 年「之前」被稱為最高建築 → had been known。\n【其他選項】(A) has been 表持續到現在,但它現在已不是最高;(C) is 現在式與事實不符;(D) would be 過去未來式語意不合。\n【例句】Mr. Wang had been a teacher for ten years before he became a writer in 2015.\n備註：參考解答(4f68a85b.txt)答案同為 B,但其解析寫成 was;依截圖選項 (B) 為 had been,已改寫為過去完成式解析。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 114, "question": "Ms. Lin ______ in Hualien for five years before she moved to Taipei in 2019.", "options": ["has lived", "had lived", "lives", "will live"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "在 2019 年搬家之前已住了五年 → 過去完成式 had lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 115, "question": "When we got to the theater, the movie ______ already ______.", "options": ["had; started", "has; started", "will; start", "is; starting"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "到達(過去)之前電影已開始 → had already started。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 116, "question": "This old house ______ empty for many years before the Chens bought it last year.", "options": ["has been", "is", "will be", "had been"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "去年買下之前已空了很多年 → had been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 117, "question": "Smart Head, one of the hottest TV programs these days, ______ people free plane tickets to Hawaii if they can answer 20 questions correctly in 15 minutes.", "options": ["have given", "gives", "giving", "to give"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜整句缺主要動詞(主詞+同位語後接現在式動詞)", "explanation": "【句型】S(, 同位語,)+ V:主詞後插入同位語,句子仍需主要動詞,且動詞單複數依主詞決定。\n【分析】主詞是 Smart Head(單數節目名),one of the hottest TV programs these days 是同位語;句子缺主要動詞,節目規則是現在的固定事實 → 現在簡單式 gives。\n【其他選項】(A) have given 主詞單數應用 has,且完成式不適合表節目規則;(C) giving、(D) to give 不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】Mr. Chen, our new English teacher, comes from Canada.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 118, "question": "Lucy, one of my best friends, ______ in Tainan with her grandparents.", "options": ["live", "lives", "living", "to live"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "主詞 Lucy 單數,同位語不影響 → lives。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 119, "question": "The night market, one of the most popular places in town, ______ open until midnight every day.", "options": ["stays", "stay", "staying", "to stay"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The night market 單數,每天的事實 → stays。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 120, "question": "My parents, both teachers at a junior high school, ______ to work by MRT every day.", "options": ["goes", "going", "to go", "go"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "主詞 My parents 複數 → go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 121, "question": "Yesterday when I got home from work, my brother ______ for dinner, so he invited me to join him.", "options": ["goes out", "went out", "has gone out", "was going out"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式表當時正要做(was going out)", "explanation": "【句型】When + S + 過去式, S + was/were + Ving:表過去某時「正在/正要」做某事。\n【分析】我昨天下班回到家時,哥哥「正要」出門吃晚餐,所以才邀我一起去 → was going out。\n【其他選項】(A) goes out 現在式不合 yesterday;(B) went out 表已經出門,就無法當面邀我;(C) has gone out 表已出門不在,也無法邀我。\n【例句】When I saw Amy, she was leaving for school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 122, "question": "When I called Ben last night, he ______ for the airport, so he couldn't talk long.", "options": ["leaves", "was leaving", "has left", "left"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "我打電話時他正要出發 → was leaving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 123, "question": "When we arrived at the station, the train ______, so we had to run.", "options": ["was leaving", "leaves", "has left", "will leave"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "抵達時火車正要開,所以要跑 → was leaving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 124, "question": "When Mom got home, Dad ______ dinner in the kitchen, so she helped him.", "options": ["cooks", "cooked", "has cooked", "was cooking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "媽媽到家時爸爸正在煮,所以去幫忙 → was cooking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 125, "question": "Lily: When will Uncle Tom come to see me?\nMom: He'll visit us this weekend. He ______ me that by e-mail.", "options": ["told", "tells", "will tell", "was going to tell"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式(已發生的事)", "explanation": "【句型】過去已發生的動作 → 過去簡單式。\n【分析】媽媽已經知道 Tom 叔叔週末會來,表示 Tom「已經」用 e-mail 告訴她了 → told。\n【其他選項】(B) tells 現在式表習慣,不合;(C) will tell 表還沒說,那媽媽就不會知道;(D) was going to tell 表「當時打算說(但可能沒說)」,不合。\n【例句】I know the answer because Sam told me this morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 126, "question": "Ann: How do you know about the party?\nBill: Kevin ______ me about it yesterday.", "options": ["tells", "told", "will tell", "is telling"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "已經告訴我,yesterday → told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 127, "question": "Dad knows I'm going to the zoo. I ______ him about it last night.", "options": ["told", "tell", "will tell", "am telling"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "last night 已告訴 → told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 128, "question": "Mia: Is Mr. Lee sick today?\nJoe: Yes. He ______ us in class this morning.", "options": ["tells", "will tell", "has told", "told"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "this morning 已過去 → told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 129, "question": "I ______ a bath when someone turned off the light. I was scared and shouted for help.", "options": ["was taking", "took", "am taking", "had taken"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式 when + 過去式", "explanation": "【句型】S + was/were + Ving + when + S + 過去簡單式。\n【分析】有人關燈(過去短動作)時,我「正在」洗澡 → was taking;後句 I was scared 也是過去情境。\n【其他選項】(B) took 只表做過,無法表示「當時正在洗」;(C) am taking 現在進行式時態不合;(D) had taken 表在關燈前已洗完,就不會害怕呼救。\n【例句】I was sleeping when the earthquake happened.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 130, "question": "I ______ my homework when the lights suddenly went out.", "options": ["do", "was doing", "have done", "am doing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "停電時正在寫作業 → was doing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 131, "question": "Ryan ______ his bike when it started to rain heavily.", "options": ["was riding", "rides", "has ridden", "is riding"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "開始下大雨時正在騎車 → was riding。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 132, "question": "My sister ______ on the phone when the doorbell rang, so I opened the door.", "options": ["talks", "has talked", "is talking", "was talking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "門鈴響時姊姊正在講電話 → was talking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 133, "question": "We ______ Aunt Polly for a long time, so we visited her last weekend.", "options": ["don't see", "haven't seen", "hadn't seen", "wouldn't see"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去完成式 hadn't p.p.(過去某時之前一直沒…)", "explanation": "【句型】S + had(not) + p.p. + for + 一段時間, so + S + 過去式:過去某動作之前一直持續的狀態用過去完成式。\n【分析】last weekend 去拜訪她(過去),在此「之前」已經很久沒見到她 → hadn't seen。\n【其他選項】(A) don't see 現在式不合過去脈絡;(B) haven't seen 表到現在都沒見,但上週末已經見過;(D) wouldn't see 語意不合。\n【例句】I hadn't eaten all day, so I was very hungry at dinner.\n備註：參考解答(4f68a85b.txt)此題為改編版,選項 (C) 為 didn't see 並以過去式解析;截圖原題 (C) 為 hadn't seen,答案同為 C,解析改依過去完成式。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 134, "question": "Ray ______ his grandparents for two years, so he flew to Canada to see them last summer.", "options": ["hasn't visited", "hadn't visited", "doesn't visit", "won't visit"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "去年夏天拜訪之前已兩年沒去 → hadn't visited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 135, "question": "Eric was very hungry at lunch because he ______ breakfast.", "options": ["hadn't eaten", "doesn't eat", "hasn't eaten", "won't eat"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "午餐時(過去)之前沒吃早餐 → hadn't eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 136, "question": "We ______ such a beautiful sunset before, so we took many pictures that evening.", "options": ["haven't seen", "don't see", "won't see", "had never seen"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "那晚之前從沒看過 → 過去完成式 had never seen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 137, "question": "See? The strange man I saw yesterday ______ around my house again. Should I call the police?", "options": ["walking", "is walking", "and walked", "to walk"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜整句缺主要動詞＋現在進行式", "explanation": "【句型】S（＋省略關代的修飾子句）＋主要動詞。The man (whom) I saw yesterday 只是主詞，後面仍需一個主要動詞。\n【分析】主詞 The strange man I saw yesterday 後缺主要動詞；See? 表示「你看，此刻他又在我家附近走來走去」，用現在進行式 is walking。\n【其他選項】(A)(D) walking、to walk 不能當主要動詞；(C) and walked 前面沒有可對等連接的動詞，且時態不合「此刻」。\n【例句】The girl I met at the party is waiting for you outside.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 138, "question": "The boy you helped last week ______ at the door now. He wants to thank you.", "options": ["standing", "to stand", "is standing", "and stood"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The boy (whom) you helped last week 後缺主要動詞，now 表此刻，用 is standing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 139, "question": "The book Mr. Lin gave me last month ______ very interesting.", "options": ["is", "being", "to be", "and was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The book (that) Mr. Lin gave me 後缺主要動詞，描述現在看法用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 140, "question": "Look! The cat we found in the park ______ with my sister's toy.", "options": ["playing", "is playing", "to play", "and played"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "Look! 表此刻正在發生，主詞後缺主要動詞，用現在進行式 is playing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 141, "question": "In my family, my sister is the only person who ______ chocolate.", "options": ["love", "loves", "loved", "loving"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜關代 who 後動詞與先行詞一致", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞＋who＋V，關係子句動詞的單複數跟著先行詞。\n【分析】先行詞 the only person 是單數；句子描述現在的喜好（主句 is），用現在簡單式第三人稱單數 loves。\n【其他選項】(A) love 是複數/原形；(C) loved 過去式與 is 的現在語境不合；(D) loving 不能當子句動詞。\n【例句】Ken is the only student who walks to school in our class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 142, "question": "Mr. Chen is the teacher who ______ us math this year.", "options": ["teach", "teaches", "teaching", "to teach"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 the teacher 單數，現在事實用 teaches。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 143, "question": "I have two friends who ______ in Kaohsiung.", "options": ["lives", "living", "live", "to live"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 two friends 複數，動詞用原形 live。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 144, "question": "The girl who ______ next to me in class is very friendly.", "options": ["sit", "sitting", "to sit", "sits"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 The girl 單數，現在習慣用 sits。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 145, "question": "Mom: What ______ after school today?\nRyan: Well, I just read some comic books.", "options": ["did you do", "do you do", "are you doing", "will you do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式疑問句 did you do", "explanation": "【句型】Wh- ＋ did ＋ S ＋ 原形V？ 問已發生的事用過去式。\n【分析】after school today 是今天已經過去的時段，且 Ryan 回答 I just read（過去式），所以問句用 did you do。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在簡單式問平常習慣；(C) 現在進行式問此刻；(D) 未來式問計畫，但事情已做完。\n【例句】What did you eat for lunch today?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 146, "question": "Dad: Where ______ last Sunday?\nAmy: I went to the zoo with Kelly.", "options": ["do you go", "did you go", "are you going", "have you gone"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "last Sunday 是過去時間，回答 went，用 did you go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 147, "question": "Teacher: What ______ during the summer vacation?\nJoe: I visited my grandparents in Tainan.", "options": ["did you do", "do you do", "will you do", "are you doing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "暑假已結束，回答 visited 過去式，問句用 did you do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 148, "question": "Mia: Who ______ with at the party last night?\nLeo: I talked with Ben and his sister.", "options": ["do you talk", "are you talking", "did you talk", "will you talk"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "last night 過去時間，回答 talked，用 did you talk。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 149, "question": "Ms. Wu: What animals ______ your sister like?\nHerbert: She likes lions and tigers.", "options": ["do", "does", "are", "is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜一般動詞疑問句 does＋S＋V", "explanation": "【句型】Wh- ＋ do/does ＋ S ＋ 原形V？ 一般動詞現在式疑問句。\n【分析】主要動詞 like 是一般動詞，主詞 your sister 是第三人稱單數，助動詞用 does；回答 She likes 也是現在式。\n【其他選項】(A) do 用於 I/you/複數主詞；(C)(D) be 動詞不能與原形一般動詞 like 搭配。\n【例句】What sports does your brother play?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 150, "question": "What kind of music ______ your parents listen to?", "options": ["does", "is", "do", "are"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "主詞 your parents 複數、listen 是一般動詞，用 do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 151, "question": "Where ______ Mr. Huang usually eat lunch?", "options": ["does", "do", "is", "are"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "主詞 Mr. Huang 單數、eat 是一般動詞，用 does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 152, "question": "How ______ your cousins go to school every day?\nThey take the MRT.", "options": ["is", "are", "does", "do"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "主詞 your cousins 複數、go 是一般動詞，用 do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 153, "question": "He ______ at home. He's in his office now.", "options": ["isn't", "can't", "hasn't", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜be 動詞否定 isn't＋地點", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ be 動詞（否定）＋ 地點，表「（不）在某處」。\n【分析】句中沒有其他動詞，at home 前需要 be 動詞；後句 He's in his office now 也用 be 動詞，所以填 isn't。\n【其他選項】(B) can't 後需原形動詞；(C) hasn't 後需過去分詞；(D) doesn't 後需原形動詞，句中都沒有動詞。\n【例句】Lisa isn't at school today. She is sick.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 154, "question": "My parents ______ in Taipei now. They are visiting friends in Hualien.", "options": ["don't", "aren't", "haven't", "can't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "句中無一般動詞，in Taipei 前用 be 動詞否定 aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 155, "question": "Sorry, Mr. Lee ______ here right now. He went to a meeting.", "options": ["isn't", "doesn't", "hasn't", "won't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "here 前缺 be 動詞，用 isn't 表「現在不在這裡」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 156, "question": "The keys ______ in my bag. Where did I put them?", "options": ["don't", "doesn't", "isn't", "aren't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The keys 複數，句中無一般動詞，用 aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 157, "question": "Andy: Did Mary ______ that square watch?\nLucy: Yes, she just bought it.", "options": ["buy", "buys", "bought", "has bought"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜Did＋S＋原形動詞", "explanation": "【句型】Did ＋ S ＋ 原形V？ 助動詞 did 後一律接原形動詞。\n【分析】問句已用助動詞 Did 表過去，後面動詞要用原形 buy。\n【其他選項】(B) buys 第三人稱單數形；(C) bought 過去式；(D) has bought 完成式，都不能放在 did 後。\n【例句】Did your brother watch the game last night?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 158, "question": "Did Tom ______ his homework before dinner?", "options": ["finishes", "finish", "finished", "finishing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "Did 後接原形動詞 finish。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 159, "question": "Kevin didn't ______ to the party yesterday because he was sick.", "options": ["went", "goes", "go", "going"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "didn't 後接原形動詞 go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 160, "question": "Did your sister ______ you a birthday card?", "options": ["give", "gave", "gives", "given"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "Did 後接原形動詞 give。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 161, "question": "Allen: ______ you have twenty minutes right now? I need to talk to you.\nBruce: Sure! Come on in.", "options": ["Are", "Do", "Have", "Should"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜have 當「擁有」用 Do 問", "explanation": "【句型】Do/Does ＋ S ＋ have ＋ N？ have 表「擁有」時是一般動詞。\n【分析】have twenty minutes 是「有二十分鐘（空檔）」，have 為一般動詞，主詞 you，用助動詞 Do。\n【其他選項】(A) Are 不能接原形動詞 have；(C) Have you…? 是完成式問句，後面要接 p.p.；(D) Should 表「應該」，語意不合（問對方有沒有空）。\n【例句】Do you have a pen I can use?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 162, "question": "______ your brother have a bike?\nYes, he rides it to school every day.", "options": ["Is", "Has", "Does", "Do"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "have 表擁有，主詞單數用 Does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 163, "question": "______ they have any questions about the test?", "options": ["Do", "Are", "Have", "Does"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "have 表擁有，主詞 they 用 Do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 164, "question": "Excuse me. ______ you have this T-shirt in a bigger size?", "options": ["Are", "Have", "Is", "Do"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "have 表「有」是一般動詞，主詞 you 用 Do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 165, "question": "Sam: ______ you have a good time at Mr. Moore's house tonight?\nTom: Yes. It was a wonderful party. I'm glad I went.", "options": ["Do", "Did", "Will", "Would"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜依回答時態判斷 Did 問句", "explanation": "【句型】Did ＋ S ＋ have a good time？ 問已發生的事用過去式。\n【分析】雖然是 tonight，但回答 It was a wonderful party 與 I went 都是過去式，表示派對已結束，問句用 Did。\n【其他選項】(A) Do 問平常習慣；(C) Will 問未來，但派對已結束；(D) Would 表禮貌請求或假設，不合語意。\n【例句】Did you have fun at the beach this morning?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 166, "question": "Ann: ______ you enjoy the concert this afternoon?\nBen: Yes! The singer was amazing.", "options": ["Do", "Will", "Did", "Are"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "回答 was 表示已發生，問句用 Did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 167, "question": "Mom: ______ you eat breakfast this morning?\nJay: No, I got up too late.", "options": ["Did", "Do", "Will", "Have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "回答 got up 過去式，問句用 Did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 168, "question": "Gina: ______ you go to the night market tonight?\nHank: Yes, I'm going with my cousins after dinner.", "options": ["Did", "Have", "Were", "Will"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "回答 I'm going after dinner 表還沒去，問未來用 Will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 169, "question": "Have you found a summer job yet? Mr. Firth ______ someone to take care of his kids during the vacation. Maybe you can talk to him.", "options": ["has looked for", "is looking for", "looks for", "was looking for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在進行式表現階段進行中", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ be ＋ Ving，表「目前這段時間正在進行」。\n【分析】Maybe you can talk to him 表示 Mr. Firth 現在仍在找人，用現在進行式 is looking for。\n【其他選項】(A) has looked for 偏向「已找過」，不強調仍在進行；(C) looks for 表習慣，不合「目前正在找」；(D) 過去進行式不合現在語境。\n【例句】My aunt is looking for a new apartment these days.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 170, "question": "Ms. Lin ______ a new English teacher for her cram school. You should send her your resume.", "options": ["is looking for", "looked for", "was looking for", "looks"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "目前仍在找人，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 171, "question": "Our class ______ for the school sports day these days. We practice every afternoon.", "options": ["prepared", "prepares", "is preparing", "was preparing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "these days 表目前這段期間正在進行，用 is preparing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 172, "question": "Don't call Grandpa now. He ______ a nap.", "options": ["took", "takes", "has taken", "is taking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "此刻正在午睡，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 173, "question": "John: Have you seen my comic books, Jean?\nJean: ______ on your desk yesterday, but Mom took them away this morning.", "options": ["They are", "They had", "They were", "They've been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式 They were＋地點", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ was/were ＋ 地點＋ 過去時間，表「過去在某處」。\n【分析】they 指 my comic books（複數）；yesterday 是明確過去時間，用 They were。\n【其他選項】(A) They are 現在式與 yesterday 不合；(B) They had 後要接名詞，語意不合；(D) 現在完成式不能和 yesterday 連用。\n【例句】My shoes were by the door last night, but now they're gone.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 174, "question": "Ted: Where are my glasses?\nMay: ______ on the sofa an hour ago. Did you check there?", "options": ["They were", "They are", "They have", "It was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "glasses 複數，an hour ago 過去時間，用 They were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 175, "question": "Iris: Have you seen my umbrella?\nOwen: ______ by the door this morning.", "options": ["They were", "It is", "It was", "It has been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "umbrella 單數，this morning 已過去，用 It was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 176, "question": "My grandparents ______ in Japan last month. Now they're back in Taiwan.", "options": ["are", "have been", "were", "had"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "last month 過去時間，主詞複數用 were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 177, "question": "Mrs. Smith ______ the movie very much. She has seen it three times.", "options": ["liked", "likes", "has liked", "will like"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在簡單式表喜好狀態", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ 現在簡單式（like/love/hate 等狀態動詞），表現在的喜好。\n【分析】後句 She has seen it three times 表示到現在看了三次，可見她現在很喜歡這部電影，用 likes。\n【其他選項】(A) liked 表過去喜歡，現在未必；(C) like 是狀態動詞，一般不用完成式表現在喜好；(D) 未來式不合，她已看過。\n【例句】Kevin loves this song. He has listened to it many times.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 178, "question": "Wendy ______ Korean food a lot. She has eaten at that Korean restaurant five times this month.", "options": ["likes", "liked", "will like", "is liking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "表現在的喜好用現在簡單式 likes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 179, "question": "My father ______ this old car. He has driven it for twenty years.", "options": ["loved", "has loved", "loves", "will love"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "現在仍喜愛，用現在簡單式 loves。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 180, "question": "Eric ______ spiders. He always runs away when he sees one.", "options": ["hated", "has hated", "is hating", "hates"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "表現在的好惡用現在簡單式 hates。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 181, "question": "Abby: Too bad you couldn't come to the beach with us. It was so much fun there! You must come next time.\nBree: No, thanks. I don't think ______ any fun. I can't swim.", "options": ["I was having", "I've had", "I have", "I'll have"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜I don't think＋未來式 I'll have", "explanation": "【句型】I don't think ＋ S ＋ will ＋ V，對未來的看法。\n【分析】Abby 說 next time 邀她下次去，Bree 推測「（下次）我不會玩得開心」，談的是未來，用 I'll have。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去進行式不合；(B) 現在完成式指到目前的經驗，不合「下次」；(C) 現在簡單式不能表示對下次的推測。\n【例句】I don't think it will rain tomorrow.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 182, "question": "Lily: Will you join the hiking trip next Sunday?\nNick: I don't think ______. I have to study for the test.", "options": ["I'll go", "I went", "I've gone", "I was going"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "談下週日的計畫（未來），用 I'll go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 183, "question": "Don't worry about the test tomorrow. I don't think it ______ too hard.", "options": ["was", "has been", "will be", "is being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow 的考試是未來，用 will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 184, "question": "Ray: Do you want to try the new roller coaster next time?\nSue: No way! I don't think ______ it.", "options": ["I enjoyed", "I've enjoyed", "I was enjoying", "I'll enjoy"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "next time 指未來，用 I'll enjoy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 185, "question": "______ the dog that bites people yours? You should keep it home.", "options": ["Can", "Does", "Has", "Is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜Is＋S＋所有代名詞？（主詞含關代子句）", "explanation": "【句型】Be ＋ S ＋ N/所有代名詞？ 主詞含 that 子句時，要找出真正主要動詞的位置。\n【分析】主詞是 the dog that bites people（bites 是子句動詞），主句沒有其他動詞，yours（= your dog）是補語，需 be 動詞 Is。\n【其他選項】(A) Can、(B) Does 後需接原形動詞；(C) Has 後需接 p.p. 或名詞，三者都缺主要動詞。\n【例句】Is the girl who sings so well your sister?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 186, "question": "______ the boy who plays the guitar your classmate?", "options": ["Does", "Is", "Can", "Has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "主詞 the boy who plays the guitar 後接名詞補語 your classmate，需 be 動詞 Is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 187, "question": "______ the cookies that Mom made yesterday still in the box?", "options": ["Are", "Do", "Is", "Have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "主詞 the cookies 複數，後接地點，用 Are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 188, "question": "______ the man who lives next door a doctor?\nYes. He works at Taipei Hospital.", "options": ["Does", "Has", "Do", "Is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "主詞單數，後接名詞補語 a doctor，用 Is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 189, "question": "Mom: Oh, no! Your sister forgot her sports shoes. When ______ she have PE class? Can you take the shoes to her school?\nPeter: It's in the afternoon. Don't worry. I'll bring them to her.", "options": ["did", "does", "has", "is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜When does＋S＋V？ 問固定時間", "explanation": "【句型】When ＋ do/does ＋ S ＋ 原形V？ 問固定課表或習慣用現在簡單式。\n【分析】PE class 是課表上的固定安排；後面 have 是原形一般動詞，主詞 she 單數，用 does。回答 It's in the afternoon 也是現在式。\n【其他選項】(A) did 問過去，但媽媽要在今天送鞋，體育課尚未上；(C) has 後需 p.p.；(D) is 後不能接原形動詞 have。\n【例句】When does your brother have piano lessons?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 190, "question": "What time ______ the school bus leave every morning?", "options": ["do", "is", "does", "did"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "每天固定時間用現在簡單式，主詞單數用 does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 191, "question": "When ______ your parents usually go jogging?\nAfter dinner.", "options": ["do", "does", "are", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "主詞 your parents 複數，習慣用 do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 192, "question": "How often ______ Jenny have swimming class?\nTwice a week.", "options": ["is", "do", "has", "does"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "主詞 Jenny 單數，固定課程用 does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 193, "question": "Nana: Did you mail the cards to your teachers?\nAnnie: No, I want to check them again. I ______ them after dinner.", "options": ["mailed", "mail", "have mailed", "will mail"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜未來式 will＋V（after dinner）", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ will ＋ V ＋ 未來時間，表將要做的事。\n【分析】Annie 說 No（還沒寄），想再檢查一次，after dinner 是之後的時間，用 will mail。\n【其他選項】(A) mailed 表已寄，與 No 矛盾；(B) mail 現在式表習慣；(C) have mailed 表已寄完，也矛盾。\n【例句】I will call you back after class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 194, "question": "Ivy: Have you cleaned your room?\nMax: Not yet. I ______ it this evening.", "options": ["will clean", "cleaned", "have cleaned", "clean"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "Not yet 還沒做，this evening 表未來，用 will clean。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 195, "question": "Sorry, I'm busy now. I ______ you with your homework after I finish my report.", "options": ["helped", "have helped", "will help", "help"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "之後才幫忙，用未來式 will help。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 196, "question": "Ray: Did you return the books to the library?\nPam: No, I ______ them back tomorrow.", "options": ["took", "have taken", "take", "will take"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow 表未來，用 will take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 197, "question": "The fishermen knew little about the island when they ______ there.", "options": ["arrived", "would arrive", "arrive", "have arrived"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜主句過去式→when 子句過去式", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ 過去式 ＋ when ＋ S ＋ 過去式，敘述過去同一時間的情況。\n【分析】主句 knew 是過去式，「他們抵達那裡時」也是過去發生的事，用 arrived。\n【其他選項】(B) would arrive 表過去的未來，語意不合；(C) arrive 現在式與 knew 時態不一致；(D) 現在完成式不合過去敘述。\n【例句】I was very tired when I got home last night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 198, "question": "Amy didn't know anyone when she first ______ to this school.", "options": ["comes", "came", "has come", "will come"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "主句 didn't know 過去式，when 子句也用過去式 came。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 199, "question": "When Tim ______ the news, he was very surprised.", "options": ["heard", "hears", "has heard", "will hear"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "主句 was 過去式，when 子句用 heard。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 200, "question": "The kids were very hungry when they ______ home.", "options": ["get", "have got", "will get", "got"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "主句 were 過去式，when 子句用 got。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 201, "question": "Alex: Why are you still here? It's already eight o'clock.\nTom: Because I ______ my work. Don't worry. It's almost done.", "options": ["wasn't finishing", "wouldn't finish", "haven't finished", "won't finish"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式否定 haven't finished", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ haven't/hasn't ＋ p.p.，表「到目前為止還沒完成」。\n【分析】still here、already eight o'clock 表到現在；It's almost done 表示工作到現在還沒做完，用 haven't finished。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去進行式不合現在情境；(B) wouldn't finish 表「不肯完成」；(D) won't finish 表「不會完成」，與 almost done 矛盾。\n【例句】I can't go out yet. I haven't done my homework.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 202, "question": "Kai: Are you ready to go?\nDan: Not yet. I ______ my breakfast.", "options": ["haven't eaten", "didn't eat", "won't eat", "wasn't eating"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "到現在還沒吃完，用現在完成式 haven't eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 203, "question": "Lucy can't give you the book now because she ______ it yet.", "options": ["didn't read", "won't read", "hasn't read", "doesn't read"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "yet 搭配現在完成式，主詞單數用 hasn't read。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 204, "question": "We ______ the answer yet. Can we have five more minutes?", "options": ["didn't find", "don't find", "won't find", "haven't found"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "到目前還沒找到，用 haven't found。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 205, "question": "Candy has decided to move to Taipei next year. When she studies in an art school there, she ______ with her aunt for five months.", "options": ["lives", "has lived", "lived", "will live"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜時間子句用現在式、主句用未來式", "explanation": "【句型】When/If ＋ 現在式（代替未來）, S ＋ will ＋ V。\n【分析】next year 才搬去，when 子句用現在式 studies 表未來，主句要用未來式 will live。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式不能當表未來的主句；(B) 現在完成式表到目前為止，但她還沒搬；(C) 過去式不合。\n【例句】When I go to Japan next month, I will visit my friend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 206, "question": "When Grandpa ______ next week, we will take him to the night market.", "options": ["will come", "comes", "came", "has come"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "when 時間子句以現在式代替未來，用 comes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 207, "question": "After Jason graduates next June, he ______ in his father's shop.", "options": ["will work", "works", "worked", "has worked"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "主句表未來，用 will work。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 208, "question": "If it ______ tomorrow, we will stay home and watch movies.", "options": ["will rain", "rained", "rains", "has rained"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "if 條件句以現在式代替未來，用 rains。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 209, "question": "The woman you met in the library yesterday ______ our school a lot of books.", "options": ["giving", "given", "to give", "will give"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜整句缺主要動詞＋未來式", "explanation": "【句型】S（＋省略關代子句）＋主要動詞。The woman (whom) you met… 是主詞，後面需要主要動詞。\n【分析】you met… yesterday 是修飾主詞的子句，句子仍缺主要動詞；選項中只有 will give 能當主要動詞，表「她將捐給學校許多書」。\n【其他選項】(A) giving、(B) given、(C) to give 都不能單獨當主要動詞。\n【例句】The man you saw at the gate will be our new coach.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 210, "question": "The boy I talked to at the bus stop ______ in the same class as my brother.", "options": ["being", "is", "to be", "been"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The boy (whom) I talked to 後缺主要動詞，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 211, "question": "The cake my mom made this morning ______ delicious.", "options": ["tastes", "tasting", "to taste", "tasted by"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The cake (that) my mom made 後缺主要動詞，用 tastes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 212, "question": "The students we met at the museum last week ______ us a visit next Friday.", "options": ["paying", "paid by", "to pay", "will pay"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "主詞後缺主要動詞，next Friday 表未來，用 will pay。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 213, "question": "Tommy is looking for the watch his uncle ______ him on his birthday.", "options": ["gives", "gave", "to give", "has given"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜省略關代的子句＋過去式（明確過去時間）", "explanation": "【句型】N ＋（that/which 省略）＋ S ＋ V，關係子句時態依自身時間決定。\n【分析】the watch (that) his uncle ___ him on his birthday，叔叔在他生日時送的，是過去發生的事，用 gave。\n【其他選項】(A) gives 現在式不合；(C) to give 不能當子句動詞；(D) 現在完成式不能與明確過去時間 on his birthday 連用。\n【例句】I still keep the letter my friend wrote me last year.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 214, "question": "Have you read the book Ms. Chen ______ us last week?", "options": ["recommends", "has recommended", "recommended", "to recommend"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "last week 明確過去時間，子句用過去式 recommended。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 215, "question": "The bike my father ______ me two years ago is still in good shape.", "options": ["bought", "buys", "has bought", "buying"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "two years ago 過去時間，用 bought。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 216, "question": "I lost the cap my sister ______ me when we were in Japan.", "options": ["gives", "has given", "giving", "gave"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "when we were in Japan 指過去，用 gave。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 217, "question": "Paul: ______ Shelly's father a businessman?\nCarl: I don't think so. I remember he teaches English.", "options": ["Are", "Is", "Do", "Does"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜Is＋S＋N？ be 動詞疑問句", "explanation": "【句型】Is/Are ＋ S ＋ N？ 句中沒有一般動詞時用 be 動詞發問。\n【分析】句中沒有一般動詞，a businessman 是主詞補語，主詞 Shelly's father 單數，用 Is。\n【其他選項】(A) Are 用於複數主詞；(C)(D) Do/Does 後需接原形一般動詞，但句中沒有。\n【例句】Is your mother a nurse?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 218, "question": "______ Jason and Ella your classmates?", "options": ["Do", "Is", "Are", "Does"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "句中無一般動詞，主詞複數用 Are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 219, "question": "______ Mr. Wang's son a basketball player?\nYes, he plays for our school team.", "options": ["Is", "Does", "Are", "Do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "句中無一般動詞，主詞單數用 Is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 220, "question": "______ your sister work at a bank?\nNo, she's a teacher.", "options": ["Is", "Are", "Do", "Does"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "句中有一般動詞 work，主詞單數用 Does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 221, "question": "Ryan: Would you like to play tennis with me?\nDara: No, thanks. ______ it for three hours already. I'm tired now.", "options": ["I play", "I'm playing", "I've played", "I'll play"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 for＋一段時間＋already", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ have/has ＋ p.p. ＋ for ＋ 一段時間，表從過去持續到現在。\n【分析】for three hours already 表「到現在已經打了三小時」，所以現在很累，用現在完成式 I've played。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式表習慣；(B) 現在進行式表此刻正在打，但她正在拒絕邀約；(D) 未來式與 already、I'm tired now 不合。\n【例句】We have waited for the bus for thirty minutes.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 222, "question": "I'm so hungry. I ______ anything since this morning.", "options": ["didn't eat", "haven't eaten", "don't eat", "won't eat"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "since this morning 到現在，用現在完成式 haven't eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 223, "question": "Ms. Lee ______ English at this school for ten years.", "options": ["has taught", "teaches", "taught", "will teach"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "for ten years 至今持續，用 has taught。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 224, "question": "My eyes hurt. I ______ at the computer for five hours already.", "options": ["look", "am looking", "will look", "have looked"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "for five hours already 表從過去到現在，用 have looked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 225, "question": "Eva: What's your ideal mate like?\nAda: Well, I want a husband who ______ well. I enjoy eating, but I hate kitchens.", "options": ["cook", "cooks", "cooking", "to cook"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜關代 who 後動詞與單數先行詞一致", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞＋who＋V，子句動詞單複數依先行詞。\n【分析】先行詞 a husband 是單數，描述一般特質（會煮飯）用現在簡單式，所以用 cooks。\n【其他選項】(A) cook 用於複數先行詞；(C) cooking、(D) to cook 都不能當關係子句的動詞。\n【例句】I need a friend who listens to me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 226, "question": "We need a leader who ______ good ideas.", "options": ["have", "has", "having", "to have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 a leader 單數，用 has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 227, "question": "Students who ______ hard usually get good grades.", "options": ["studies", "studying", "to study", "study"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 Students 複數，用原形 study。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 228, "question": "My grandma has a cat that ______ on her bed every night.", "options": ["sleeps", "sleep", "sleeping", "to sleep"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 a cat 單數，習慣用 sleeps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 229, "question": "Simon: Why ______ Jerry and Lisa play cards with us?\nHenry: Because they want to go to the movies.", "options": ["don't", "isn't", "aren't", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜Why don't＋複數主詞＋V？", "explanation": "【句型】Why ＋ don't/doesn't ＋ S ＋ 原形V？ 問「為什麼不…」。\n【分析】play 是原形一般動詞，主詞 Jerry and Lisa 是複數，助動詞用 don't；回答 Because they want… 說明原因。\n【其他選項】(B)(C) be 動詞不能接原形動詞 play；(D) doesn't 用於單數主詞。\n【例句】Why don't your parents come to the school concert?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 230, "question": "Why ______ your brother eat vegetables?\nHe just doesn't like them.", "options": ["don't", "doesn't", "isn't", "aren't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "主詞 your brother 單數，後接原形 eat，用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 231, "question": "Why ______ you and Kim join the dance club?\nWe're too busy.", "options": ["don't", "aren't", "doesn't", "isn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "主詞 you and Kim 複數，後接原形 join，用 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 232, "question": "Why ______ the students in the classroom?\nThey're having PE class.", "options": ["don't", "doesn't", "isn't", "aren't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "句中無一般動詞，in the classroom 前用 be 動詞，主詞複數用 aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 233, "question": "Rex did not feel the earthquake this morning. He ______ in the park at the time.", "options": ["jogged", "was jogging", "has jogged", "would jog"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去進行式 at the time", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ was/were ＋ Ving ＋ at the time / at that moment，表過去某時正在進行。\n【分析】at the time 指今天早上地震發生的那一刻，Rex 當時正在公園慢跑，所以沒感覺到，用過去進行式 was jogging。\n【其他選項】(A) jogged 只表過去做過，不能表現「當時正在」；(C) 現在完成式不合過去時間點；(D) would jog 表過去習慣或假設，語意不合。\n【例句】I was taking a shower when you called me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 234, "question": "Sorry, I didn't answer your call. I ______ a bath at that time.", "options": ["was taking", "took", "have taken", "take"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "at that time 表過去某時正在進行，用 was taking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 235, "question": "What ______ you doing at 9 p.m. last night?\nI was watching TV.", "options": ["did", "are", "were", "have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "問過去某時正在做什麼，用 were you doing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 236, "question": "When the lights went out, we ______ dinner.", "options": ["have", "had had", "are having", "were having"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "停電那一刻正在吃晚餐，用過去進行式 were having。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 237, "question": "Ed and Jill ______ camping this weekend, so they have to finish their homework by Friday.", "options": ["went", "were going", "are going", "have gone"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在進行式表近未來計畫", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ am/is/are ＋ Ving ＋ 未來時間，表已安排好的近未來計畫（go/come/leave 常見）。\n【分析】this weekend 是即將到來的週末，so they have to finish… by Friday 表示還沒出發，用 are going 表已安排的計畫。\n【其他選項】(A) went 過去式；(B) were going 過去進行式，都不合未來；(D) have gone 表已經去了，與「週五前要寫完功課」矛盾。\n【例句】My family is flying to Okinawa next Monday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 238, "question": "Hurry up! The train ______ in five minutes.", "options": ["left", "is leaving", "has left", "was leaving"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "in five minutes 表即將發生，用 is leaving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 239, "question": "We ______ a barbecue party tomorrow night. Would you like to come?", "options": ["are having", "had", "have had", "were having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow night 已安排好的計畫，用 are having。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 240, "question": "Uncle Joe ______ to visit us next Saturday, so Mom is cleaning the house.", "options": ["came", "has come", "was coming", "is coming"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "next Saturday 近未來計畫，用 is coming。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 241, "question": "If we play some interesting games in class, there ______ more fun in learning English.", "options": ["are", "has", "will be", "will have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜If 子句現在式＋主句 there will be", "explanation": "【句型】If ＋ 現在式, there will be ＋ N。條件句主句用未來式；there 後只能接 be 動詞。\n【分析】If 子句 play 是現在式表未來條件，主句表結果用未來式；「會有更多樂趣」是 there be 句型，所以用 there will be。\n【其他選項】(A) are 現在式不表未來結果，且 fun 不可數不用 are；(B)(D) there 後不可接 has/have。\n【例句】If it doesn't rain tomorrow, there will be a lot of people at the beach.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 242, "question": "If you come early, there ______ enough seats for everyone.", "options": ["will be", "will have", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "條件句主句用未來式，there 後接 be，用 will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 243, "question": "There ______ a big storm tomorrow, so the school will be closed.", "options": ["has", "is having", "will be", "will have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow 表未來，there 後用 will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 244, "question": "If the city builds a new park here, there ______ more places for kids to play.", "options": ["have", "will have", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "if 條件句的結果用未來式，there will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 245, "question": "I ______ swimming for several years before I went to this high school. I gave it up because of heavy schoolwork.", "options": ["have practiced", "am practicing", "practiced", "would practice"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式（已結束的一段時間）", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ 過去式 ＋ for ＋ 一段時間 ＋ before ＋ 過去事件，表過去一段已結束的時間。\n【分析】before I went to this high school 是過去，且 I gave it up 表示現在已不練，所以「練了好幾年」是已結束的過去，用 practiced。\n【其他選項】(A) have practiced 表持續到現在，但已放棄；(B) am practicing 表此刻正在練；(D) would practice 偏「過去的習慣/假設」，與 for several years 搭配不自然。\n【例句】She lived in Japan for three years before she moved back to Taiwan.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 246, "question": "My father ______ in a bank for ten years before he opened his own store.", "options": ["worked", "has worked", "is working", "works"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "開店前在銀行工作的十年已結束，用過去式 worked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 247, "question": "Ken ______ the piano for five years when he was a child, but now he plays the drums.", "options": ["has played", "plays", "played", "is playing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "when he was a child 指過去且已結束，用 played。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 248, "question": "We ______ in Tainan for two years. Then we moved to Taichung last year.", "options": ["have lived", "live", "are living", "lived"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "住台南的兩年已結束，用過去式 lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 249, "question": "David looked out of the balcony window and saw a woman get in his car ______ away.", "options": ["drive", "drove", "and drive", "and drove"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 saw＋O＋V1 and V2（對等）", "explanation": "【句型】感官動詞 saw ＋ O ＋ V1 and V2，兩個動詞要用 and 連接且形式相同（都用原形或都用 Ving）。\n【分析】saw a woman get in his car（原形 get），後面的動作也要用原形，並用 and 連接：get in his car and drive away。\n【其他選項】(A) 缺連接詞 and；(B)(D) drove 是過去式，與 get 形式不對等。\n【例句】I saw him open the door and walk in.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 250, "question": "Lisa heard her brother open the window and ______ out.", "options": ["shouts", "shouted", "shout", "to shout"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "heard＋O＋V1 and V2，與 open 對等用原形 shout。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 251, "question": "We watched the kids jump into the pool ______ happily.", "options": ["and swim", "swam", "and swam", "to swim"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "watched＋O＋原形 jump，用 and 連接原形 swim。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 252, "question": "Mom saw the dog run into the kitchen ______ the meat.", "options": ["ate", "eats", "and ate", "and eat"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "saw＋O＋run and eat，兩動詞皆用原形並以 and 連接。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 253, "question": "Ariel ______ every night for a week before her Chinese test and got a very good grade.", "options": ["studied", "studies", "has studied", "was going to study"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜過去簡單式（與 got 時態一致）", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ V1（過去式）＋ and ＋ V2（過去式），對等動詞時態一致；敘述過去已完成的事。\n【分析】後面 got a very good grade 是過去式，表示考試已結束；考前一週每晚讀書也是過去的事，用 studied。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在式不合；(C) 現在完成式不用來敘述已結束的過去事件；(D) was going to study 表「原本打算讀」，與拿高分不合。\n【例句】Sam practiced every day before the contest and won first prize.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 254, "question": "Jack ______ for an hour after dinner and then went to bed.", "options": ["reads", "has read", "read", "is reading"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "then went 是過去式，前一動作也用過去式 read。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 255, "question": "Mina saved money for six months and finally ______ a new bike.", "options": ["bought", "buys", "has bought", "will buy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "saved 過去式，對等用 bought。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 256, "question": "My brother ______ hard for the race last month and won a gold medal.", "options": ["trains", "has trained", "is training", "trained"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "last month 且 won 過去式，用 trained。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 257, "question": "Tom ______ ten pounds over the past two months. He looks much thinner now.", "options": ["loses", "has lost", "will lose", "was losing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式 over the past + 時間", "explanation": "【句型】over the past + 一段時間 搭配現在完成式 have/has + p.p.，表從過去到現在的累積結果。\n【分析】over the past two months「過去兩個月以來」，結果是現在看起來瘦很多（He looks much thinner now），用 has lost。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在簡單式表習慣；(C) 未來式不合已發生的結果；(D) 過去進行式表過去某時正在進行，與現在結果無關。\n【例句】My sister has read five novels over the past month.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 258, "question": "Our town ______ a lot over the past ten years. There are many new buildings now.", "options": ["changes", "changed", "has changed", "will change"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "over the past ten years 持續到現在，用現在完成式 has changed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 259, "question": "Mr. Chen ______ in this school since 2015, so he knows every teacher here.", "options": ["has taught", "teaches", "taught", "is teaching"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間點，用現在完成式 has taught。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 260, "question": "Lisa: You look tired.\nMike: I ______ well for the past few days because of the exam.", "options": ["don't sleep", "didn't sleep", "won't sleep", "haven't slept"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "for the past few days 延續到現在，用 haven't slept。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 261, "question": "Life in the mountains ______ quieter than life in big cities.", "options": ["are", "is", "to be", "being"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜不可數名詞主詞 + 單數動詞（主詞動詞一致）", "explanation": "【句型】主詞 + 介系詞片語 + 動詞：動詞跟著真正的主詞變化；不可數名詞視為單數。\n【分析】真正的主詞是 Life（不可數名詞，單數），in the mountains 只是修飾的介系詞片語，所以用 is。\n【其他選項】(A) are 誤把 mountains 當主詞；(C) to be、(D) being 不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】The weather in the south is warmer than in the north.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 262, "question": "The water in these bottles ______ not clean enough to drink.", "options": ["are", "were", "is", "being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "主詞 water 不可數，視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 263, "question": "The price of the shoes ______ too high for me.", "options": ["is", "are", "being", "to be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "真正主詞是 price（單數），用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 264, "question": "The students in Mr. Chen's class ______ very friendly.", "options": ["is", "was", "being", "are"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "主詞 students 複數，用 are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 265, "question": "Bill: Have you ever been to Hong Kong?\nTed: Yes, ______. It's really a fun place to go.", "options": ["five days", "for three years", "in one month", "twice already"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜會考歷屆｜現在完成式（經驗）回答次數 twice already", "explanation": "【句型】Have you ever been to ＋ 地點？（現在完成式表經驗）→ 回答次數 once / twice / ... times\n【分析】Bill 問「曾經去過香港嗎」，Ted 說 Yes 後補充「已經去過兩次了」，用 twice already 表經驗次數。\n【其他選項】(A) five days 缺 for，且不回答經驗；(B) for three years 表持續期間，「去過」不能持續三年；(C) in one month 表「一個月後」，用於未來，不合。\n【例句】Have you ever eaten stinky tofu? — Yes, many times.\n備註：本題考現在完成式（經驗）的回應方式，並非疑問詞或名詞子句，建議改歸「時態＋整句結構」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 266, "question": "Amy: Have you ever seen a koala?\nJoe: No, ______. I hope I can see one in Australia.", "options": ["never", "once", "I haven't", "I have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "No 後的簡答用 I haven't，與 Have you…? 呼應。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 267, "question": "Ivy has ______ to Japan three times. She loves Tokyo.", "options": ["gone", "been", "went", "go"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "have been to 表「去過（已回來）」，搭配次數。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 268, "question": "Leo: How many times have you watched this movie?\nMay: ______. It's my favorite.", "options": ["For two hours", "Last week", "Four times", "In a minute"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "How many times 問次數，回答 Four times。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 269, "question": "Do you know what Lindsey's first job was? Before becoming a movie star, she ______ the floors at the supermarket.", "options": ["mops", "is mopping", "has mopped", "mopped"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜115會考｜過去簡單式 mopped（過去的事實）", "explanation": "【句型】過去簡單式：描述過去發生、已結束的事實或工作。\n【分析】線索 what Lindsey's first job was、Before becoming a movie star：她現在是電影明星，拖地是「過去」的第一份工作 → mopped。\n【其他選項】(A) mops：現在簡單式，表示現在的習慣；(B) is mopping：現在進行式，表示此刻正在做；(C) has mopped：現在完成式，不用於描述過去某段已結束時期的工作。\n【例句】Before she became a teacher, Ms. Huang worked at a bookstore.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 270, "question": "Before moving to Kaohsiung, my family ______ in Hualien for five years.", "options": ["live", "lived", "are living", "will live"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "搬家前的過去事實，用過去式 lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 271, "question": "When my dad was young, he ______ newspapers every morning to make money.", "options": ["delivered", "delivers", "is delivering", "has delivered"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "when my dad was young 表過去，用 delivered。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 272, "question": "Ivy is a famous singer now, but ten years ago she ______ songs on the street.", "options": ["sings", "has sung", "sang", "is singing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "ten years ago 表過去時間，用過去式 sang。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 273, "question": "Tom: Sam, could you help me in the kitchen now?\nSam: No, I ______ TV. It's the most important game of the season.", "options": ["watch", "watched", "have watched", "am watching"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜115會考｜現在進行式 am watching（說話當下正在進行）", "explanation": "【句型】現在進行式 am/is/are + Ving：說話當下正在進行的動作。\n【分析】線索 now、No：Tom 問「現在」能否幫忙，Sam 拒絕，因為他「此刻正在看」比賽 → am watching。\n【其他選項】(A) watch：現在簡單式，表習慣，無法說明此刻在忙；(B) watched：過去式，已看完就能幫忙；(C) have watched：表已經看過／完成，也不構成拒絕理由。\n【例句】Please be quiet. The baby is sleeping now.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 274, "question": "Mom: Can you take out the trash, Kevin?\nKevin: Wait a minute. I ______ my homework.", "options": ["did", "am doing", "have done", "do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "說話當下正在寫作業，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 275, "question": "Listen! Someone ______ the piano next door.", "options": ["is playing", "plays", "played", "has played"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "Listen! 表當下正在發生，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 276, "question": "Amy: Where is Dad?\nBob: He ______ the car in the garage right now.", "options": ["washes", "washed", "is washing", "has washed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "right now 表此刻正在洗車，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 277, "question": "Nick: ______ you finish the work before five o'clock?\nKate: I don't think so. It'll take more than an hour. It's already four thirty now.", "options": ["Are", "Do", "Can", "Be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜助動詞 can 表能力／可能", "explanation": "【句型】Can + 主詞 + 原形動詞…? 詢問「能不能做到」。\n【分析】Kate 回答還要一個多小時、現在已經四點半，表示「五點前做不完」，Nick 問的是能力／可能性，用 Can。\n【其他選項】(A) Are 後面不能接原形動詞 finish；(B) Do you finish 問的是習慣，不合語意；(D) Be 不能放句首形成問句。\n【例句】Can you come to my party this Saturday?\n備註：講義 p.56", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 278, "question": "Amy: ______ you carry this heavy box for me?\nBen: Sure. Where should I put it?", "options": ["Do", "Could", "Are", "Did"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "請求別人幫忙用 Could you + 原形動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 279, "question": "Mom: ______ you see the stars from your window last night?\nTom: No. It was too cloudy.", "options": ["Could", "Can", "Are", "Were"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "last night 是過去，問過去能不能看到，用 Could。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 280, "question": "My little brother is only two, so he ______ read yet.", "options": ["isn't", "doesn't", "can't", "wasn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "兩歲還不會讀書是能力問題，用 can't + 原形動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 281, "question": "Kelly: Who ______ the housework in your family?\nLucie: Everyone shares some.", "options": ["does", "is doing", "can do", "did"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜現在簡單式表習慣；Who 當主詞用單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】Who + 單數動詞…? 問主詞；表習慣、常態用現在簡單式。\n【分析】Lucie 回答 Everyone shares some（現在式），說的是家中平常的分工，Who 當主詞視為第三人稱單數，用 does。\n【其他選項】(B) is doing 是「現在正在做」，不合常態語意；(C) can do 是「誰會做」，問能力不合答句；(D) did 是過去式，與答句 shares 時態不符。\n【例句】Who usually walks the dog in your house?\n備註：講義 p.60", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 282, "question": "Ivy: Who ______ you to school every morning?\nRay: My father does.", "options": ["is taking", "took", "takes", "take"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "every morning 表習慣，Who 當主詞用第三人稱單數 takes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 283, "question": "My grandmother ______ a walk in the park after dinner every day.", "options": ["takes", "is taking", "took", "take"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "every day 表習慣，主詞第三人稱單數，用 takes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 284, "question": "Look! The children ______ kites on the hill. They look so happy.", "options": ["fly", "flies", "flew", "are flying"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "Look! 表示眼前正在發生，用現在進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 285, "question": "I ______ swimming for several years before I went to this high school. I gave it up because of heavy schoolwork.", "options": ["have practiced", "am practicing", "practiced", "would practice"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜過去簡單式（過去的事，已結束）vs. 現在完成式", "explanation": "【句型】過去已結束的動作（即使持續一段時間 for several years）用過去簡單式。\n【分析】before I went to this high school 與 I gave it up 表示練游泳是過去的事，而且現在已放棄，用 practiced。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式表持續到現在，與「已放棄」矛盾；(B) 現在進行式表正在練，矛盾；(D) would practice 表過去習慣雖可能，但空格需陳述一段已結束的經歷，會考答案為過去簡單式。\n【例句】My father worked in Japan for five years before he came back to Taiwan.\n備註：講義 p.94", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 286, "question": "Mia ______ in Tainan for ten years, but she moved to Taipei in 2020.", "options": ["has lived", "lives", "lived", "is living"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "已搬走，住台南是已結束的過去事件，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 287, "question": "Jack ______ the guitar since he was eight. He still plays it every day.", "options": ["has played", "played", "plays", "was playing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間且持續到現在，用現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 288, "question": "We ______ in the same class for three years in junior high, but now we go to different schools.", "options": ["are", "have been", "will be", "were"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "國中同班已結束，用過去式 were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 289, "question": "Mom: Linda, you've been playing computer games all evening! Have you finished your report?\nLinda: Well, ______ most of it this afternoon, and I'll finish it by Friday.", "options": ["I would do", "I did", "I was doing", "I'll do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜過去簡單式（this afternoon 已過去）", "explanation": "【句型】過去已完成的動作用過去簡單式；this afternoon 若已過去，就用過去式。\n【分析】媽媽說她已玩了一整晚（all evening），所以 this afternoon 已過去；「下午做完了大部分」是已完成的動作，用 I did。\n【其他選項】(A) would do 表過去的未來或假設，不合；(C) was doing 描述過去某時刻正在進行，無法表示「已做完大部分」；(D) I'll do 是未來式，但下午已過。\n【例句】It's nine p.m. now. I cleaned my room this morning.\n備註：講義 p.94", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 290, "question": "It's eight o'clock at night. I ______ my homework this afternoon, so now I can watch TV.", "options": ["finish", "will finish", "finished", "am finishing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "晚上八點時下午已過，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 291, "question": "It's only ten in the morning. I ______ my grandparents this afternoon.", "options": ["visited", "will visit", "have visited", "was visiting"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "現在是早上，下午尚未到，用未來式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 292, "question": "Dad: Where were you at four this afternoon?\nAndy: I ______ basketball with my friends at the park.", "options": ["played", "play", "am playing", "was playing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "過去某個時間點正在做的事，用過去進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 293, "question": "I always ______ my wife with the housework for two hours every weekend when we lived in London.", "options": ["helped", "helps", "am helping", "was going to help"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜過去簡單式表過去習慣（when we lived…）", "explanation": "【句型】過去的習慣（always / every weekend）用過去簡單式。\n【分析】when we lived in London 表示過去的時間，always…every weekend 表示習慣，所以用 helped。\n【其他選項】(B) helps 是現在式，且主詞 I 不接 helps；(C) am helping 是現在進行式，時間不合；(D) was going to help 是「過去原本打算要幫」，不表習慣。\n【例句】When I was a child, I often played in the river near my house.\n備註：講義 p.94", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 294, "question": "When my grandpa was young, he ______ to school on foot every day.", "options": ["walks", "walked", "is walking", "has walked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "when he was young 是過去，every day 是習慣，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 295, "question": "Now Emma ______ to school by MRT, but she used to take the bus.", "options": ["goes", "went", "was going", "had gone"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "Now 表現在的習慣，用現在簡單式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 296, "question": "When we were in Kaohsiung, my sister and I usually ______ on the beach on Sundays.", "options": ["are walking", "walk", "walked", "have walked"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "過去在高雄時的習慣，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 297, "question": "Daisy: Have you found the information you need?\nTyler: I ______ the Net for an hour last night but still couldn't find any.", "options": ["surfed", "have surfed", "would surf", "have been surfing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜明確過去時間 last night 用過去式，不用現在完成式", "explanation": "【句型】有明確過去時間（last night, yesterday, … ago）用過去簡單式，不可用現在完成式。\n【分析】句中有 last night，且後句用 couldn't，表示是過去的事，用 surfed。for an hour 不代表一定要用完成式。\n【其他選項】(B)(D) 現在完成（進行）式不能與 last night 連用；(C) would surf 表過去習慣或假設，不合語意。\n【例句】I studied in the library for three hours yesterday.\n備註：講義 p.261", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 298, "question": "I ______ Tina at the bookstore two days ago.", "options": ["have seen", "saw", "see", "have been seeing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "two days ago 是明確過去時間，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 299, "question": "Fred ______ his grandparents three times this year.", "options": ["visits", "is visiting", "was visiting", "has visited"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "this year 尚未結束，表到目前為止的經驗，用現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 300, "question": "Mom: Have you cleaned your room?\nKai: Yes. I ______ it this morning before breakfast.", "options": ["cleaned", "have cleaned", "clean", "will clean"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "this morning before breakfast 是過去明確時間，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 301, "question": "Jenny: Ivan told me that Alice ______ around about you. Is there anything I should know?\nDrew: No way! You must be kidding.", "options": ["has asked", "used to ask", "was asking", "will ask"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜現在完成式表最近持續的影響（lately）", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 have/has + p.p. 表示「最近發生、與現在有關」的事（常搭配 lately、recently）\n【分析】Jenny 問 Is there anything I should know?，表示 Alice 打聽 Drew 這件事是最近的、到現在仍有影響 → has asked（最近一直在打聽）。\n【其他選項】(B) used to ask 表示過去常常、現在不再，不合語意；(D) will ask 是未來，Ivan 不會轉述還沒發生的事；(C) was asking 見 note。\n【例句】Ben told me that Lisa has moved to Tainan.\n備註：講義 p.335；老師紅筆訂正為 (A) 並註 lately。依時態一致，(C) was asking 亦說得通，本題以老師答案為準，講解時宜補充。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 302, "question": "Mom: You look tired. ______ well lately?\nAndy: Not really. I have too much homework.", "options": ["Did you sleep", "Have you slept", "Will you sleep", "Do you sleep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "lately 表最近到現在，用現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 303, "question": "Kelly ______ three books since the summer vacation started.", "options": ["reads", "was reading", "used to read", "has read"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間點，用現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 304, "question": "Leo: Where is Mr. Wang?\nNina: He ______ to the office. He'll be back soon.", "options": ["has gone", "has been", "used to go", "will go"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "人去了還沒回來，用 has gone to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 305, "question": "There ______ something wrong with the coffee machine since yesterday. Be sure to get someone to fix it today, please.", "options": ["was", "is", "will be", "has been"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜講義錯題｜There has been … since（現在完成式）", "explanation": "【句型】There has/have been + N + since + 過去時間（從過去持續到現在）\n【分析】since yesterday 表示從昨天一直到現在都壞了，後句還要今天找人修 → has been。\n【其他選項】(A) was 只表過去；(B) is 現在式不能搭配 since；(C) will be 是未來。\n【例句】There have been many visitors since the museum opened.\n備註：講義 p.337", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 306, "question": "There ______ no rain in this town since last month. The farmers are worried.", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 1（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "since last month 用現在完成式 has been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 307, "question": "There ______ a big typhoon last week, and many trees fell down.", "options": ["was", "has been", "is", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 2（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "last week 為過去時間，用 was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 308, "question": "There ______ three new students in our class since September.", "options": ["are", "have been", "has been", "were"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "時態＋整句結構｜類似題 3（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間，複數 students 用 have been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "時態＋整句結構"}, {"id": 309, "question": "Chris loves walking with Anna on snowy days, but Anna hates ______ very much.", "options": ["them", "so", "one", "it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜代名詞 it 代替前述整件事", "explanation": "【句型】代名詞 it 可代替前面提到的一件事或動名詞片語。\n【分析】Anna 討厭的是「在下雪天和 Chris 散步」這件事，用單數代名詞 it 代替 walking with… on snowy days。\n【其他選項】(A) them 指複數名詞（如 snowy days），語意不合；(B) so 不能當 hate 的受詞；(C) one 代替同類的單數可數名詞，不能指一件事。\n【例句】My brother likes getting up early, but I hate it.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 310, "question": "Jenny enjoys swimming in the sea, but her mom thinks ______ is dangerous.", "options": ["one", "it", "they", "them"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "it 代替 swimming in the sea 這件事。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 311, "question": "I lost my umbrella yesterday, so I need to buy a new ______.", "options": ["it", "them", "one", "that"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "one 代替同類但不同的一把傘。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 312, "question": "Tim bought three books and put ______ on his desk.", "options": ["them", "it", "one", "they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "them 代替複數名詞 three books，作受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 313, "question": "There ______ more than twenty clubs in our school. Which one would you like to join?", "options": ["has", "have", "is", "are"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There are＋複數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】There is ＋ 單數N / There are ＋ 複數N，表「（某處）有…」。\n【分析】後面名詞 more than twenty clubs 是複數，表示「學校裡有二十多個社團」，用 There are。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) There 後不接 has/have；(C) is 用於單數名詞。\n【例句】There are thirty students in my class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 314, "question": "There ______ a cat and two dogs in the yard.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "There be 動詞看最靠近的名詞 a cat（單數），用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 315, "question": "There ______ some milk in the fridge. You can drink it.", "options": ["are", "have", "is", "has"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "milk 不可數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 316, "question": "How many people ______ in your family?", "options": ["is there", "have there", "has there", "are there"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "How many＋複數名詞，問句用 are there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 317, "question": "______ will be a welcome party next week for the new students. Will you come with me?", "options": ["It", "There", "They", "We"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There will be 表未來存在", "explanation": "【句型】There will be + N 表「將會有…」。\n【分析】句意「下週將會有一場歡迎新生的派對」，表示某事物「存在／舉行」，用 There will be a welcome party。\n【其他選項】(A) It will be 需有前面提過的指代對象，這裡沒有；(C) They 無指代對象且 party 為單數；(D) We will be a party 語意不通。\n【例句】There will be a school concert this Friday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 318, "question": "______ will be a typhoon tomorrow, so the school will be closed.", "options": ["It", "They", "There", "This"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "表「明天將會有颱風」的存在句，用 There will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 319, "question": "Look at the poster. There ______ a book fair at the city library next month.", "options": ["will be", "will have", "is going", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "There 句型只能接 be 動詞，next month 表未來，用 There will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 320, "question": "Kevin: Will ______ any snacks at the meeting?\nAmy: Yes, Mr. Lin will bring some cookies.", "options": ["it be", "there be", "they have", "there have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "問「將會有點心嗎」用疑問句 Will there be + N?。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 321, "question": "(In the teachers' office)\nMiss Huang: Sue, ______ students in the classroom?\nMiss Cheng: I don't think so. School's over.\nMiss Huang: But I hear people talking over there.", "options": ["are they", "do they", "is there", "are there"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜Are there + 複數名詞（疑問句）", "explanation": "【句型】Are there + 複數N + 地點? 問「某地有沒有…」。\n【分析】問「教室裡還有學生嗎」是問存在，students 為複數，用 are there。\n【其他選項】(A) are they students 意為「他們是學生嗎」，they 無指代；(B) do they 後缺動詞；(C) is there 後接單數名詞。\n【例句】Are there any eggs in the fridge?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 322, "question": "Mom: ______ any milk in the bottle?\nTim: No, I drank it all this morning.", "options": ["Is there", "Are there", "Does it", "Is it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "milk 是不可數名詞，問「有沒有牛奶」用 Is there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 323, "question": "Ben: ______ many people at the night market last night?\nLisa: Yes, it was very crowded.", "options": ["Was there", "Were there", "Did they", "Were they"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "last night 過去 + people 複數，用 Were there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 324, "question": "Student: Excuse me, are there any free seats on this bus?\nDriver: Sorry, ______. You'll have to stand.", "options": ["there aren't", "they aren't", "it isn't", "there isn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "對 Are there…? 的否定簡答為 No, there aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 325, "question": "Paul: What did you find under his desk?\nTom: Oh, ______ all kinds of things: a basketball, pencils, a hat, and fries!", "options": ["there were", "it was", "it had", "there was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There were + 複數名詞（過去存在）", "explanation": "【句型】There were + 複數N 表「過去有…」。\n【分析】問句 did you find 為過去式；「桌子底下有各種東西」表存在，all kinds of things 為複數，用 there were。\n【其他選項】(B) it was 指單一事物，不合；(C) it had 無指代對象，「有」不用 have 表存在；(D) there was 後接單數。\n【例句】There were many birds in the tree yesterday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 326, "question": "When we got to the beach, ______ a lot of trash on the sand.", "options": ["it was", "there were", "there was", "they had"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "trash 不可數，過去存在用 there was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 327, "question": "Ten years ago, ______ only two convenience stores in this small town.", "options": ["there were", "there was", "it had", "they were"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "ten years ago 過去 + two stores 複數，用 there were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 328, "question": "Mia: How was the class party?\nJoe: Great! ______ pizza, cake, and games for everyone.", "options": ["It had", "They were", "There was", "There has"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "There be 依最靠近的名詞 pizza（單數/不可數）決定，過去用 there was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 329, "question": "Jack: There is going to ______ a dance show on Saturday. Would you like to go with me?\nNina: Sure. I can't wait for it.", "options": ["be", "do", "get", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There is going to be", "explanation": "【句型】There is going to be + N 表「將會有…」。\n【分析】be going to 後接原形動詞；There 句型的動詞只能是 be，所以填 be。\n【其他選項】(B) do、(C) get、(D) have 都不能與 There 句型搭配表存在。\n【例句】There is going to be a test tomorrow.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 330, "question": "The weatherman says there is going to ______ heavy rain this afternoon.", "options": ["have", "be", "come", "get"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "There is going to be 為固定句型，表「將會有」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 331, "question": "______ going to be a basketball game between Class 801 and Class 802 tomorrow.", "options": ["It is", "They are", "There are", "There is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "a basketball game 單數，用 There is going to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 332, "question": "Sam: Is there going to ______ a field trip next week?\nTeacher: Yes, we're going to the science museum.", "options": ["have", "has", "be", "being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "疑問句 Is there going to be + N?，going to 後接原形 be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 333, "question": "Grace: How many pencils ______ in your pencil box?\nAllen: Only one.", "options": ["are there", "are they", "is there", "is it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜How many + 複數N + are there", "explanation": "【句型】How many + 複數N + are there + 地點? 問「某處有多少…」。\n【分析】How many pencils 為複數，問「鉛筆盒裡有幾枝鉛筆」用 are there；即使回答只有一枝，問句仍用複數。\n【其他選項】(B) are they 表「它們是…」，不是問存在；(C) is there 搭配單數；(D) is it 不合句型。\n【例句】How many students are there in your class?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 334, "question": "Amy: How many chairs ______ in the meeting room?\nBob: Twenty, I think.", "options": ["is there", "are there", "are they", "do they"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "How many chairs 複數，用 are there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 335, "question": "How much water ______ in the bottle? I want to drink some.", "options": ["is there", "are there", "is it", "are they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "How much + 不可數名詞 water，用 is there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 336, "question": "Teacher: How many students ______ in the library when the bell rang?\nJason: About ten.", "options": ["are there", "is there", "was there", "were there"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "when the bell rang 過去 + students 複數，用 were there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 337, "question": "Jenny's bag is very heavy because ______ filled with toy cars.", "options": ["it is", "they are", "there is", "there are"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜代名詞 it 指單數名詞 + be filled with", "explanation": "【句型】S + be filled with + N 表「裝滿…」；代名詞 it 指前面提過的單數名詞。\n【分析】被裝滿的是 Jenny's bag（單數），用 it 代替，it is filled with toy cars。\n【其他選項】(B) they 指複數，但 bag 為單數；(C)(D) there is/are 表存在，後面要接名詞，不能直接接 filled with。\n【例句】This box is light because it is empty.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 338, "question": "I can't drink this soup because ______ too hot.", "options": ["they are", "it is", "there is", "this has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "it 代替前面單數名詞 this soup。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 339, "question": "Mark bought two new shirts, but ______ too small for him.", "options": ["it is", "there are", "they are", "there is"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "they 代替前面複數名詞 two new shirts。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 340, "question": "Don't open the window. ______ very cold outside today.", "options": ["It's", "There's", "They're", "This has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "談天氣溫度用 it 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 341, "question": "Grace: How many people ______ in the office when the fire happened?\nHarry: Five. Luckily, nobody got hurt.", "options": ["did they", "had they", "were there", "would there be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜How many + N + were there（過去）", "explanation": "【句型】How many + 複數N + were there + 地點? 問「過去某處有多少…」。\n【分析】when the fire happened 為過去時間，people 為複數，問存在用 were there。\n【其他選項】(A) did they、(B) had they 後缺動詞且 they 無指代；(D) would there be 表假設或過去的未來，不合事實詢問。\n【例句】How many people were there at the concert last night?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 342, "question": "Reporter: How many cars ______ on the bridge when it broke yesterday?\nPolice: About twenty.", "options": ["were there", "are there", "did they", "was there"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "yesterday 過去 + cars 複數，用 were there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 343, "question": "Dad: How many fish ______ in the river when you were a child?\nGrandpa: So many! The water was very clean then.", "options": ["are there", "have there", "were there", "did there"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "when you were a child 過去，問存在用 were there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 344, "question": "Teacher: How many mistakes ______ in your test this time?\nKen: Only two. I did much better.", "options": ["there were", "were they", "did they have", "were there"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "疑問句要倒裝成 were there；考試已考過，用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 345, "question": "Doris: Why ______ so many things to do when I'm busy enough?\nFrank: That's because you don't know how to use your time well.", "options": ["does it have", "have", "are they", "are there"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜Why are there + 複數N（疑問句）", "explanation": "【句型】Why are there + 複數N…? 問「為什麼有這麼多…」。\n【分析】「為什麼有這麼多事要做」表存在，so many things 為複數，用 are there。\n【其他選項】(A) does it have 無指代對象；(B) have 前缺主詞；(C) are they 表「它們是…」，they 無指代。\n【例句】Why are there so many people in the park today?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 346, "question": "Why ______ so much noise outside? I can't fall asleep.", "options": ["are there", "is there", "does it", "is it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "noise 不可數，問存在用 is there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 347, "question": "Lily: Why ______ so many cars on the road this morning?\nTom: Because it's Monday.", "options": ["are there", "is there", "do they", "are they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "so many cars 複數，用 are there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 348, "question": "Why ______ no students in the classroom right now? Where did they go?", "options": ["is it", "there are", "are there", "do there"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "疑問詞後接倒裝 are there + no + 複數N。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 349, "question": "Somewhere along the road, ______ a shop which sells things from foreign countries.", "options": ["that is", "it is", "it has", "there is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There is + 單數N + 地點", "explanation": "【句型】(地點), there is + 單數N 表「某處有…」。\n【分析】「這條路上某處有一家賣外國商品的店」表存在，a shop 為單數，用 there is。\n【其他選項】(A) that is 指特定事物，此處無指代；(B) it is 無指代對象；(C) it has 不能用來表示某地有某物。\n【例句】Near my school, there is a small bookstore.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 350, "question": "In the middle of the park, ______ a big tree with a swing on it.", "options": ["it is", "there is", "it has", "there has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "某地有某物用 there is + 單數N。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 351, "question": "On the second floor of this building, ______ two music rooms and a library.", "options": ["there are", "there is", "it has", "they are"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "two music rooms 複數，用 there are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 352, "question": "Behind our house, ______ a river where my brother and I used to fish.", "options": ["it was", "they were", "there were", "there was"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "used to 表過去，a river 單數，用 there was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 353, "question": "Kate: Earl, is that tall boy your brother?\nEarl: Yes, ______.\nKate: But you two look so different!", "options": ["it is", "he is", "that is", "you are"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜簡答用人稱代名詞 he is", "explanation": "【句型】Is that + 人 …? 簡答時改用人稱代名詞：Yes, he/she is.\n【分析】問句主詞 that tall boy 指男生，簡答用 he 代替，Yes, he is.\n【其他選項】(A) it 用於指物或不確定身分的人（如電話中 Who is it?）；(C) 簡答不用 that；(D) you 指對方，不合語意。\n【例句】Is that girl your cousin? — Yes, she is.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 354, "question": "Amy: Is that woman with long hair your English teacher?\nBen: Yes, ______. She's very nice.", "options": ["it is", "she is", "that is", "her is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "that woman 為女性，簡答用 she is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 355, "question": "Tom: Are those boys on the court your classmates?\nJay: No, ______. They're from another school.", "options": ["they aren't", "those aren't", "there aren't", "we aren't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "those boys 複數，簡答用 they aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 356, "question": "(Someone knocks on the door.)\nMom: Who is ______?\nDad: It's me. I forgot my key.", "options": ["he", "that one", "it", "they"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "不知門外是誰時用 Who is it?，回答 It's me.", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 357, "question": "When I entered the house for the first time, I found ______ was a big round table in the living room.", "options": ["it", "that", "there", "this"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜found + (that) there was + N", "explanation": "【句型】I found (that) + 子句；子句表存在用 there was + N。\n【分析】found 後省略 that，子句「客廳裡有一張大圓桌」用 there was a big round table。\n【其他選項】(A) it was 無指代對象；(B) that 若當連接詞，子句缺主詞；若當代名詞，「那是一張圓桌」語意不合；(D) this 為指示代名詞，不合語意。\n【例句】When I opened the box, I found there was a letter inside.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 358, "question": "When Lucy opened the fridge, she found ______ was nothing to eat.", "options": ["it", "there", "that", "they"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "found 後子句表「沒有東西」，用 there was nothing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 359, "question": "I heard ______ was no school tomorrow because of the typhoon.", "options": ["there", "it", "they", "this"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "heard (that) 後子句表「沒有…」，用 there was no + N。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 360, "question": "When we got to the theater, we were told that ______ no tickets left.", "options": ["it was", "they were", "there was", "there were"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "no tickets 複數名詞，存在句用 there were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 361, "question": "This restaurant makes delicious chicken rice, so ______ always full of people at mealtime.", "options": ["it is", "they are", "there is", "there are"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜代名詞 it 指單數名詞 + be full of", "explanation": "【句型】S + be full of + N 表「充滿…」；it 代替前面的單數名詞。\n【分析】擠滿人的是 This restaurant（單數），用 it 代替：it is always full of people。\n【其他選項】(B) they 指複數，不合；(C)(D) there is/are 後要接名詞表存在，不能接 full of。\n【例句】The night market sells cheap food, so it is always crowded.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 362, "question": "The new park has a big playground, so ______ always full of kids on weekends.", "options": ["they are", "there is", "it is", "there are"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "it 代替單數名詞 the new park。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 363, "question": "These shoes are cheap and comfortable, so ______ popular with students.", "options": ["they are", "it is", "there are", "there is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "they 代替複數名詞 these shoes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 364, "question": "I like this bookstore because ______ many interesting comic books in it.", "options": ["it is", "they are", "it is having", "there are"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "in it 表「在店裡」，存在句用 there are + 複數N。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 365, "question": "Now we have to take a taxi home because ______ are no buses after eleven o'clock.", "options": ["here", "there", "they", "we"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜There are no + 複數N", "explanation": "【句型】There are no + 複數N 表「沒有…」。\n【分析】「十一點後就沒有公車了」表不存在，no buses 複數，用 there are no buses。\n【其他選項】(A) here are 表「這就是…」，不合語意；(C) they 無指代對象；(D) we are no buses 語意不通。\n【例句】There are no clouds in the sky today.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 366, "question": "We can't play outside because ______ no lights on the playground at night.", "options": ["there are", "it is", "they are", "there is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "no lights 複數，用 there are no。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 367, "question": "I'm hungry, but ______ no food in the kitchen.", "options": ["there are", "it has", "there is", "they have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "food 不可數，用 there is no。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 368, "question": "Ten years ago, ______ no MRT stations in this part of the city.", "options": ["there are", "they were", "there was", "there were"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "ten years ago 過去 + 複數 stations，用 there were no。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 369, "question": "I think ______ is more fun to go to the movies with my friends than with my family.", "options": ["that", "there", "one", "it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜會考歷屆｜虛主詞 it（it is + adj. + to V）", "explanation": "【句型】It is + adj. + to V：it 為虛主詞，代替後面的不定詞片語 to go to the movies…。\n【分析】I think 後的子句中，真正的主詞是 to go to the movies with my friends，放到後面，前面用虛主詞 it：it is more fun to go…。\n【其他選項】(A) that 不能當虛主詞；(B) there is 後面接名詞表「有…」，不接 more fun to V；(C) one 指「一個（東西）」，語意不合。\n【例句】It is interesting to learn about other cultures.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 370, "question": "______ is not polite to talk loudly on the MRT.", "options": ["That", "It", "There", "This"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "虛主詞 it 代替後面的 to talk…。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 371, "question": "I find ______ hard to remember all these new words.", "options": ["it", "that", "there", "one"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "find it + adj. + to V，it 為虛受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 372, "question": "Do you think ______ is easier to take the train than to drive there?", "options": ["that", "there", "it", "one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "虛主詞 it 代替 to take the train。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 373, "question": "There ______ more than twenty clubs in our school. Which one would you like to join?", "options": ["has", "have", "is", "are"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜講義錯題｜There are + 複數名詞（表「有」）", "explanation": "【句型】There is + 單數／不可數名詞；There are + 複數名詞，表示「某處有…」。\n【分析】主詞是 more than twenty clubs（複數），所以用 There are。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) has/have 表「擁有」，不可與 There 連用表「有」；(C) is 用於單數名詞。\n【例句】There are many trees in the park.\n備註：講義 p.41", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 374, "question": "There ______ a lot of milk in the bottle. You don't need to buy more.", "options": ["are", "is", "has", "have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "milk 是不可數名詞，用 There is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 375, "question": "There ______ two new students in our class last week.", "options": ["was", "are", "were", "had"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "last week 是過去時間，two new students 是複數，用 There were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 376, "question": "Is there a bookstore near your house?—No, there ______. But there are two convenience stores.", "options": ["isn't", "aren't", "doesn't", "don't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "There be／代名詞 it, they｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "問句 Is there a bookstore，單數，否定簡答用 there isn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "There be／代名詞 it, they"}, {"id": 377, "question": "Now I often think of those days with Pip, my pet dog. When I read in my room, he ______ quietly beside me.", "options": ["will come and sit", "comes and sits", "has come and sat", "used to come and sit"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "used to｜會考歷屆｜used to＋V 表過去習慣", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ used to ＋ V，表「過去常常…（現在已不再）」。\n【分析】Now I often think of those days 表示在回憶過去，Pip 已不在身邊；「以前我看書時他常來坐在我身邊」用 used to come and sit。\n【其他選項】(A) 未來式不合回憶；(B) 現在式表示現在仍如此，與 those days 矛盾；(C) 現在完成式不表過去的習慣。\n【例句】My grandpa used to tell me stories before bed.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 378, "question": "There ______ a big tree in front of my school, but it was cut down last year.", "options": ["used to be", "is used to", "uses to be", "is using"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "used to｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "表示過去有但現在沒有，用 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 379, "question": "When I was little, my mom ______ me to the park every Sunday.", "options": ["takes", "is taking", "used to take", "has taken"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "When I was little 過去習慣，用 used to take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 380, "question": "Andy ______ shy, but now he talks to everyone in class.", "options": ["is", "has been", "is used to", "used to be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "used to｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "過去如此、現在不同，用 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 381, "question": "In my school days, I ______ to English radio programs every day. That was how I learned English at that time.", "options": ["listen", "have listened", "used to listen", "was listening"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜會考歷屆｜used to + 原V（過去習慣）", "explanation": "【句型】S + used to + 原V 表「過去常常…（現在不再）」。\n【分析】In my school days、at that time 指過去一段時期，every day 表當時的習慣，用 used to listen。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式不合過去時間；(B) 現在完成式表持續到現在，不合 at that time；(D) 過去進行式表過去某一時刻正在做，不表長期習慣。\n【例句】I used to ride my bike to school when I was in elementary school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 382, "question": "When my grandpa was young, he ______ go fishing in the river behind his house.", "options": ["used to", "is used to", "uses to", "was used to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "used to｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "表過去的習慣用 used to + 原V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 383, "question": "Amy ______ shy, but now she talks with everyone in class.", "options": ["is used to be", "used to be", "was used to", "uses to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "used to｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "過去的狀態現在已改變，用 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 384, "question": "Jason: Did you ______ play the piano?\nNancy: Yes, but I stopped when I was ten.", "options": ["used to", "uses to", "use to", "using to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "疑問句有 did，後面 used to 要改原形 use to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 385, "question": "Willy has changed a lot. He ______ get up early to do exercise. But now he wakes up late and is late for school every day.", "options": ["forgot to", "hated to", "used to", "volunteered to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜會考歷屆｜used to + 原V vs. But now", "explanation": "【句型】S + used to + 原V, but now… 表「以前常…，但現在不再」。\n【分析】Willy has changed a lot 與 But now he wakes up late 形成今昔對比，前句是過去的習慣，用 used to get up early。\n【其他選項】(A) forgot to「忘了去做」；(B) hated to「討厭做」；(D) volunteered to「自願做」，都無法呈現「以前常做、現在不做」的改變。\n【例句】Eric used to eat a lot of fast food, but now he eats vegetables every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 386, "question": "Ms. Lin ______ drive to work, but now she takes the MRT to save money.", "options": ["used to", "hoped to", "forgot to", "refused to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "used to｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "今昔對比（but now），用 used to 表過去習慣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 387, "question": "There ______ a big tree in front of our school, but it was cut down last year.", "options": ["is used to be", "used to be", "was used to", "uses to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "used to｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "過去存在現在不在，用 There used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 388, "question": "My brother ______ play online games all night. Now he goes to bed at ten.", "options": ["decided to", "is used to", "used to", "learned to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "Now 對比過去的習慣，用 used to + 原V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 389, "question": "My husband ______ send me flowers every week before we got married. But now he never does.", "options": ["should", "used to", "was going to", "was afraid to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "used to｜會考歷屆｜used to + 原V（過去習慣）", "explanation": "【句型】S + used to + 原V 表過去的習慣。\n【分析】before we got married（過去）與 But now he never does（現在）對比，「以前每週送花，現在都不送了」，用 used to send。\n【其他選項】(A) should「應該」；(C) was going to「當時打算」；(D) was afraid to「不敢」，皆不合今昔對比的語意。\n【例句】We used to visit our grandparents every summer, but now we seldom do.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 390, "question": "Before she moved to Taipei, Grandma ______ take a walk by the sea every evening.", "options": ["used to", "is used to", "was going to", "should"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "used to｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "before she moved 指過去，表過去習慣用 used to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 391, "question": "Kevin ______ be afraid of dogs, but now he has two dogs at home.", "options": ["is used to", "used to", "was used to", "uses to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "used to｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "過去狀態現已改變，用 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 392, "question": "Ben: Do you still collect stamps?\nAnn: No, but I ______ when I was a kid.", "options": ["use to", "am used to", "used to", "was used"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "省略句 I used to (collect stamps)，表小時候的習慣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 393, "question": "We know you ______ work for big shopping centers. Would you tell us why you choose such a small shoe store like us now?", "options": ["are used to", "get used to", "used to", "will be used to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜講義錯題｜used to + VR（過去習慣）vs. be used to + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】used to + 原形動詞（過去常常，現在不再）；be/get used to + Ving/N（習慣於）\n【分析】空格後是原形 work，且後句 now 選了小鞋店，表示「以前」在大型購物中心工作 → used to work。\n【其他選項】(A)(B)(D) be/get used to 的 to 是介系詞，後要接 working，且「習慣」不合語意。\n【例句】I used to live in Kaohsiung, but now I live in Taipei.\n備註：講義 p.319", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 394, "question": "There ______ a bookstore on this corner, but now it's a coffee shop.", "options": ["is used to be", "used to be", "was used to being", "gets used to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "used to｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "以前是書店、現在不是，用 used to + 原形 be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 395, "question": "Jason moved to Canada last year. Now he ______ the cold weather.", "options": ["used to", "uses to", "is used to", "used to being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "used to｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "現在習慣於冷天氣，be used to + 名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 396, "question": "My dad ______ smoke, but he stopped five years ago.", "options": ["used to", "is used to", "gets used to", "was used to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "used to｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "過去抽菸、現在不抽，used to + 原形 smoke。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "used to"}, {"id": 397, "question": "Jane's parents are always happy to see their grandchildren, but mine ______ less so when I visit them with my kids.", "options": ["is", "are", "do", "does"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 be 動詞（mine = my parents → are）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + be + adj., but S2 + be (+ less so). 省略句沿用前句的 be 動詞。\n【分析】前句用 Jane's parents are happy；後句 mine = my parents（複數），省略 happy，用 are（less so = less happy）。\n【其他選項】(A) is 用於單數主詞；(C)(D) do/does 代替一般動詞，但前句是 be 動詞 are。\n【例句】Tom's sisters are very tall, but mine aren't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 398, "question": "Your dog is very friendly, but ours ______. It always barks at strangers.", "options": ["doesn't", "isn't", "aren't", "don't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "ours = our dog（單數），前句 be 動詞，用 isn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 399, "question": "Amy's shoes are new, but mine ______. I've worn them for three years.", "options": ["don't", "isn't", "doesn't", "aren't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "mine = my shoes（複數），沿用 be 動詞，用 aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 400, "question": "My parents were angry about my grades, but Jack's ______. They just told him to study harder.", "options": ["weren't", "didn't", "wasn't", "don't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "Jack's = Jack's parents（複數），前句 were，用 weren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 401, "question": "Our teacher Ms. Wu seldom laughs, but when she ______, everyone in the same building can hear her.", "options": ["can", "does", "has", "will"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 does 代替一般動詞 laughs", "explanation": "【句型】S + 一般動詞…, but when S + does（省略原動詞）。\n【分析】前句 laughs 為一般動詞現在式第三人稱單數；when she does = when she laughs，用 does 代替。\n【其他選項】(A) can 表能力，與前句不對應；(C) has 用於完成式；(D) will 不用在時間副詞子句中表未來，且與前句時態不合。\n【例句】My brother rarely cooks, but when he does, the food is great.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 402, "question": "Kevin doesn't often sing, but when he ______, everyone stops to listen.", "options": ["is", "does", "has", "do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "when he does = when he sings，主詞第三人稱單數用 does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 403, "question": "My parents seldom go to the movies, but when they ______, they always buy popcorn.", "options": ["are", "does", "do", "have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "when they do = when they go，主詞複數用 do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 404, "question": "Grandpa hardly ever got angry, but when he ______, all of us were scared.", "options": ["does", "was", "had", "did"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "前句 got 為過去式，用 did 代替。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 405, "question": "Lora likes to eat bananas that are already a little brown on the outside, and so ______ I.", "options": ["am", "do", "have", "will"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜附和句 and so + 助動詞 + 主詞（so do I）", "explanation": "【句型】…, and so + 助動詞/be 動詞 + 主詞 表「…也是」。\n【分析】前句動詞 likes 為一般動詞現在式，主詞 I 用 do：and so do I（= and I do, too）。注意 that are… 是形容詞子句，不是主要動詞。\n【其他選項】(A) am 對應 be 動詞；(C) have 對應完成式；(D) will 對應未來式，皆不合 likes。\n【例句】Ben plays the guitar, and so do I.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 406, "question": "Mary is interested in Japanese culture, and so ______ her brother.", "options": ["does", "is", "has", "do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "前句 be 動詞 is，用 so is her brother。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 407, "question": "Peter went to the concert last night, and so ______ his friends.", "options": ["did", "were", "do", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "前句 went 為過去式一般動詞，用 so did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 408, "question": "I have finished my homework, and so ______ Jenny.", "options": ["does", "did", "is", "has"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "前句 have finished 為現在完成式，主詞 Jenny 單數，用 so has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 409, "question": "Dad: Have you brushed your teeth yet?\nAnn: No, but I ______ before I go to bed.", "options": ["haven't", "have", "won't", "will"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜簡答／省略句 will 表未來", "explanation": "【句型】No, but I will (+ 原V) 表「還沒，但等一下會」。\n【分析】現在還沒刷牙（No），但 before I go to bed「睡前」會刷，用 will 表未來，省略 brush my teeth。\n【其他選項】(A) haven't 與 but 轉折矛盾；(B) have 與 No 矛盾；(C) won't 與「睡前」的語意矛盾。\n【例句】I haven't called Grandma yet, but I will tonight.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 410, "question": "Mom: Have you cleaned your room?\nTim: Not yet, but I ______ after lunch.", "options": ["will", "have", "did", "won't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "還沒做但之後會做，用 will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 411, "question": "Teacher: Did you hand in your report?\nAmy: No, I didn't. But I ______ tomorrow, I promise.", "options": ["do", "will", "did", "have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow 表未來，用 will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 412, "question": "Lily: Are you going to the party tonight?\nSam: No, I ______. I have to study for the test.", "options": ["won't go to", "don't", "am not", "haven't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "問句 Are you going to…，簡答用 am not。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 413, "question": "David: Have you seen John's sister?\nKevin: Yes, I ______. She's the most beautiful girl I've ever seen.", "options": ["have", "had", "did", "saw"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜簡答對應助動詞 Have you…? – Yes, I have", "explanation": "【句型】Have you + p.p.…? → Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.\n【分析】問句用現在完成式 Have you seen，簡答用同一助動詞 have。\n【其他選項】(B) had 為過去完成式；(C) did 對應 Did you…?；(D) saw 是一般動詞，簡答要用助動詞。\n【例句】Has Linda finished her homework? — Yes, she has.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 414, "question": "Mia: Has your brother ever been to Japan?\nLeo: Yes, he ______. He went there last summer.", "options": ["did", "is", "has", "was"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "Has…? 用 has 簡答。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 415, "question": "Tina: Did you watch the baseball game last night?\nJoe: Yes, I ______. It was exciting!", "options": ["did", "have", "watched", "was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "Did you…? 用 did 簡答。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 416, "question": "Ken: Have you and Sue finished the science project?\nAnn: No, we ______. We need two more days.", "options": ["didn't", "don't", "aren't", "haven't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "Have you…? 否定簡答用 haven't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 417, "question": "Linda: Do you have to get up early in the morning?\nPeter: Yes, I ______. I can't be late for school.", "options": ["do", "can", "have", "am"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜簡答 Do you have to…? – Yes, I do", "explanation": "【句型】Do you have to + 原V? → Yes, I do. / No, I don't (have to).\n【分析】have to 視為一般動詞，問句助動詞為 Do，簡答用 do。\n【其他選項】(B) can 不對應 Do；(C) have 不能單獨當簡答助動詞（have to 不是 Have you…? 的完成式）；(D) am 是 be 動詞。\n【例句】Does she have to wear a uniform? — Yes, she does.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 418, "question": "Ben: Does your sister have to take the bus to school?\nAmy: No, she ______. Our dad drives her.", "options": ["doesn't", "hasn't", "isn't", "don't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Does…have to? 否定簡答用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 419, "question": "Mark: Did you have to work last weekend?\nNick: Yes, I ______. I was so tired.", "options": ["had", "did", "was", "have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Did you have to…? 簡答用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 420, "question": "Student: Must we finish the worksheet today?\nTeacher: No, you ______. You can finish it tomorrow.", "options": ["mustn't", "can't", "don't have to", "aren't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "Must…? 否定回答「不必」用 don't have to，mustn't 是「禁止」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 421, "question": "Jane: Did you get up early this morning?\nTina: No, I didn't, but my brother ______. He gets up early every day.", "options": ["does", "is", "did", "was"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 did 代替過去式一般動詞", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + didn't, but S2 + did. 省略句依時態用助動詞。\n【分析】this morning 已過去，問句 Did you get up early…?；my brother did = my brother got up early（過去式），用 did。\n【其他選項】(A) does 為現在式，雖然後句說 every day，但這裡講的是今天早上；(B)(D) be 動詞不對應一般動詞 get up。\n【例句】I didn't finish the cake, but my sister did.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 422, "question": "Carl didn't bring an umbrella, but his sister ______. She always checks the weather.", "options": ["does", "did", "was", "has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "前句 didn't bring 為過去，後句用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 423, "question": "Mom: Did you feed the cat this morning?\nRay: No, I didn't, but Dad ______.", "options": ["did", "does", "was", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "this morning 過去，用 did 代替 fed the cat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 424, "question": "Most students didn't understand the joke, but Jason ______. He laughed out loud.", "options": ["does", "doesn't", "didn't", "did"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "轉折 but 表肯定，過去式用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 425, "question": "Betty goes jogging every day in the park, and Allen ______, too.", "options": ["is", "does", "has", "was"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜附和句 S + does, too", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + 一般動詞(現在式), and S2 + does/do, too. 表「…也是」。\n【分析】前句 goes 為一般動詞現在式，主詞 Allen 單數，用 does 代替 goes jogging。\n【其他選項】(A)(D) is/was 為 be 動詞，不對應 goes；(C) has 對應完成式或 have 動詞。\n【例句】My mom drinks coffee every morning, and my dad does, too.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 426, "question": "Frank likes spicy food, and his parents ______, too.", "options": ["does", "are", "do", "is"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "前句一般動詞現在式，主詞 his parents 複數用 do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 427, "question": "Helen was late for school yesterday, and Kevin ______, too.", "options": ["was", "did", "is", "does"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "前句 be 動詞過去式 was，Kevin 單數用 was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 428, "question": "I don't like horror movies, and my sister ______, either.", "options": ["does", "isn't", "didn't", "doesn't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "否定附和用 either，現在式單數用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 429, "question": "Frank read a comic book yesterday, but his brother ______.", "options": ["does", "doesn't", "did", "didn't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 but S + didn't（read 過去式）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V(過去式), but S2 + didn't. 表「…但另一人沒有」。\n【分析】yesterday 表過去，read 在此是過去式（主詞 Frank 單數卻沒加 s）；but 表轉折，後句為否定，用 didn't。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 現在式不合 yesterday；(C) did 為肯定，與 but 的轉折不合。\n【例句】Lisa cut her hair last week, but her sister didn't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 430, "question": "Tom put his phone in his bag, but Ryan ______. He left it on the desk.", "options": ["doesn't", "did", "didn't", "don't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "put 主詞單數沒加 s → 過去式；but 轉折用 didn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 431, "question": "Jenny hurt her leg in the game last week, but the other players ______.", "options": ["didn't", "don't", "weren't", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "last week 過去式，複數主詞否定用 didn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 432, "question": "My friends didn't go to the beach on Sunday, but I ______.", "options": ["don't", "went", "was", "did"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "前否定 didn't go，but 轉折肯定用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 433, "question": "No one thought James would appear at Katie's party. So when he ______, everyone was surprised and could not believe their eyes.", "options": ["would", "was", "had", "did"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 did 代替 appeared", "explanation": "【句型】when + S + did（省略一般動詞過去式）。\n【分析】when he did = when he appeared；事情發生在過去（everyone was surprised），一般動詞過去式用 did 代替。\n【其他選項】(A) would 表過去的未來，when 子句中不用；(B) was 是 be 動詞，不對應 appear；(C) had 為過去完成式，不合時間順序。\n【例句】Nobody expected Ann to win, so when she did, we all cheered.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 434, "question": "We didn't think it would snow on the mountain. So when it ______, we were all excited.", "options": ["would", "did", "was", "had"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "when it did = when it snowed，過去式用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 435, "question": "No one believed Leo could pass the test. But he ______, and he got 90 points!", "options": ["did", "could", "was", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "過去事實 he did = he passed，用 did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 436, "question": "Everyone thought Grace would call her mom first. But she ______. She called her best friend.", "options": ["wouldn't", "doesn't", "wasn't", "didn't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "實際上沒打給媽媽，過去式否定用 didn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 437, "question": "Tommy uses chopsticks well, but his younger brothers ______, so they usually eat with spoons.", "options": ["don't", "doesn't", "aren't", "isn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 but S(複數) + don't", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + 一般動詞(現在式), but S2 + don't/doesn't.\n【分析】前句 uses 為一般動詞現在式；後句主詞 his younger brothers 為複數，省略 use chopsticks well，用 don't。\n【其他選項】(B) doesn't 用於單數主詞；(C)(D) be 動詞不對應 uses。\n【例句】Emma speaks Japanese, but her parents don't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 438, "question": "My dad drinks coffee every day, but my mom ______. She only drinks tea.", "options": ["don't", "isn't", "doesn't", "didn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "前句一般動詞現在式，主詞 my mom 單數用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 439, "question": "Lucy is good at math, but her classmates ______.", "options": ["aren't", "don't", "isn't", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "前句 be 動詞，複數主詞用 aren't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 440, "question": "I know how to swim, but my little sisters ______ yet.", "options": ["doesn't", "aren't", "didn't", "don't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "前句一般動詞 know，主詞複數用 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 441, "question": "Jane always does well on English tests, but her sisters ______.", "options": ["doesn't", "aren't", "don't", "didn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 but S(複數) + don't", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + 一般動詞(現在式), but S2 + don't/doesn't.\n【分析】前句 does well 為一般動詞現在式（always 表習慣）；後句主詞 her sisters 複數，用 don't（= don't do well）。\n【其他選項】(A) doesn't 用於單數；(B) aren't 為 be 動詞，不對應 does well；(D) didn't 為過去式，不合 always 的現在習慣。\n【例句】Leo always gets up early, but his roommates don't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 442, "question": "Kevin often helps his mom with housework, but his brother ______.", "options": ["doesn't", "don't", "isn't", "didn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "現在式習慣，主詞單數用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 443, "question": "These students always bring their own cups, but some teachers ______.", "options": ["doesn't", "aren't", "don't", "didn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "主詞 some teachers 複數，現在式用 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 444, "question": "My cousins are interested in history, but I ______.", "options": ["don't", "am not", "isn't", "doesn't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "前句 be 動詞 are，主詞 I 用 am not。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 445, "question": "Mom: Peter, be sure to finish your school report before you go to bed.\nPeter: OK, Mom, I ______.", "options": ["am", "do", "have", "will"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜簡答 I will 承諾未來", "explanation": "【句型】回應請求或提醒時用 I will.（= I will finish it）表承諾。\n【分析】媽媽提醒「睡前務必寫完報告」，事情尚未完成，Peter 答應之後會做，用 will。\n【其他選項】(A) am 為 be 動詞，不對應 finish；(B) do 表現在習慣；(C) have 表已經完成，與「睡前要完成」矛盾。\n【例句】Teacher: Don't forget to bring your textbook tomorrow. — Student: I won't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 446, "question": "Dad: Remember to lock the door when you leave.\nAmy: Sure, I ______.", "options": ["am", "will", "do", "did"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "答應未來會做，用 I will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 447, "question": "Teacher: Don't forget to return the library books on Friday.\nBen: Don't worry. I ______.", "options": ["won't", "don't", "will", "didn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "Don't forget… 的回應為 I won't（forget）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 448, "question": "Mom: Please call me when you get to Grandma's house.\nJoe: OK, I ______.", "options": ["am", "have", "did", "will"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "承諾抵達後會打電話，用 I will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 449, "question": "Melody has a great interest in planting flowers, but her sister ______. She can't even stay in the garden for one minute.", "options": ["can't", "doesn't", "isn't", "won't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 doesn't 代替 has（一般動詞）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + has (一般動詞), but S2 + doesn't.\n【分析】前句 has a great interest 的 has 是一般動詞「有」（不是完成式助動詞），後句主詞 her sister 單數，用 doesn't（= doesn't have an interest）。\n【其他選項】(A) can't 不對應 has；(C) isn't 為 be 動詞；(D) won't 為未來式。\n【例句】Tom has a pet dog, but his cousin doesn't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 450, "question": "Ann has a lot of free time on weekends, but her parents ______. They are always busy.", "options": ["haven't", "aren't", "don't", "doesn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "has 為一般動詞，主詞複數用 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 451, "question": "My brother has a smartphone, but I ______. My parents think I'm too young.", "options": ["don't", "haven't", "am not", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "have 為一般動詞，主詞 I 用 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 452, "question": "Kevin has finished his homework, but his sister ______. She's still working on it.", "options": ["doesn't", "hasn't", "isn't", "didn't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "has finished 為現在完成式，has 是助動詞，用 hasn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 453, "question": "Ken's brothers like to watch tennis, but Ken ______. He is crazy about baseball.", "options": ["is", "isn't", "does", "doesn't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 一般動詞否定 doesn't", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V, but S2 + don't/doesn't. 後句省略相同的動詞部分，只留助動詞。\n【分析】前句 like 是一般動詞；後句主詞 Ken 為第三人稱單數，且 He is crazy about baseball 表示他不喜歡看網球 → doesn't (like to watch tennis)。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) is/isn't 是 be 動詞，無法代替一般動詞 like；(C) does 表「他也喜歡」，與後句語意矛盾。\n【例句】My parents drink coffee, but I don't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 454, "question": "My parents enjoy hiking, but my little sister ______. She thinks it's too tiring.", "options": ["does", "doesn't", "is", "isn't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "前句 enjoy 為一般動詞，主詞 my little sister 單數且語意否定，用 doesn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 455, "question": "Tina didn't finish her homework last night, but her brother ______. He finished it before dinner.", "options": ["did", "didn't", "was", "does"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "前句是過去式一般動詞，後句語意肯定（他完成了），用 did 代替 finished his homework。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 456, "question": "Most of my classmates are good at math, but Leo ______. He always needs help.", "options": ["does", "doesn't", "is", "isn't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "前句用 be 動詞 are good at，後句主詞 Leo 單數、語意否定，用 isn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 457, "question": "My sister does not like the jacket, and I don't, ______.", "options": ["either", "so", "too", "yet"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜否定句的「也」：either", "explanation": "【句型】否定句 + and S + don't/isn't..., either. 表「…也不」。\n【分析】前後兩句都是否定（does not like / I don't），句尾表「也不」要用 either。\n【其他選項】(B) so 用於肯定倒裝 and so do I；(C) too 只用於肯定句；(D) yet 表「尚未／然而」，語意不合。\n【例句】Tom can't speak Japanese, and I can't, either.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 458, "question": "Ben can't swim, and his sister can't, ______.", "options": ["too", "either", "so", "neither"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "兩句皆為否定，句尾「也不」用 either。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 459, "question": "I love spicy food, and my dad does, ______.", "options": ["either", "neither", "too", "not"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "兩句皆為肯定，句尾「也」用 too。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 460, "question": "Amy isn't afraid of snakes, and ______ is her brother.", "options": ["so", "either", "too", "neither"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "否定的倒裝句 neither + be/助動詞 + S 表「…也不」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 461, "question": "Many of my classmates have had the experience of taking an airplane, but I ______.", "options": ["don't", "wasn't", "won't", "haven't"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜省略句 現在完成式否定 haven't", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + have/has + p.p., but S2 + haven't/hasn't. 後句省略 p.p. 以後的部分。\n【分析】前句 have had the experience 是現在完成式，後句主詞 I，語意否定 → haven't (had the experience)。\n【其他選項】(A) don't 是現在簡單式；(B) wasn't 是過去式 be 動詞；(C) won't 是未來式，皆與前句時態不對應。\n【例句】Lisa has finished her report, but I haven't.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 462, "question": "Most of my friends have seen the new movie, but I ______. I'll see it this weekend.", "options": ["don't", "didn't", "haven't", "won't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "前句 have seen 為現在完成式，後句否定用 haven't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 463, "question": "My brother has never been to Japan, but I ______. I went there last summer.", "options": ["have", "haven't", "do", "am"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "前句 has been 為現在完成式，後句語意肯定（我去過），用 have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 464, "question": "Jenny had lunch at school yesterday, but Kevin ______. He went home to eat.", "options": ["doesn't", "didn't", "hasn't", "wasn't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "前句 had 為過去式一般動詞，後句否定用 didn't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 465, "question": "Alice: Have you ever been to a baseball game?\nJamie: No, never. ______\nAlice: Sure. Baseball is my favorite sport.", "options": ["Do you?", "Have you?", "Don't you?", "Haven't you?"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜會考歷屆｜反問省略句 Have you?", "explanation": "【句型】反問對方「你呢？」：助動詞/be 動詞 + 主詞？（時態跟前句一致）\n【分析】Alice 用 Have you ever been 現在完成式發問，Jamie 回答後反問「你呢？去過嗎？」→ Have you (ever been to a baseball game)?\n【其他選項】(A) Do you? 是現在簡單式，與 have been 不對應；(C)(D) 否定問句帶有「難道你不…嗎」的驚訝語氣，不合單純反問的語意。\n【例句】A: Have you finished your homework? B: Not yet. Have you?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 466, "question": "Eric: I'm so excited about the school trip tomorrow. ______\nGina: Yes, I am! I've packed my bag already.", "options": ["Do you?", "Are you?", "Did you?", "Have you?"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "前句用 be 動詞 I'm excited，反問用 Are you?，與 Gina 的 Yes, I am 對應。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 467, "question": "Mia: I didn't see the fireworks last night. ______\nRay: Yes, I did. They were beautiful.", "options": ["Were you?", "Do you?", "Have you?", "Did you?"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "前句為過去式一般動詞 didn't see，反問用 Did you?。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 468, "question": "Nick: I've never tried stinky tofu. ______\nAnn: Yes, many times. I love it!", "options": ["Do you?", "Did you?", "Have you?", "Are you?"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "前句 I've never tried 為現在完成式，反問用 Have you?。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 469, "question": "Cherry ______ very fast, and her brother, Paul, does, too.", "options": ["can swim", "swims", "is swimming", "swim"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜講義錯題｜…, and S + does, too（一般動詞現在式的省略）", "explanation": "【句型】前句用一般動詞現在式，後句以 do/does 代替，S + does, too。\n【分析】後半句用 does，表示前句是一般動詞現在簡單式；主詞 Cherry 是第三人稱單數，用 swims。\n【其他選項】(A) can swim 後面應說 Paul can, too；(C) is swimming 後面應說 Paul is, too；(D) swim 與第三人稱單數主詞不一致。\n【例句】Lisa likes cats, and her sister does, too.\n備註：講義 p.56", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 470, "question": "Kevin ______ to school by bike, and his best friend does, too.", "options": ["is going", "goes", "can go", "go"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "後句用 does 代替一般動詞，前句主詞第三人稱單數用 goes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 471, "question": "Jenny is good at singing, and her cousin ______, too.", "options": ["does", "do", "is", "can"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "前句用 be 動詞 is，後句以 is 代替。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 472, "question": "My parents didn't watch TV last night, and I ______, either.", "options": ["didn't", "don't", "wasn't", "haven't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "前句是過去式一般動詞否定，後句用 didn't 代替，either 表「也不」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 473, "question": "Rick: Ted bought a pie for Cindy and she ate it. I thought she would never eat things like that.\nElle: She ______. She was just being polite. She didn't want to hurt Ted's feelings.", "options": ["doesn't", "isn't", "didn't", "wasn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜講義錯題｜現在簡單式表習慣＋助動詞 doesn't 代替一般動詞", "explanation": "【句型】省略句：用助動詞 do/does/did 代替前面提過的一般動詞；表習慣用現在簡單式。\n【分析】Elle 意思是「她（平常）不吃那種東西」= She doesn't (eat things like that)，是一向的習慣，用現在式；eat 是一般動詞，用 doesn't。\n【其他選項】(B)(D) isn't／wasn't 是 be 動詞，不能代替 eat；(C) didn't 表「她當時沒吃」，與 she ate it 矛盾。\n【例句】Does Tom drink coffee?—No, he doesn't. He only drinks tea.\n備註：講義 p.59", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 474, "question": "Ann: Your dad cooked dinner today! I thought he never cooks.\nBob: He ______. Mom is sick, so he had to do it.", "options": ["isn't", "didn't", "doesn't", "wasn't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "「他平常不煮飯」是習慣，用一般動詞現在式否定 doesn't 代替 cook。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 475, "question": "Lily: Did Sam go to the concert yesterday?\nMike: No, he ______. He had a bad cold.", "options": ["didn't", "doesn't", "wasn't", "isn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "問句是 Did，答句用 didn't 代替 go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 476, "question": "Paul: Is your sister afraid of dogs?\nJoy: Yes, she ______. She always runs away from them.", "options": ["does", "is", "did", "was"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "be afraid of 用 be 動詞，簡答用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 477, "question": "Wayne: I'd be surprised if you got apples from that tree.\nNita: ______ In fact, it's a peach tree.", "options": ["So would I.", "Neither would I.", "So had I.", "Neither had I."], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜講義錯題｜附和句 So would I（肯定句附和）", "explanation": "【句型】肯定附和：So + 助動詞/be + 主詞；否定附和：Neither + 助動詞/be + 主詞（助動詞要與原句一致）\n【分析】I'd be surprised = I would be surprised，是肯定句，助動詞 would → So would I.（我也會很驚訝）；後句 it's a peach tree 支持「蘋果樹長不出蘋果」。\n【其他選項】(B) Neither 附和否定句，原句沒有 not；(C)(D) I'd 在 be 前是 would，不是 had。\n【例句】A: I'd like some tea. B: So would I.\n備註：講義 p.316", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 478, "question": "Ben: I'd love to visit Japan someday.\nIris: ______ I've always wanted to see Mt. Fuji.", "options": ["Neither would I.", "So had I.", "So would I.", "So did I."], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "I'd love = I would love，肯定句附和用 So would I。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 479, "question": "Kevin: I can't swim very well.\nRita: ______ Let's take lessons together.", "options": ["Neither can I.", "So can I.", "Neither do I.", "So am I."], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "原句否定且助動詞為 can，用 Neither can I。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 480, "question": "Tina has finished her report, and ______.", "options": ["so did Leo", "so has Leo", "Leo hasn't, either", "neither has Leo"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、助動詞 has，附和用 so has Leo。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 481, "question": "Michael seldom writes letters, and Pete doesn't, ______.", "options": ["either", "too", "neither", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜講義錯題｜否定附和 either（seldom 為否定）", "explanation": "【句型】否定附和：主詞 + 否定助動詞, either ＝ neither + 助動詞 + 主詞\n【分析】seldom（很少）有否定意味，且空格前已有 doesn't → 句尾用 either。\n【其他選項】(B) too 用於肯定附和；(C) neither 本身否定，不能接在 doesn't 後（雙重否定）；(D) so 用於肯定且要倒裝放句首。\n【例句】Amy doesn't eat meat, and I don't, either.\n備註：講義 p.316", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 482, "question": "Jack never goes to bed early, and his sister doesn't, ______.", "options": ["too", "either", "neither", "so"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "never 為否定，後接 doesn't，句尾用 either。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 483, "question": "Lily hardly eats vegetables, and ______ her brother.", "options": ["so does", "either does", "neither does", "too does"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "hardly 為否定，倒裝附和用 neither does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 484, "question": "Mia likes playing basketball, and Ken does, ______.", "options": ["too", "either", "neither", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "肯定附和放句尾用 too。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "省略句（助動詞／be動詞）"}, {"id": 485, "question": "Robert: Charles wanted to borrow $1,000 from me yesterday.\nMandy: You didn't lend him the money, ______?", "options": ["would you", "wouldn't you", "did you", "didn't you"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 前否定後肯定（didn't → did you）", "explanation": "【句型】附加問句：前句否定 → 附加問句肯定；助動詞依前句時態。\n【分析】You didn't lend him the money 為過去式否定句，附加問句用肯定的 did you。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) would 與前句 didn't 不對應；(D) didn't you 是否定，前後同為否定不合規則。\n【例句】You didn't tell Mom about it, did you?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 486, "question": "Your brother doesn't eat meat, ______?", "options": ["doesn't he", "does he", "is he", "did he"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "前否定（doesn't）後肯定，用 does he。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 487, "question": "Ms. Chang was your English teacher last year, ______?", "options": ["wasn't she", "was she", "didn't she", "isn't she"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "前肯定 was，後否定 wasn't she。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 488, "question": "You haven't seen my glasses, ______?", "options": ["did you", "do you", "haven't you", "have you"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "前否定 haven't，後肯定 have you。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 489, "question": "Getting up early on a cold morning is not easy, ______?", "options": ["are you", "do you", "does it", "is it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 Ving 主詞→it", "explanation": "【句型】Ving（動名詞）當主詞 → 附加問句主詞用 it；前否定、後肯定。\n【分析】主詞 Getting up early on a cold morning 是動名詞片語，代名詞用 it；動詞 is not 是 be 動詞否定 → is it。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 主詞 you 不對；(C) does 為一般動詞助動詞，但前句是 be 動詞 is。\n【例句】Swimming in the river is dangerous, isn't it?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 490, "question": "Playing video games all night is bad for your eyes, ______?", "options": ["are they", "isn't it", "doesn't it", "is it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞用 it，前句 be 動詞肯定，後用 isn't it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 491, "question": "To finish the report in one day wasn't easy for Leo, ______?", "options": ["was it", "wasn't it", "did he", "was he"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "不定詞主詞用 it，前句 wasn't 否定，後用肯定 was it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 492, "question": "Everyone in Class 8 likes Ms. Lin, ______?", "options": ["doesn't she", "does it", "don't they", "isn't it"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "Everyone 當主詞時附加問句用 they，前肯定後用 don't they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 493, "question": "Alice really likes having noodles for breakfast, ______?", "options": ["doesn't she", "is she", "hasn't she", "did she"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 現在式一般動詞 doesn't", "explanation": "【句型】現在簡單式一般動詞肯定句 → 附加問句用 don't/doesn't + 代名詞。\n【分析】likes 為一般動詞現在式（第三人稱單數），主詞 Alice → she，前肯定後否定 → doesn't she。\n【其他選項】(B) is 是 be 動詞，且未變否定；(C) hasn't 用於現在完成式；(D) did 是過去式且未變否定。\n【例句】Your father works in a bank, doesn't he?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 494, "question": "Your brother plays basketball after school, ______?", "options": ["does he", "doesn't he", "isn't he", "didn't he"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "plays 為現在式一般動詞，前肯定後用 doesn't he。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 495, "question": "Mark and Joe don't eat meat, ______?", "options": ["do they", "don't they", "are they", "did they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "前句 don't eat 為否定，後用肯定 do they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 496, "question": "Grandma watched the news last night, ______?", "options": ["doesn't she", "wasn't she", "hasn't she", "didn't she"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "watched 為過去式一般動詞，附加問句用 didn't she。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 497, "question": "The tall man over there is our new English teacher, ______?", "options": ["is he", "is there", "isn't he", "isn't there"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 be 動詞，主詞換代名詞", "explanation": "【句型】be 動詞肯定句 → 附加問句 isn't/aren't + 代名詞（主詞名詞要改成代名詞）。\n【分析】主詞 The tall man 為男性單數 → he；動詞 is 肯定 → isn't he。over there 是地點副詞，不是 There be 句型。\n【其他選項】(A) 未變否定；(B)(D) there 是誤把 over there 當成 There be 句型的主詞。\n【例句】The girl next to Amy is your cousin, isn't she?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 498, "question": "The girl in the red dress is your cousin, ______?", "options": ["is she", "isn't it", "isn't she", "doesn't she"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The girl → she，be 動詞肯定，用 isn't she。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 499, "question": "Those shoes on the floor aren't yours, ______?", "options": ["are they", "aren't they", "are those", "do they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "Those shoes 用 they 代替，前否定後用 are they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 500, "question": "That was a great game, ______?", "options": ["was it", "isn't it", "didn't it", "wasn't it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "主詞 That 用 it 代替，was 過去式肯定，後用 wasn't it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 501, "question": "Lucy: Do you think Sally and Martin should get married?\nRose: Why not? They love each other, ______?", "options": ["will they", "won't they", "do they", "don't they"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 複數主詞 don't they", "explanation": "【句型】現在簡單式一般動詞肯定句（複數主詞）→ 附加問句 don't they。\n【分析】They love each other 為現在式一般動詞、肯定句，主詞複數 → don't they。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) will/won't 是未來式，與 love 現在式不對應；(C) do they 沒有變否定。\n【例句】Your cousins live in Kaohsiung, don't they?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 502, "question": "Ivy: Let's ask Tom and Kate to go with us.\nRay: Good idea. They like hiking, ______?", "options": ["do they", "don't they", "aren't they", "didn't they"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "They like 現在式肯定，後用 don't they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 503, "question": "Your parents work in Taichung, ______?", "options": ["don't they", "aren't they", "do they", "doesn't it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "Your parents 複數用 they，work 現在式肯定，後用 don't they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 504, "question": "The twins never go to bed before midnight, ______?", "options": ["don't they", "are they", "do they", "aren't they"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "never 使句子為否定，附加問句要用肯定 do they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 505, "question": "Oscar: I'm going to the museum. Bus Number 286 goes there, ______?\nDavid: Yes, but you can take a Number 287, too.", "options": ["does it", "doesn't it", "is it", "isn't it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 單數名詞主詞→it, doesn't it", "explanation": "【句型】現在式一般動詞肯定句（第三人稱單數）→ 附加問句 doesn't + 代名詞。\n【分析】主詞 Bus Number 286 是物 → it；goes 為一般動詞現在式肯定 → doesn't it。\n【其他選項】(A) does it 沒有變否定；(C)(D) is/isn't 是 be 動詞，與一般動詞 goes 不對應。\n【例句】This bus stops at Taipei Main Station, doesn't it?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 506, "question": "This train stops at Banqiao, ______?", "options": ["does it", "is it", "isn't it", "doesn't it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "主詞 This train → it，stops 現在式肯定，後用 doesn't it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 507, "question": "Your cat doesn't eat fish, ______?", "options": ["doesn't it", "does it", "is it", "isn't it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "前句 doesn't eat 否定，後用肯定 does it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 508, "question": "The library opens at nine on Sundays, ______?", "options": ["doesn't it", "isn't it", "does it", "won't it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "opens 為現在式一般動詞肯定，後用 doesn't it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 509, "question": "She's going to Europe, ______ she?", "options": ["doesn't", "hasn't", "isn't", "won't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 be going to → isn't she", "explanation": "【句型】be going to + V → 附加問句用 be 動詞（isn't/aren't）。\n【分析】She's = She is，句子是 She is going to (go to) Europe，前肯定 → isn't she。\n【其他選項】(A) doesn't 用於一般動詞；(B) 誤把 's 當成 has，但後面是 going 不是 p.p.；(D) won't 雖有未來意思，但句中助動詞是 is，不是 will。\n【例句】You're going to join the contest, aren't you?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 510, "question": "Your parents are going to buy a new car, ______?", "options": ["don't they", "won't they", "aren't they", "haven't they"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "be going to 的附加問句用 be 動詞，前肯定用 aren't they。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 511, "question": "Lisa isn't going to join the dance contest, ______?", "options": ["is she", "isn't she", "does she", "will she"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "前句 isn't going to 否定，後用肯定 is she。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 512, "question": "It's going to rain this afternoon, ______?", "options": ["doesn't it", "won't it", "hasn't it", "isn't it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "It's = It is，be going to 用 isn't it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 513, "question": "You've studied English for a long time, ______?", "options": ["did you", "didn't you", "have you", "haven't you"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "附加問句｜會考歷屆｜附加問句 現在完成式 haven't you", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式肯定句 → 附加問句 haven't/hasn't + 代名詞。\n【分析】You've studied = You have studied（for a long time 為完成式線索），前肯定 → haven't you。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) did/didn't 用於過去簡單式；(C) have you 沒有變否定。\n【例句】Mike has lived here for ten years, hasn't he?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 514, "question": "Kelly has lived in Tainan since she was five, ______?", "options": ["doesn't she", "hasn't she", "didn't she", "isn't she"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "has lived 為現在完成式，後用 hasn't she。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 515, "question": "You haven't finished your science report yet, ______?", "options": ["have you", "haven't you", "did you", "do you"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "前句 haven't finished 否定，後用肯定 have you。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 516, "question": "Your brother has a new phone, ______?", "options": ["hasn't he", "isn't he", "doesn't he", "didn't he"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "has 在此是一般動詞「擁有」（不是完成式助動詞），附加問句用 doesn't he。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 517, "question": "Having three cups of coffee a day can't be bad for our health, ______?", "options": ["can it", "can they", "is it", "are they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜115會考｜動名詞主詞的附加問句（單數 it；否定句接肯定問句）", "explanation": "【句型】附加問句：前否定 → 後肯定；助動詞跟主要句相同；主詞用代名詞。動名詞（Ving 片語）當主詞視為單數，用 it 代替。\n【分析】主要句助動詞是 can't，所以附加問句用肯定的 can；主詞 Having three cups of coffee a day 是一件事，代名詞用 it → can it。\n【其他選項】(B) can they：動名詞主詞不能用 they；(C) is it、(D) are they：主要句的助動詞是 can，不是 be 動詞。\n【例句】Reading in bed isn't good for your eyes, is it?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 518, "question": "Playing video games all night won't help you get good grades, ______?", "options": ["will it", "won't it", "will they", "do you"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞視為單數 it；前句 won't 否定，後接肯定 will it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 519, "question": "Swimming in the river is dangerous, ______?", "options": ["is it", "isn't it", "aren't they", "doesn't it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "前句肯定 is，附加問句用否定 isn't；動名詞主詞用 it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 520, "question": "Eating vegetables every day can keep you healthy, ______?", "options": ["can it", "can't they", "can't it", "doesn't it"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "附加問句｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "前句肯定 can，附加問句用 can't；動名詞主詞用 it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "附加問句"}, {"id": 521, "question": "John will stay with his sister until he ______ an apartment.", "options": ["will find", "would find", "finds", "found"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜until 副詞子句用現在式代替未來", "explanation": "【句型】S + will + V + until + S + V（現在簡單式）。時間副詞子句用現在式表示未來。\n【分析】主句 will stay 是未來，until 引導的時間副詞子句不可用 will，要用現在式；主詞 he 單數 → finds。\n【其他選項】(A) 副詞子句不可用 will；(B) would 用於過去的未來或假設；(D) found 過去式與主句未來不合。\n【例句】I'll wait here until you come back.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 522, "question": "We'll wait here until the rain ______.", "options": ["stops", "will stop", "stopped", "is stopped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "until 引導時間副詞子句，用現在式 stops 代替未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 523, "question": "As soon as Amy ______ home, she will call you.", "options": ["will get", "got", "gets", "is getting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "as soon as 時間副詞子句用現在式表未來，主詞單數用 gets。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 524, "question": "Don't leave the classroom until the bell ______.", "options": ["will ring", "rang", "is ringing", "rings"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "until 副詞子句用現在簡單式 rings 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 525, "question": "Before she ______ about it, you should tell Daphne you broke her favorite cup.", "options": ["asks", "asked", "was asking", "will ask"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜before 副詞子句用現在式代替未來", "explanation": "【句型】Before + S + V（現在簡單式）, S + should/will + V。時間副詞子句以現在式表未來。\n【分析】主句 you should tell 是對未來的建議，「在她問起之前」是未來的事，before 子句用現在式 → asks。\n【其他選項】(B)(C) 過去式／過去進行式與主句的建議不合；(D) 時間副詞子句不可用 will。\n【例句】Please wash your hands before you eat.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 526, "question": "After Sam ______ his homework, his mom will let him play games.", "options": ["will finish", "finishes", "finished", "finishing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "after 時間副詞子句用現在式 finishes 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 527, "question": "Please turn off the lights before you ______ the room.", "options": ["leave", "left", "will leave", "leaving"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "before 副詞子句用現在式 leave 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 528, "question": "When my cousin ______ to Taipei next month, I'll show her around.", "options": ["came", "will come", "comes", "coming"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "when 引導時間副詞子句，即使有 next month 仍用現在式 comes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 529, "question": "I'm not sure if Kevin ______ this morning, but if he does, I'll tell him that you called.", "options": ["will come in", "comes in", "has come in", "came in"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜if（是否）名詞子句保留未來式", "explanation": "【句型】if/whether（是否）引導名詞子句時，該用未來式就用未來式；if（如果）引導條件副詞子句時才用現在式代替未來。\n【分析】if Kevin ___ 是 I'm not sure 的受詞（名詞子句），意思是「他是否會進來」，要用 will come in。後面的 if he does 是條件副詞子句，才用現在式。\n【其他選項】(B) comes in 是副詞子句的用法，此處 if 是「是否」；(C) 現在完成式表已來，與 this morning 尚未發生的不確定語意不合；(D) 過去式，則後句 if he does 不合。\n【例句】I don't know if Amy will come to the party tomorrow.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 530, "question": "Nobody knows if it ______ tomorrow, so bring your umbrella just in case.", "options": ["rains", "will rain", "rained", "has rained"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "if 表「是否」，引導 knows 的受詞（名詞子句），未來的事用 will rain。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 531, "question": "If it ______ tomorrow, the sports day will be canceled.", "options": ["will rain", "rained", "rains", "has rained"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "if 表「如果」，為條件副詞子句，用現在式 rains 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 532, "question": "I wonder whether Jack ______ to my birthday party next Saturday.", "options": ["comes", "came", "has come", "will come"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "whether 引導名詞子句（wonder 的受詞），未來的事用 will come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 533, "question": "Tonight I'll stay at the office until I ______ the work.", "options": ["finish", "am finishing", "finished", "will finish"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜until 副詞子句用現在式代替未來", "explanation": "【句型】S + will + V + until + S + V（現在簡單式）。\n【分析】主句 I'll stay 為未來，until 引導的時間副詞子句用現在簡單式 finish 代替未來。\n【其他選項】(B) 進行式不合「做完為止」的語意；(C) 過去式與 Tonight、I'll 不合；(D) 時間副詞子句不可用 will。\n【例句】We won't start the meeting until Mr. Lee arrives.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 534, "question": "I'll keep practicing the piano until I ______ the song perfectly.", "options": ["will play", "play", "played", "am played"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "until 副詞子句用現在式 play 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 535, "question": "Mom won't go to bed until Dad ______ home tonight.", "options": ["gets", "will get", "got", "getting"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "not...until 副詞子句仍用現在式，主詞 Dad 單數用 gets。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 536, "question": "We'll stay in the classroom until the teacher ______ us to leave.", "options": ["will tell", "told", "tells", "telling"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "until 副詞子句用現在式 tells 表未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 537, "question": "If the weather is fine this weekend, my family ______ to the beach for two days.", "options": ["go", "went", "have gone", "will go"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜if 條件句：主句用未來式", "explanation": "【句型】If + S + V（現在式）, S + will + V。條件子句用現在式，主要子句用未來式。\n【分析】If 子句 is fine 用現在式表未來條件，主句是 this weekend 將發生的事 → will go。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式不能表示「到時候會去」；(B) 過去式不合 this weekend；(C) 現在完成式表已完成，不合。\n【例句】If you hurry, you will catch the bus.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 538, "question": "If you ______ hard, you will pass the test.", "options": ["study", "will study", "studied", "studying"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "if 條件子句用現在式 study 代替未來。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 539, "question": "If Tim gets up late again, he ______ the school bus.", "options": ["misses", "missed", "has missed", "will miss"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "if 子句用現在式，主要子句用未來式 will miss。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 540, "question": "If my parents ______ me a new bike, I'll ride it to school every day.", "options": ["will buy", "bought", "buy", "buying"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "if 條件子句用現在式 buy 表未來，主詞複數不加 s。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 541, "question": "If Frank ______ to the office tonight, give this package to him.", "options": ["came", "comes", "has come", "will come"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜會考歷屆｜if 條件子句＋祈使句", "explanation": "【句型】If + S + V（現在式）, 祈使句（原形動詞開頭）。\n【分析】主句 give this package to him 是祈使句，If 條件子句用現在式表未來（tonight）；Frank 第三人稱單數 → comes。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去式不合 tonight；(C) 現在完成式不合；(D) 條件副詞子句不可用 will。\n【例句】If you see Amy, tell her to call me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 542, "question": "If anyone ______ for me while I'm out, please take a message.", "options": ["calls", "will call", "called", "calling"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "if 條件子句用現在式；anyone 視為單數，用 calls。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 543, "question": "If you ______ any questions after class, come to my office.", "options": ["had", "will have", "have", "having"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "主句為祈使句，if 子句用現在式 have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 544, "question": "If Grandpa ______ tired during the walk, let him sit down for a while.", "options": ["will feel", "felt", "feeling", "feels"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "if 條件子句用現在式，主詞 Grandpa 單數用 feels。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 545, "question": "Mr. Olson went to the doctor when he found he ______ his hair. He hoped he would be able to keep his thick hair.", "options": ["was losing", "is losing", "will lose", "has lost"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜115會考｜過去進行式 was losing（主要子句為過去式）", "explanation": "【句型】過去進行式 was/were + Ving：過去某時正在進行（逐漸發生）的事；主要子句是過去式時，名詞子句也用過去時態。\n【分析】線索 went、found、hoped 都是過去式；掉頭髮是一個逐漸進行的過程，他發現當時「正在掉髮」，且還希望保住濃密頭髮（表示還沒掉光）→ was losing。\n【其他選項】(B) is losing：現在進行式，與過去式 found 時態不一致；(C) will lose：未來式，不符過去時間；(D) has lost：現在完成式，時態不合，且表示已掉光，與「希望保住濃密頭髮」矛盾。\n【例句】When I got home, I found my brother was cooking dinner.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 546, "question": "When Mom came into my room, she found I ______ a comic book, not my textbook.", "options": ["read", "am reading", "was reading", "have read"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "過去某時正在進行的動作用過去進行式 was reading。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 547, "question": "Lily noticed her cat ______ weight, so she gave it less food.", "options": ["was gaining", "is gaining", "will gain", "gains"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "主要子句 noticed 為過去式，體重「正在增加」用 was gaining。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 548, "question": "I didn't answer the phone last night because I ______ a shower.", "options": ["take", "was taking", "am taking", "have taken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "昨晚電話來時「正在洗澡」，用過去進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 549, "question": "When I ______ the door, I ______ nobody but some white roses on the ground.", "options": ["opened; saw", "was opening; saw", "was opening; will see", "opened; see"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜講義錯題｜when 子句與主要子句的時態一致（過去短暫動作）", "explanation": "【句型】When + S + 過去式, S + 過去式（兩個短暫動作接連發生）。\n【分析】開門和看見都是過去發生的短暫動作，一開門就看到地上的玫瑰，所以兩格都用過去簡單式 opened; saw。\n【其他選項】(B) 開門是瞬間動作，不宜用進行式 was opening；(C) will see 是未來式，前後時態矛盾；(D) see 是現在式，與 opened 時態不一致。\n【例句】When I got home, I found a letter on the table.\n備註：講義 p.121", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 550, "question": "When Ken ______ into the classroom, everyone ______ \"Happy birthday!\"", "options": ["walks; shouted", "walked; shouted", "was walking; shouts", "walked; will shout"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "過去接連發生的兩個短暫動作，都用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 551, "question": "When the phone rang, I ______ a shower, so I didn't answer it.", "options": ["took", "take", "was taking", "am taking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "電話響時正在洗澡，持續的動作用過去進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 552, "question": "When you ______ to Tainan next month, I'll show you around.", "options": ["come", "will come", "came", "are coming to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "時間副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 553, "question": "I'll do it whether you ______ me or not. But with your help, I can do it better and faster.", "options": ["help", "will help", "have helped", "helped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜講義錯題｜whether…or not 副詞子句以現在式代替未來式", "explanation": "【句型】whether…or not（不論…與否）引導副詞子句，與 if、when 相同：主要子句用未來式，副詞子句用現在式代替未來。\n【分析】主要子句 I'll do it 是未來式，whether 子句用現在式 help。\n【其他選項】(B) 副詞子句不用 will 表未來；(C) 現在完成式表已完成，不合語意；(D) 過去式與未來情境不合。\n【例句】We'll go hiking whether it rains or not.\n備註：講義 p.276", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 554, "question": "If it ______ tomorrow, the sports day will be canceled.", "options": ["will rain", "rains", "rained", "is going to rain"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "if 條件副詞子句用現在式代替未來式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 555, "question": "I'm not sure whether Kevin ______ to the party tomorrow.", "options": ["comes", "came", "will come", "has come"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "whether 引導名詞子句（當 sure 的受詞），未來的事照常用 will。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 556, "question": "Mom will be happy whether we ______ the game or not.", "options": ["win", "will win", "won", "winning"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "whether…or not 副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 557, "question": "Hank: When will you come again? Soon?\nLucy: Perhaps not, but if I ______, I'll call you. You have my word.", "options": ["am", "did", "do", "will"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜講義錯題｜if 條件句用現在式代替未來式＋do 代替動詞", "explanation": "【句型】if/when 引導的副詞子句，用現在式代替未來式；助動詞 do 可代替前面的一般動詞\n【分析】if I do = if I come（again）；主要子句 I'll call you 是未來，if 子句用現在式 → do。\n【其他選項】(A) am 是 be 動詞，不能代替一般動詞 come；(B) did 是過去式，時間不合；(D) if 條件子句不用 will。\n【例句】I'm not sure if I'll win, but if I do, I'll buy you dinner.\n備註：講義 p.335", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 558, "question": "I don't think Joe will join us tonight, but if he ______, we'll need one more chair.", "options": ["will", "does", "is", "did"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "if 子句現在式代替未來式，does 代替 joins。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 559, "question": "When you ______ to Taichung next week, please visit my uncle.", "options": ["will go", "went", "go", "going"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "when 副詞子句用現在式代替未來式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 560, "question": "Lisa may not be free tomorrow, but if she ______, she'll help us clean the classroom.", "options": ["is", "does", "will be", "was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "代替 be free，if 子句用現在式 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 561, "question": "He said we ______ up at the school gate after school. I waited for half an hour, but he never showed up.", "options": ["met", "have met", "will meet", "would meet"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜講義錯題｜間接引述的過去未來式 would + VR", "explanation": "【句型】主要子句為過去式（said/told/thought）時，名詞子句中的「未來」用 would + 原形動詞\n【分析】said 是過去，說的時候見面還沒發生（after school），而後來他沒出現 → would meet。\n【其他選項】(A) met 表示已經見面，與 he never showed up 矛盾；(B) have met 同樣表已見面；(C) will 沒有隨 said 改為過去。\n【例句】Mom said she would buy me a new bike.\n備註：講義 p.337", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 562, "question": "Peter told me he ______ me with my math, but he was too busy.", "options": ["helps", "would help", "will help", "has helped"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "told 為過去，子句中的未來用 would help。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 563, "question": "The weatherman said it ______ rain today, so I brought my umbrella.", "options": ["would", "will be", "has", "is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "said 為過去，預報的未來用 would rain。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 564, "question": "I thought you ______ to the party, so I saved a seat for you.", "options": ["come", "have come", "would come", "will come"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "thought 為過去，子句用 would come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "副詞子句與名詞子句的時態"}, {"id": 565, "question": "The police haven't found the little girl who ______ at a supermarket. They'll keep doing all they can to find her.", "options": ["took away", "taken away", "has taken away", "was taken away"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜過去式被動 was taken away", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ was/were ＋ p.p.，過去式被動語態。\n【分析】先行詞 the little girl 是「被帶走」的人，且是在超市發生的過去事件，用過去式被動 was taken away。\n【其他選項】(A) took away 是主動，表示女孩帶走別人；(B) taken away 缺 be 動詞；(C) has taken away 是主動完成式，語意與結構都不對。\n【例句】The wallet was stolen on the bus yesterday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 566, "question": "The window ______ by the strong wind last night.", "options": ["broke", "was broken", "has broken", "breaking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "窗戶是被風打破，過去被動 was broken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 567, "question": "The man who ______ in the car accident is now in the hospital.", "options": ["hurt", "has hurt", "was hurt", "hurting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "人是受傷的一方，用被動 was hurt。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 568, "question": "This old temple ______ more than two hundred years ago.", "options": ["was built", "built", "has built", "was building"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "寺廟是被建造的，過去被動 was built。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 569, "question": "The housework in Mr. and Mrs. Wang's family ______ between them and their kids. Everyone's got their own job to do.", "options": ["is shared", "are shared", "shares", "share"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜被動語態 單數主詞 is p.p.", "explanation": "【句型】S（物）+ be + p.p. 被動語態；be 動詞依主詞單複數。\n【分析】家事是「被分擔」的 → 被動；主詞是 The housework（不可數，單數），in Mr. and Mrs. Wang's family 只是修飾語 → is shared。\n【其他選項】(B) are 誤把 Mr. and Mrs. Wang 當主詞；(C)(D) 主動語態，家事不會自己分擔。\n【例句】The cake was cut into eight pieces.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 570, "question": "English ______ in many countries around the world.", "options": ["speaks", "is spoken", "are spoken", "speaking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "英語是「被說」的，主詞單數用 is spoken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 571, "question": "The classroom ______ by the students every afternoon.", "options": ["cleans", "is cleaning", "is cleaned", "are cleaned"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "教室被學生打掃，主詞單數、現在習慣用 is cleaned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 572, "question": "The money in the boxes ______ to help poor children.", "options": ["is used", "are used", "uses", "use"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "主詞是不可數名詞 The money（in the boxes 為修飾語），被動用 is used。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 573, "question": "Many famous people visit this restaurant. Popular singers like A-mei and Jay Chou ______ here with their friends.", "options": ["to be often seen", "often seen", "are often seen", "and are often seen"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜被動語態 are often seen（頻率副詞位置）", "explanation": "【句型】S + be + (頻率副詞) + p.p. 被動語態。\n【分析】歌手們「常被看到」在這裡 → 被動；主詞 Popular singers 複數，且句子缺主要動詞 → are often seen。\n【其他選項】(A) 不定詞不能當主要動詞；(B) 少了 be 動詞；(D) 多了連接詞 and，前面沒有可並列的動詞。\n【例句】This song is often heard on the radio.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 574, "question": "Chinese New Year is a big holiday in Taiwan. Red envelopes ______ to children at this time.", "options": ["give", "giving", "are given", "to be given"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "紅包是「被給」的，主詞複數，用 are given 當主要動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 575, "question": "The park is very clean. Trash ______ on the ground.", "options": ["is seldom found", "seldom finds", "to be seldom found", "seldom found"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "垃圾「很少被發現」→ 被動 is seldom found，頻率副詞放 be 動詞後。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 576, "question": "Many famous paintings ______ in this museum.", "options": ["show", "are shown", "showing", "and are shown"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "畫作被展示 → 被動 are shown，句中需主要動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 577, "question": "Susan: Oh, no! The door and the window ______!\nVictor: Who could have done this?\nSusan: Go in quickly and see if we've lost anything.", "options": ["are breaking", "have broken", "were broken", "will break"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜過去式被動 were broken", "explanation": "【句型】S（物）+ was/were + p.p. 過去式被動。\n【分析】Who could have done this?「是誰做的？」表示門窗是「被人破壞」的，且已經發生；主詞 The door and the window 複數 → were broken。\n【其他選項】(A) 進行式表示正在自己破掉，與「誰做的」不合；(B) 主動語態，門窗自己弄破了某物，語意不通；(D) 未來式不合已發生的情況。\n【例句】The cups were broken by the cat last night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 578, "question": "The window ______ by a baseball yesterday.", "options": ["broke", "was broken", "has broken", "is breaking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "by a baseball 與 yesterday 顯示過去式被動 was broken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 579, "question": "My bike ______ last night. I had to walk to school today.", "options": ["stole", "has stolen", "was stolen", "is stealing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "腳踏車是「被偷」的，昨晚發生 → was stolen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 580, "question": "Lucy: Where's the cake?\nMax: Sorry, it ______ by my little brother an hour ago.", "options": ["was eaten", "ate", "has eaten", "eats"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "蛋糕被吃掉，an hour ago 用過去式被動 was eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 581, "question": "My dog Jimmy loves ______ with a comb. Every time I comb his hair, he will close his eyes and fall asleep.", "options": ["to brush", "brushing", "to be brushing", "being brushed"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜動名詞被動 being p.p.（love + being p.p.）", "explanation": "【句型】love + Ving / to V；被動時為 love + being p.p. / to be p.p.。\n【分析】狗是「被梳毛」的一方（Every time I comb his hair），要用被動 → being brushed。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 主動，表示狗去梳別的東西；(C) to be brushing 是進行式，仍為主動語意。\n【例句】Most kids don't like being told what to do.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 582, "question": "Babies like ______ by their parents.", "options": ["holding", "to hold", "being held", "held"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "嬰兒是「被抱」的，like 後接動名詞被動 being held。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 583, "question": "Nobody enjoys ______ at in public.", "options": ["laughing", "being laughed", "to laugh", "laughed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "enjoy 後接 Ving，「被嘲笑」用被動 being laughed at。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 584, "question": "My little sister hates ______ to bed early on weekends.", "options": ["being sent", "sending", "to send", "sent"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "妹妹是「被送去睡覺」的，用 being sent。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 585, "question": "A new road is going to ______ in town because traffic is getting busier and busier.", "options": ["build", "building", "be built", "have built"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜be going to + be p.p.", "explanation": "【句型】S（物）+ be going to + be + p.p. 未來式被動。\n【分析】新的道路是「被建造」的 → 被動；is going to 後接原形 be → be built。\n【其他選項】(A) build 主動，路不會自己蓋；(B) going to 的 to 是不定詞，後不接 Ving；(D) have built 為主動完成式。\n【例句】A new library is going to be opened next year.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 586, "question": "The science report must ______ by Friday.", "options": ["finish", "be finished", "finishing", "have finished"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "報告「被完成」，助動詞 must 後接 be + p.p.。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 587, "question": "A big concert is going to ______ in the park next Saturday.", "options": ["be held", "hold", "holding", "held"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "音樂會「被舉辦」，be going to + be held。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 588, "question": "Your room should ______ every week.", "options": ["clean", "cleaning", "to clean", "be cleaned"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "房間「被打掃」，should + be + p.p.。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 589, "question": "Most of Jeff's best books ______ when he was sick and poor.", "options": ["have written", "were written", "would write", "wrote"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜過去式被動 were written", "explanation": "【句型】S（物）+ was/were + p.p. 過去式被動。\n【分析】書是「被寫」出來的 → 被動；when he was sick and poor 為過去時間；主詞 Most of Jeff's best books 複數 → were written。\n【其他選項】(A) 主動完成式，且與過去時間 when he was... 不合；(C)(D) 主動語態，書不會自己寫。\n【例句】This song was written by a high school student.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 590, "question": "This bridge ______ about fifty years ago.", "options": ["built", "has built", "was built", "is built"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "橋「被建造」於五十年前 → was built。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 591, "question": "The new rules ______ to all students yesterday.", "options": ["were explained", "explained", "have explained", "are explaining"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "規則「被解釋」，yesterday 用過去式被動 were explained。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 592, "question": "Most of the old photos ______ by Grandpa when he was young.", "options": ["took", "were taken", "have taken", "would take"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "照片「被拍」，by Grandpa、when he was young → were taken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 593, "question": "These pictures ______ when we took a trip to Kenting National Park.", "options": ["took", "will take", "were taken", "will be taken"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜過去式被動 were taken", "explanation": "【句型】S（物）+ was/were + p.p. 過去式被動。\n【分析】照片是「被拍」的 → 被動；when we took a trip 為過去 → were taken。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 主動語態，照片不會自己拍；(D) 未來式被動，與 took 過去時間不合。\n【例句】These cookies were made by my mom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 594, "question": "These cookies ______ by my sister last night.", "options": ["baked", "were baked", "will bake", "are baking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "餅乾「被烤」，last night → were baked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 595, "question": "The letter ______ to the wrong address last week, so it never arrived.", "options": ["sent", "will send", "is sent", "was sent"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "信「被寄」到錯的地址，last week → was sent。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 596, "question": "The new library ______ next year by the mayor.", "options": ["will be opened", "opened", "was opened", "will open"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "by the mayor 表被動，next year 用未來式被動 will be opened。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 597, "question": "\"Are you dating anyone special now?\" is a question that popular movie stars ______ in an interview.", "options": ["to be often asked", "are often asked", "being often asked", "who are often asked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜被動語態 ask 雙受詞（be asked + 事物）", "explanation": "【句型】ask + 人 + 問題 → 人 + be asked + 問題（被動）。\n【分析】a question (that) popular movie stars are often asked，明星是「被問」問題的人 → 被動；that 子句需要完整動詞 → are often asked。\n【其他選項】(A)(C) 不定詞、動名詞不能當子句的動詞；(D) who 多餘，that 子句中已有主詞 stars。\n【例句】This is a question students are often asked in job interviews.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 598, "question": "The students ______ to bring their own cups to school from next week.", "options": ["ask", "asking", "are asked", "to be asked"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "學生「被要求」帶杯子 → are asked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 599, "question": "Last year, Mr. Chen ______ a prize by the school for his excellent teaching.", "options": ["was given", "gave", "giving", "has given"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "by the school 表被動，Mr. Chen「被頒給」獎 → was given + 獎項。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 600, "question": "This is the gift that every winner ______ by the school after the race.", "options": ["gives", "giving", "who is given", "is given"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "that 子句需動詞，得獎者「被給予」禮物 → is given。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 601, "question": "Alison doesn't like ______ what to do. She only does things she wants to do.", "options": ["told", "to tell", "be told", "to be told"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "主動與被動語態｜會考歷屆｜like + to be p.p.（被動不定詞）", "explanation": "【句型】like + to V；若主詞是「被」做某事，則用被動不定詞 to be + p.p.。\n【分析】like 後接 to V；Alison 是「被別人告訴」該做什麼，後句 She only does things she wants to do 也說明她不喜歡被指使，所以用被動 to be told。\n【其他選項】(A) told：like 後不直接接過去分詞；(B) to tell 是主動「告訴別人」，語意不對；(C) be told 少了 to。\n【例句】Little kids don't like to be left alone at home.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 602, "question": "Nobody likes ______ at in front of the whole class.", "options": ["laughing", "to laugh", "to be laughed", "be laughed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "主詞是「被嘲笑」，like 後用被動不定詞 to be laughed (at)。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 603, "question": "Peter hopes ______ to Mary's birthday party this Saturday.", "options": ["to be invited", "to invite", "inviting", "be invited"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "Peter 是「被邀請」，hope 後接 to be invited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 604, "question": "This old bridge needs ______ before the typhoon comes.", "options": ["repair", "to be repaired", "to repair", "be repaired"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "主動與被動語態｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "橋是「被修理」，need 後接被動不定詞 to be repaired。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "主動與被動語態"}, {"id": 605, "question": "Jo won't be happy if you're late for his party tonight, so ______ sure that you arrive on time.", "options": ["make", "makes", "to make", "is making"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜祈使句 Make sure…", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句以原形動詞開頭（省略主詞 you）：Make sure (that) + 子句 = 務必、確定…\n【分析】so 後面接一個完整的句子，但空格前沒有主詞，表示這是對聽話者下指令的祈使句，所以用原形動詞 make，Make sure that you arrive on time.「務必準時到」。\n【其他選項】(B) makes 需要第三人稱單數主詞；(C) to make 是不定詞，不能當句子的主要動詞；(D) is making 缺主詞，且語意不是「正在」。\n【例句】It's raining hard, so make sure you bring an umbrella.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 606, "question": "The test starts at eight, so ______ sure you get to school before then.", "options": ["makes", "make", "making", "to make"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "so 後接祈使句，原形動詞開頭 make sure。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 607, "question": "The museum is closed on Mondays, so ______ to check the date before you go.", "options": ["remembering", "remembered", "to remember", "remember"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "so 後無主詞，為祈使句，用原形動詞 remember。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 608, "question": "Mom: The soup is very hot, Tina. ______ careful!", "options": ["Be", "Being", "Is", "To be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "祈使句以原形動詞開頭，be 動詞原形為 Be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 609, "question": "Cindy enjoys ______ her dad read stories to her before bed.", "options": ["to listen to", "listening to", "listen to", "listens to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜enjoy + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】enjoy + Ving（動名詞）＝喜歡做某事；enjoy 後面不可接 to V。\n【分析】動詞 enjoys 後面要接動名詞，所以用 listening to；listen to + 人 + 原形動詞（read）表示「聽某人唸…」。\n【其他選項】(A) to listen to：enjoy 不接不定詞；(C) listen to：原形動詞不能直接接在 enjoys 後；(D) listens to：一個子句不能有兩個主要動詞。\n【例句】My grandpa enjoys taking a walk in the park every morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 610, "question": "Ben enjoys ______ basketball with his classmates after school.", "options": ["play", "playing", "to play", "plays"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "enjoy 後接 Ving，用 playing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 611, "question": "My sister has finished ______ her room, so she can watch TV now.", "options": ["cleaning", "to clean", "clean", "cleaned"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "finish 後接 Ving，用 cleaning。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 612, "question": "Would you mind ______ the window? It's really cold in here.", "options": ["to close", "close", "closed", "closing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "mind 後接 Ving，用 closing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 613, "question": "If you're interested in our business plan, ______ this number and ask for Ms. Lee. She'll answer your questions.", "options": ["calling", "call", "and call", "to call"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜If 子句 + 祈使句", "explanation": "【句型】If + 子句, + 祈使句（原形動詞開頭）。\n【分析】逗號前是 If 副詞子句，主要子句沒有主詞，是叫對方「打這支電話」的祈使句，所以用原形動詞 call，並與後面的 and ask 對稱。\n【其他選項】(A) calling 不能當主要子句的動詞；(C) and call：If 子句與主要子句之間不需要 and；(D) to call 是不定詞，不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】If you feel sick, go to the school nurse.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 614, "question": "If you have any questions about the homework, ______ me an e-mail.", "options": ["sending", "to send", "send", "sent"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "If 子句後的主要子句為祈使句，用原形動詞 send。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 615, "question": "If you want to get a better grade, ______ more time on your studies.", "options": ["spend", "spending", "spends", "and spend"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "主要子句無主詞，是祈使句，用原形 spend。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 616, "question": "When you see the post office, ______ left and you'll find the bookstore.", "options": ["turning", "to turn", "turned", "turn"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "When 子句後接祈使句，用原形動詞 turn。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 617, "question": "Wendy: Do you know where the library is?\nSimon: Just ______ going for two more blocks and you'll see it.", "options": ["keep", "to keep", "keeping", "keeps"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜keep + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句 + and + 未來式：原形動詞開頭…, and you will…；keep + Ving＝持續做…。\n【分析】Simon 在指路，「再繼續走兩個街區你就會看到」，Just 後為祈使句，要用原形動詞 keep，再接 going。\n【其他選項】(B) to keep、(C) keeping 都不能當祈使句的開頭動詞；(D) keeps 需要第三人稱單數主詞。\n【例句】Keep walking and you'll find the bus stop on your right.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 618, "question": "Coach: Don't stop! Just ______ running and you'll finish the race.", "options": ["keeping", "keep", "kept", "to keep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "祈使句用原形動詞 keep，後接 running。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 619, "question": "______ hard and you will pass the test.", "options": ["Studying", "To study", "Study", "Studies"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 + and + will，句首用原形動詞 Study。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 620, "question": "The baby kept ______ all night, so his parents didn't sleep well.", "options": ["cry", "to cry", "cried", "crying"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "keep + Ving 表示持續，用 crying。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 621, "question": "Josh has planned to make a trip to New York and ______ some of his friends there.", "options": ["visit", "visits", "visiting", "visited"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜對等連接詞 and 連接兩個不定詞（to make…and (to) visit）", "explanation": "【句型】plan to V1 and (to) V2：and 連接對等的不定詞，第二個 to 可省略，保留原形動詞。\n【分析】and 前面是 to make a trip，後面要與它對等，to 省略後用原形動詞 visit：plan to make a trip and (to) visit friends。\n【其他選項】(B) visits、(D) visited 是有時態變化的動詞，與 to make 不對等；(C) visiting 是動名詞，也不對等。\n【例句】I want to go to the night market and buy some snacks.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 622, "question": "Amy decided to stay home and ______ a cake for her mom.", "options": ["making", "make", "made", "makes"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "decide to stay and (to) make，and 後用原形動詞 make。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 623, "question": "We hope to finish the project early and ______ a short break.", "options": ["took", "taking", "take", "takes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "hope to finish and (to) take，對等用原形 take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 624, "question": "Leo enjoys reading novels and ______ to music in his free time.", "options": ["listening", "listen", "listens", "to listen"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "enjoy reading and listening，and 前後都是 Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 625, "question": "Judy: The ball game will be on TV tomorrow at six in the morning.\nLucy: ______ up early and you won't miss it.", "options": ["Get", "To get", "Getting", "Gets"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜祈使句 + and + 未來式", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句（原形動詞）+ and + S + will…＝如果…就會…。\n【分析】Lucy 建議 Judy「早點起床，你就不會錯過」，句首沒有主詞，是祈使句，用原形動詞 Get。\n【其他選項】(B) To get 表目的，後面不能接 and you won't…；(C) Getting 當主詞時後面要接動詞；(D) Gets 缺主詞。\n【例句】Practice every day and you'll play the piano better.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 626, "question": "______ this medicine and you will feel better soon.", "options": ["Taking", "Take", "Takes", "Taken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 + and + will，用原形 Take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 627, "question": "______ the bus, or you will be late for school.", "options": ["Hurrying for", "To hurry for", "Hurries for", "Hurry for"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 + or，用原形動詞 Hurry。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 628, "question": "Ken: I want to be a good singer.\nTeacher: ______ singing every day and you'll get better.", "options": ["Practice", "Practicing", "To practice", "Practiced"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "祈使句用原形動詞 Practice。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 629, "question": "A-ming: Dad, can I go dancing tomorrow?\nMr. Wu: ______ your homework and we'll talk about it.", "options": ["Finishes", "Finishing", "To finish", "Finish"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜祈使句 + and + 未來式", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句（原形動詞開頭）+ and + S + will…＝先…，就…。\n【分析】爸爸叫 A-ming「先把功課寫完，我們再談」，句首沒有主詞，是祈使句，用原形動詞 Finish。\n【其他選項】(A) Finishes 缺主詞；(B) Finishing 當主詞時須接動詞，不能接 and we'll；(C) To finish 表目的，句子不完整。\n【例句】Clean your room and you can play video games.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 630, "question": "Mom: ______ your vegetables and you can have some ice cream.", "options": ["Eat", "Eating", "To eat", "Eats"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 + and，用原形動詞 Eat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 631, "question": "Sam: Can I borrow your bike?\nTom: Sure. ______ it back by Friday, OK?", "options": ["Bringing", "Brings", "Bring", "To bring"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "祈使句用原形動詞 Bring。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 632, "question": "______ off your shoes before you come into the house.", "options": ["Taking", "Takes", "To take", "Take"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "對別人下指令的祈使句，用原形 Take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 633, "question": "It was important for Kevin ______ his homework quickly because he had to help his parents sell fruit in the night market.", "options": ["finish", "to finish", "finishes", "finished"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜It is + adj. + for 人 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】It is/was + 形容詞 + for + 人 + to V：it 是虛主詞，真正主詞是後面的不定詞。\n【分析】句型 It was important for Kevin ___，空格要接不定詞 to finish，表示「對 Kevin 來說，快點寫完功課很重要」。\n【其他選項】(A) finish 少了 to；(C) finishes、(D) finished 是有時態的動詞，不能放在 for Kevin 後面。\n【例句】It is hard for me to wake up early on Monday mornings.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 634, "question": "It is not easy for little kids ______ still for a long time.", "options": ["sit", "sat", "to sit", "sitting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "It is + adj. + for 人 + to V，用 to sit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 635, "question": "It was exciting for us ______ the famous singer at the airport.", "options": ["to see", "see", "saw", "sees"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "虛主詞 it 句型，用不定詞 to see。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 636, "question": "It is necessary for everyone ______ a helmet when riding a scooter.", "options": ["wear", "wears", "wore", "to wear"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "It is necessary for 人 to V，用 to wear。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 637, "question": "It's cold outside; ______ sure to put on your coat before you leave the house.", "options": ["be", "it is", "being", "it will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜祈使句 Be sure to V", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句以原形動詞開頭；Be sure to V＝務必要…。\n【分析】分號後是提醒對方「出門前一定要穿外套」的祈使句，be 動詞原形 be，Be sure to put on your coat。\n【其他選項】(B) it is、(D) it will be：主詞 it 不能 sure to 穿外套，語意錯；(C) being 不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】Be sure to lock the door when you go out.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 638, "question": "The exam is very important, so ______ sure to get enough sleep tonight.", "options": ["being", "be", "is", "to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 Be sure to V，用原形 be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 639, "question": "______ quiet in the library, please. People are studying.", "options": ["Being", "Is", "To be", "Be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "祈使句用 be 動詞原形 Be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 640, "question": "It may rain this afternoon; ______ to take an umbrella with you.", "options": ["remember", "remembering", "to remember", "it remembers"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "分號後為祈使句，用原形 remember。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 641, "question": "The most convenient way to get around this small town is ______ a bike.", "options": ["to ride", "to have ridden", "rides", "rode"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜to V 當主詞補語（The way to V is to V）", "explanation": "【句型】S + be + to V：不定詞放在 be 動詞後當主詞補語，說明主詞的內容。\n【分析】主詞是 The most convenient way（最方便的方式），is 後要說明「方式是什麼」，用不定詞 to ride a bike「騎腳踏車」。\n【其他選項】(B) to have ridden 是完成式不定詞，表示「已經騎過」，與一般事實不合；(C) rides、(D) rode 是有時態的動詞，不能接在 is 之後。\n【例句】My dream is to travel around the world.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 642, "question": "The best way to learn English is ______ it every day.", "options": ["used", "to use", "uses", "to have used"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "be 後接 to V 當補語，用 to use。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 643, "question": "Ann's plan for this summer is ______ how to swim.", "options": ["learns", "learned", "to have learned", "to learn"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "plan is to V，說明計畫的內容，用 to learn。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 644, "question": "The only thing we can do now is ______ for the rain to stop.", "options": ["to wait", "waits", "waited", "to have waited"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "be 後接不定詞補語，用 to wait。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 645, "question": "Dad always tells me not ______ only for tests. If that's all I'm doing, he says, I will soon lose interest in learning.", "options": ["study", "studying", "studied", "to study"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜會考歷屆｜tell + 人 + not to V", "explanation": "【句型】tell + 人 + (not) to V＝告訴某人（不要）做某事；否定 not 放在 to 前面。\n【分析】tells me not ___ 是 tell sb not to V 的句型，所以用 to study：爸爸叫我不要只為了考試念書。\n【其他選項】(A) study 少了 to；(B) studying、(C) studied 都不符合 tell sb (not) to V 的句型。\n【例句】The doctor told my mom not to eat too much salt.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 646, "question": "Our teacher asked us not ______ in the hallway.", "options": ["running", "to run", "run", "ran"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "ask 人 not to V，用 to run。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 647, "question": "Mom told me ______ my little brother with his homework.", "options": ["to help", "help", "helping", "helped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "tell 人 to V，用 to help。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 648, "question": "The sign warns people not ______ the animals in the zoo.", "options": ["feed", "fed", "feeding", "to feed"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "warn 人 not to V，用 to feed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）"}, {"id": 649, "question": "Watching American movies ______ one of the activities we enjoy most in our English class.", "options": ["is", "are", "to be", "being"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞（Ving）片語當主詞，視為單數，後接單數動詞 is。\n【分析】主詞是 Watching American movies（看美國電影這件事），雖然有 movies，但真正的主詞是動名詞 Watching，所以用單數 is。\n【其他選項】(B) are：誤把 movies 當主詞；(C) to be、(D) being 都不能當句子的主要動詞。\n【例句】Riding a bike to school is good exercise.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 650, "question": "Collecting stamps ______ my father's favorite hobby.", "options": ["are", "being", "is", "to be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "動名詞片語當主詞視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 651, "question": "Eating too many snacks ______ bad for your teeth.", "options": ["is", "are", "have", "being"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "主詞是 Eating（單數），用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 652, "question": "Taking care of three little kids ______ a lot of work for Mrs. Lin.", "options": ["are", "make", "to be", "means"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞視為單數，動詞用第三人稱單數 means。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 653, "question": "Playing games on the cellphone ______ popular with high school students.", "options": ["is", "are", "being", "to be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞（Ving）片語當主詞，視為單數，用單數動詞。\n【分析】主詞是 Playing games on the cellphone（玩手機遊戲這件事），是動名詞片語，視為單數，用 is；不要被 games 誤導。\n【其他選項】(B) are：把 games 誤當主詞；(C) being、(D) to be 不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】Chatting with friends online is popular among teenagers.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 654, "question": "Sending messages on LINE ______ the easiest way to reach my parents.", "options": ["are", "is", "being", "to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "動名詞片語當主詞視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 655, "question": "Making new friends ______ not always easy for shy students.", "options": ["are", "to be", "is", "being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "Making new friends 為單數主詞，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 656, "question": "Drinking sweet drinks every day ______ people gain weight easily.", "options": ["makes", "make", "making", "to make"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞為單數，用 makes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 657, "question": "Playing sports at least three times a week ______ good for your health.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞視為單數；be good for…＝對…有益。\n【分析】主詞是 Playing sports…（做運動這件事），視為單數；後面是形容詞 good，要用 be 動詞，所以用 is。\n【其他選項】(B) are 是複數，誤把 sports 當主詞；(C) has、(D) have 後面不能直接接形容詞 good。\n【例句】Going to bed early is good for growing kids.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 658, "question": "Eating breakfast every morning ______ important for students.", "options": ["are", "has", "is", "have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，後接形容詞用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 659, "question": "Using your cellphone in bed ______ bad for your eyes.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "主詞為動名詞片語，視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 660, "question": "Swimming in this river ______ dangerous, so please don't do it.", "options": ["have", "are", "has", "is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "Swimming 為單數主詞，後接形容詞用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 661, "question": "Learning foreign languages ______ me to know more about other countries.", "options": ["helps", "helping", "help", "to help"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 第三人稱單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞，視為單數，現在式動詞加 -s；help + 人 + (to) V。\n【分析】主詞是 Learning foreign languages（學外語這件事），視為第三人稱單數，句子缺主要動詞，所以用 helps。\n【其他選項】(B) helping、(D) to help 不能當主要動詞；(C) help 是複數形，誤把 languages 當主詞。\n【例句】Reading English newspapers helps me learn new words.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 662, "question": "Traveling to different countries ______ people open their minds.", "options": ["help", "helps", "helping", "to help"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 helps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 663, "question": "Doing yoga every night ______ my mom sleep better.", "options": ["make", "making", "to make", "makes"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "Doing yoga 為單數主詞，用 makes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 664, "question": "Listening to English songs ______ me a lot of fun.", "options": ["gives", "give", "giving", "to give"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，現在式用 gives。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 665, "question": "Asking questions ______ Henna learn more and better.", "options": ["help", "helps", "helping", "to help"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 第三人稱單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞視為單數；help + 人 + (to) V。\n【分析】主詞是 Asking questions（問問題這件事），視為第三人稱單數，句子需要主要動詞，所以用 helps。\n【其他選項】(A) help：誤把 questions 當複數主詞；(C) helping、(D) to help 不能當主要動詞。\n【例句】Taking notes in class helps Andy remember the lessons.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 666, "question": "Writing a diary every day ______ Joy improve her English.", "options": ["help", "helping", "helps", "to help"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 helps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 667, "question": "Drawing pictures ______ the little boy happy.", "options": ["makes", "make", "making", "to make"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "Drawing pictures 為單數主詞，用 makes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 668, "question": "Taking a hot bath after work ______ my father relax.", "options": ["help", "to help", "helping", "helps"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 helps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 669, "question": "I usually carry a camera on my trips; taking pictures ______ a good way for me to remember the experience.", "options": ["to be", "is", "being", "are"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞，視為單數，用 is。\n【分析】分號後是新的句子，主詞是 taking pictures（拍照這件事），視為單數，用 is；不要被 pictures 誤導成 are。\n【其他選項】(A) to be、(C) being 不能當主要動詞；(D) are 誤把 pictures 當主詞。\n【例句】Keeping a diary is a good way to remember your school life.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 670, "question": "Walking the dogs ______ my brother's job every evening.", "options": ["are", "is", "being", "to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 671, "question": "I like art; visiting museums ______ one of my favorite things to do.", "options": ["is", "are", "to be", "being"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "visiting museums 為單數主詞，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 672, "question": "Watering the plants ______ the first thing Grandpa does every morning.", "options": ["are", "being", "were", "is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數、現在式，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 673, "question": "Reading comic books ______ fun.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數 be 動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞視為單數；fun 在此當形容詞/名詞補語，前面用 be 動詞。\n【分析】主詞是 Reading comic books（看漫畫這件事），視為單數，後面接 fun 作補語，用 is。\n【其他選項】(B) are：誤把 books 當主詞；(C) has、(D) have：fun 前要用 be 動詞，不用 have。\n【例句】Cooking with my mom is fun.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 674, "question": "Flying kites on the beach ______ a lot of fun.", "options": ["are", "has", "is", "have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，接補語用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 675, "question": "Building sandcastles ______ fun for the kids.", "options": ["is", "are", "have", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "Building sandcastles 視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 676, "question": "Telling jokes to my classmates ______ always fun.", "options": ["are", "has", "have", "is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 677, "question": "Playing in the water ______ lots of fun on a hot summer day.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜動名詞當主詞 + 單數 be 動詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞片語當主詞視為單數；S + be + (lots of) fun。\n【分析】主詞是 Playing in the water（玩水這件事），單數；lots of fun 是補語，前面用 be 動詞 is。\n【其他選項】(B) are 用於複數主詞；(C) has、(D) have 不能表示「是很好玩的」。\n【例句】Camping in the mountains is lots of fun.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 678, "question": "Riding a bike along the river ______ a lot of fun.", "options": ["have", "is", "has", "are"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 679, "question": "Making dumplings with my family ______ great fun during Chinese New Year.", "options": ["are", "have", "is", "has"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "動名詞主詞單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 680, "question": "Shopping with friends ______ more fun than shopping alone.", "options": ["is", "are", "has", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "Shopping 視為單數，用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 681, "question": "______ a map with you when you go to a place for the first time.", "options": ["Have taken", "Take", "Taking", "To take"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜祈使句句首用原形動詞", "explanation": "【句型】祈使句：句首用原形動詞，省略主詞 you，表示命令或建議。\n【分析】整句沒有主詞也沒有其他主要動詞，是給人的建議「第一次去一個地方時要帶地圖」，所以用原形動詞 Take。\n【其他選項】(A) Have taken 是完成式，缺主詞；(C) Taking 當主詞時後面要有動詞；(D) To take 表目的，後面缺主要子句。\n【例句】Wear a hat when you go out on a sunny day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 682, "question": "______ your hands before you eat.", "options": ["Washing", "To wash", "Wash", "Washed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "祈使句句首用原形動詞 Wash。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 683, "question": "______ some water with you when you go hiking.", "options": ["Bring", "Bringing", "Brought", "To bring"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "給建議的祈使句用原形 Bring。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 684, "question": "______ the light when you leave the classroom.", "options": ["Turning off", "To turn off", "Turned off", "Turn off"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "祈使句用原形 Turn off。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 685, "question": "______ in the daytime is not good for you. You may not sleep well at night and feel tired the next day.", "options": ["Slept", "Sleeps", "Have slept", "Sleeping"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜Ving 當主詞", "explanation": "【句型】句首 Ving（動名詞）當主詞 + 單數動詞。\n【分析】句子已有主要動詞 is，空格需要一個主詞，「白天睡覺」這件事用動名詞 Sleeping 當主詞。\n【其他選項】(A) Slept、(B) Sleeps、(C) Have slept 都是動詞的變化形，不能當主詞，且會讓句子有兩個動詞。\n【例句】Swimming in the sea is exciting.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 686, "question": "______ too much fast food is bad for your health.", "options": ["Eat", "Eats", "Eating", "Ate"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "句子已有動詞 is，句首用 Ving 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 687, "question": "______ to music makes me relaxed.", "options": ["Listening", "Listen", "Listened", "Listens"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "makes 為主要動詞，句首用動名詞 Listening。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 688, "question": "______ on the phone while driving is very dangerous.", "options": ["Talks", "Talking", "Talk", "Talked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "句首動名詞 Talking 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 689, "question": "______ the lesson before class gives me a better idea about what the teacher is going to teach.", "options": ["Preview", "Previews", "Previewed", "Previewing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜Ving 當主詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】句首 Ving（動名詞）片語當主詞，後接單數動詞。\n【分析】句子的主要動詞是 gives，空格需要主詞，用動名詞 Previewing（預習）：Previewing the lesson before class gives me…。\n【其他選項】(A) Preview 原形放句首是祈使句，但句子已有 gives；(B) Previews、(C) Previewed 是動詞，不能當主詞。\n【例句】Reviewing your notes after class helps you remember more.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 690, "question": "______ a cup of hot milk before bed makes Jenny sleepy.", "options": ["Drinks", "Drinking", "Drink", "Drank"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "makes 為主要動詞，句首用 Drinking 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 691, "question": "______ English songs helps Kevin practice his listening.", "options": ["Singing", "Sing", "Sang", "Sings"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "helps 為主要動詞，句首用動名詞 Singing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 692, "question": "______ with classmates gives me new ideas for the project.", "options": ["Talk", "Talks", "Talked", "Talking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "句首動名詞 Talking 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 693, "question": "John always goes to bed late at night, so ______ early is difficult for him.", "options": ["get up", "got up", "gets up", "getting up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜會考歷屆｜Ving 當子句主詞", "explanation": "【句型】動名詞（Ving）片語當主詞 + 單數動詞。\n【分析】so 後是新的子句，主要動詞是 is，空格需要主詞，用動名詞 getting up early「早起這件事」。\n【其他選項】(A) get up、(B) got up、(C) gets up 都是動詞形式，不能當主詞，子句會有兩個動詞。\n【例句】Waking up at six is not easy for me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 694, "question": "Mia is afraid of water, so ______ in the sea is scary for her.", "options": ["swimming", "swim", "swam", "swims"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "is 為主要動詞，空格用動名詞 swimming 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 695, "question": "Ted is very shy, so ______ in front of people is hard for him.", "options": ["speaks", "speaking", "speak", "spoke"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "子句主詞用動名詞 speaking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 696, "question": "My house is far from school, so ______ there takes me an hour.", "options": ["walk", "walked", "walking", "walks"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "takes 為主要動詞，主詞用 walking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "句首動詞的選擇（祈使句、Ving主詞、To V目的）"}, {"id": 697, "question": "The teacher ______ his students vacuum the floor of the classroom after the party.", "options": ["asked", "wanted", "found", "had"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜使役動詞 have + 人 + 原形動詞", "explanation": "【句型】使役動詞 have / make / let + 受詞 + 原形動詞（V）。\n【分析】受詞 his students 後面接原形動詞 vacuum，只有使役動詞 had 可以這樣用：老師叫學生派對後吸地板。\n【其他選項】(A) asked、(B) wanted 後面要接 to V（asked them to vacuum）；(C) found 後接 Ving 或形容詞（found them vacuuming）。\n【例句】My mom had me wash the dishes after dinner.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 698, "question": "Mr. Lin ______ his son clean the car last Sunday.", "options": ["told", "had", "wanted", "asked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "受詞後接原形 clean，用使役動詞 had。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 699, "question": "The coach ______ the players run around the field ten times.", "options": ["made", "asked", "wanted", "told"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "受詞後接原形 run，用使役動詞 made。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 700, "question": "Ms. Wang ______ us to bring our dictionaries tomorrow.", "options": ["let", "had", "made", "asked"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "受詞後接 to V，用 asked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 701, "question": "The teachers make us ______ harder by giving us tests.", "options": ["study", "studied", "to study", "studying"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜使役動詞 make + 人 + 原形動詞", "explanation": "【句型】make（使役動詞）+ 受詞 + 原形動詞＝讓/迫使某人做某事。\n【分析】make us 後面接原形動詞，所以用 study：老師用考試讓我們更用功念書。\n【其他選項】(B) studied 是過去式；(C) to study：主動的 make 後不接 to；(D) studying 不接在 make + 受詞後。\n【例句】The sad movie made my sister cry.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 702, "question": "The funny clown made all the children ______.", "options": ["laughing", "to laugh", "laugh", "laughed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "make + 受詞 + 原形動詞 laugh。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 703, "question": "My parents let me ______ out with my friends on Saturday nights.", "options": ["go", "going", "to go", "went"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "let + 受詞 + 原形動詞 go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 704, "question": "Mom had the repairman ______ the washing machine yesterday.", "options": ["fixing", "fix", "to fix", "fixes"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "have + 人 + 原形動詞 fix。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 705, "question": "Deborah put some sugar and cream in her coffee to make it ______ better.", "options": ["taste", "tasted", "tasting", "to taste"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜使役動詞 make + 物 + 原形動詞（連綴動詞 taste）", "explanation": "【句型】make + 受詞 + 原形動詞；taste + 形容詞/副詞比較級（better）＝嚐起來…。\n【分析】make it ___ 中 make 是使役動詞，後接原形動詞 taste：加糖和奶精讓咖啡「嚐起來」更好喝。\n【其他選項】(B) tasted：make 後不接過去式（咖啡不是「被嚐」）；(C) tasting、(D) to taste 都不能接在主動的 make + 受詞之後。\n【例句】Adding some lemon makes the fish taste fresher.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 706, "question": "This new haircut makes Ray ______ younger.", "options": ["looking", "look", "to look", "looks"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "make + 受詞 + 原形動詞 look。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 707, "question": "Opening the windows will make the room ______ less hot.", "options": ["feel", "felt", "feeling", "to feel"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "make + 受詞 + 原形動詞 feel。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 708, "question": "Some salt will make the soup ______ much better.", "options": ["tastes", "to taste", "tasting", "taste"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "make + 受詞 + 原形動詞 taste。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 709, "question": "Mrs. Wilson ______ her son wash the dishes after dinner.", "options": ["had", "told", "wanted", "invited"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜使役動詞 have + O + 原形V", "explanation": "【句型】使役動詞 have / make / let + 受詞 + 原形動詞。\n【分析】空格後是 her son + wash（原形動詞），只有使役動詞 had 可接「受詞＋原形V」，意為「叫兒子晚餐後洗碗」。\n【其他選項】(B) told、(C) wanted、(D) invited 後面都要接 O + to V（told her son to wash…），不能接原形動詞。\n【例句】Mr. Lin had the students clean the classroom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 710, "question": "Ms. Chen ______ her students read the story aloud in class yesterday.", "options": ["asked", "had", "wanted", "told"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "空格後接 her students + read（原形），只有使役動詞 had 可接「受詞＋原形V」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 711, "question": "Dad ______ me take out the trash every night.", "options": ["makes", "asks", "tells", "wants"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "使役動詞 make + 受詞 + 原形V；asks / tells / wants 都要接 to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 712, "question": "The coach ______ the players run around the field ten times this morning.", "options": ["told", "wanted", "had", "asked"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "run 為原形動詞，只能搭配使役動詞 had（叫…做…）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 713, "question": "If I finish my homework before eight o'clock, my parents will let me ______ TV for one hour.", "options": ["watch", "watching", "to watch", "have watched"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜let + O + 原形V", "explanation": "【句型】let + 受詞 + 原形動詞（讓某人做某事）。\n【分析】let me 之後必須接原形動詞，故選 watch：「爸媽會讓我看一小時電視」。\n【其他選項】(B) watching 為 Ving；(C) to watch 為不定詞，let 後不加 to；(D) have watched 為完成式，不能放在受詞後。\n【例句】My mom let me go to the movies with Amy.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 714, "question": "Our teacher won't let us ______ our cell phones in class.", "options": ["using", "to use", "used", "use"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "let + 受詞 + 原形V，故選 use。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 715, "question": "Please let me ______ you with those heavy boxes.", "options": ["help", "to help", "helping", "helped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "let me 後接原形動詞 help。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 716, "question": "Kevin's father let him ______ the new bike in the park last Sunday.", "options": ["to ride", "riding", "ride", "rode"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "let 為使役動詞，受詞後接原形 ride，過去式由 let 表達。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 717, "question": "My mother ______ me send a letter yesterday.", "options": ["asked", "had", "told", "wanted"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜使役動詞 have + O + 原形V", "explanation": "【句型】have + 受詞 + 原形動詞（叫某人去做某事）。\n【分析】空格後為 me + send（原形動詞），只有使役動詞 had 符合：「媽媽昨天叫我去寄一封信」。\n【其他選項】(A) asked、(C) told、(D) wanted 須接 O + to V（asked me to send），不能直接接原形。\n【例句】I had my brother turn off the lights.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 718, "question": "Grandma ______ me buy some eggs at the store this morning.", "options": ["wanted", "told", "had", "asked"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "buy 為原形，只有使役動詞 had 可用。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 719, "question": "Mr. Wu ______ Tina to close the windows before she left.", "options": ["told", "had", "made", "let"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "空格後是 to close，只有 told 可接 O + to V；had / made / let 接原形V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 720, "question": "The manager ______ Leo fix the copy machine yesterday afternoon.", "options": ["wanted", "had", "asked", "hoped"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "fix 為原形動詞，只有使役動詞 had 可接「受詞＋原形V」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 721, "question": "Jenny plays the piano very well. Her mother makes her ______ two hours every day.", "options": ["practice", "practiced", "practicing", "to practice"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜會考歷屆｜make + O + 原形V", "explanation": "【句型】make + 受詞 + 原形動詞（強迫／使某人做某事）。\n【分析】makes her 之後要接原形動詞 practice：「媽媽每天要她練兩小時」。\n【其他選項】(B) practiced 為過去式；(C) practicing 為 Ving；(D) to practice 為不定詞，主動語態的 make 後不加 to。\n【例句】The sad movie made me cry.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 722, "question": "The funny video made all of us ______ out loud.", "options": ["to laugh", "laughing", "laughed", "laugh"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "make + 受詞 + 原形V，故選 laugh。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 723, "question": "Our English teacher makes us ______ ten new words every week.", "options": ["learn", "to learn", "learning", "learned"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "makes us 後接原形 learn。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 724, "question": "Don't make your little sister ______ alone at home.", "options": ["to stay", "stay", "staying", "stayed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "使役動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "使役動詞 make 後接受詞＋原形 stay。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "使役動詞"}, {"id": 725, "question": "People got very excited when they watched Ms. Smith ______ at the party.", "options": ["danced", "dancing", "has danced", "to dance"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 watch＋O＋Ving", "explanation": "【句型】感官動詞（see/watch/hear/feel）＋ O ＋ 原形V（看到全程）/ Ving（正在進行）。\n【分析】watched Ms. Smith ___ 是感官動詞句型，受詞後接 dancing 表「看她正在跳舞」。選項中沒有原形 dance，故選 dancing。\n【其他選項】(A) danced 過去式、(C) has danced 完成式都不能放在感官動詞的受詞後；(D) 主動句中感官動詞後不接 to V。\n【例句】I heard someone singing in the next room.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 726, "question": "I saw a cat ______ across the street just now.", "options": ["runs", "to run", "running", "ran"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "saw＋O＋Ving 表看到正在進行的動作。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 727, "question": "Did you hear the baby ______ last night?", "options": ["cry", "to cry", "cried", "cries"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "hear＋O＋原形V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 728, "question": "Ben felt the ground ______ during the earthquake.", "options": ["shook", "to shake", "has shaken", "shaking"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "feel＋O＋Ving 表感覺到正在發生的動作。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 729, "question": "My cat got excited when it saw the boy ______ the birds.", "options": ["catches", "catching", "to catch", "caught"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 see + O + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】感官動詞 see / watch / hear / feel + 受詞 + 原形V（全程）或 Ving（正在進行）。\n【分析】saw the boy 後接 Ving 表示看到男孩「正在抓」鳥，選 catching。\n【其他選項】(A) catches 為現在式動詞，句中已有動詞 saw；(C) to catch 感官動詞後不接 to V；(D) caught 為過去式／p.p.，男孩是主動抓，不用被動。\n【例句】I saw Ben playing basketball after school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 730, "question": "We heard someone ______ the guitar next door last night.", "options": ["to play", "plays", "playing", "played"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "hear + 受詞 + Ving 表示聽到某人正在做某事。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 731, "question": "Did you see the dog ______ across the street just now?", "options": ["running", "to run", "runs", "ran"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "感官動詞 see + 受詞 + Ving（或原形），選 running。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 732, "question": "Lucy watched her brother ______ a model plane in the living room.", "options": ["builds", "to build", "built", "building"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "watch + 受詞 + Ving 表示看到正在進行的動作。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 733, "question": "Bruce: When did Roger change his job?\nLaura: He hasn't changed his job. He still works in the same computer store.\nBruce: But I saw him ______ watches on the street corner.", "options": ["sold", "to sell", "have sold", "selling"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 see + O + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】see + 受詞 + Ving / 原形V（看到某人正在做某事）。\n【分析】saw him 之後接 Ving，表示「我看到他在街角賣手錶」，故選 selling。\n【其他選項】(A) sold 表被動或過去式，不合；(B) to sell 感官動詞後不接 to V；(C) have sold 完成式不能放在受詞後。\n【例句】I saw Mr. Huang waiting for the bus.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 734, "question": "Mia: Is Tom still sick?\nRay: I don't think so. I saw him ______ soccer on the field this morning.", "options": ["to play", "playing", "played", "has played"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "saw him + Ving，表示看到他正在踢足球。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 735, "question": "I noticed a man ______ pictures of our school gate.", "options": ["taking", "to take", "takes", "taken"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "notice 為感官動詞，受詞後接 Ving 表進行。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 736, "question": "We saw Grandpa ______ flowers in the garden when we got home.", "options": ["waters", "to water", "watering", "has watered"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "saw + 受詞 + Ving，表示看到他正在澆花。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 737, "question": "The little boy jumped up and down happily when he saw a bee ______ into the house.", "options": ["flown", "to fly", "flying", "has flown"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 see + O + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】see + 受詞 + Ving / 原形V。\n【分析】saw a bee 後接 Ving，表示看到蜜蜂「正飛進」屋子，選 flying。\n【其他選項】(A) flown 為過去分詞，表被動不合理；(B) to fly 感官動詞後不接 to V；(D) has flown 為完成式動詞，不能接在受詞後。\n【例句】She saw a bird flying over the lake.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 738, "question": "The kids shouted when they saw a big fish ______ out of the pond.", "options": ["to jump", "jumping", "jumped", "has jumped"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "saw + 受詞 + Ving，表示看到魚正在跳出池塘。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 739, "question": "I felt something ______ up my leg during the camping trip.", "options": ["climbed", "to climb", "has climbed", "climbing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "feel 為感官動詞，受詞後接 Ving 表示感覺到正在發生的動作。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 740, "question": "Amy heard the baby ______ in the next room.", "options": ["crying", "cried", "to cry", "cries"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "hear + 受詞 + Ving，表示聽到嬰兒正在哭。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 741, "question": "When I was walking along the river, I saw some fish ______ out of the water.", "options": ["jumped", "to jump", "jumping", "are jumping"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 see + O + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】see + 受詞 + Ving / 原形V。\n【分析】saw some fish 之後接 Ving，表示看到魚「正跳出」水面，選 jumping。\n【其他選項】(A) jumped 為過去式，句中已有動詞 saw；(B) to jump 感官動詞後不加 to；(D) are jumping 為完整動詞，不能接在受詞後。\n【例句】We saw some ducks swimming in the pond.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 742, "question": "While Joe was waiting for the bus, he saw two cats ______ on the road.", "options": ["fight", "to fight", "fought", "are fighting"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "see + 受詞 + 原形V 也可，表示看到整個動作；其他選項形式錯誤。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 743, "question": "Can you hear the birds ______ in the trees?", "options": ["sang", "singing", "to sing", "are singing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "hear + 受詞 + Ving，表示聽到正在唱歌。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 744, "question": "I watched the sun ______ behind the mountains from the window.", "options": ["to go down", "went down", "going down", "is going down"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "watch + 受詞 + Ving，表示看著太陽正在下山。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 745, "question": "Cindy cried out when she saw a motorcycle ______ into her cat.", "options": ["bump", "bumped", "to bump", "has bumped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜會考歷屆｜感官動詞 see + O + 原形V", "explanation": "【句型】see + 受詞 + 原形V（看到整個動作發生）／Ving（正在進行）。\n【分析】saw a motorcycle 後可接原形 bump，表示看到機車撞上她的貓的整個過程。\n【其他選項】(B) bumped 為過去式／p.p.，不可接在受詞後表主動；(C) to bump 感官動詞後不接 to V；(D) has bumped 為完成式動詞。\n【例句】I saw a boy fall off his bike.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 746, "question": "Everyone heard the teacher ______ the door loudly.", "options": ["to shut", "shut", "has shut", "shuts"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "hear + 受詞 + 原形V，表示聽到整個動作，shut 原形＝過去式同形，此處為原形用法。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 747, "question": "Henry saw the vase ______ off the table and break.", "options": ["to fall", "fell", "fall", "has fallen"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "see + 受詞 + 原形V，與後面原形 break 對等。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 748, "question": "Did you feel the ground ______ during the earthquake last night?", "options": ["shake", "to shake", "shook", "has shaken"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "感官動詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "feel + 受詞 + 原形V，表示感覺到地面搖晃。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "感官動詞"}, {"id": 749, "question": "There's a subway station near my house. ______ takes me only ten minutes to get to my office.", "options": ["It", "There", "The one", "The station"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V（做某事花某人多少時間），It 為虛主詞，代替後面的 to V。\n【分析】句中有 takes me ten minutes to get to my office，主詞須用虛主詞 It。\n【其他選項】(B) There 不能與 takes 連用；(C) The one、(D) The station 當主詞時，車站本身不會「花我十分鐘去辦公室」，語意與句型皆不合。\n【例句】It takes Amy half an hour to walk to school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 750, "question": "My grandparents live in Hualien. ______ takes us about three hours to get there by train.", "options": ["There", "It", "That trip", "They"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V，It 為虛主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 751, "question": "It ______ Jason two weeks to finish the science project.", "options": ["took", "spent", "cost", "paid"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "It + take + 人 + 時間 + to V；spent 主詞須為人。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 752, "question": "How long does it take ______ from Taipei to Tainan by bus?", "options": ["go", "going", "to go", "went"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 時間 + to V，故選 to go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 753, "question": "It took the police lots of time ______ who entered Liu's house and killed her one year ago.", "options": ["and found out", "find out", "finding out", "to find out"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】It takes / took + 人 + 時間 + to V。\n【分析】It took the police lots of time 之後要接不定詞 to find out：「警方花了很多時間才查出是誰…」。\n【其他選項】(A) and found out 破壞 It took…to V 句型；(B) find out 原形不能直接接；(C) finding out 為 spend 句型（spend time Ving）的用法。\n【例句】It took me an hour to fix my bike.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 754, "question": "It took Nina a whole afternoon ______ her bedroom.", "options": ["cleaning", "to clean", "cleaned", "clean"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 755, "question": "Peter spent three days ______ the puzzle.", "options": ["to finish", "finish", "finishing", "finished"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 時間 + Ving；與 It takes…to V 區分。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 756, "question": "How long did it take you ______ the speech by heart?", "options": ["learn", "learning", "learned", "to learn"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "it take + 人 + 時間 + to V，選 to learn。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 757, "question": "Gary: When you go shopping, do you usually ______ with your credit card?\nTony: No, I don't have a credit card.", "options": ["use", "pay", "spend", "waste"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜pay with + 付款方式", "explanation": "【句型】pay with / by + 付款方式（用信用卡、現金等付錢）；pay (money) for 物品。\n【分析】空格後接 with your credit card，表示「用信用卡付款」，選 pay。\n【其他選項】(A) use 是及物動詞，要說 use your credit card，不需 with；(C) spend 後要接金錢或時間（spend money on…）；(D) waste 浪費，語意不合。\n【例句】Can I pay with my EasyCard here?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 758, "question": "The store only takes cash, so you can't ______ by credit card.", "options": ["pay", "spend", "cost", "borrow"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "pay by credit card 用信用卡付款。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 759, "question": "How much did you ______ for those new sneakers?", "options": ["cost", "spend", "pay", "take"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "人 + pay + 金錢 + for + 物品。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 760, "question": "My sister ______ NT$500 on books last month.", "options": ["paid", "cost", "took", "spent"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 金錢 + on + 物品。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 761, "question": "Charles ______ a day in the department store looking for a hat for his wife.", "options": ["cost", "spent", "saw", "made"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜人 + spend + 時間 + Ving", "explanation": "【句型】人 + spend + 時間／金錢 + (in) Ving。\n【分析】主詞是人 Charles，後接 a day 和 looking for…，符合 spend 時間 Ving：「花了一天在百貨公司找帽子」。\n【其他選項】(A) cost 主詞須為物（事物花費某人金錢）；(C) saw、(D) made 不能接「時間 + Ving」表示花時間。\n【例句】Wendy spent two hours doing her homework.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 762, "question": "Leo ______ the whole weekend playing video games.", "options": ["took", "cost", "spent", "paid"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 時間 + Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 763, "question": "This jacket ______ me NT$1,200.", "options": ["cost", "spent", "paid", "took"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "物 + cost + 人 + 金錢，主詞是 jacket。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 764, "question": "We spent an hour ______ for the bus in the rain.", "options": ["wait", "waiting", "to wait", "waited"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "spend + 時間 + Ving，選 waiting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 765, "question": "Lisa's room was very dirty. It took her three hours ______ it.", "options": ["clean", "cleaned", "has cleaned", "to clean"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】It takes / took + 人 + 時間 + to V。\n【分析】It took her three hours 之後接不定詞 to clean：「她花了三小時打掃房間」。\n【其他選項】(A) clean 原形不能直接接；(B) cleaned 過去式，句中已有動詞 took；(C) has cleaned 完成式動詞，不能放在此處。\n【例句】It took us ten minutes to walk to the park.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 766, "question": "The math problem was hard. It took Andy an hour ______ it.", "options": ["to solve", "solved", "solving", "solve"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 767, "question": "It ______ me two years to save enough money for this camera.", "options": ["spent", "took", "paid", "cost"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "It + take + 人 + 時間 + to V 表示花費時間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 768, "question": "Ivy ______ three hours to read the novel.", "options": ["spent", "cost", "paid", "took"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "人 + take + 時間 + to V 也可表示花時間；spent 後須接 Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 769, "question": "David forgot to bring money with him, so I ______ him NT$60 to pay for his lunch.", "options": ["borrowed", "lent", "ordered", "spent"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜lend + 人 + 物（借出）", "explanation": "【句型】lend + 人 + 物 ＝ lend + 物 + to + 人（借出）；borrow + 物 + from + 人（借入）。\n【分析】David 忘了帶錢，所以「我借給他 60 元」，用 lent（lend 過去式）。\n【其他選項】(A) borrowed 是向別人借，不能接「人＋物」雙受詞；(C) ordered 訂購／點餐；(D) spent 花費，不能接「人＋錢」。\n【例句】Can you lend me your eraser?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 770, "question": "I left my umbrella at home, so I ______ one from my classmate.", "options": ["lent", "borrowed", "paid", "gave"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "borrow + 物 + from + 人，向某人借東西。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 771, "question": "Could you ______ me your dictionary for a minute?", "options": ["lend", "borrow", "spend", "take"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "lend + 人 + 物，把東西借給某人。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 772, "question": "Mary ______ her notebook to Ken because he missed the class.", "options": ["borrowed", "cost", "lent", "spent"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "lend + 物 + to + 人，借出筆記給 Ken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 773, "question": "It's ______ me a lot of time to find out what I really want to do in the future.", "options": ["paying", "spending", "taking", "using"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V（進行式 taking）", "explanation": "【句型】It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V（此處為現在進行式 It's taking）。\n【分析】主詞是虛主詞 It，後接 me a lot of time to find out…，只有 take 符合：「我花了很多時間在找出未來想做什麼」。\n【其他選項】(A) pay 用於金錢；(B) spend 主詞須為人，且接 Ving；(D) use 不能接「人＋時間＋to V」。\n【例句】It's taking Ben a long time to get used to his new school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 774, "question": "It ______ Joan a week to plan the class trip.", "options": ["took", "spent", "paid", "used"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "It + take + 人 + 時間 + to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 775, "question": "Mr. Ho is ______ a lot of money fixing his old car.", "options": ["taking", "costing", "spending", "lending"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 金錢 + Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 776, "question": "The concert tickets ______ us NT$3,000 in total.", "options": ["spent", "took", "paid", "cost"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "物 + cost + 人 + 金錢。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 777, "question": "I can ______ you the book, but you have to give it back to me in three days.", "options": ["borrow", "lend", "read", "show"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜lend vs. borrow", "explanation": "【句型】lend + 人 + 物（把東西借給某人）；borrow + 物 + from + 人（向某人借）。\n【分析】後句 you have to give it back to me「你要還給我」，表示書是我借出去的，選 lend。\n【其他選項】(A) borrow 是「借入」，且不接「人＋物」；(C) read you the book 唸書給你聽，與「還給我」不合；(D) show 給…看，不需要「歸還」。\n【例句】Jack lent me his bike for a day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 778, "question": "May I ______ your pen? I'll return it after class.", "options": ["lend", "borrow", "give", "keep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "向別人借東西用 borrow，後句「下課歸還」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 779, "question": "The library ______ books to students for two weeks.", "options": ["lends", "borrows", "spends", "costs"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "lend + 物 + to + 人，圖書館把書借出給學生。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 780, "question": "Ted ______ NT$100 from his sister, and he has to pay her back tomorrow.", "options": ["lent", "paid", "borrowed", "cost"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "borrow + 物 + from + 人，向姊姊借錢。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 781, "question": "Studying in a foreign country ______ me a lot of money. That's why I had to sell my apartment.", "options": ["cost", "lost", "made", "spent"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜物 + cost + 人 + 金錢", "explanation": "【句型】事物（主詞）+ cost + 人 + 金錢（某事物花了某人多少錢）。\n【分析】主詞是動名詞 Studying in a foreign country（事物），後接 me a lot of money，選 cost（過去式同形）：「出國念書花了我很多錢，所以得賣掉公寓」。\n【其他選項】(B) lost 不接「人＋金錢」雙受詞；(C) made me money 是「讓我賺錢」，與賣房子語意相反；(D) spent 主詞須為人（人 spend 錢 on…）。\n【例句】The trip to Japan cost my family NT$100,000.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 782, "question": "Fixing the broken phone ______ Ryan NT$2,000 last week.", "options": ["spent", "cost", "paid", "took"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "事物 + cost + 人 + 金錢；主詞是 Fixing the broken phone。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 783, "question": "How much does a bowl of beef noodles ______ at this shop?", "options": ["cost", "spend", "pay", "take"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "物品當主詞問價錢用 cost。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 784, "question": "Helen ______ NT$800 on a birthday gift for her mom.", "options": ["cost", "took", "spent", "lent"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 金錢 + on + 物。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 785, "question": "My dog hates to take a bath. It usually ______ me one hour to make him clean.", "options": ["needs", "spends", "takes", "uses"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜會考歷屆｜It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V。\n【分析】虛主詞 It 後接 me one hour to make him clean，只有 takes 符合：「通常花我一小時才能把牠洗乾淨」。\n【其他選項】(A) needs 不接「人＋時間＋to V」；(B) spends 主詞須為人，接 Ving；(D) uses 不能表示花費時間的此句型。\n【例句】It takes my brother twenty minutes to get dressed.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 786, "question": "It ______ Mandy half an hour to blow-dry her long hair.", "options": ["spends", "takes", "costs", "pays"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 787, "question": "Mandy ______ half an hour drying her long hair every night.", "options": ["spends", "takes", "costs", "pays"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "人 + spend + 時間 + Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 788, "question": "It will take you about five minutes ______ there on foot.", "options": ["get", "getting", "got", "to get"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V，選 to get。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "特殊動詞（spend/cost/take/pay/lend/borrow）"}, {"id": 789, "question": "Mr. and Mrs. Wu have three daughters. Two are in high school, and ______ is in elementary school.", "options": ["each", "the other", "the one", "the next"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜two…, the other（三者中剩下的一個）", "explanation": "【句型】三者中：two…, the other…（兩個…，剩下的那一個…）；兩者中：one…, the other…。\n【分析】三個女兒，兩個念高中，剩下最後一個念小學，用 the other（= the other daughter）。\n【其他選項】(A) each 每一個，語意不合；(C) the one 「那一個」需有修飾語指明是哪一個；(D) the next 下一個，有順序意，不合。\n【例句】I have three pets. Two are cats, and the other is a dog.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 790, "question": "Ben has two brothers. One lives in Taichung, and ______ lives in Taipei.", "options": ["another", "other", "the other", "others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "兩者中 one…, the other…。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 791, "question": "There are four students in the room. Three are reading, and ______ is sleeping.", "options": ["the other", "another", "others", "the others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "四人中三個…，剩下唯一的一個用 the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 792, "question": "I don't like this shirt. Can you show me ______ one?", "options": ["the others", "another", "other", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "another one 另一件（不特定）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 793, "question": "I want to find another dentist because ______ pulled out a good tooth last time I went to him.", "options": ["I", "me", "mine", "myself"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 mine（= my dentist）", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞 mine = my + 名詞，可當主詞。\n【分析】拔牙的是牙醫，不是「我」；後面 last time I went to him 的 him 也指牙醫。所以空格是 mine = my dentist：「我想換牙醫，因為我的牙醫上次拔掉我一顆好牙」。\n【其他選項】(A) I 雖是主格，但「我拔掉一顆好牙」不合理，也與 to him 不呼應；(B) me 受格不能當主詞；(D) myself 反身代名詞不能當主詞。\n【例句】Your bike is new, but mine is very old.\n備註：參考答案 bf15af99.txt 給 A (I)。但「我」拔牙不合理，且 him 指牙醫，正解應為 C mine（= my dentist）；此題已依語意改為 C，請老師確認。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 794, "question": "Tina's computer is fast, but ______ is very slow. I need a new one.", "options": ["my", "me", "mine", "myself"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "mine = my computer，當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 795, "question": "I forgot my umbrella, so Kevin shared ______ with me.", "options": ["his", "him", "he", "himself"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "his = his umbrella，所有格代名詞當受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 796, "question": "Our classroom is on the second floor. Where is ______?", "options": ["you", "your", "yourself", "yours"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "yours = your classroom，所有格代名詞當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 797, "question": "I guess the rainwater has come in from the kitchen. See? ______ of the windows are closed except the one in the kitchen.", "options": ["All", "Both", "Most", "Some"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜All of … except …", "explanation": "【句型】All of the + 複數名詞 + except…（除了…之外全部都…）。\n【分析】雨水從廚房進來，因為「除了廚房那扇窗之外，所有窗戶都關著」；except the one in the kitchen 只排除一扇，其餘全部，選 All。\n【其他選項】(B) Both 只用於兩者，題中窗戶不只兩扇；(C) Most、(D) Some 表示「大部分／一些」，與 except 只排除一扇的語意不合，也無法推論雨水只從廚房進來。\n【例句】All of the students passed the test except Tom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 798, "question": "______ of my classmates came to the party except Ivy. She was sick.", "options": ["Both", "All", "Few", "Some"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "except Ivy 只排除一人，表示其餘全部都來，用 All。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 799, "question": "I have two cousins. ______ of them live in Kaohsiung.", "options": ["Both", "All", "Each", "Most"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "兩者都用 Both，接複數動詞 live。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 800, "question": "There are thirty students in my class, and ______ of them wear glasses. Only five don't.", "options": ["all", "both", "most", "none"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "三十人中只有五人不戴，即「大部分」，用 most。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 801, "question": "Nora: Can I check your drawer for some tools we can use?\nMatt: Sure. Take a look. See if you can find ______ in there.", "options": ["any", "it", "others", "those"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜any（條件／疑問句中的「任何」）", "explanation": "【句型】any 用於疑問、否定、if 條件句，表「任何（一些）」，可當代名詞。\n【分析】See if you can find any (tools)「看看你能不能在裡面找到任何（可用的）工具」，選 any。\n【其他選項】(B) it 指特定單數，但 tools 為複數且未特定；(C) others「其他的」，前面沒提到已有的工具，語意不合；(D) those 指特定的那些，Matt 不知道有哪些工具。\n【例句】I need some stamps. Do you have any?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 802, "question": "Amy: I need some glue for my project.\nBen: Sorry, I don't have ______.", "options": ["one", "it", "any", "some"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "否定句中用 any 表示「任何（一些）」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 803, "question": "These cookies are delicious. Would you like ______?", "options": ["some", "any", "it", "other"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "表示邀請、提供東西的疑問句用 some。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 804, "question": "I lost my eraser. Do you have ______ I can borrow?", "options": ["it", "one", "them", "those"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "one 代替「一個不特定的」橡皮擦（單數可數名詞）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 805, "question": "______ of my sisters are older than I am. I'm the youngest of the three children in my family.", "options": ["Both", "Few", "Most", "Some"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜Both of（兩者都）", "explanation": "【句型】Both of + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞（兩者都…）。\n【分析】家中三個小孩、我最小，所以我有兩個姊姊，而且「兩個都比我大」，選 Both。\n【其他選項】(B) Few 很少，語意不合；(C) Most、(D) Some 用於三者以上的一部分，只有兩個姊姊時不適用。\n【例句】Both of my parents are teachers.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 806, "question": "I have two dogs. ______ of them like to sleep on my bed.", "options": ["All", "Both", "Each", "Neither"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "兩隻狗都喜歡，用 Both，接複數動詞 like。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 807, "question": "Jay has two sisters, but ______ of them can swim.", "options": ["neither", "both", "all", "none"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "兩者都不用 neither；but 表示轉折。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 808, "question": "I'm the oldest of the four children in my family. ______ of my brothers are younger than I am.", "options": ["Both", "Some", "All", "Few"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "四個小孩我最大，另外三個（三者以上）全部比我小，用 All。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 809, "question": "Beatrice loves to draw apples. You can see ______ in her notebooks, on her letters, and even on her school bag!", "options": ["one", "others", "them", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜them 代替前面特定的複數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】代名詞 them 代替前面提過的「特定」複數名詞。\n【分析】空格指的是 Beatrice 畫的那些 apples（複數、特定），當 see 的受詞，用受格 them。\n【其他選項】(A) one 代替單數且不特定的名詞；(B) others「其他的」，前面沒有對比的東西；(D) which 是疑問詞／關係代名詞，不能單獨當受詞。\n【例句】I bought some cookies and gave them to my friends.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 810, "question": "Leo collects stamps from different countries. He keeps ______ in a big album.", "options": ["it", "them", "one", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "them 代替前面特定的複數名詞 stamps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 811, "question": "I lost my pencil case. Have you seen ______?", "options": ["it", "one", "them", "another"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "it 代替前面特定的單數名詞 my pencil case。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 812, "question": "I need a ruler. Do you have ______?", "options": ["it", "them", "one", "those"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "one 代替不特定的單數名詞 a ruler。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 813, "question": "My wife enjoys going to the movies with her friends, but I like to watch TV at home by ______.", "options": ["I", "me", "myself", "mine"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜by + 反身代名詞（獨自）", "explanation": "【句型】by + 反身代名詞 ＝ alone（獨自）。\n【分析】主詞是 I，與「太太和朋友去看電影」對比，「我喜歡自己一個人在家看電視」，用 by myself。\n【其他選項】(A) I 主格；(B) me 受格；(D) mine 所有格代名詞；三者都不能用於「by + 反身代名詞」表「獨自」。\n【例句】Mia went to Japan by herself last summer.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 814, "question": "Steve is only six, but he can take the bus to school by ______.", "options": ["himself", "him", "his", "he"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "by himself 獨自，主詞為 he。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 815, "question": "The twins cooked dinner by ______ for the first time.", "options": ["them", "themselves", "theirs", "their"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The twins 為複數，用 by themselves。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 816, "question": "Lily, did you finish this painting by ______? It looks great!", "options": ["you", "your", "yours", "yourself"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "對 Lily 說話，用 by yourself 表「你自己一個人」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 817, "question": "Ms. Johnson has been taking phone calls since she entered the office this morning. Just when she thought she could finally leave work, ______ call came in.", "options": ["another", "each", "the next", "the other"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜another + 單數名詞（又一個）", "explanation": "【句型】another + 單數名詞（再一個、又一個，不特定）。\n【分析】她整天一直接電話，正以為可以下班時，「又一通」電話打進來，選 another call。\n【其他選項】(B) each call 每一通，與 came in（一通進來）語意不合；(C) the next call 指順序上的下一通，無法表達「又來一通」的無奈；(D) the other 用於兩者中的另一個，電話不只兩通。\n【例句】I've already eaten two pieces of cake, but I want another one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 818, "question": "Ken finished his hamburger quickly and ordered ______ one.", "options": ["other", "another", "the other", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "another + 單數名詞，表示再一個。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 819, "question": "We have already visited three museums today. Let's not go to ______ museum.", "options": ["another", "other", "the others", "each"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "已去了三間，不要再去「又一間」，用 another museum。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 820, "question": "Lucy has two pens. One is red, and ______ is blue.", "options": ["another", "other", "the other", "others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "兩者中 one…, the other…。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 821, "question": "I don't like any one of these three watches. Can you show me ______ one?", "options": ["the others", "other", "either", "another"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜another one（另一個，不特定）", "explanation": "【句型】another + 單數名詞／one（另一個，不特定）。\n【分析】這三支錶都不喜歡，請店員拿「另一支」（店裡其他任一支）來看，用 another one。\n【其他選項】(A) the others 指剩下的全部（複數），不能接 one；(B) other 後接複數名詞，不接單數 one；(C) either 用於兩者之一，這裡有三支錶。\n【例句】This cup is dirty. Please give me another one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 822, "question": "This T-shirt is too small for me. Do you have ______ one in a bigger size?", "options": ["the other", "another", "others", "other"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "不特定的另一件，用 another one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 823, "question": "There are two roads to the station. You can take ______ one.", "options": ["either", "another", "other", "others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "兩者之一用 either。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 824, "question": "Some students like math, and ______ students like English.", "options": ["another", "the other", "other", "either"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "other + 複數名詞，表示「其他的」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 825, "question": "My parents have different hobbies. One enjoys baking; ______ enjoys taking pictures.", "options": ["another", "the next", "the other", "the second"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜one…, the other…（兩者）", "explanation": "【句型】兩者中：one…, the other…（一個…，另一個…）。\n【分析】parents 只有兩人，一個喜歡烘焙，另一個（剩下的那位）喜歡拍照，用 the other。\n【其他選項】(A) another 用於三者以上中不特定的另一個；(B) the next 下一個，有順序意；(D) the second 第二個，不用於兩者對比的句型。\n【例句】I have two hands. One is holding a cup, and the other is holding a book.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 826, "question": "Ann has two cats. One is white, and ______ is black.", "options": ["the other", "another", "other", "others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "兩者中 one…, the other…。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 827, "question": "There are five boys on the team. One is from Japan, and ______ are from Taiwan.", "options": ["the other", "others", "another", "the others"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "五人中一人之外，「剩下的全部」用 the others。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 828, "question": "Some people like coffee; ______ like tea.", "options": ["the other", "another", "others", "other"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "Some…, others…（有些…，有些…），不特定的其他人。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 829, "question": "The book under Mary's desk is ______, but I don't know why it is there.", "options": ["us", "me", "my", "mine"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 mine（= my book）", "explanation": "【句型】S + be + 所有格代名詞（mine / yours / his / hers / ours / theirs）。\n【分析】「Mary 桌下那本書是我的，但我不知道它為什麼在那裡」，空格當補語，用 mine（= my book）。\n【其他選項】(A) us、(B) me 為受格，不能表示「…的」；(C) my 為所有格形容詞，後面必須接名詞。\n【例句】That red umbrella is hers.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 830, "question": "Excuse me, is this blue jacket ______? I found it in the gym.", "options": ["your", "yours", "you", "yourself"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "yours = your jacket，當補語。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 831, "question": "These aren't our seats. ______ are in the next row.", "options": ["Ours", "Our", "Us", "We"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "Ours = Our seats，當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 832, "question": "The idea was not Tom's; it was ______. She thought of it first.", "options": ["her", "she", "hers", "herself"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "hers = her idea，所有格代名詞當補語。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 833, "question": "The poor family have only ______ bread for today. Nothing is left for them to eat tomorrow.", "options": ["enough", "few", "much", "other"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜enough + 不可數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】enough + 名詞（足夠的…）；only enough… for today 只夠今天。\n【分析】後句「明天就沒東西可吃了」，所以麵包「只夠今天吃」，選 enough。\n【其他選項】(B) few 修飾可數複數名詞，bread 不可數；(C) only much bread 不是正確用法，且「很多」與「明天沒得吃」矛盾；(D) other bread 其他的麵包，語意不合。\n【例句】We don't have enough time to finish the test.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 834, "question": "Hurry up! We only have ______ time to catch the last bus.", "options": ["few", "many", "enough", "other"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "enough time 剛好足夠的時間；time 不可數不用 few / many。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 835, "question": "There is ______ milk in the bottle. Let's buy some more.", "options": ["a little", "little", "a few", "few"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "milk 不可數，little 表「幾乎沒有」，所以要再買。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 836, "question": "Sorry, I can't buy the bag. I don't have ______ money with me.", "options": ["enough", "many", "few", "another"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "not enough money 錢不夠；money 不可數。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 837, "question": "My mom told me to take care of ______ in England. She worried that I couldn't eat or sleep well there.", "options": ["me", "myself", "her", "herself"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜take care of + 反身代名詞", "explanation": "【句型】動作者與受詞為同一人時用反身代名詞：take care of oneself（照顧自己）。\n【分析】told me to take care of…，照顧的人（我）和被照顧的人（我）是同一人，用 myself：「媽媽叫我在英國要照顧好自己」。\n【其他選項】(A) me 受格，同一人時須用反身代名詞；(C) her、(D) herself 指媽媽，但媽媽擔心的是「我」吃睡不好，語意不合。\n【例句】Please take care of yourself when you travel.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 838, "question": "Grandpa is ninety, but he can still take care of ______.", "options": ["him", "his", "himself", "he"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "主詞與受詞同一人（Grandpa），用 himself。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 839, "question": "Be careful with the knife, or you'll hurt ______.", "options": ["yourself", "you", "your", "yours"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "you 自己傷到自己，用反身代名詞 yourself。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 840, "question": "The teacher told us to enjoy ______ at the school party.", "options": ["us", "our", "ours", "ourselves"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "enjoy oneself 玩得愉快；動作者 we 與受詞同一人。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 841, "question": "My grandfather spends ______ of his free time reading newspapers.", "options": ["one", "both", "most", "many"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜most of + 不可數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】most of + the/所有格 + 不可數名詞／複數名詞「大部分的…」\n【分析】free time 是不可數名詞，most 可修飾不可數名詞 → most of his free time「他大部分的空閒時間」。\n【其他選項】(A) one of 後須接複數可數名詞；(B) both 指「兩者」，free time 不是兩個；(D) many of 只能接複數可數名詞，free time 不可數。\n【例句】Linda spends most of her money on books.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 842, "question": "Kevin spends ______ of his weekend playing basketball with his friends.", "options": ["most", "many", "both", "one"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "weekend 時間不可數概念，most of his weekend「他大部分的週末」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 843, "question": "______ of the water in this bottle is gone. Who drank it?", "options": ["Many", "Few", "Most", "Both"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "water 不可數，只能用 most of the water，動詞 is 單數。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 844, "question": "My sister wastes ______ of her time on her phone, so her grades are going down.", "options": ["many", "one", "both", "most"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "time 不可數，most of her time「她大部分的時間」；many/one/both 需接可數名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 845, "question": "It almost killed Kevin to take care of his baby sister for one afternoon. He wondered how his mom could do ______ every day.", "options": ["her", "it", "one", "them"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜it 代替前面提到的整件事", "explanation": "【句型】it 可代替前文提到的「整件事／整個動作」：do it「做這件事」\n【分析】do ______ every day 指的是前面「照顧小妹妹一整個下午」這件事 → 用單數 it 代替整件事，how his mom could do it every day。\n【其他選項】(A) her 指人（妹妹），do her 語意不通；(C) one 代替「不特定的同類名詞」，不能代替一件特定的事；(D) them 指複數，前文只有一件事。\n【例句】Cleaning the whole house is hard work, but my dad does it every weekend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 846, "question": "Writing a diary in English is not easy, but Amy has done ______ for three years.", "options": ["one", "it", "them", "that one"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "it 代替前面「用英文寫日記」這件事。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 847, "question": "Ben: Climbing Jade Mountain was so tiring!\nTina: Really? I'd still like to try ______ someday.", "options": ["them", "one", "it", "this one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "it 指前面提到的「爬玉山」這件事。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 848, "question": "Getting up at five every morning sounds terrible. I can't imagine doing ______ every day.", "options": ["it", "them", "one", "its"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "doing it 代替「每天五點起床」這件事。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 849, "question": "______ other waiters in the restaurant have worked here longer than Clark; only Lois and Lana started working here before him.", "options": ["All", "Most", "Some", "Few"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜few + 複數名詞（很少，幾乎沒有）", "explanation": "【句型】few + 複數可數名詞「很少、幾乎沒有」（表否定語氣）\n【分析】後句說「只有 Lois 和 Lana 比他早來」→ 比 Clark 資歷久的服務生只有兩位，非常少 → Few other waiters have worked here longer than Clark「很少其他服務生在這裡做得比他久」。\n【其他選項】(A) All 表示全部都比他久，與「只有兩位」矛盾；(B) Most 表示大部分都比他久，也與「只有兩位」矛盾；(C) Some 沒有「只有少數」的限制語氣，無法呼應 only。\n【例句】Few students in my class can speak Japanese; only Ken and Mei can.\n備註：教師原解答（bf15af99.txt）為 (B) Most，但與後句「only Lois and Lana started working here before him」矛盾：比 Clark 資歷深的只有兩人，應為「很少」→ 正解 (D) Few（亦為會考官方答案）。此處採 D。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 850, "question": "______ people came to the concert because of the heavy rain. The hall was almost empty.", "options": ["Many", "Few", "Most", "All"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "演奏廳幾乎是空的 → 很少人來，用 Few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 851, "question": "This question is very hard. ______ students got it right; only Tom did.", "options": ["Few", "Most", "Some", "All"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "只有 Tom 答對 → 很少學生答對，用 Few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 852, "question": "Eric is new in town, so he has ______ friends here. He often feels lonely.", "options": ["many", "a lot of", "few", "most"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "他常覺得孤單 → 朋友很少，用 few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 853, "question": "I don't think Katie will read any one of the books you've picked out for her: ______ look(s) very boring.", "options": ["it", "one", "some", "they"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜they 代替特定複數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】they / them 代替前面提過的「特定複數名詞」\n【分析】冒號後是在說明原因：前面「你為她挑的那些書」是特定的複數名詞 → 用 they 代替，they look very boring「它們看起來都很無聊」。\n【其他選項】(A) it 代替特定單數名詞，但書是複數；(B) one 代替不特定的單數，且只說一本無法解釋她一本都不讀；(C) some 指「其中一些」，但 Katie 是任何一本都不讀，表示全部都無聊。\n【例句】I bought these cookies yesterday. They taste great.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 854, "question": "Mom bought three new plates last week, but ______ were broken by my little brother today.", "options": ["it", "they", "one", "some one"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "they 指前面特定的 three new plates。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 855, "question": "Have you seen my glasses? I can't find ______ anywhere.", "options": ["it", "one", "them", "ones"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "glasses 為複數名詞，且是「我的」特定那副 → 用受格 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 856, "question": "Jason showed me the photos from his trip. ______ were really beautiful.", "options": ["They", "It", "One", "Them"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "主詞位置代替特定複數 the photos → They。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 857, "question": "I cannot understand why Steven bought so many watches but never wears ______ of them.", "options": ["any", "both", "every", "others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜否定句 any of them", "explanation": "【句型】否定句中用 any of + 複數受格「任何一個」；not/never ... any = 一個也不\n【分析】never wears any of them「從來不戴其中任何一支」，them 指前面 so many watches，否定句用 any。\n【其他選項】(B) both 只用於兩個，而他買了很多支；(C) every 不能直接接 of；(D) others 是代名詞，後面不能再接 of them。\n【例句】I have many old toys, but I don't play with any of them now.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 858, "question": "Lily has a lot of skirts, but she hasn't worn ______ of them this year.", "options": ["every", "any", "both", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "否定句 hasn't worn any of them「一件也沒穿過」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 859, "question": "There are ten questions on the test, and Mark didn't answer ______ of them correctly.", "options": ["any", "each", "every", "another"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "否定句 didn't answer any of them「一題都沒答對」；every 不能接 of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 860, "question": "I asked my classmates for help, but ______ of them had time to help me.", "options": ["any", "every", "none", "each one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "肯定句形式卻表「沒有人」→ none of them；any 不能單獨當肯定句主詞表否定。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 861, "question": "______ of the books on the desk is about the famous writers of our country.", "options": ["A lot", "A few", "Both", "One"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜one of + the + 複數名詞 + 單數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】One of + the + 複數名詞 + 單數動詞（is/was/has）「…之中的一個」\n【分析】動詞是單數 is → 主詞須為單數 → One of the books is ...「桌上的書之中有一本是關於…」。\n【其他選項】(A) A lot of the books 為複數，動詞應用 are；(B) A few of the books 為複數，動詞應用 are；(C) Both of the books 為複數，動詞應用 are。\n【例句】One of my friends lives in Tainan.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 862, "question": "______ of the students in my class has a pet snake.", "options": ["Both", "One", "Many", "A few"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "動詞 has 單數 → One of the students。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 863, "question": "______ of my cousins are studying in Japan now.", "options": ["One", "Each", "Two", "Every"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "動詞 are 複數 → Two of my cousins；One/Each 須用單數動詞，every 不能接 of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 864, "question": "One of the boys in the park ______ my brother.", "options": ["are", "were", "have", "is"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "主詞是 One（單數）→ 動詞用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 865, "question": "Mary got two dolls from her grandfather on her birthday, and she liked ______ very much.", "options": ["her", "it", "ones", "them"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜them 代替特定複數名詞（受格）", "explanation": "【句型】they / them 代替前文特定的複數名詞；動詞後用受格 them\n【分析】liked 後要接受格，代替前面特定的 two dolls（複數）→ she liked them very much。\n【其他選項】(A) her 指女性的人，不是指娃娃；(B) it 代替單數，娃娃有兩個；(C) ones 代替「不特定」的同類名詞，但這裡是指那兩個特定的娃娃。\n【例句】Dad gave me two comic books, and I read them in one night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 866, "question": "Grandma made some dumplings for us, and we ate ______ all.", "options": ["it", "them", "ones", "they"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "代替特定的 dumplings（複數），作受詞用 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 867, "question": "I found three kittens in the park and took ______ home.", "options": ["them", "they", "it", "ones"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "take 後接受格，代替特定的 three kittens → them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 868, "question": "These shoes are too small for me. Can I try on bigger ______?", "options": ["them", "it", "ones", "one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "要試「不特定的、較大的鞋子」（複數）→ ones。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 869, "question": "______ of the gift boxes are already put under the Christmas tree.", "options": ["One", "Any", "All", "Much"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜all of + the + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】All of + the + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞「全部的…都…」\n【分析】動詞是複數 are，gift boxes 是可數複數 → All of the gift boxes are ...「所有的禮物盒都已經放在聖誕樹下了」。\n【其他選項】(A) One of ... 須接單數動詞 is；(B) Any 多用於否定句、疑問句，肯定句當主詞語意不合；(D) Much 修飾不可數名詞，gift boxes 可數。\n【例句】All of the students are in the classroom now.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 870, "question": "______ of the cookies on the plate were eaten by my brother.", "options": ["Much", "All", "One", "Every"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "cookies 可數複數，動詞 were 複數 → All of the cookies。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 871, "question": "______ of the milk in the fridge has gone bad.", "options": ["Many", "All", "Few", "Both"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "milk 不可數，all 可接不可數名詞，動詞 has 單數。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 872, "question": "All of my classmates ______ excited about the school trip next week.", "options": ["is", "was", "has", "are"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "All of + 複數名詞 → 動詞用複數 are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 873, "question": "Paula: Is that big toy store Mr. and Mrs. Chen's?\nKelly: Yes, it's ______. My daughter loves going there.", "options": ["his", "hers", "ours", "theirs"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 theirs", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞＝所有格＋名詞：mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs\n【分析】問句問的是 Mr. and Mrs. Chen's（陳先生和陳太太兩個人的）→ 複數「他們的」→ theirs = their toy store。\n【其他選項】(A) his 只指陳先生一人；(B) hers 只指陳太太一人；(C) ours 是「我們的」，與問句不符。\n【例句】These seats aren't ours. They're theirs.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 874, "question": "Ann: Are those bikes Tom and Jerry's?\nBob: Yes, they're ______. They ride them to school every day.", "options": ["his", "theirs", "ours", "yours"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "Tom and Jerry 兩人 → theirs。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 875, "question": "Ms. Lin: Is this umbrella your sister's?\nKen: Yes, it's ______.", "options": ["hers", "his", "theirs", "her"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "sister 為女性單數 → hers = her umbrella；her 後須接名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 876, "question": "Jim: Whose house is this? Is it yours and your brother's?\nAlan: Yes, it's ______. We just moved in.", "options": ["theirs", "yours", "his", "ours"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "我和哥哥的 → 我們的 ours。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 877, "question": "Yesterday was my daughter's birthday. We took ______ to a restaurant and had a big dinner.", "options": ["me", "him", "her", "you"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜受格代名詞 her", "explanation": "【句型】人稱代名詞：動詞後用受格（me, you, him, her, us, them）\n【分析】took 後須接受格，代替前句的 my daughter（女兒，女性單數）→ her。\n【其他選項】(A) me 主詞是 We，「我們帶我」語意不通；(B) him 指男性，與 daughter 不符；(D) you 指對話中的對方，與前句無關。\n【例句】My grandpa is sick, so we visit him every Sunday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 878, "question": "My son's school is far from our home, so I drive ______ there every morning.", "options": ["her", "him", "them", "it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "son 為男性 → 受格 him。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 879, "question": "Our teacher was very kind to us, so we bought ______ a card on Teachers' Day.", "options": ["him", "his", "he", "her's"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "買卡片給老師，動詞後用受格 him；his 是所有格，he 是主格。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 880, "question": "My parents work very hard. I want to take ______ on a trip to Japan.", "options": ["they", "their", "them", "theirs"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "代替 my parents（複數），動詞後用受格 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 881, "question": "Susan bought ______ bread in the supermarket, but she did not buy anything to drink.", "options": ["many", "some", "any", "one"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜肯定句 some + 不可數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】some + 複數名詞／不可數名詞（多用於肯定句）；any 多用於否定句、疑問句\n【分析】前半句是肯定句，bread 是不可數名詞 → some bread「一些麵包」。\n【其他選項】(A) many 修飾可數複數名詞，bread 不可數；(C) any 一般用於否定句或疑問句；(D) one 修飾單數可數名詞，bread 不可數（要說 a loaf of bread）。\n【例句】I'd like some juice, please.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 882, "question": "Mom put ______ sugar in the tea, so it tastes sweet.", "options": ["many", "a", "some", "any"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、sugar 不可數 → some sugar。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 883, "question": "We don't have ______ milk at home. Can you buy some?", "options": ["any", "some", "many", "a"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "否定句用 any milk。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 884, "question": "Peter ate ______ apples after school because he was hungry.", "options": ["much", "a", "any", "some"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、apples 可數複數 → some apples；much 修飾不可數。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 885, "question": "There are two supermarkets near my house. The one on the corner sells bread, but ______ doesn't.", "options": ["another", "that", "the next", "the other"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜兩者：one ... the other ...", "explanation": "【句型】兩者之中：one ... the other ...（一個…，另一個…）\n【分析】two supermarkets 只有兩家，前面已提 The one on the corner，剩下的唯一一家用 the other。\n【其他選項】(A) another 用於三者以上的「另一個」；(B) that 無法明確指「剩下的那一家」；(C) the next「下一個」，用於順序，不符語意。\n【例句】I have two cats. One is white, and the other is black.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 886, "question": "Amy has two brothers. One is a doctor, and ______ is a teacher.", "options": ["another", "the other", "other", "the others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "兩兄弟中的另一個 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 887, "question": "I lost one of my gloves, so I can only wear ______ now.", "options": ["the other", "another", "others", "the others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "手套一雙兩隻，剩下那一隻 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 888, "question": "There are two bus stops near the school. One is in front of the gate, and ______ is behind the gym.", "options": ["another", "others", "the other", "other"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "兩個公車站，剩下的那一個 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 889, "question": "I was told to interview three guys at different times today. The first was on time. The second was late, and ______ never came.", "options": ["the last", "the only one", "some", "another"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜三者順序：the first / the second / the last", "explanation": "【句型】依順序列舉：the first ... the second ... the last／the third（最後一個）\n【分析】一共三個人，前面已說 The first、The second，剩下的就是第三個（最後一個）→ the last。\n【其他選項】(B) the only one「唯一一個」，但共有三人；(C) some 表「一些」，指不特定多數；(D) another 指「還有另一個（不是最後）」，不能表示剩下的最後一位。\n【例句】We read three books this term. The first was funny, the second was sad, and the last was scary.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 890, "question": "Jenny ran three races yesterday. She won the first, lost the second, and won ______ again.", "options": ["the last", "another", "others", "the other one"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "共三場，剩下的最後一場 → the last。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 891, "question": "There are three rooms upstairs. The first is mine, the second is my sister's, and ______ is my parents'.", "options": ["another", "the third", "other", "the others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "三個房間依序排列，第三間 → the third。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 892, "question": "I have three pets. One is a dog, another is a cat, and ______ is a rabbit.", "options": ["another", "others", "the other", "other"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "三者：one ... another ... the other（剩下最後一個）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 893, "question": "Jogging is the only exercise I enjoy. I find ______ other kinds of exercise boring.", "options": ["all", "few", "many", "some"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜all + other + 複數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】all + other + 複數名詞「所有其他的…」；the only ... 與 all other ... 呼應\n【分析】「慢跑是我唯一喜歡的運動」→ 其他所有的運動我都覺得無聊 → all other kinds of exercise。\n【其他選項】(B) few「很少」→ 很少覺得無聊，與 the only 矛盾；(C) many、(D) some 只表示「許多／一些」，暗示還有其他喜歡的運動，與「唯一」矛盾。\n【例句】Math is the only subject I'm good at. All other subjects are hard for me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 894, "question": "Kelly only eats apples. She doesn't like ______ other fruits at all.", "options": ["some", "any", "many", "few"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "否定句 not ... any other fruits「其他任何水果都不喜歡」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 895, "question": "Tom is the tallest boy in our class. He is taller than ______ other boys in the class.", "options": ["all", "some", "few", "many"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "最高 = 比班上所有其他男生高 → all other boys。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 896, "question": "This is the only shop that sells fresh bread in town. ______ other shops sell only cookies.", "options": ["Few", "Some", "Many", "All"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "唯一賣新鮮麵包的店 → 其他所有店都只賣餅乾 → All。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 897, "question": "Stella: Is this Simon's book? I found it under the chair.\nJoyce: No, it's ______. Thank you. I've been looking for it.", "options": ["I", "me", "my", "mine"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 mine", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞＝所有格＋名詞：mine = my book\n【分析】Joyce 說不是 Simon 的，又說「謝謝，我一直在找它」→ 是「我的」書；空格後沒有名詞 → 用所有格代名詞 mine。\n【其他選項】(A) I 主格；(B) me 受格，都不表「所有」；(C) my 是所有格，後面必須接名詞（my book）。\n【例句】This pencil case isn't yours. It's mine.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 898, "question": "Ted: Whose cap is this?\nRay: Oh, it's ______. I left it here this morning.", "options": ["me", "mine", "my", "I"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "空格後無名詞，表「我的」→ mine。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 899, "question": "Your bag is red, and ______ is blue.", "options": ["my", "me", "mine", "I"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "mine = my bag，作主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 900, "question": "Teacher: Is this your homework, Nick?\nNick: Yes, it's ______. Sorry I forgot to write my name.", "options": ["mine", "my", "me", "myself"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "所有格代名詞 mine = my homework。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 901, "question": "We know ______ about the new boss except that she just came back from the US. We hope to know her better.", "options": ["everything", "nothing", "other things", "something"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜nothing ... except ...", "explanation": "【句型】know nothing about ... except ...「除了…之外對…一無所知」\n【分析】except「除了…之外」，加上後句「希望更了解她」→ 我們對新老闆所知甚少，只知道她剛從美國回來 → know nothing about her except ...。\n【其他選項】(A) everything「什麼都知道」與「希望更了解她」矛盾；(C) other things「其他事情」語意不通；(D) something 無法與 except 形成「只知道這件事」的限定語氣。\n【例句】I ate nothing for breakfast except a banana.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 902, "question": "Ivy was so sick that she ate ______ all day except some soup.", "options": ["something", "nothing", "everything", "anything"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "病得很重 → 除了湯什麼都沒吃 → nothing ... except。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 903, "question": "It's a quiet night. I can hear ______ except the sound of the rain.", "options": ["nothing", "everything", "something", "anything"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "安靜的夜晚，除了雨聲什麼都聽不到 → nothing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 904, "question": "The room is empty. There's ______ in it except an old chair.", "options": ["everything", "something", "anything", "nothing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "房間空的 → 除了舊椅子沒有任何東西 → nothing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 905, "question": "I haven't been to the movies these days. Are there any good ______ this week?", "options": ["ones", "others", "them", "those"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜ones 代替不特定的複數同類名詞", "explanation": "【句型】one / ones 代替「不特定」的同類名詞；形容詞 + one(s)\n【分析】空格前有形容詞 good，指的是「不特定的好電影」（複數）→ any good ones = any good movies。\n【其他選項】(B) others 前不能加形容詞 good；(C) them 指特定的複數，且不能放在形容詞後；(D) those 前不能加形容詞。\n【例句】These apples are too small. Do you have bigger ones?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 906, "question": "My shoes are too old. I need to buy new ______.", "options": ["one", "ones", "them", "it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "不特定的新鞋子（複數）→ new ones。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 907, "question": "This T-shirt is too small for me. Do you have a bigger ______?", "options": ["one", "ones", "it", "them"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "a bigger + 單數不特定 → one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 908, "question": "I don't like the red cups. I prefer the blue ______.", "options": ["it", "them", "those", "ones"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "the + 形容詞 + ones 代替複數同類名詞 cups。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 909, "question": "Mrs. Wang has two sons. ______ of them go to junior high school.", "options": ["One", "Both", "Some", "Many"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜both of them（兩者都）", "explanation": "【句型】both of + 複數受格／the + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞「兩者都」\n【分析】two sons 剛好兩個，動詞 go 為複數 → Both of them go to ...「兩個都讀國中」。\n【其他選項】(A) One of them 須接單數動詞 goes；(C) Some、(D) Many 用於三個以上，不用於兩者。\n【例句】I have two sisters. Both of them like music.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 910, "question": "Tim has two dogs, and ______ of them are very friendly.", "options": ["all", "both", "each", "one"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "兩隻狗、動詞 are 複數 → both of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 911, "question": "There are two windows in the room. ______ of them is broken.", "options": ["Both", "Two", "One", "All"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "動詞 is 單數 → One of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 912, "question": "My parents are teachers. ______ of them teach at the same school.", "options": ["Both", "All", "One", "Each"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "父母兩人、動詞 teach 複數 → Both。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 913, "question": "Michelle Walden, ______ of the best basketball players in our school history, was called \"Flying Walden\" because she could jump very high.", "options": ["any", "each", "one", "who"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜one of + the + 最高級 + 複數名詞（同位語）", "explanation": "【句型】one of the + 最高級 + 複數名詞「最…的…之一」；此處作主詞的同位語\n【分析】逗號中間是補充說明 Michelle Walden 的同位語：one of the best basketball players「最優秀的籃球員之一」。\n【其他選項】(A) any of 用於否定或疑問，語意不通；(B) each of the best players「每一位」，不能說明一個人；(D) who 引導關係子句需有動詞（who was one of ...），此處沒有動詞。\n【例句】Mr. Lee, one of the most popular teachers in our school, teaches math.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 914, "question": "Taipei 101 is ______ of the tallest buildings in the world.", "options": ["one", "each", "any", "all"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "one of the + 最高級 + 複數名詞 → 最高的建築之一。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 915, "question": "Jeremy Lin, one of the most famous basketball ______ in Taiwan, visited our school.", "options": ["player", "players", "player's", "playing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "one of the + 複數名詞 → players。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 916, "question": "Kenting, ______ of the most beautiful places in Taiwan, has many visitors every summer.", "options": ["who", "any", "one", "each"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "逗號中間為同位語 one of the most beautiful places；who 需要動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 917, "question": "Mrs. Luo: Who put these socks in the refrigerator?\nMr. Luo: I don't know. They're not ______. Ask your son.", "options": ["me", "mine", "my", "myself"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 mine", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞＝所有格＋名詞：mine = my socks\n【分析】Mr. Luo 說不知道，「它們不是我的，去問你兒子」→ 空格後沒有名詞 → mine = my socks。\n【其他選項】(A) me 受格，「它們不是我」語意不通；(C) my 是所有格，後面要接名詞；(D) myself 反身代名詞，語意不通。\n【例句】Those comic books aren't mine. They're my brother's.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 918, "question": "Lisa: Are these your keys?\nMike: No, they aren't ______. Maybe they're Jason's.", "options": ["my", "me", "mine", "myself"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "空格後無名詞 → mine = my keys。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 919, "question": "That's not your seat. ______ is next to the window.", "options": ["Your", "Yours", "You", "Yourself"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "作主詞，yours = your seat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 920, "question": "Ben: Is this your sister's jacket?\nJoe: No, it's not ______. She never wears pink.", "options": ["hers", "her", "she", "herself"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "空格後無名詞 → hers = her jacket。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 921, "question": "Elsa: Do you know anyone from Class A?\nJeff: No, I don't know any of ______.", "options": ["they", "their", "theirs", "them"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜介系詞 of 後接受格 them", "explanation": "【句型】介系詞（of）後接受格：any / some / all / none of + them\n【分析】of 是介系詞，後面須接受格；指的是 Class A 的人（複數）→ any of them。\n【其他選項】(A) they 是主格，不能放在介系詞後；(B) their 所有格，後面須接名詞；(C) theirs 所有格代名詞＝their + N，語意不通。\n【例句】I have many cousins, but I don't see any of them often.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 922, "question": "There are five new students in our class. I've talked to all of ______.", "options": ["they", "them", "their", "theirs"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "介系詞 of 後接受格 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 923, "question": "Dad bought some donuts, and I ate two of ______.", "options": ["them", "they", "it", "their"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "of 後接受格，指 donuts（複數）→ them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 924, "question": "Kate: Have you met Mr. Lin and his wife?\nLeo: Yes, I had dinner with ______ last week.", "options": ["they", "their", "them", "theirs"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "介系詞 with 後接受格 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 925, "question": "Noah: I've had too many cookies. My throat is so dry.\nQuinn: What would you like to drink then?\nNoah: ______ you can get. Just get it now!", "options": ["Something", "Nothing", "Everything", "Anything"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜anything（任何東西都可以）", "explanation": "【句型】anything + (that) 子句「任何…的東西（都可以）」\n【分析】Noah 口很乾，急著要喝東西，不挑 → Anything you can get「你能拿到的任何東西都好」，後句 get it now 的 it 為單數。\n【其他選項】(A) Something「某樣東西」，沒有「什麼都可以」的意思；(B) Nothing「什麼都不要」與口渴矛盾；(C) Everything「所有東西」，不合理，且後句用 it 指一樣東西。\n【例句】I'm so hungry that I can eat anything.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 926, "question": "Waiter: What would you like to drink?\nJack: ______ is fine. I'm not picky.", "options": ["Nothing", "Anything", "Everything", "Something"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "不挑剔 → 什麼都可以 → Anything。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 927, "question": "I'm so bored. I'll read ______ you give me.", "options": ["anything", "nothing", "something", "everyone"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "無聊到給什麼都看 → anything。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 928, "question": "Mom: What do you want for dinner?\nKim: I don't care. I'll eat ______.", "options": ["something", "nothing", "everything", "anything"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "不在乎 → 什麼都吃 → anything。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 929, "question": "After a big party, it took me ______ time to clean the apartment. I'm tired now.", "options": ["enough", "every", "little", "some"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜some + 不可數名詞（肯定句）", "explanation": "【句型】It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V；some + 不可數名詞（肯定句）「一些、相當的」\n【分析】time 為不可數名詞；派對後整理公寓、現在很累 → 花了我一些（不少）時間 → some time。\n【其他選項】(A) enough time「足夠的時間」，與「累」無因果關係，語意不自然；(B) every 須接單數可數名詞；(C) little time「幾乎沒時間」，與「很累」矛盾。\n【例句】It took Mike some time to finish the puzzle.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 930, "question": "The math problem was really hard. It took me ______ time to solve it.", "options": ["some", "little", "every", "few"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "題目很難 → 花了一些時間；time 不可數，不用 few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 931, "question": "The test was so easy that it took Amy ______ time to finish it.", "options": ["much", "little", "many", "few"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "很簡單 → 幾乎不花時間 → little time。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 932, "question": "I need ______ time to think about your idea. Can I tell you tomorrow?", "options": ["many", "few", "some", "every"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、time 不可數 → some time。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 933, "question": "Philip: Is that red car Miss Brown's?\nWalter: Yes, it's ______. Beautiful, isn't it?", "options": ["hers", "his", "ours", "theirs"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 hers", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞＝所有格＋名詞：hers = her car\n【分析】問句問 Miss Brown's（布朗小姐，女性單數）→ 回答「是她的」→ hers = her car。\n【其他選項】(B) his 指男性；(C) ours「我們的」與問句不符；(D) theirs 指多人，Miss Brown 只有一人。\n【例句】This purple pen isn't mine. It's hers.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 934, "question": "Ray: Is that blue bike Mr. Chen's?\nSam: Yes, it's ______.", "options": ["hers", "his", "theirs", "its"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "Mr. Chen 男性 → his = his bike。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 935, "question": "Gina: Is this your mom's cell phone?\nPaul: Yes, it's ______. She left it on the sofa.", "options": ["hers", "her", "his", "she"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "mom 女性，後無名詞 → hers。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 936, "question": "Those seats are Tina and Leo's, not ______. Ours are in Row 5.", "options": ["theirs", "his", "ours", "yours"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "後句 Ours are in Row 5 → 前面說「不是我們的」→ ours。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 937, "question": "Gary is the best teacher I've ever known. No one ______ teaches so well.", "options": ["all", "another", "else", "other"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜no one else（沒有其他人）", "explanation": "【句型】不定代名詞／疑問詞 + else「其他的」：no one else, someone else, anything else, what else\n【分析】Gary 是最好的老師 → 沒有其他人教得這麼好 → No one else；else 放在 no one 後面修飾它。\n【其他選項】(A) all 不能放在 no one 後；(B) another 是形容詞／代名詞，不能放在 no one 後面；(D) other 須放在名詞前（no other teacher），不能放在 no one 後。\n【例句】Is there anything else you want to buy?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 938, "question": "Sally knows the answer, but nobody ______ in the class does.", "options": ["other", "else", "another", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "nobody else「沒有其他人」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 939, "question": "I don't want this one. Do you have anything ______?", "options": ["else", "other", "another", "others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "anything else「其他任何東西」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 940, "question": "What ______ did you do in Tainan besides eating snacks?", "options": ["other", "another", "else", "others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "疑問詞 + else → What else「還有什麼」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 941, "question": "Elise: I need a dress for tomorrow's party, but I don't have one.\nFiona: Why don't you try on my red one? I bought ______ last week.", "options": ["it", "one", "ones", "them"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜it 代替前面提到的特定單數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】it 代替「前面提過的那個特定單數名詞」；one 代替「不特定」的同類名詞\n【分析】I bought ______ last week 指的就是前面提到的那件特定的「我的紅洋裝（my red one）」→ 用 it。\n【其他選項】(B) one 指不特定的一件，但 Fiona 買的就是那件紅洋裝；(C) ones、(D) them 都是複數，與單數 dress 不符。\n【例句】I lost my umbrella yesterday, but I found it this morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 942, "question": "Rick: Where's my phone?\nAmy: I saw ______ on the kitchen table.", "options": ["one", "it", "them", "ones"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "指特定的「Rick 的手機」→ it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 943, "question": "I don't have an eraser. Can you lend me ______?", "options": ["one", "it", "them", "ones"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "借「一個（不特定的）橡皮擦」→ one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 944, "question": "Jack: Do you like my new watch?\nLily: Yes! Where did you buy ______?", "options": ["one", "them", "ones", "it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "指 Jack 那支特定的新錶 → it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 945, "question": "All the dresses are pretty, but I think ______ black one is the best for the party tomorrow.", "options": ["any", "each", "some", "the"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜定冠詞 the + 形容詞 + one（特定的那一個）", "explanation": "【句型】the + 形容詞 + one 指「特定的那一個」\n【分析】在所有洋裝中挑出「那件黑色的」，是特定的一件 → the black one。\n【其他選項】(A) any black one「任何一件黑色的」，肯定句中語意不通，且不特定；(B) each 表「每一件」，與 the best（唯一最好的）矛盾；(C) some 後接複數或不可數名詞，不接單數 one。\n【例句】I like both bags, but the brown one is cheaper.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 946, "question": "There are three cakes on the table. I'll take ______ chocolate one.", "options": ["any", "the", "some", "each"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "指特定的那個巧克力蛋糕 → the chocolate one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 947, "question": "These caps all look nice, but ______ blue one fits me best.", "options": ["the", "a", "some", "any"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "從中特別指出那頂藍色的 → the blue one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 948, "question": "Kevin: Which notebook is yours?\nAnna: ______ one with a cat on it.", "options": ["A", "Some", "Any", "The"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "特定的「有貓圖案的那本」→ The one with ...。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 949, "question": "Alice: This cake is so delicious! Where did you buy it?\nOscar: I didn't buy it. I made it ______!", "options": ["for me", "to me", "mine", "myself"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜反身代名詞 myself（強調親自）", "explanation": "【句型】反身代名詞放句尾可強調「親自、自己」：I made it myself.\n【分析】Oscar 說不是買的，是「我自己做的」→ 用反身代名詞 myself 強調是本人親手做的。\n【其他選項】(A) for me「為我做的」，主詞是 I，應為 for myself；(B) to me 語意不通；(C) mine 所有格代名詞，「我做了它我的」不通。\n【例句】Did you paint this picture yourself?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 950, "question": "Nobody helped Jenny with her homework. She did it all by ______.", "options": ["her", "hers", "herself", "she"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "by oneself「靠自己、獨自」→ by herself。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 951, "question": "Ted: Who cut your hair?\nIan: I cut it ______. Does it look OK?", "options": ["me", "myself", "mine", "my"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "強調「我自己剪的」→ myself。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 952, "question": "Kids, please help ______ to the fruit on the table.", "options": ["yourselves", "yourself", "you", "your"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "對多個小孩說 help yourselves to「自行取用」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 953, "question": "Mike: I heard there are many monkeys in this mountain. But I didn't see any of them last time when I was here.\nCarl: Hope we can see ______ today.", "options": ["another", "others", "some", "themselves"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜some 用於肯定、期望的語氣", "explanation": "【句型】some 用於肯定句或表期望的句子：Hope we can see some (monkeys).\n【分析】Carl 希望今天能看到「一些」猴子 → 期望語氣的肯定句用 some，some = some monkeys。\n【其他選項】(A) another 指「另一隻」，前面一隻都沒看到；(B) others 指「其他的」，前面沒有提到已看到的猴子；(D) themselves 反身代名詞，主詞是 we，不能用 themselves。\n【例句】I'm making cookies. Would you like some?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 954, "question": "We have no eggs at home. Let's buy ______ on the way home.", "options": ["some", "any", "another", "others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、要買一些蛋 → some。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 955, "question": "I heard there are many fireflies here, but I didn't see ______ last night.", "options": ["some", "any", "others", "another"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "否定句 didn't see any。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 956, "question": "There are lots of fish in the river. I hope we can catch ______ today.", "options": ["any", "another", "some", "others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "肯定的期望語氣 → some。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 957, "question": "There are many trees in the park. ______ of them are over fifty years old.", "options": ["Both", "Most", "Much", "One"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜most of them + 複數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】most of + 複數受格／the + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞「其中大部分」\n【分析】many trees（很多棵），動詞 are 複數 → Most of them are ...「其中大部分都超過五十年」。\n【其他選項】(A) Both 只用於兩者，但樹有很多棵；(C) Much 修飾不可數名詞；(D) One of them 須接單數動詞 is。\n【例句】There are thirty students in my class. Most of them live near the school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 958, "question": "I have a lot of comic books. ______ of them are from Japan.", "options": ["Both", "Much", "Most", "One"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "很多本、動詞 are → Most of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 959, "question": "There are twenty houses on this street. ______ of them is for sale.", "options": ["Most", "One", "Both", "All"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "動詞 is 單數 → One of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 960, "question": "Most of the students in our school ______ uniforms on Mondays.", "options": ["wears", "is wearing", "has worn", "wear"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "Most of + 複數名詞 → 複數動詞 wear。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 961, "question": "Gary: I can't find my pen.\nNina: Is the one on Jack's desk ______?\nGary: Yes. Thank you.", "options": ["mine", "ours", "theirs", "yours"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 yours", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞＝所有格＋名詞：yours = your pen\n【分析】Gary 找不到他的筆，Nina 問「Jack 桌上那支是你的嗎？」→ 對 Gary 說「你的」→ yours = your pen。\n【其他選項】(A) mine 指 Nina 自己的，與 Gary 找筆不符；(B) ours「我們的」不符；(C) theirs「他們的」不符。\n【例句】Is this umbrella yours? It's been here all day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 962, "question": "Sue: I lost my notebook.\nTom: Is the one on the floor ______?\nSue: Yes, it is!", "options": ["mine", "yours", "his", "theirs"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "Tom 問 Sue「地上那本是你的嗎」→ yours。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 963, "question": "Teacher: Whose jacket is this, Ben? Is it ______?\nBen: No, it's Andy's.", "options": ["yours", "your", "you", "yourself"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "後無名詞，問「是你的嗎」→ yours。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 964, "question": "Mom: These are your toys. Put ______ away, please.", "options": ["yours", "they", "its", "them"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "put ... away 中間接受格 them，代替 your toys。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 965, "question": "Nana and Fred are good friends, and ______ are baseball fans.", "options": ["all of them", "both of them", "some of them", "one of them"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜both of them（兩人都）", "explanation": "【句型】both of them + 複數動詞「兩者都」\n【分析】Nana and Fred 恰好兩個人，動詞 are 複數 → both of them are baseball fans「兩人都是棒球迷」。\n【其他選項】(A) all of them 用於三者以上；(C) some of them 用於三者以上的部分；(D) one of them 須接單數動詞 is。\n【例句】Ken and Ray are twins, and both of them like dancing.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 966, "question": "Lisa and Mia are classmates, and ______ love singing.", "options": ["all of them", "each of them", "both of them", "one of them"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "兩人、動詞 love 複數 → both of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 967, "question": "My uncle has two cars, and ______ is red.", "options": ["one of them", "both of them", "all of them", "some of them"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "動詞 is 單數 → one of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 968, "question": "Our team has ten players, and ______ come to practice every day.", "options": ["both of them", "each them", "one of them", "all of them"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "十個人（三者以上）、動詞 come 複數 → all of them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 969, "question": "On the way to work, Natasha was surprised to find she was wearing a white earring on one ear and a gray earring on ______.", "options": ["another", "the next", "the other", "the second"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜兩者：one ... the other", "explanation": "【句型】兩者之中：one ... the other ...\n【分析】人只有兩隻耳朵，前面已說 on one ear，剩下那一隻就是 the other（ear）。\n【其他選項】(A) another 用於三者以上的「另一個」；(B) the next「下一個」表示順序，不適用；(D) the second「第二個」，兩隻耳朵沒有先後順序之分。\n【例句】I hold a pen in one hand and a book in the other.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 970, "question": "Mr. Ho has two daughters. One lives in Taipei, and ______ lives in Kaohsiung.", "options": ["another", "the other", "others", "the others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "兩個女兒，剩下那一個 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 971, "question": "The street has shops on one side and a park on ______.", "options": ["the other", "another", "others", "the next"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "街道只有兩側 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 972, "question": "I have three friends from Japan. One is from Tokyo, ______ is from Osaka, and the other is from Kyoto.", "options": ["the other", "others", "another", "the others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "三者：one ... another ... the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 973, "question": "Cell phones are convenient; every person in my family has ______.", "options": ["it", "one", "them", "those"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜one 代替不特定的同類單數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】one = a/an + 同類單數名詞（不特定）\n【分析】每個家人各自擁有「一支（不特定的）手機」→ has one = has a cell phone。\n【其他選項】(A) it 指特定的那一支，但不是所有人共用同一支；(C) them、(D) those 是複數，every person has 每人一支，且非特定。\n【例句】I don't have a dictionary. Can I borrow one?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 974, "question": "Many students in my class have bikes, but I don't have ______.", "options": ["it", "them", "one", "ones"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "不特定的「一輛腳踏車」→ one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 975, "question": "Kelly: Is there a bank near here?\nLeo: Yes, there's ______ next to the post office.", "options": ["one", "it", "them", "ones"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "不特定的一家銀行 → one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 976, "question": "I like your new bag. Where did you buy ______?", "options": ["one", "them", "ones", "it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "指對方那個特定的新包包 → it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 977, "question": "When Sean came to Taiwan several years ago, ______ people knew about him. But now he is a famous cook in Taiwan.", "options": ["any", "few", "little", "most"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜few + 可數複數（幾乎沒有）", "explanation": "【句型】few + 可數複數名詞 = 幾乎沒有（否定意味）；little + 不可數名詞 = 幾乎沒有。\n【分析】people 為可數複數；後句 But now he is a famous cook 表對比 → 以前「幾乎沒有人」認識他 → few people。\n【其他選項】(A) any 用於否定/疑問句，肯定句此處不合；(C) little 接不可數名詞；(D) most 意為「大部分人」，與 But 的對比矛盾。\n【例句】Few students came to the meeting because it was raining hard.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 978, "question": "The new shop is in a small lane, so ______ people know about it.", "options": ["little", "much", "few", "a little"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "people 可數複數，且語意為「幾乎沒有人知道」→ few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 979, "question": "There is ______ milk in the bottle. Let's buy some more.", "options": ["little", "few", "many", "a few"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "milk 不可數，且需再買 → 幾乎沒有 → little。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 980, "question": "Kevin is shy, so he has ______ friends at his new school. He often eats lunch alone.", "options": ["many", "few", "a lot", "little"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "friends 可數複數，常獨自吃午餐 → 幾乎沒有朋友 → few。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 981, "question": "Sue: Your hat looks so comfortable!\nAnn: It's more than comfortable. If you wear a hat like ______, you won't feel cold on a windy day.", "options": ["I", "myself", "one", "this"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜代名詞 one（同類不定的一個）", "explanation": "【句型】one = a/an + 單數名詞，代替前面提過、同類但不特定的東西；it 則指同一個東西。\n【分析】a hat like ______ 中填 one = a hat，意思是「像這樣的一頂帽子」，泛指同類帽子 → one。\n【其他選項】(A) I 是主格，不能放在介系詞 like 後；(B) myself 為反身代名詞，「像我自己的帽子」語意不通；(D) this 為指示代名詞，本題考點是以 one 代替前面的 hat，選 one 最佳。\n【例句】I lost my umbrella, so I need to buy a new one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 982, "question": "My pencil is broken. Can you lend me ______?", "options": ["it", "one", "this", "them"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "向人借「一枝」不特定的鉛筆 → one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 983, "question": "I like your bag. Where did you buy ______?", "options": ["one", "ones", "it", "that one's"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "問的是對方那一個特定的包包 → it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 984, "question": "These shoes are too small. Do you have bigger ______?", "options": ["one", "it", "them", "ones"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "代替複數 shoes 的不特定同類 → ones。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 985, "question": "______ of the students in my school do not have the experience of going to a foreign country. Only a few do.", "options": ["Any", "Both", "Most", "One"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜Most of the + 複數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】Most of the + 複數名詞 + 複數動詞 =「大部分的……」。\n【分析】Only a few do（只有少數人去過）→ 大部分人沒去過 → Most；且動詞 do not have 為複數。\n【其他選項】(A) Any of… 很少放肯定/否定陳述句句首當主詞；(B) Both 只用於兩者，學校學生不只兩人；(D) One of the students 需接單數動詞 does not。\n【例句】Most of my classmates go to cram school after class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 986, "question": "______ of my friends like basketball. Only two of them prefer baseball.", "options": ["Most", "Both", "Either", "Each"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "只有兩人喜歡棒球 → 大部分喜歡籃球，動詞 like 為複數 → Most。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 987, "question": "I have two sisters. ______ of them are teachers.", "options": ["All", "Both", "Most", "Every"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "只有兩個姊妹，兩者都 → Both。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 988, "question": "______ of the boys in my class has a cell phone. Only Tim doesn't.", "options": ["Most", "All", "Each", "Both"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "動詞 has 為單數 → Each of the + 複數名詞 + 單數動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 989, "question": "Tony: Will you go to Cindy's party tonight?\nJane: No, I have to do my homework. Don't you have ______?\nTony: Well, I already finished it at school.", "options": ["you", "your", "yours", "you're"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜所有格代名詞 yours = your homework", "explanation": "【句型】所有格代名詞 mine / yours / his / hers / ours / theirs = 所有格 + 名詞，後面不再接名詞。\n【分析】Jane 前句說 my homework，問 Tony「你沒有你的（作業）嗎？」→ yours = your homework。\n【其他選項】(A) you 為受格，「你沒有你」不通；(B) your 為所有格，後面必須接名詞；(D) you're = you are，文法錯誤。\n【例句】This is my seat. Yours is next to the window.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 990, "question": "Mia: Is this pencil case ______, Ben?\nBen: No, mine is blue.", "options": ["your", "yours", "you", "yourself"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "後面無名詞 → yours = your pencil case。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 991, "question": "Our classroom is on the second floor, and ______ is on the third floor.", "options": ["their", "them", "theirs", "they"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "theirs = their classroom，後面無名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 992, "question": "Amy forgot her umbrella, so I lent her ______.", "options": ["my", "mine", "me", "I"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "lent her ______ 需名詞 → mine = my umbrella。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 993, "question": "Spring is a wonderful season because ______ is usually warm and sunny.", "options": ["which", "this", "one", "it"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜會考歷屆｜代名詞 it 指前面提到的特定單數名詞", "explanation": "【句型】it 代替前面提過的「同一個」單數名詞。\n【分析】because 子句的主詞要指前面的 Spring（春天這個季節本身）→ it。\n【其他選項】(A) which 為關係代名詞，不能在 because 後當新子句主詞；(B) this 指「這個」，通常指眼前事物，代替前面主詞不自然；(C) one 代替同類但不特定的東西，不是指 Spring 本身。\n【例句】I love my new bike because it is light and fast.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 994, "question": "Taipei 101 is famous because ______ was once the tallest building in the world.", "options": ["one", "it", "that one", "which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "指前面同一棟 Taipei 101 → it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 995, "question": "My bike was stolen yesterday, so I have to buy a new ______.", "options": ["it", "one", "them", "ones"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "買一輛新的（同類不特定）→ one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 996, "question": "I bought a storybook last week, but I haven't read ______ yet.", "options": ["one", "them", "it", "its"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "指上週買的那一本 → it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 997, "question": "You can't push that door open with only one hand. It's too heavy. You have to use ______!", "options": ["all", "another", "both", "one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜115會考｜不定代名詞 both（兩者都）vs. another／one／all", "explanation": "【句型】both 用於「兩者」都；all 用於三者以上；another 再一個（另一個）；one 一個。\n【分析】線索 with only one hand、too heavy：單手推不開，人只有兩隻手，所以要用「兩隻手」→ both。\n【其他選項】(A) all：用於三者以上，手只有兩隻；(B) another：另一隻手，仍是單手；(D) one：一隻手，正是推不開的原因。\n【例句】I have two brothers, and both of them live in Taichung.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 998, "question": "Kelly has two pens. ______ of them are blue.", "options": ["Both", "All", "Each", "Either"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "兩者都用 Both，接複數動詞 are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 999, "question": "This cookie is really good. Can I have ______ one?", "options": ["other", "another", "the others", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "再要「另一個」用 another + 單數名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1000, "question": "There are thirty students in my class, and ______ of them passed the test.", "options": ["both", "either", "all", "neither"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "三十人（三者以上）都通過用 all。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1001, "question": "Ken is going abroad with a woman he met online, though he doesn't know ______ well.", "options": ["her", "each other", "any", "another"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜115會考｜人稱代名詞受格 her", "explanation": "【句型】及物動詞 + 受格代名詞（him / her / them…）。\n【分析】know 後要接受詞，指的是前面提到的 a woman（單數女性）→ 受格 her。\n【其他選項】(B) each other 彼此：主詞須為兩人以上（如 they），本句主詞是 he；(C) any 任何：不能指特定的那位女子；(D) another 另一個：指的是別人，語意不合。\n【例句】I met a new classmate yesterday, but I don't remember her name.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1002, "question": "My uncle bought a new car, and he washes ______ every Sunday.", "options": ["it", "them", "him", "its"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "代替單數物品 a new car，受格用 it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1003, "question": "Amy and Joy have been friends for ten years. They know ______ very well.", "options": ["themselves", "each other", "another", "them"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "兩人「彼此」了解，主詞為複數 They。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1004, "question": "These cookies are for my grandparents. I made ______ myself.", "options": ["it", "they", "them", "their"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "代替複數 these cookies，受格用 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1005, "question": "Our dog Lassie hides under the bed every time the moon comes out. She has been ______ for years, but we don't know why.", "options": ["it", "like this", "like us", "that"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜115會考｜like this（像這樣）指代前述整件事", "explanation": "【句型】be like this：像這樣（指前面描述的情況、行為）。\n【分析】線索 hides under the bed every time the moon comes out：狗每次月亮出來就躲床下，這種「行為狀態」已經好幾年了 → She has been like this for years。\n【其他選項】(A) it：She has been it 不合文法，it 不能當補語代替整段行為；(C) like us：「像我們一樣」，與躲床下的語意不合；(D) that：She has been that 句意不完整（需說 like that）。\n【例句】My little brother cries when it thunders. He has been like this since he was a baby.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1006, "question": "Ray always forgets his homework. He has been ______ since last semester.", "options": ["like this", "it", "this one", "that one"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "指前述「總是忘記作業」的情況，用 like this。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1007, "question": "Lucy smiles at everyone she meets. Her mom was ______ when she was young, too.", "options": ["it", "like that", "them", "like her mom"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "「像那樣」指前述愛笑的特點，用 like that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1008, "question": "Look! You should hold the chopsticks ______, not like that.", "options": ["this", "it", "like this", "them"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "示範「像這樣」拿筷子，用 like this。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1009, "question": "We couldn't find bus stops on ______ side of this road, so we decided to go to the next street.", "options": ["both", "neither", "any", "either"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜講義錯題｜either + 單數名詞（否定句中＝兩者皆不）", "explanation": "【句型】either + 單數名詞（兩者中任一）；not … either ＝ neither（兩者都不）；both + 複數名詞\n【分析】馬路有兩側，後接單數 side，且句中已有否定 couldn't → either side（兩邊都找不到）。\n【其他選項】(A) both 要接複數 sides；(B) neither 本身否定，和 couldn't 形成雙重否定；(C) any 用於三者以上，馬路只有兩側。\n【例句】I don't like either of the two movies.\n備註：講義 p.317", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1010, "question": "There are tall trees on ______ sides of the river.", "options": ["either", "each", "both", "every"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 1（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "後接複數 sides，用 both。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1011, "question": "I tried on two pairs of shoes, but ______ of them fit me, so I bought nothing.", "options": ["neither", "either", "both", "none"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 2（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "兩者都不合且無否定詞，用 neither。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1012, "question": "Sam has two sisters, but he doesn't talk to ______ of them very often.", "options": ["neither", "both", "any", "either"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞｜類似題 3（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "已有否定 doesn't，兩者用 either。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞"}, {"id": 1013, "question": "For Mike, the price is ______ important thing when he shops for jeans. He cares even more about the shape and the size of the pockets.", "options": ["the more", "the most", "the less", "the least"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜the least + 形容詞（最不……）", "explanation": "【句型】the least + 形容詞 = 最不……（最高級的相反）。\n【分析】後句 He cares even more about the shape and the size（更在意款式和口袋大小）→ 價格是「最不重要」的事 → the least important。\n【其他選項】(A)(C) the more / the less 為比較級，不用在 the ___ thing 這種三者以上的最高級句中；(B) the most important 與後句「更在意別的」矛盾。\n【例句】For me, math is the least interesting subject.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1014, "question": "Ben never studies for tests. For him, grades are the ______ important thing in school.", "options": ["less", "least", "more", "most"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "從不讀書 → 成績最不重要 → least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1015, "question": "This is the ______ expensive phone in the store; it costs only NT$2,000.", "options": ["least", "most", "more", "less"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "只要兩千元 → 最便宜（最不貴）→ least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1016, "question": "Of all the sports, swimming is the ______ popular one in my class. Almost everyone loves it.", "options": ["least", "less", "most", "more"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "幾乎人人都愛 → 最受歡迎 → most。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1017, "question": "My daughter is much ______ now. The pants she wore last year are already too short for her.", "options": ["higher", "longer", "older", "taller"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜much + 比較級；tall 描述人身高", "explanation": "【句型】much + 比較級（……得多）；人的身高用 tall/taller。\n【分析】去年的褲子現在太短了 → 女兒長高了很多 → much taller。\n【其他選項】(A) higher 多用於物體離地高度，不用來說人長高；(B) longer 描述長度，不用於人；(C) older 雖然一年後確實變老，但不能解釋褲子變短的原因。\n【例句】Tom is much taller than his little brother.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1018, "question": "Jason grew a lot last year. He is much ______ than his father now.", "options": ["higher", "taller", "longer", "older"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "人長高 → taller。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1019, "question": "The kite flew ______ and ______ into the sky.", "options": ["taller; taller", "longer; longer", "higher; higher", "bigger; bigger"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "物體離地越來越高 → higher and higher。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1020, "question": "Your hair is much ______ now. Do you want a haircut?", "options": ["taller", "longer", "higher", "older"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "頭髮變長 → longer。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1021, "question": "The jacket is ______ than the dress or the pants.", "options": ["expensive", "very expensive", "more expensive", "the most expensive"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜比較級 more + 形容詞 + than", "explanation": "【句型】A + be + 比較級 + than + B；多音節形容詞用 more + adj.。\n【分析】句中有 than → 用比較級 more expensive。\n【其他選項】(A) 原級不可接 than；(B) very 修飾原級，不能接 than；(D) 最高級不能與 than 連用。\n【例句】This book is more interesting than that one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1022, "question": "Riding a bike is ______ than driving a car for the earth.", "options": ["good", "better", "best", "the best"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "有 than → 比較級，good 的比較級為 better。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1023, "question": "This question is ______ than the last one. I can't answer it.", "options": ["more difficult", "difficult", "the most difficult", "very difficult"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "有 than → more difficult。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1024, "question": "Of all the dishes on the menu, the beef noodles are ______.", "options": ["more popular", "popular than", "the most popular", "very popular than"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "Of all（在所有之中）→ 最高級。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1025, "question": "This restaurant sells the best steak in Taipei; you can't find ______ steak in the city.", "options": ["delicious", "more delicious", "the most delicious", "deliciously"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜否定 + 比較級 = 最高級", "explanation": "【句型】否定詞 + 比較級（can't find more…）= 表達最高級意思「找不到更……的」。\n【分析】前句說這家是台北最好吃的牛排 → 在城裡找不到「更好吃的」牛排 → more delicious（隱含 than this）。\n【其他選項】(A) 說「找不到好吃的牛排」與前句矛盾；(C) 說「找不到最好吃的」也與前句矛盾；(D) deliciously 為副詞，不能修飾名詞 steak。\n【例句】Nobody in my class runs faster than Eric.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1026, "question": "Grace is the smartest girl in our school. No one is ______ than she is.", "options": ["smart", "smarter", "smartest", "the smartest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "No one + 比較級 = 最高級語意 → smarter。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1027, "question": "This is the best day of my life. I have never felt ______.", "options": ["happy", "happiest", "happier", "the happiest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "never + 比較級（從沒更快樂過）→ happier。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1028, "question": "Mount Jade is ______ than any other mountain in Taiwan.", "options": ["higher", "high", "highest", "the highest"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "比較級 + than any other + 單數名詞 = 最高級語意。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1029, "question": "Young boys really grow fast. Both my sons are already ______ than I am.", "options": ["tall", "taller", "tallest", "the tallest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜比較級 + than", "explanation": "【句型】A + be + 形容詞比較級(-er) + than + B。\n【分析】句中有 than I am → 用比較級 taller。\n【其他選項】(A) 原級不可接 than；(C)(D) 最高級不能與 than 連用。\n【例句】My cat is heavier than my dog.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1030, "question": "Today is ______ than yesterday. Let's turn on the air conditioner.", "options": ["hot", "hotter", "hottest", "the hottest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "有 than → hotter（雙寫 t）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1031, "question": "Amy's room is ______ than mine. She cleans it every day.", "options": ["clean", "cleanest", "the cleanest", "cleaner"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "有 than → cleaner。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1032, "question": "Henry is the ______ of the three brothers.", "options": ["younger", "young", "youngest", "more young"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "三者之中 → 最高級 the youngest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1033, "question": "My sister thinks red hair is ______ fashionable than black hair.", "options": ["very", "much", "more", "the most"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜more + 形容詞 + than（much 須接比較級）", "explanation": "【句型】多音節形容詞比較級 = more + adj. + than；much 只能修飾比較級，不能自己構成比較級。\n【分析】fashionable 為多音節，後有 than → more fashionable。\n【其他選項】(A) very 只修飾原級，不能接 than；(B) much 需寫成 much more fashionable，單用 much 錯誤；(D) the most 為最高級，不能接 than。\n【例句】Taking the MRT is more convenient than driving.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1034, "question": "I think playing outside is ______ interesting than watching TV.", "options": ["very", "much", "more", "most"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "interesting 多音節 + than → more。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1035, "question": "This dress is ______ more beautiful than that one.", "options": ["very", "much", "most", "so"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "修飾比較級用 much，very 不能修飾比較級。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1036, "question": "Science is ______ useful subject of all to me.", "options": ["more", "much", "the most", "very"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "of all（所有之中）→ 最高級 the most useful。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1037, "question": "Lucy looks ______ in pants than in a dress.", "options": ["pretty", "prettily", "prettier", "the prettiest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜連綴動詞 look + 形容詞比較級", "explanation": "【句型】連綴動詞 look / feel / sound / taste / smell + 形容詞；有 than 用比較級。\n【分析】look 後接形容詞，且句中有 than → prettier（y 改 i 加 -er）。\n【其他選項】(A) 原級不可接 than；(B) prettily 為副詞，不能接在連綴動詞 look 後；(D) 最高級不能與 than 連用。\n【例句】This soup tastes better than that one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1038, "question": "You look ______ with short hair than with long hair.", "options": ["young", "younger", "youngly", "youngest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "look + 形容詞比較級 + than → younger。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1039, "question": "After a good sleep, Ken felt much ______ than yesterday.", "options": ["good", "well", "better", "best"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "feel + 形容詞比較級 → better。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1040, "question": "The cake smells ______. Can I have a piece?", "options": ["nicely", "nice", "nicer than", "the nicest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "smell 為連綴動詞，接形容詞原級 nice（無 than）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1041, "question": "The students got ______ when they saw their favorite movie star eating at the next table.", "options": ["excited", "excitedly", "exciting", "excitingly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜get + -ed 形容詞（人的感受）", "explanation": "【句型】get / feel / be + V-ed 形容詞 = 人「感到……」；V-ing 形容詞 = 事物「令人……的」。\n【分析】主詞 The students 是人，看到偶像而「感到興奮」→ got excited。\n【其他選項】(B)(D) 為副詞，不能接在連綴動詞 get 後；(C) exciting 表「令人興奮的」，用來形容事物，學生本身不是令人興奮的。\n【例句】Mia got bored during the long speech.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1042, "question": "The baseball game was so ______ that everyone stood up and shouted.", "options": ["excited", "exciting", "excitedly", "excite"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "形容比賽（事物）令人興奮 → exciting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1043, "question": "Sam was ______ when he heard the loud noise at midnight.", "options": ["frightening", "frightened", "frighten", "frighteningly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "人感到害怕 → frightened。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1044, "question": "I felt ______ because the movie was too long and slow.", "options": ["bored", "boring", "boredly", "bore"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "人感到無聊 → bored。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1045, "question": "Rose: Who's that man wearing a white jacket?\nLisa: He's Dr. Wu's son.\nRose: Really? They look ______ like brothers than father and son.", "options": ["as", "less", "more", "not"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜look more like…than…（比較級）", "explanation": "【句型】look more like A than B =「看起來比較像 A 而不像 B」。\n【分析】Rose 很驚訝（Really?），表示兩人看起來年齡相近 →「看起來更像兄弟而不像父子」→ more like。\n【其他選項】(A) as 需用 as…as 句型，不能接 than；(B) less 意思變成「比較不像兄弟」，與 Really? 的驚訝不合；(D) not 不能與 than 搭配成比較句。\n【例句】The dog looks more like a wolf than a pet.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1046, "question": "Mr. Lin is fifty, but he looks ______ like a college student than a dad.", "options": ["more", "as", "most", "very"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "看起來比較像大學生 → more like…than…。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1047, "question": "The cat is as ______ as a small dog.", "options": ["big", "bigger", "biggest", "more big"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "as + 原級 + as。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1048, "question": "For me, math is ______ difficult than English, so I'm better at math.", "options": ["more", "less", "the least", "as"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "數學比較好 → 數學「比較不難」→ less difficult。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1049, "question": "Your refrigerator shouldn't be making loud noises now, but if it ______ does, just give me a call and I'll come check it again.", "options": ["already", "even", "finally", "still"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜頻率/強調副詞 still（仍然）", "explanation": "【句型】still = 仍然、還是（狀況持續）；放在一般動詞/助動詞 does 前。\n【分析】修理後「不應該」再有噪音，但如果它「仍然」有 → still does。\n【其他選項】(A) already 已經，用於肯定句表示提早完成，不合「萬一還有」；(B) even 甚至，語意不通；(C) finally 終於，表示等待後才發生，與語意不符。\n【例句】It's ten o'clock, but Ken is still sleeping.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1050, "question": "I told my brother to turn off the TV an hour ago, but he is ______ watching it.", "options": ["already", "still", "yet", "ever"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "一小時前就叫他關了，他仍在看 → still。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1051, "question": "Hurry up! The movie has ______ started.", "options": ["still", "yet", "already", "ever"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "肯定句「已經開始」→ already。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1052, "question": "We waited for two hours, and the bus ______ came.", "options": ["finally", "still", "already", "even"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "等了兩小時後才來 → finally（終於）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1053, "question": "In the future, there will ______ be greater basketball players than Stephen Curry, but now we believe he is the best!", "options": ["again", "already", "never", "perhaps"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞 perhaps（也許）", "explanation": "【句型】perhaps = maybe（也許），表推測；放在 will 之後、be 之前。\n【分析】but now we believe he is the best 表示「將來『也許』會有更好的球員，但現在他是最好的」→ perhaps。\n【其他選項】(A) again 再次，語意不合；(B) already 已經，不與 In the future 搭配；(C) never 意為「絕不會有」，與 but 的轉折語意不符。\n【例句】It will perhaps rain this afternoon, so take an umbrella.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1054, "question": "I'm not sure where Amy is. She is ______ in the library.", "options": ["never", "perhaps", "already", "again"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "不確定 → 推測「也許」→ perhaps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1055, "question": "Jack promised he would ______ be late again.", "options": ["perhaps", "already", "never", "still"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "承諾「再也不會」遲到 → never。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1056, "question": "I have ______ finished my homework, so I can play now.", "options": ["already", "perhaps", "never", "yet"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "肯定句、現在完成式「已經」完成 → already。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1057, "question": "Angela: Do you know Oscar?\nGeorge: Of course. I know him very ______.", "options": ["often", "little", "young", "well"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞 well（know sb. well）", "explanation": "【句型】know + sb. + (very) well =「非常了解某人」；well 為副詞修飾動詞 know。\n【分析】Of course（當然）表示很熟 → know him very well。\n【其他選項】(A) often 常常，know him very often 不通；(B) little 很少，與 Of course 矛盾；(C) young 為形容詞，不能修飾動詞 know。\n【例句】Lily speaks English very well.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1058, "question": "Ted plays the piano very ______. He has won many prizes.", "options": ["good", "well", "nice", "often"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "修飾動詞 plays 用副詞 well。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1059, "question": "Cindy is a ______ singer. Everyone loves her voice.", "options": ["well", "good", "better than", "best"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "修飾名詞 singer 用形容詞 good。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1060, "question": "I don't feel ______ today. I think I have a cold.", "options": ["good at", "best", "well", "better than"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "feel well = 身體健康。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1061, "question": "Simon is an interesting person. He gets excited ______.", "options": ["easy", "easier", "easiest", "easily"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞修飾動詞/形容詞 easily", "explanation": "【句型】修飾動詞或整個動作用副詞（-ly）；get excited easily =「很容易興奮」。\n【分析】空格修飾 gets excited 這個動作 → 副詞 easily。\n【其他選項】(A)(B)(C) 都是形容詞（原級、比較級、最高級），不能修飾動作；且無 than / the 等比較句線索。\n【例句】My little sister cries easily.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1062, "question": "Ken is a good student. He can answer hard questions ______.", "options": ["easy", "easily", "easier", "easiest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "修飾動詞 answer → 副詞 easily。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1063, "question": "Please speak ______. The baby is sleeping.", "options": ["quiet", "quieter", "quietly", "quietest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "修飾動詞 speak → quietly。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1064, "question": "This math problem is ______. Everyone can do it.", "options": ["easy", "easily", "more easily", "easiest"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "be 動詞後接形容詞 → easy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1065, "question": "I think the road ends here; it won't go any ______. Shouldn't we turn back?", "options": ["closer", "farther", "faster", "longer"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜not…any + 比較級 farther（更遠）", "explanation": "【句型】not … any + 比較級 =「再也不能更……」；farther = 更遠（距離）。\n【分析】路到盡頭了 → 不能「再往前更遠」→ won't go any farther；所以要回頭。\n【其他選項】(A) closer 更近，語意與「路已到盡頭」不合；(C) faster 更快，與路的盡頭無關；(D) longer 用於 no longer/not any longer 表時間「不再」，此處講距離，用 farther。\n【例句】I'm too tired. I can't walk any farther.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1066, "question": "The library is ______ from my home than the park, so I take a bus there.", "options": ["farther", "closer", "nearer", "shorter"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "要搭公車 → 圖書館比較遠 → farther。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1067, "question": "Ann moved to Tainan, so she doesn't live here any ______.", "options": ["farther", "longer", "faster", "closer"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "not…any longer = 不再（時間）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1068, "question": "Please come ______. I can't hear you.", "options": ["farther", "closer", "longer", "later"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "聽不見 → 靠近一點 → closer。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1069, "question": "Jo likes summer the ______ because she has serious problems sleeping in the summer heat.", "options": ["least", "last", "first", "best"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜like…the least（最不喜歡）", "explanation": "【句型】like + N + the least / the best =「最不喜歡／最喜歡」。\n【分析】夏天太熱讓她嚴重失眠 → 最不喜歡夏天 → the least。\n【其他選項】(B) the last 最後的，不用來表喜好程度；(C) the first 第一的，不修飾 like；(D) the best 最喜歡，與失眠的原因矛盾。\n【例句】Of all the subjects, I like history the least.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1070, "question": "Eric likes basketball the ______. He plays it every day after school.", "options": ["least", "best", "last", "less"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "每天打 → 最喜歡 → the best。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1071, "question": "Lily is afraid of insects, so she likes summer camp the ______.", "options": ["least", "best", "most", "first"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "怕蟲 → 最不喜歡 → the least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1072, "question": "Of all fruits, I like mangoes ______ than bananas.", "options": ["best", "the most", "better", "the least"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "有 than → 比較級 better。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1073, "question": "The singer sings beautifully. I cannot think of anyone with a ______ voice.", "options": ["best", "better", "more", "most"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜否定 + 比較級 = 最高級（a better voice）", "explanation": "【句型】否定 + 比較級 = 最高級語意（想不到有人擁有「更好」的聲音）；a + 比較級 + N。\n【分析】前句說歌手唱得很美 → 想不到有誰的聲音「更好」→ a better voice。\n【其他選項】(A) best 最高級需加 the，不能用 a best；(C) more 後需接形容詞，a more voice 不通；(D) most 同樣缺形容詞且需 the。\n【例句】I have never had a better meal than this.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1074, "question": "This is a great school. I can't imagine a ______ place to study.", "options": ["best", "better", "good", "most"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "否定 + 比較級表最高級 → a better place。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1075, "question": "Lucy is the kindest girl. No one is ______ than she is.", "options": ["kind", "kinder", "kindest", "the kindest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "No one + 比較級 + than → kinder。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1076, "question": "That was ______ movie I have ever seen.", "options": ["a better", "good", "the best", "best"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "I have ever seen → 最高級 the best。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1077, "question": "All the packages are ______ checked at the airport to keep everyone safe.", "options": ["careful", "carefully", "more careful", "the most careful"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞 carefully 修飾過去分詞（被動）", "explanation": "【句型】be + 副詞 + p.p.（被動語態中，副詞修飾過去分詞動作）。\n【分析】are checked 為被動，修飾「檢查」這個動作要用副詞 → carefully checked。\n【其他選項】(A)(C)(D) 都是形容詞（原級、比較級、最高級），不能修飾動詞 checked。\n【例句】The cake was carefully made by my mom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1078, "question": "The old pictures were ______ kept in a box by my grandmother.", "options": ["careful", "carefully", "care", "carefuller"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "修飾 kept 動作 → 副詞 carefully。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1079, "question": "The children played ______ in the park all afternoon.", "options": ["happy", "happily", "happier", "happiest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "修飾動詞 played → happily。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1080, "question": "Be ______! The floor is wet.", "options": ["carefully", "careful", "care", "more carefully"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "Be + 形容詞 → careful。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1081, "question": "In this five-person game, the one who finds ______ hidden balls will win the last free ticket for the movie A Born Player.", "options": ["many", "some", "the more", "the most"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜the most + 複數名詞（數量最多）", "explanation": "【句型】the most + 複數名詞 =「最多的……」（三者以上比較）。\n【分析】五人遊戲中，找到「最多」藏球的人贏得票 → the most hidden balls。\n【其他選項】(A) many 很多，無比較意，無法決定贏家；(B) some 一些，同樣無法比出勝負；(C) the more 用於 the + 比較級, the + 比較級 句型或兩者比較，五人中用最高級。\n【例句】The student who reads the most books this month will get a prize.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1082, "question": "In our class, Steve has ______ comic books. He has over 300.", "options": ["many", "the most", "more", "the more"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "全班中最多 → the most。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1083, "question": "Lisa has ______ stickers than her sister.", "options": ["much", "the most", "more", "most"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "有 than → 比較級 more。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1084, "question": "Of the four teams, our team scored ______ points, so we came in last.", "options": ["the fewest", "the most", "more", "many"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "得最後一名 → 得分最少 → the fewest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1085, "question": "It's raining ______. I think you should stay here until the rain stops.", "options": ["politely", "heavily", "clearly", "easily"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞詞義 rain heavily", "explanation": "【句型】rain heavily 雨下得很大（副詞修飾動詞）\n【分析】後句「你應該待到雨停」，可知雨下得很大，rain heavily 為固定搭配。\n【其他選項】(A) politely 有禮貌地；(C) clearly 清楚地；(D) easily 容易地，皆不能形容下雨。\n【例句】It snowed heavily last night, so the roads were closed.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1086, "question": "Please speak ______. The baby is sleeping in the next room.", "options": ["quietly", "loudly", "heavily", "quickly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "寶寶在睡覺，要「小聲地」說話，quietly 修飾動詞 speak。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1087, "question": "The wind is blowing so ______ that many trees fell down.", "options": ["gently", "strongly", "slowly", "kindly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "樹都倒了，表示風颳得很「強烈」，blow strongly。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1088, "question": "Kevin answered all the questions ______, so the teacher gave him full marks.", "options": ["carelessly", "badly", "correctly", "heavily"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "拿到滿分，表示他答得「正確」，correctly 修飾 answered。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1089, "question": "Johnny had been talking about going to England, but never got to go. This summer, he ______ did it.", "options": ["also", "even", "finally", "only"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞詞義 finally 終於", "explanation": "【句型】finally ＋ 動詞：終於（做了某事）\n【分析】前面說他一直說要去英國卻「never got to go」，今年夏天他「終於」去了，finally 最符合語意。\n【其他選項】(A) also 也；(B) even 甚至；(D) only 只有，皆不合「盼了很久終於達成」的語意。\n【例句】After three tries, Mia finally passed the swimming test.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1090, "question": "We waited for the bus for almost an hour. It ______ came at 8:30.", "options": ["already", "finally", "seldom", "still"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "等了快一小時，公車「終於」來了，用 finally。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1091, "question": "Tina practiced the piano every day for months, and she ______ won first prize in the contest.", "options": ["finally", "never", "almost", "hardly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "長時間努力後「終於」得獎，用 finally。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1092, "question": "Ben wanted a dog for years. Last week his parents ______ said yes.", "options": ["still", "yet", "ever", "finally"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "想了很多年，父母「終於」答應，用 finally。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1093, "question": "I sent Lucy two e-mails last week, but she has not answered me ______.", "options": ["already", "also", "either", "yet"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜否定句句尾 yet", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式否定句 have/has not p.p. ... yet「還沒」\n【分析】has not answered 為現在完成式否定，表示「到現在還沒回覆」，句尾用 yet。\n【其他選項】(A) already 用於肯定句；(B) also 不放否定句尾；(C) either 表「也不」，需有前面的否定句呼應，此處語意不合。\n【例句】I haven't finished my homework yet.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1094, "question": "Has the movie started ______? I just got to the theater.", "options": ["yet", "still", "ago", "once"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "現在完成式疑問句「已經…了嗎」句尾用 yet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1095, "question": "Don't worry. I have ______ bought the tickets for the concert.", "options": ["yet", "already", "ever", "either"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "肯定句表「已經」用 already。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1096, "question": "Amy hasn't decided what to cook for dinner ______.", "options": ["already", "too", "ago", "yet"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "現在完成式否定句「還沒」，句尾用 yet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1097, "question": "Anyone who reads Loren's business plan will quickly see some serious problems in it, or ______ feel something is not right.", "options": ["at least", "even", "in fact", "still"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞片語 at least 至少", "explanation": "【句型】A, or at least B：A，或「至少」B（退一步的說法）\n【分析】讀的人會看出嚴重問題，「或至少」會覺得哪裡不對勁；後者程度較弱，為退一步說法，用 at least。\n【其他選項】(B) even 甚至（程度更強，與後項較弱不合）；(C) in fact 事實上；(D) still 仍然，皆不合語意。\n【例句】You should call your grandma, or at least send her a message.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1098, "question": "I can't help you move today, but I can ______ lend you my car.", "options": ["at least", "at last", "at first", "at once"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "不能幫忙搬家，但「至少」可以借車，退一步說法用 at least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1099, "question": "If you can't finish the whole book, ______ read the first three chapters.", "options": ["at all", "at least", "at times", "at most"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "讀不完整本，「至少」讀前三章，用 at least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1100, "question": "The trip will cost ______ NT$5,000, so start saving now.", "options": ["at last", "at once", "at least", "at first"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "「至少」要花五千元，at least 修飾數量。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1101, "question": "Amy: Would you like some coffee?\nBill: No, thanks. I ______ drink coffee. Coffee hurts my stomach.", "options": ["almost", "already", "seldom", "still"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜頻率副詞 seldom 很少", "explanation": "【句型】頻率副詞 seldom（很少）放在一般動詞前\n【分析】Bill 說咖啡會傷胃，所以他「很少」喝咖啡，用 seldom。\n【其他選項】(A) almost 幾乎（需接 never/always 等）；(B) already 已經；(D) still 仍然，皆與「咖啡傷胃而拒絕」不合。\n【例句】My dad seldom eats fast food because it's not healthy.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1102, "question": "Jenny is very healthy. She ______ gets sick.", "options": ["often", "seldom", "usually", "always"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "身體很健康，所以「很少」生病，用 seldom。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1103, "question": "Mark loves sports. He ______ plays basketball after school.", "options": ["never", "seldom", "usually", "hardly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "熱愛運動，所以放學「通常」打籃球，用 usually。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1104, "question": "It ______ snows in Kaohsiung because the weather there is warm.", "options": ["always", "often", "sometimes", "seldom"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "高雄天氣溫暖，「很少」下雪，用 seldom。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1105, "question": "Billy: I've been fixing the computer for over three hours, but it still doesn't work.\nNana: Why don't you take a rest and try ______? Maybe you'll do better then.", "options": ["early", "finally", "later", "once"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜時間副詞 later 稍後", "explanation": "【句型】try later 晚一點再試\n【分析】Nana 建議先休息（take a rest），「之後」再試，後句 then 指休息後那時，故用 later。\n【其他選項】(A) early 早；(B) finally 終於；(D) once 一次／曾經，皆不合「休息後再試」的語意。\n【例句】I'm busy now. Can you call me later?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1106, "question": "Mom: Dinner isn't ready yet. Can you set the table ______?\nKen: Sure, just call me.", "options": ["ago", "later", "already", "before"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "晚餐還沒好，「待會」再擺餐具，用 later。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1107, "question": "The store is closed now. Let's come back two hours ______.", "options": ["ago", "before", "later", "yet"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "一段時間 + later 表「…之後」，用 later。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1108, "question": "I met Rita at the station ten minutes ______, but she has left now.", "options": ["ago", "later", "soon", "after"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "過去式 met 搭配「…以前」用 ago。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1109, "question": "Sandy: How was your vacation in America?\nLinda: It couldn't be worse! I don't ______ want to talk about it!", "options": ["even", "least", "never", "then"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞 even 甚至（加強語氣）", "explanation": "【句型】not even ＋ V：甚至連…都不\n【分析】It couldn't be worse 表示糟透了，所以「連談都不想談」，用 even 加強語氣。\n【其他選項】(B) least 最少，不能放此位置；(C) never 與 don't 構成雙重否定，文法錯誤；(D) then 然後，不合語意。\n【例句】Tom was so tired that he didn't even eat dinner.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1110, "question": "The test was so easy that ______ my little brother could answer the questions.", "options": ["even", "still", "yet", "ever"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "「甚至連」弟弟都會，even 加強語氣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1111, "question": "Sam left in a hurry. He didn't ______ say goodbye to us.", "options": ["never", "even", "also", "too"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "not even「甚至連…都沒」，匆忙到連再見都沒說。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1112, "question": "This phone is ______ more expensive than the one I bought last year.", "options": ["very", "many", "even", "so"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "even 可修飾比較級表「更加」；very、so 不能修飾比較級，many 修飾名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1113, "question": "Steve was ______ late for school this morning; the bell rang right after he walked into the classroom.", "options": ["almost", "already", "really", "seldom"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜副詞 almost 差點", "explanation": "【句型】almost ＋ adj./V：差一點、幾乎\n【分析】他一走進教室鐘就響了（right after），表示他「差點」遲到，但沒遲到，用 almost。\n【其他選項】(B) already 已經遲到，與鐘聲在他進教室後才響矛盾；(C) really 真的遲到，同樣矛盾；(D) seldom 很少，與 this morning 單一事件不合。\n【例句】I almost missed the train, but I got on it just in time.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1114, "question": "Lily ______ fell off her bike, but she caught the handle just in time.", "options": ["almost", "already", "seldom", "ever"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "及時抓住把手，表示「差點」跌倒，用 almost。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1115, "question": "It's ______ ten o'clock. We should go to bed soon.", "options": ["never", "hardly", "almost", "yet"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "「快要」十點了，almost 修飾時間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1116, "question": "Hurry up! The movie has ______ started.", "options": ["almost", "already", "yet", "seldom"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "現在完成式「已經」開始，用 already；almost 不放 has 與 p.p. 之間表此意。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1117, "question": "Bobby: Where's the food I ordered? I've waited for thirty minutes!\nWaiter: I'm really sorry, but the kitchen is very busy. You'll have it ______.", "options": ["already", "early", "once", "soon"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜時間副詞 soon 很快", "explanation": "【句型】未來式 will ＋ V ... soon：很快就會…\n【分析】服務生道歉並說明廚房很忙，「很快」就會上菜，You'll（未來式）搭配 soon。\n【其他選項】(A) already 已經，不與未來式搭配；(B) early 提早，語意不合（已經等很久）；(C) once 一次／曾經，不合語意。\n【例句】Don't worry. The bus will come soon.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1118, "question": "Get well ______! We all miss you at school.", "options": ["soon", "ago", "yet", "already"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "Get well soon「早日康復」，soon 表很快。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1119, "question": "Mom is on her way home. She'll be here ______.", "options": ["ago", "yet", "soon", "ever"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "未來式 she'll be here 搭配 soon「很快」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1120, "question": "Vivian got up ______ this morning to catch the first train.", "options": ["soon", "early", "late", "yet"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "為了趕第一班車而「早」起，get up early。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1121, "question": "Gina worked late and was worried she might not be able to catch the bus. ______, she saw a bus coming just after she arrived at the bus station.", "options": ["Luckily", "Quickly", "Safely", "Truly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜句首副詞 Luckily 幸運地", "explanation": "【句型】句首副詞＋逗點，修飾整句（表說話者的看法）\n【分析】她擔心趕不上公車，結果一到站就看到公車來了，「幸運地」最合語意。\n【其他選項】(B) Quickly 快速地；(C) Safely 安全地；(D) Truly 真正地，皆無法表達「運氣好」的轉折。\n【例句】Luckily, nobody was hurt in the accident.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1122, "question": "I forgot my umbrella this morning. ______, it didn't rain all day.", "options": ["Sadly", "Luckily", "Slowly", "Loudly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "忘了帶傘但沒下雨，「幸運地」用 Luckily。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1123, "question": "We planned a picnic for Sunday. ______, it rained heavily, so we stayed home.", "options": ["Luckily", "Happily", "Unluckily", "Easily"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "下大雨只好待在家，「不幸地」用 Unluckily。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1124, "question": "Leo studied hard for weeks. ______, he passed the test with a high score.", "options": ["Finally", "Rudely", "Sadly", "Lazily"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "努力數週後「終於」高分通過，用 Finally。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1125, "question": "The boss called from the airport an hour ______, so I guess he will arrive at the office soon.", "options": ["after", "ago", "before", "later"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜時間副詞 ago（過去式）", "explanation": "【句型】一段時間＋ago：…以前（搭配過去式）\n【分析】called 為過去式，「一小時前」從機場打電話來，所以很快會到辦公室，用 an hour ago。\n【其他選項】(A) after 須接受詞或作連接詞；(C) before 單獨用時多搭配完成式，表「以前某時」，此處語意不精確；(D) later 表「…之後」，與過去式 called 及後句語意不合。\n【例句】Jason left the classroom five minutes ago.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1126, "question": "My grandparents moved to Tainan twenty years ______.", "options": ["ago", "later", "after", "since"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "過去式 moved 搭配「二十年前」，用 ago。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1127, "question": "Joe started learning Japanese in 2022. Three years ______, he went to study in Tokyo.", "options": ["ago", "before", "later", "yet"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "以過去某時點為準「三年後」，用 later。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1128, "question": "Ivy: When did you see Mr. Lin?\nPeter: About ten minutes ______. He was in the office.", "options": ["later", "after", "soon", "ago"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "回答過去時間「十分鐘前」用 ago。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1129, "question": "This kind of animal is ______ seen in everyday life because it lives 4,000m under the sea and is hard to find.", "options": ["commonly", "possibly", "seldom", "still"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜頻率副詞 seldom 很少", "explanation": "【句型】be ＋ seldom ＋ p.p.（被動語態中頻率副詞放 be 動詞後）\n【分析】because 後說牠住在深海、很難找到，所以在日常生活中「很少」被看到，用 seldom。\n【其他選項】(A) commonly 常常地，與「很難找到」矛盾；(B) possibly 可能地；(D) still 仍然，皆不合因果。\n【例句】This old road is seldom used now.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1130, "question": "Mr. Chen is a very busy doctor. He is ______ at home before 10 p.m.", "options": ["always", "seldom", "usually", "often"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "醫生很忙，所以「很少」十點前在家，用 seldom。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1131, "question": "Grace is ______ late for school. She gets up at six every morning.", "options": ["often", "usually", "always", "seldom"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "每天六點起床，所以「很少」遲到，用 seldom。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1132, "question": "This song is ______ heard on the radio. Everyone knows it.", "options": ["often", "seldom", "never", "hardly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "大家都知道這首歌，因為「常常」在廣播聽到，用 often。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1133, "question": "Marsha thought her friends would do something ______ to celebrate her birthday, but they just gave her a little card.", "options": ["correct", "honest", "quick", "special"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜something ＋ adj. 後位修飾", "explanation": "【句型】something/anything/nothing ＋ 形容詞（形容詞放後面修飾）\n【分析】but 後說朋友只給了一張小卡片，表示她原本期待「特別的」慶祝，用 something special。\n【其他選項】(A) correct 正確的；(B) honest 誠實的；(C) quick 快速的，皆不合「期待慶生」語意。\n【例句】Let's do something fun this weekend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1134, "question": "I'm thirsty. Can I have something ______ to drink?", "options": ["cold", "hungry", "busy", "sleepy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "something＋adj.，口渴想喝「冷的」東西。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1135, "question": "The news report was boring. There was ______ in it.", "options": ["interesting nothing", "nothing interesting", "something boring", "anything new"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "nothing＋adj.，形容詞放後面，「沒有有趣的事」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1136, "question": "Did you see ______ at the night market last night?", "options": ["strange anything", "something stranger", "anything strange", "any strange thing it"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "疑問句用 anything，形容詞放其後：anything strange。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1137, "question": "When I am hungry, any food looks ______ to me.", "options": ["common", "delicious", "simple", "honest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜連綴動詞 look ＋ adj.", "explanation": "【句型】連綴動詞 look/smell/taste/sound/feel ＋ 形容詞\n【分析】肚子餓的時候，任何食物看起來都很「美味」，looks delicious 最合理。\n【其他選項】(A) common 普通的；(C) simple 簡單的；(D) honest 誠實的，皆與「餓」無因果關係。\n【例句】The cake smells sweet and looks delicious.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1138, "question": "You look ______. Did you stay up late last night?", "options": ["tired", "tiredly", "tiring", "tire"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "連綴動詞 look 後接形容詞，人覺得累用 tired。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1139, "question": "This new song sounds ______. Let's listen to it again.", "options": ["badly", "nicely", "great", "greatly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "sound 為連綴動詞，後接形容詞 great。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1140, "question": "The milk smells ______. Don't drink it.", "options": ["fresh", "sweet", "delicious", "bad"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "叫你別喝，表示牛奶聞起來「壞了」，smell bad。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1141, "question": "The town looks very ______ now. It has changed a lot.", "options": ["serious", "worried", "favorite", "different"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜look ＋ adj.（different 不同的）", "explanation": "【句型】連綴動詞 look ＋ 形容詞\n【分析】後句說「它改變很多」（has changed a lot），所以小鎮現在看起來很「不一樣」，用 different。\n【其他選項】(A) serious 嚴肅的；(B) worried 擔心的（形容人）；(C) favorite 最喜愛的，不能用 very 修飾且語意不合。\n【例句】You look different with short hair.\n備註：本題未使用 too…to／enough／so…that 句型，考的是連綴動詞＋形容詞詞義，建議改歸「形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1142, "question": "Kelly's new house is very ______ from her old one. It has a big garden now.", "options": ["different", "same", "similar", "famous"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "be different from「與…不同」，有了大花園表示不同。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1143, "question": "The twins look the ______, so it's hard to tell who is who.", "options": ["different", "same", "other", "alike"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "look the same「看起來一樣」，所以分不出誰是誰。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1144, "question": "After the rain, the air smells ______ and clean.", "options": ["freshly", "dirty", "fresh", "badly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "連綴動詞 smell 接形容詞 fresh，且與 clean 並列。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1145, "question": "Mary had an accident and was badly hurt. The doctor says it is ______ for her to go to school today.", "options": ["illegal", "special", "convenient", "impossible"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜It is ＋ adj. ＋ for sb ＋ to V（impossible）", "explanation": "【句型】It is ＋ adj. ＋ for ＋ 人 ＋ to V\n【分析】她出了意外、傷得很重（badly hurt），醫生說今天她「不可能」去上學，用 impossible。\n【其他選項】(A) illegal 違法的；(B) special 特別的；(C) convenient 方便的，皆不合「受重傷」的語意。\n【例句】It is impossible for me to finish all this work in one hour.\n備註：本題為 It is adj. for sb to V 句型＋形容詞詞義，不是 too…to／enough／so…that，建議改歸「形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1146, "question": "It is ______ for children to swim in this river. The water is too deep.", "options": ["safe", "dangerous", "easy", "fun"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "水太深，對小孩來說游泳很「危險」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1147, "question": "The MRT station is right next to my school, so it is very ______ for me to go home.", "options": ["convenient", "impossible", "difficult", "terrible"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "捷運站就在學校旁，回家很「方便」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1148, "question": "It is ______ for students to read every day. It helps them learn more words.", "options": ["useless", "boring", "important", "illegal"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "每天閱讀能學更多字，所以很「重要」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1149, "question": "There are five stories in this book. The one about a shy police officer is the most ______ to me.", "options": ["interest", "interested", "interesting", "interestingly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜會考歷屆｜最高級 the most ＋ -ing 形容詞（interesting）", "explanation": "【句型】the most ＋ 形容詞（最高級）；V-ing 形容詞形容「事物令人…」，p.p. 形容詞形容「人感到…」\n【分析】主詞 The one（指那個故事）是事物，表「令人覺得有趣」，且 the most 後須接形容詞，用 interesting。\n【其他選項】(A) interest 為名詞／動詞；(B) interested 用於形容人感到有興趣；(D) interestingly 為副詞，不能當補語。\n【例句】This is the most exciting game I have ever watched.\n備註：本題考最高級與 -ing／-ed 形容詞，與 too…to／enough／so…that 無關，建議改歸「形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1150, "question": "Of all the subjects, science is the most ______ to Mia. She always falls asleep in class.", "options": ["bored", "boring", "bore", "boringly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "事物令人覺得無聊用 boring，the most＋adj.。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1151, "question": "Everyone was ______ when they heard the news about the typhoon day off.", "options": ["excited", "exciting", "excitement", "excitingly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "主詞是人「感到興奮」，用 excited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1152, "question": "This is the ______ movie I have ever seen. I cried three times.", "options": ["more touching", "touched", "most touched", "most touching"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "最高級 the most＋-ing 形容詞，電影「令人感動」用 touching。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1153, "question": "That Steven lost his job makes his wife really ______.", "options": ["surprise", "surprises", "surprising", "surprised"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜講義錯題｜make + 人 + 情緒形容詞 p.p.（surprised）", "explanation": "【句型】make + 受詞 + 形容詞（受詞補語）；人感到…用 -ed，事物令人…用 -ing。\n【分析】受詞是 his wife（人），描述她「感到驚訝」，用 surprised。主詞 That Steven lost his job 是名詞子句，視為單數，所以動詞用 makes。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) surprise／surprises 是動詞或名詞，不能當受詞補語修飾人的感受；(C) surprising 表「令人驚訝的」，形容事物。\n【例句】The bad news made everyone sad and worried.\n備註：講義 p.260", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1154, "question": "The long speech made the students ______.", "options": ["bore", "bored", "boring", "bores"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "學生（人）感到無聊，用 bored。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1155, "question": "The ending of the movie was so ______ that many people cried.", "options": ["touched", "touch", "touching", "touches"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "電影結局（事物）令人感動，用 touching。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1156, "question": "Getting a full score on the test made Ray very ______.", "options": ["excited", "exciting", "excite", "excitement"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "Ray 感到興奮，make + 人 + excited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1157, "question": "A ______ number of people lose their jobs. Many of them are not ready to face what has happened in their life.", "options": ["surprise", "surprised", "surprising", "surprisingly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜講義錯題｜a surprising number of + 複數 N（-ing 形容詞修飾事物）", "explanation": "【句型】a + adj. + number of + 複數名詞；事物令人…用 -ing 形容詞。\n【分析】空格修飾名詞 number，需要形容詞；「數量令人驚訝」是事物帶給人的感覺，用 surprising。\n【其他選項】(A) surprise 是名詞／動詞；(B) surprised 形容人感到驚訝；(D) surprisingly 是副詞，不能修飾名詞。\n【例句】An amazing number of tourists visit Jiufen every weekend.\n備註：講義 p.261", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1158, "question": "It's ______ that a ten-year-old boy can speak five languages.", "options": ["amazed", "amazing", "amaze", "amazingly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "事情令人驚奇，用 -ing 形容詞 amazing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1159, "question": "The test was ______ easy, so everyone finished it in twenty minutes.", "options": ["surprising", "surprised", "surprisingly", "surprise"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "修飾形容詞 easy 要用副詞 surprisingly。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1160, "question": "We were ______ to hear that our teacher is leaving the school.", "options": ["shocking", "shock", "shockingly", "shocked"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "人感到震驚用 shocked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1161, "question": "Look at the rainbow! ______ wonderful work of nature!", "options": ["So", "How", "Too", "What a"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜講義錯題｜感嘆句 What a + adj. + N!", "explanation": "【句型】What + a/an + 形容詞 + 單數可數名詞 (+ S + V)!；How + 形容詞/副詞 (+ S + V)!\n【分析】wonderful 後有名詞 work（作品，可數單數）→ What a wonderful work of nature!\n【其他選項】(A) So、(C) Too 不能引導感嘆句；(B) How 後只接形容詞或副詞，不能再接名詞。\n【例句】What a cute puppy it is!\n備註：講義 p.320；本題為感嘆句，清單無對應分類，歸入綜合。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1162, "question": "______ beautiful the flowers are!", "options": ["What", "What a", "How", "So"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "形容詞後直接接主詞動詞，沒有名詞，用 How。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1163, "question": "______ interesting story! I want to read it again.", "options": ["What an", "How", "What", "How an"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "interesting 以母音開頭 + 單數名詞 story，用 What an。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1164, "question": "______ nice weather we have today! Let's go hiking.", "options": ["What a", "How", "What", "How a"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "weather 不可數，用 What + adj. + N，不加 a。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "形容詞、比較級最高級、副詞"}, {"id": 1165, "question": "I don't have ______ workers to finish painting the office in two days. Can you find some more to do the job?", "options": ["enough", "few", "most", "total"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜enough + 複數名詞 + to V", "explanation": "【句型】enough + 名詞 + to V「足夠的…去做…」\n【分析】後句「你能再找一些人來做嗎？」→ 表示工人不夠 → I don't have enough workers to finish ...「我沒有足夠的工人來完成…」。\n【其他選項】(B) don't have few workers 雙重否定，語意不通；(C) most workers 後不接 to V 表目的，且語意不符；(D) total 是形容詞「全部的、總的」，用法與語意都不符。\n【例句】We don't have enough chairs for everyone.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1166, "question": "Sorry, I don't have ______ money to buy this jacket.", "options": ["enough", "few", "many", "most"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "enough money to V「足夠的錢去買…」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1167, "question": "There aren't ______ seats in the classroom. Five students have to stand.", "options": ["few", "enough", "most", "little"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "五個學生得站著 → 座位不夠 → enough seats。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1168, "question": "Joe is old ______ to drive a car now.", "options": ["enough", "so", "too", "very"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "形容詞 + enough + to V「夠…可以…」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1169, "question": "Diane had a bad cold last week. She is still too ______ to go mountain climbing with you.", "options": ["busy", "short", "weak", "young"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜too ＋ adj. ＋ to V", "explanation": "【句型】too ＋ adj. ＋ to V：太…而不能…\n【分析】上週重感冒（a bad cold），所以身體仍「太虛弱」而不能去爬山，用 weak。\n【其他選項】(A) busy 忙碌、(B) short 矮、(D) young 年輕，都與「感冒」沒有因果關係。\n【例句】Grandpa is too old to ride a bike now.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1170, "question": "The box is too ______ for Amy to lift. Let's help her.", "options": ["light", "heavy", "small", "cheap"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "too＋adj.＋for sb＋to V，箱子「太重」抬不動。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1171, "question": "It's too ______ to swim in the river today. The water is like ice.", "options": ["cold", "hot", "warm", "sunny"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "水像冰一樣，「太冷」不能游泳。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1172, "question": "Ken was ______ to stay awake during the long movie.", "options": ["enough sleepy", "so sleepy", "too sleepy", "very sleepy"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "too＋adj.＋to V 表「太…而不能」；so 需搭配 that 子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1173, "question": "Sabine walks so ______ in the apartment that sometimes you don't even know she's just passed by. You wonder if her feet ever touch the floor.", "options": ["freely", "lightly", "shyly", "slowly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜so ＋ adv. ＋ that（lightly 輕輕地）", "explanation": "【句型】so ＋ adj./adv. ＋ that 子句：如此…以致於…\n【分析】that 子句說你甚至不知道她走過，懷疑她的腳有沒有碰到地，表示她走路「很輕」，用 lightly。\n【其他選項】(A) freely 自由地；(C) shyly 害羞地；(D) slowly 慢慢地，都無法解釋「腳像沒碰到地」。\n【例句】The boy spoke so quietly that nobody heard him.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1174, "question": "Ray ran so ______ that he won the race easily.", "options": ["slowly", "fast", "lazily", "quietly"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "so＋adv.＋that，跑得「很快」所以輕鬆獲勝。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1175, "question": "Nina sang so ______ that people at the back of the hall couldn't hear her.", "options": ["softly", "loudly", "clearly", "well"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "後面的人聽不到，表示唱得「很小聲」，softly。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1176, "question": "The teacher explained the rule so ______ that everyone understood it at once.", "options": ["badly", "quickly", "clearly", "strangely"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "大家立刻懂了，表示解釋得「很清楚」，clearly。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1177, "question": "More and more cows on this farm are getting sick. The problem is so ______ that the farm will be closed from tomorrow on.", "options": ["heavy", "popular", "serious", "strong"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜so ＋ adj. ＋ that（serious 嚴重的）", "explanation": "【句型】so ＋ adj. ＋ that 子句：如此…以致於…\n【分析】越來越多牛生病，問題「如此嚴重」以致農場要關閉，problem 搭配 serious。\n【其他選項】(A) heavy 重的；(B) popular 受歡迎的；(D) strong 強壯的，皆不能形容 problem 的嚴重程度。\n【例句】The traffic jam was so serious that we were two hours late.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1178, "question": "The math test was so ______ that almost everyone got 100.", "options": ["easy", "hard", "serious", "boring"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "幾乎人人滿分，考試「很簡單」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1179, "question": "Andy was so ______ that he ate three bowls of rice.", "options": ["full", "hungry", "sick", "sleepy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "吃了三碗飯，表示「很餓」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1180, "question": "The ______ was so serious that many people lost their homes.", "options": ["party", "game", "earthquake", "holiday"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "許多人失去家園，是嚴重的「地震」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1181, "question": "Yesterday I went to the beach with my brother. The sun was so ______ that it hurt my eyes!", "options": ["big", "bright", "sunny", "warm"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜so ＋ adj. ＋ that（bright 明亮刺眼）", "explanation": "【句型】so ＋ adj. ＋ that 子句：如此…以致於…\n【分析】that 子句說「眼睛很痛」，可知陽光「太亮、刺眼」，用 bright。\n【其他選項】(A) big 大的；(C) sunny 晴朗的（形容天氣，不形容 the sun）；(D) warm 溫暖的，不會造成眼睛痛。\n【例句】The light was so bright that I couldn't open my eyes.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1182, "question": "The room was so ______ that I couldn't find the light switch.", "options": ["bright", "dark", "clean", "big"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "找不到電燈開關，表示房間「很暗」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1183, "question": "The music was so ______ that our neighbors complained.", "options": ["loud", "soft", "quiet", "nice"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "鄰居抱怨，表示音樂「太大聲」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1184, "question": "The soup was so ______ that I burned my tongue.", "options": ["cold", "salty", "hot", "sweet"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "燙到舌頭，表示湯「很燙」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1185, "question": "Little Jenny was not sure if the strange old man was still following her, but she was just ______.", "options": ["too angry to talk", "too difficult to be with", "too tired to follow", "too scared to look back"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜too ＋ adj. ＋ to V（too scared to）", "explanation": "【句型】too ＋ adj. ＋ to V：太…而不能…\n【分析】她「不確定」怪老人是否還跟著她，原因是她「太害怕而不敢回頭看」，but 前後語意連貫，選 too scared to look back。\n【其他選項】(A) 太生氣而不能說話；(B) 太難相處；(C) 太累而不能跟隨，都無法解釋她為何「不確定是否仍被跟蹤」。\n【例句】The kitten was too scared to come out from under the bed.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1186, "question": "Ben didn't finish his dinner because he was ______.", "options": ["too hungry to stop", "too full to eat more", "too young to cook", "too fast to wait"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "沒吃完晚餐，因為「太飽吃不下」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1187, "question": "The question was ______, so even the teacher needed time to think.", "options": ["too hard to answer quickly", "too easy to answer", "too short to read", "too boring to forget"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "連老師都要想，表示「太難而無法馬上回答」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1188, "question": "Tony wanted to watch the fireworks, but he was ______ and fell asleep at 9 p.m.", "options": ["too excited to sleep", "too happy to cry", "too sleepy to stay up", "too busy to rest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "九點就睡著，表示「太睏而無法熬夜」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1189, "question": "My son has grown bigger and become too ______ for me to carry on my back.", "options": ["long", "heavy", "handsome", "serious"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜會考歷屆｜too ＋ adj. ＋ for sb ＋ to V", "explanation": "【句型】too ＋ adj. ＋ for ＋ 人 ＋ to V：太…以致某人不能…\n【分析】兒子長大了，變得「太重」而我背不動（carry on my back），用 heavy。\n【其他選項】(A) long 長的；(C) handsome 英俊的；(D) serious 嚴肅的，都不會造成「背不動」。\n【例句】This bag is too heavy for my grandma to carry.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1190, "question": "The shelf is too ______ for little Tim to reach.", "options": ["low", "high", "short", "near"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "太「高」所以小提姆拿不到。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1191, "question": "This English novel is too ______ for first graders to read.", "options": ["difficult", "easy", "cheap", "thin"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "一年級生讀不懂，因為太「難」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1192, "question": "The coffee is ______ for me to drink. Let me wait a few minutes.", "options": ["enough hot", "so hot", "too hot", "very hot"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "too＋adj.＋for sb＋to V「太燙而無法喝」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1193, "question": "Jessie saw the movie years ago. It touched her heart so much that she can remember ______ clearly even now. The story is so touching and too sad for her to forget ______. Jessie is usually very busy. Happily, she can finally have free time to watch ______ again this evening.", "options": ["×；×；×", "it；it；×", "it；×；it", "it；×；×"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜講義錯題｜so…that 子句受詞不可省；too…to 句中與主詞相同的受詞要省略", "explanation": "【句型】so…that + 完整子句（受詞不可省）；S + be + too + adj. + to V，若 to V 的受詞就是主詞，受詞要省略。\n【分析】第一格：that 子句要完整，remember 的受詞 it 要寫；第二格：too sad for her to forget，forget 的受詞就是主詞 The story，要省略；第三格：have free time to watch it，watch 的受詞（電影）不是主詞 she，不能省，要寫 it。\n【其他選項】(A)(D) 第一格或第三格省略受詞，句子不完整；(B) 第二格的 it 與主詞重複，錯誤。\n【例句】The box is too heavy for me to carry. / The box is so heavy that I can't carry it.\n備註：講義 p.259", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1194, "question": "This math problem is too difficult for me to ______.", "options": ["solve it", "solve", "solving it", "solved"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "too…to 句中受詞就是主詞 problem，要省略。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1195, "question": "The soup was so hot that I couldn't ______ right away.", "options": ["drink it", "drink", "to drink", "drinking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "so…that 後面是完整子句，drink 的受詞 it 不可省。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1196, "question": "The shoes are ______ for Tim to wear. He needs a smaller pair.", "options": ["so big", "enough big", "too big", "very big that"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "too…to／enough／so…that｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "too + adj. + for sb. + to V 表「太…而無法」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "too…to／enough／so…that"}, {"id": 1197, "question": "Jill: Have you decided ______ you will celebrate your 30th birthday?\nSue: Yeah, I'm going to have a big barbecue party.", "options": ["how", "where", "what", "when"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜WH 名詞子句 how（如何）", "explanation": "【句型】decide ＋ 疑問詞 ＋ S ＋ V（間接問句當受詞，用直述句語序）\n【分析】Sue 回答「要辦一個烤肉派對」，說的是慶祝的「方式」，所以問 how you will celebrate。\n【其他選項】(B) where 應回答地點；(C) what 需要子句缺受詞，但 celebrate 已有受詞 your 30th birthday；(D) when 應回答時間。\n【例句】I don't know how I can get to the museum.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1198, "question": "Tim: Do you know ______ the concert will start?\nLisa: At seven thirty, I think.", "options": ["where", "when", "why", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "回答「七點半」是時間，用 when。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1199, "question": "Mom: Can you tell me ______ you got this cut on your arm?\nRay: I fell off my bike on the way home.", "options": ["what", "who", "which", "how"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "回答受傷的經過方式，用 how。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1200, "question": "Have you decided ______ you will go for the summer vacation?\nI'm going to Hualien with my family.", "options": ["where", "what", "who", "how much"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "回答「花蓮」是地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1201, "question": "Alice: Do you know ______ Grandma is going to visit us?\nWilly: It's next week. She told me on the phone. And we'll take her to the national park.", "options": ["where", "when", "whether", "why"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜WH 名詞子句 when（何時）", "explanation": "【句型】Do you know ＋ 疑問詞 ＋ S ＋ V？（間接問句）\n【分析】Willy 回答「It's next week」，是時間，所以問 when Grandma is going to visit us。\n【其他選項】(A) where 應回答地點；(C) whether 應回答是否（Yes/No）；(D) why 應回答原因。\n【例句】Do you know when the next bus will come?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1202, "question": "Ann: Do you know ______ Mr. Wu is absent today?\nBen: He has a bad cold.", "options": ["why", "when", "where", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "回答「他重感冒」是原因，用 why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1203, "question": "Kim: Could you tell me ______ the library is?\nMan: It's across from the post office.", "options": ["when", "why", "where", "whether"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "回答位置，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1204, "question": "Sam: I wonder ______ the school sports day will be held.\nJoy: On November 20th.", "options": ["where", "who", "what", "when"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "回答日期，用 when。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1205, "question": "George: ______ do you practice playing the piano?\nTommy: When my mom is at home, I have to practice EVERY DAY, but she's away on a business trip this week!", "options": ["How about", "How long", "How much", "How often"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜疑問詞 How often（頻率）", "explanation": "【句型】How often ＋ 助動詞 ＋ S ＋ V？問「多久一次」（頻率）\n【分析】Tommy 回答「媽媽在家時要 EVERY DAY 練習」，是頻率，所以用 How often。\n【其他選項】(A) How about 提議或詢問意見，後接名詞／Ving；(B) How long 問時間長度；(C) How much 問價錢或數量。\n【例句】How often do you go to the gym? — Twice a week.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1206, "question": "Lily: ______ does it take to walk to the MRT station?\nOscar: About ten minutes.", "options": ["How often", "How long", "How far", "How many"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "回答「十分鐘」是所需時間長度，用 How long。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1207, "question": "Dad: ______ do you clean your room?\nAmy: Once a week, on Saturday.", "options": ["How often", "How soon", "How long", "How much"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "回答「一週一次」是頻率，用 How often。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1208, "question": "Jay: ______ is your school from your home?\nEric: About two kilometers.", "options": ["How long", "How often", "How far", "How soon"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "回答距離「兩公里」，用 How far。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1209, "question": "Ken: ______ is a boat ticket for children?\nPaul: How old is your child? It's free for kids under three years old.", "options": ["How long", "How much", "How often", "How soon"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜疑問詞 How much（價錢）", "explanation": "【句型】How much ＋ be ＋ 物品？詢問價錢\n【分析】Paul 回答「三歲以下免費（free）」，說的是票價，所以問 How much is a boat ticket。\n【其他選項】(A) How long 問時間長度；(C) How often 問頻率；(D) How soon 問「多快、還要多久」。\n【例句】How much is this T-shirt? — It's 300 dollars.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1210, "question": "Customer: ______ are these apples?\nClerk: Three for 100 dollars.", "options": ["How many", "How old", "How much", "How long"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "回答價錢「三顆一百元」，用 How much。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1211, "question": "Nick: ______ will the train arrive?\nStaff: In five minutes.", "options": ["How soon", "How much", "How often", "How far"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "回答「五分鐘後」，問還要多快，用 How soon。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1212, "question": "Teacher: ______ students are there in your class?\nJoe: Twenty-eight.", "options": ["How much", "How long", "How often", "How many"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "students 為可數名詞，問數量用 How many。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1213, "question": "We are surprised that Sally and Ray decided to get married. No one knows ______. They often fight with each other and are unhappy together.", "options": ["why", "where", "when", "how"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜WH 名詞子句（省略）why", "explanation": "【句型】know ＋ 疑問詞（＋ S ＋ V）；此處 why 後省略 they decided to get married\n【分析】大家很驚訝，因為他們常吵架、在一起不快樂，所以沒人知道他們「為什麼」要結婚，用 why。\n【其他選項】(B) where 地點；(C) when 時間；(D) how 方式，都不能解釋後句「常吵架」所帶出的疑惑。\n【例句】Lisa left the party early, but nobody knows why.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1214, "question": "Ray was not at school today, and his teacher doesn't know ______. Maybe he is sick.", "options": ["where", "why", "what", "which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "後句猜測「也許生病了」，是在推測原因，用 why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1215, "question": "I want to visit Sun Moon Lake, but I'm not sure ______ to get there. Is there a bus?", "options": ["how", "why", "who", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "問有沒有公車，是交通方式，how to get there。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1216, "question": "Someone left a bag in the classroom, but no one knows ______ it belongs to.", "options": ["what", "why", "whom", "when"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "belong to 後缺受詞，指「人」，用 whom（口語亦可 who）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1217, "question": "Carson: Bye, girls. See you tomorrow, Phoebe.\nShirley: ______ did Carson say he would see you tomorrow?\nPhoebe: We're going out for a picnic. Do you want to come?", "options": ["What", "When", "Where", "Why"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜疑問詞 Why ＋ did ＋ S ＋ say ＋ 子句", "explanation": "【句型】疑問詞 ＋ did ＋ S ＋ say ＋ (that) 子句？\n【分析】Phoebe 回答「我們明天要去野餐」，說明 Carson 會見到她的「原因」，所以問 Why。\n【其他選項】(A) What：say 後已有完整子句 he would see you tomorrow，不缺受詞；(B) When：時間 tomorrow 已知；(C) Where：回答並未針對地點。\n【例句】Why did Mom say we couldn't watch TV tonight?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1218, "question": "Kevin: ______ did the teacher say about the test?\nJane: She said it would be on Friday.", "options": ["Why", "What", "Where", "How"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "say about 後缺受詞（說了什麼），用 What。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1219, "question": "Ella: ______ did you say we would meet?\nHank: In front of the library.", "options": ["Where", "Why", "What", "Who"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "回答「圖書館前」為地點，用 Where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1220, "question": "Dad: ______ did Tina say she would come home?\nMom: Around nine o'clock.", "options": ["Why", "What", "When", "How"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "回答「九點左右」為時間，用 When。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1221, "question": "Willy found ______ the novel he bought last week was under his bed.", "options": ["that", "where", "whether", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜that 名詞子句當受詞（found that）", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ V（find/know/think）＋ that ＋ 完整句子（that 名詞子句當受詞）\n【分析】空格後 the novel (he bought last week) was under his bed 是完整句子，表示發現「一件事實」，用 that。\n【其他選項】(B) where：子句已有地點 under his bed，不缺地點；(C) whether 是否，與 found 一個確定事實不合；(D) which 為關係代名詞，前面須有先行詞且子句須缺主詞／受詞。\n【例句】Emma found that her phone was in her school bag.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1222, "question": "Mr. Lee told us ______ the field trip was canceled because of the rain.", "options": ["what", "that", "which", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "後接完整句子表告知事實，用 that 名詞子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1223, "question": "I'm not sure ______ Ben will join us tonight. He hasn't answered my message.", "options": ["that", "what", "whether", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "not sure「不確定是否」，用 whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1224, "question": "Sandy didn't know ______ her brother put her umbrella. She looked everywhere.", "options": ["where", "that", "what", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "put her umbrella 後缺地點，且她到處找，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1225, "question": "A-wei: This typhoon is so terrible!\nA-fen: Yes, I'm not sure ______ we can still go fishing tomorrow.", "options": ["who", "what", "which", "whether"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜whether 名詞子句（是否）", "explanation": "【句型】not sure ＋ whether/if ＋ S ＋ V：不確定是否…\n【分析】颱風很可怕，所以不確定明天「是否」還能去釣魚；空格後是完整句子，表「是或否」，用 whether。\n【其他選項】(A) who、(B) what、(C) which 引導的子句須缺主詞或受詞，但 we can still go fishing tomorrow 是完整句子。\n【例句】I wonder whether it will rain this weekend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1226, "question": "Mia: Can you ask Mark ______ he wants to come to the movies with us?\nTom: Sure, I'll call him now.", "options": ["what", "whether", "which", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "問「是否」想來，後接完整句子，用 whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1227, "question": "I don't know ______ to buy for Mom's birthday. Any ideas?", "options": ["what", "whether", "where", "why"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "buy 後缺受詞（買什麼），用 what to buy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1228, "question": "The teacher asked us ______ we had finished the reading report.", "options": ["which", "what", "who", "if"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "問是否完成，後接完整句子，用 if（＝whether）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1229, "question": "Susan: Do you know ______ you have talked on the phone? Aren't you thirsty?\nWalter: Oh, come on! I've only talked for thirty minutes!", "options": ["how old", "how often", "how many", "how long"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜間接問句 how long（多久）", "explanation": "【句型】Do you know + 疑問詞 + S + V（間接問句）；how long 問「多久（一段時間）」。\n【分析】Walter 回答 I've only talked for thirty minutes（才講三十分鐘），回答的是一段時間，且 have talked 為現在完成式，搭配 how long 問持續多久。\n【其他選項】(A) how old 問年紀；(B) how often 問頻率（多常）；(C) how many 後面要接可數名詞，問數量。\n【例句】Do you know how long the movie will last?（你知道這部電影會播多久嗎？）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1230, "question": "Tom: Do you know ______ Mr. Lin has taught at our school?\nAmy: For about ten years.", "options": ["how long", "how often", "how far", "how soon"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "回答 For about ten years 是一段時間，用 how long 問「多久」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1231, "question": "Mom: How ______ have you played video games today?\nKen: Only one hour, Mom.", "options": ["often", "many", "long", "much"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "回答 one hour 為時間長度，How long 問持續多久。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1232, "question": "I wonder ______ it takes to get to Kaohsiung by train. Is it more than two hours?", "options": ["how much", "how long", "how often", "how old"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "it takes + 時間，問「花多久時間」用 how long。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1233, "question": "Jane is going fishing tomorrow. She wants to know ______ the weather will be fine.", "options": ["how", "what", "whether", "why"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜whether 是否（名詞子句）", "explanation": "【句型】know + whether/if + S + V：「是否……」，引導 Yes/No 問句改成的名詞子句。\n【分析】the weather will be fine 是完整句子，不缺主詞或受詞；Jane 想知道「天氣是否會好」，是 Yes/No 的問題，用 whether。\n【其他選項】(A) how 問方法或程度，語意不通；(B) what 後面子句需缺少名詞（主詞或受詞），此句完整；(D) why 問原因，語意不合「明天要去釣魚，想知道天氣……」。\n【例句】I don't know whether Amy will come to the party.（我不知道 Amy 是否會來派對。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1234, "question": "Kevin asked me ______ I had finished my science report. I said, \"Not yet.\"", "options": ["what", "whether", "where", "which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "子句完整且回答是 Not yet（Yes/No 題），用 whether 表「是否」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1235, "question": "We are not sure ______ the school trip will be canceled because of the rain.", "options": ["if", "what", "how", "who"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "子句結構完整，表示「是否會取消」，用 if/whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1236, "question": "Mia: Can you tell me ______ the library is open on Sundays?\nClerk: Yes, it opens at nine.", "options": ["why", "what", "when", "whether"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "店員回答 Yes，原問題是 Yes/No 問句，改成名詞子句用 whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1237, "question": "Nancy: Did the teacher tell us ______ to get to the station?\nSusan: Yes. She said we should meet there at ten.", "options": ["how", "what", "when", "where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜疑問詞 when + to V（何時）", "explanation": "【句型】疑問詞 + to V（when to V = 何時做……）。\n【分析】Susan 回答 She said we should meet there at ten（老師說十點在那裡集合），回答的是「時間」，所以 Nancy 問老師是否說了「何時要到車站」，用 when to get to the station。\n【其他選項】(A) how to get to... 問交通方式，回答應是搭公車、走路等；(B) what to get to...：get to 後已有 the station，不缺受詞；(D) where to get to the station：地點 the station 已出現，重複。\n【例句】Please tell me when to start the test.（請告訴我何時開始考試。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1238, "question": "Mr. Lee didn't tell us ______ to hand in the report. Is it due on Friday?", "options": ["when", "what", "who", "how"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "後句問是不是星期五交，問時間用 when to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1239, "question": "Grandpa doesn't know ______ to send a message on his new phone, so I'm teaching him.", "options": ["how", "where", "who", "whose"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "教爺爺「如何」傳訊息，用 how to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1240, "question": "Lily: I can't decide ______ to buy for Mom's birthday.\nJoe: How about some flowers?", "options": ["how", "where", "what", "when"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "buy 缺受詞（買什麼），用 what to buy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1241, "question": "I want to go camping in the mountains this afternoon, but a typhoon is coming. I'm not sure ______ the road to the mountains will be closed.", "options": ["how", "what", "whether", "why"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜whether 是否（名詞子句）", "explanation": "【句型】be not sure + whether/if + S + V：「不確定是否……」。\n【分析】颱風要來，「不確定通往山區的路是否會封閉」；the road ... will be closed 是完整句子，表 Yes/No 的不確定，用 whether。\n【其他選項】(A) how 問方式，語意不通；(B) what 後的子句需缺名詞，此句完整；(D) why 問原因，與「颱風來了不確定路況」語意不合。\n【例句】I'm not sure whether I can finish the work today.（我不確定今天能否做完工作。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1242, "question": "It's cloudy now. Dad isn't sure ______ we can see the stars tonight.", "options": ["whether", "what", "which", "who"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "子句完整，表「是否能看到星星」用 whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1243, "question": "Ben: Is the new restaurant open today?\nAnn: I don't know. Let me call and ask ______ it's open.", "options": ["what", "where", "if", "why"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "問「是否營業」，Yes/No 問題用 if。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1244, "question": "The doctor will check ______ Grandma's leg is getting better.", "options": ["that", "what", "how many", "whether"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "check whether + 完整子句：檢查是否好轉。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1245, "question": "Anita: I saw Nora in the teacher's office this morning. Do you know ______ she was there?\nBrian: She cheated on tests.", "options": ["how", "if", "when", "why"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜間接問句 why（原因）", "explanation": "【句型】Do you know + why + S + V：問「為什麼」，回答說明原因。\n【分析】Brian 回答 She cheated on tests（她考試作弊），是在說明 Nora 在辦公室的「原因」，所以用 why。\n【其他選項】(A) how 問方式；(B) if 問「是否」，回答應為 Yes/No；(C) when 問時間，但 Anita 已說 this morning，且回答不是時間。\n【例句】Do you know why Ken was late for school?（你知道 Ken 為什麼上學遲到嗎？）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1246, "question": "Mom: Do you know ______ your sister is crying?\nTim: She lost her favorite doll.", "options": ["where", "why", "when", "how"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "回答說明哭的原因，用 why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1247, "question": "Jenny: Can you tell me ______ Eric didn't come to the meeting?\nLeo: He was sick in bed.", "options": ["why", "what", "which", "whose"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "回答生病是原因，用 why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1248, "question": "Nobody knows ______ the old man moved to this small village. Some say he wanted a quiet life.", "options": ["what", "whether", "why", "who"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "後句推測搬來的理由，用 why 問原因。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1249, "question": "Teacher: Does anyone know ______ the famous writer was born?\nMei-ling: I know! In Taitung, right?\nTeacher: You got it!", "options": ["how", "when", "where", "whether"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜間接問句 where（地點）", "explanation": "【句型】Does anyone know + where + S + V：問地點。\n【分析】Mei-ling 回答 In Taitung（在台東），是地點，所以問「這位作家在哪裡出生」用 where。\n【其他選項】(A) how 問方式；(B) when 問時間，答案應是年份；(D) whether 問「是否」，語意不通（是否出生？）。\n【例句】Do you know where Kevin lives?（你知道 Kevin 住在哪裡嗎？）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1250, "question": "Sam: Do you know ______ Mom put my soccer shoes?\nSis: They're under your bed.", "options": ["when", "how", "where", "who"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "回答 under your bed 是地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1251, "question": "I forgot ______ I parked my bike. Was it near the gym or the library?", "options": ["where", "what", "why", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "後句在想地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1252, "question": "Teacher: Who can tell me ______ the first Olympic Games were held?\nAndy: In Greece!", "options": ["when", "where", "how", "whether"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "回答 In Greece 是地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1253, "question": "Alice: How often do you wash your hair?\nBetty: ______.", "options": ["One day", "Twice a week", "Since yesterday", "Three days ago"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜How often 的回答（頻率）", "explanation": "【句型】How often…? 問頻率，回答用 once/twice/three times + a day/week、every day、sometimes 等。\n【分析】Alice 問 How often（多常洗頭），Betty 要回答頻率 Twice a week（一週兩次）。\n【其他選項】(A) One day 是「某一天」，不是頻率；(C) Since yesterday 用於完成式，回答 How long；(D) Three days ago 回答 When（過去時間點）。\n【例句】A: How often do you go swimming? B: Once a month.（一個月一次。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1254, "question": "Ted: How often do you visit your grandparents?\nJoy: ______.", "options": ["Last Sunday", "Every weekend", "For two hours", "Next month"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "How often 問頻率，Every weekend 是頻率。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1255, "question": "Doctor: ______ do you eat fast food?\nPaul: About three times a week.", "options": ["How long", "How soon", "How much", "How often"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "回答 three times a week 是頻率，用 How often。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1256, "question": "Kate: How often does the bus come?\nMan: ______.", "options": ["Every twenty minutes", "Twenty minutes ago", "In twenty minutes", "For twenty minutes"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "every + 時間表示「每隔……」，回答頻率。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1257, "question": "Lisa is new here, so she doesn't know ______ the restroom is.", "options": ["that", "where", "whether", "which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜間接問句 where（地點）", "explanation": "【句型】know + where + S + be：問位置。\n【分析】Lisa 是新來的，不知道「洗手間在哪裡」；the restroom is 後面缺地點，用 where。\n【其他選項】(A) that 後接完整句，但 the restroom is 不完整（缺補語）；(C) whether 後需完整子句，也不合語意；(D) which 需接名詞或在選擇中使用，語意不合。\n【例句】Could you tell me where the bus stop is?（你能告訴我公車站在哪裡嗎？）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1258, "question": "I can't remember ______ my keys are. Have you seen them?", "options": ["what", "where", "that", "whether"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "my keys are 後缺地點，用 where 問鑰匙在哪。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1259, "question": "The visitor asked me ______ the museum was.", "options": ["where", "that", "which", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問博物館在哪裡，the museum was 後缺地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1260, "question": "Ivy just moved to Taichung. She wants to know ______ the nearest MRT station is.", "options": ["whose", "whether", "where", "who"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問最近的捷運站在哪，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1261, "question": "Kevin: ______ sweater looks better on me, the red one or the blue one?\nBetty: The red one, I think.", "options": ["Which", "How", "Where", "What"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜Which + 名詞（二選一）", "explanation": "【句型】Which + 名詞…, A or B?：在有限選項中「哪一個」。\n【分析】句尾給了兩個選擇 the red one or the blue one，在兩者中選一個，用 Which sweater。\n【其他選項】(B) How 不能直接接名詞 sweater；(C) Where 問地點；(D) What 用於沒有限定範圍的問題，有明確選項時用 Which。\n【例句】Which do you like better, cats or dogs?（貓和狗你比較喜歡哪個？）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1262, "question": "Waiter: ______ would you like, tea or coffee?\nMrs. Wang: Coffee, please.", "options": ["What time", "Which", "How", "Who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "有 tea or coffee 兩個選擇，用 Which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1263, "question": "Ray: ______ bus goes to the zoo, No. 5 or No. 12?\nDriver: No. 12.", "options": ["Which", "Whose", "What time", "How"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "在兩路公車中選一，用 Which + 名詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1264, "question": "Sue: There are three pens here. ______ one is yours?\nMax: The green one.", "options": ["How", "Who", "Which", "Where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "從三支筆中挑出一支，用 Which one。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1265, "question": "Lucy: ______ is Ted doing in the kitchen?\nRyan: He's cooking dinner for us.", "options": ["What", "Where", "Who", "Why"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜What 問做什麼", "explanation": "【句型】What + be + S + doing?：問「正在做什麼」。\n【分析】doing 缺受詞，且 Ryan 回答 He's cooking dinner（他在煮晚餐），說明做的事情，用 What。\n【其他選項】(B) Where 問地點，但題目已有 in the kitchen；(C) Who 問人，但主詞 Ted 已有；(D) Why 問原因，回答應有 because 等原因說明。\n【例句】What are you doing now? I'm doing my homework.（你在做什麼？我在寫功課。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1266, "question": "Dad: ______ did you do last weekend?\nJudy: I went hiking with my classmates.", "options": ["Where", "What", "How", "Who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "回答做了什麼事，用 What。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1267, "question": "Amy: ______ are the boys doing on the playground?\nTom: They're playing basketball.", "options": ["What", "Why", "When", "Which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "doing 缺受詞，問做什麼用 What。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1268, "question": "Jack: ______ is Grandpa going to do after he retires?\nMom: He's going to grow vegetables.", "options": ["Where", "How", "What", "Whose"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "do 缺受詞，回答要做的事，用 What。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1269, "question": "I was surprised to know from the newspaper yesterday ______ flowers do not always smell sweet; some can smell like dead fish.", "options": ["that", "when", "where", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜that 名詞子句（know that…）", "explanation": "【句型】know + that + 完整子句（陳述一個事實）。\n【分析】flowers do not always smell sweet 是完整句子，表示從報紙得知的「事實內容」，用 that 引導名詞子句當 know 的受詞。\n【其他選項】(B) when 表時間，語意不通；(C) where 表地點，語意不通；(D) which 不能引導這種陳述事實的受詞子句（也不能當關代，前面無先行詞）。\n【例句】I know that you are trying your best.（我知道你盡力了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1270, "question": "We learned in class ______ bats are not blind.", "options": ["that", "which", "what", "where"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "learned 後接完整事實子句，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1271, "question": "Did you hear ______ our school will have a new swimming pool next year?", "options": ["what", "where", "that", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "後面是完整句子的消息內容，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1272, "question": "The scientist found ______ some fish can climb trees.", "options": ["which", "when", "who", "that"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "found that + 完整子句，表示發現的事實。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1273, "question": "My father told me last night ______ we're going to the Food Festival this weekend. My brother and I felt very excited.", "options": ["whether", "where", "what", "that"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜that 名詞子句（tell + 人 + that…）", "explanation": "【句型】tell + 人 + that + 完整子句：告訴某人某事。\n【分析】we're going to the Food Festival this weekend 是完整句子，是爸爸告訴的「內容」，而且我們因此很興奮，表示是確定的事，用 that。\n【其他選項】(A) whether 表「是否」，不確定，與 felt very excited 不合；(B) where 問地點，但地點 Food Festival 已出現；(C) what 後的子句需缺名詞，此句完整。\n【例句】Ms. Chen told us that the test was put off.（陳老師告訴我們考試延期了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1274, "question": "Mom told me ______ she would make my favorite cake. I couldn't wait to get home.", "options": ["that", "what", "whether", "how"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "完整子句是告知的內容且是確定的事，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1275, "question": "Coach said ______ we played very well in the game. We were so happy.", "options": ["what", "that", "where", "which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "said that + 完整子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1276, "question": "Our teacher told us ______ there would be no class tomorrow because of the typhoon.", "options": ["where", "which", "that", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "完整的消息內容用 that 引導。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1277, "question": "Jacky would like to bring that poor dog back home, but he isn't sure ______ his mother likes dogs.", "options": ["how", "what", "whether", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜whether 是否（名詞子句）", "explanation": "【句型】be not sure + whether + 完整子句：不確定是否……\n【分析】his mother likes dogs 是完整子句，他「不確定媽媽是否喜歡狗」，是 Yes/No 的不確定，用 whether。\n【其他選項】(A) how 問程度/方式，語意不通；(B) what 後子句要缺名詞，likes dogs 已有受詞；(D) which 須在選項中選擇，語意不合。\n【例句】I'm not sure whether my brother is at home now.（我不確定我哥現在在不在家。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1278, "question": "Rita wants to join the dance club, but she doesn't know ______ her parents will agree.", "options": ["whether", "which", "what", "that"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "不知道父母「是否」同意，用 whether。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1279, "question": "Can you check ______ the store has any milk left?", "options": ["what", "where", "if", "how"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "check if + 完整子句，查看是否還有牛奶。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1280, "question": "Steve wondered ______ the girl remembered his name.", "options": ["who", "what", "which", "whether"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "wonder whether + 完整子句，不知是否記得。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1281, "question": "Daisy: I went to Taitung to visit my uncle there.\nGrace: Really? ______ were you there?\nDaisy: For two weeks.", "options": ["How long", "How often", "How soon", "What time"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜How long 問期間", "explanation": "【句型】How long…? 問「多久」，回答用 for + 一段時間。\n【分析】Daisy 回答 For two weeks（兩個星期），表示待了一段時間，用 How long。\n【其他選項】(B) How often 問頻率；(C) How soon 問「再過多久」（未來），回答用 in + 時間；(D) What time 問幾點。\n【例句】A: How long have you lived here? B: For five years.（五年了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1282, "question": "Peter: ______ did you stay in Japan?\nMay: For ten days.", "options": ["What time", "How often", "How long", "How soon"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "for ten days 是期間，用 How long。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1283, "question": "Joan: ______ will the concert be over?\nStaff: In about twenty minutes.", "options": ["How soon", "How long", "How often", "What day"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "in + 時間表示「再過多久」，用 How soon。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1284, "question": "Nick: ______ have you known Linda?\nOlive: Since we were in elementary school.", "options": ["How often", "How long", "What time", "When"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間配完成式，問持續多久，用 How long。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1285, "question": "Alice learned from the TV news ______ Nora Jones was coming to Taiwan the next day.", "options": ["that", "where", "which", "whether"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜that 名詞子句（learn that…）", "explanation": "【句型】learn (from…) + that + 完整子句：得知某事。\n【分析】Nora Jones was coming to Taiwan the next day 是完整句子，是從電視新聞「得知的事實」，用 that。\n【其他選項】(B) where 問地點，但 to Taiwan 已有地點；(C) which 不能引導這個名詞子句；(D) whether 表「是否」，新聞報導的是確定的事。\n【例句】I learned from my friend that the shop was closed.（我從朋友那裡得知那家店關了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1286, "question": "We heard from the radio ______ the MRT would stop running because of the storm.", "options": ["which", "that", "where", "whether"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "聽到的是確定消息，完整子句用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1287, "question": "Grace read in a magazine ______ eating breakfast is good for students.", "options": ["that", "what", "who", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "read that + 完整事實子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1288, "question": "Ken found out from his classmates ______ the field trip was canceled.", "options": ["what", "whose", "where", "that"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "得知的事實內容，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1289, "question": "Kathy: ______ your French class, Jerry?\nJerry: I couldn't understand a word the first month, but it's getting better now.", "options": ["How's", "What's", "When is", "Which is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜How is…?（問情況如何）", "explanation": "【句型】How is + 名詞?：問某事「情況如何、進行得怎樣」。\n【分析】Jerry 回答第一個月聽不懂、現在越來越好，是在描述課上得「怎麼樣」，用 How's（How is）。\n【其他選項】(B) What's your French class? 問「是什麼課」，語意不合；(C) When is 問時間，回答應是時間；(D) Which is 用於選擇，此處沒有選項。\n【例句】A: How's your new school? B: It's great!（新學校怎麼樣？很棒！）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1290, "question": "Grandma: ______ your new job, Tina?\nTina: It's busy, but I like it a lot.", "options": ["What's", "How's", "Where's", "Who's"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "回答描述工作狀況，用 How's 問情況。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1291, "question": "Dad: ______ the weather in Hualien today?\nUncle: It's sunny and warm.", "options": ["How's", "When's", "Which is", "Whose is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "How's the weather? 問天氣如何。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1292, "question": "Coach: ______ your leg now, Danny?\nDanny: Much better, thanks.", "options": ["Where is", "What is", "How is", "Which is"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "問腿的狀況，用 How is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1293, "question": "Emma: ______ umbrella is it?\nSherry: It's Ann's. She forgot to take it home.", "options": ["What", "Where", "Which", "Whose"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜Whose + 名詞（誰的）", "explanation": "【句型】Whose + 名詞 + is it?：問「誰的……」，回答用所有格（Ann's / mine…）。\n【分析】Sherry 回答 It's Ann's（是 Ann 的），表所有者，用 Whose umbrella。\n【其他選項】(A) What umbrella 問「什麼雨傘」，不合回答；(B) Where 不能直接接名詞；(C) Which umbrella 用於在幾把中選一把，回答應是 The red one 等。\n【例句】A: Whose bike is this? B: It's my brother's.（是我哥的。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1294, "question": "Teacher: ______ notebook is this? There's no name on it.\nBilly: It's mine.", "options": ["Whose", "Which", "What", "Who"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "回答 mine 表所有，用 Whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1295, "question": "Kelly: ______ shoes are these?\nAndy: They're my sister's.", "options": ["Which", "Who", "Whose", "Where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "回答 my sister's，用 Whose 問誰的。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1296, "question": "Mom: ______ cell phone is ringing?\nEddie: It's Dad's. He left it on the sofa.", "options": ["What", "Whose", "Which", "How"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "回答 Dad's，問所有者用 Whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1297, "question": "Sarah: ______ does your little sister get up?\nWilly: About six.", "options": ["How often", "How old", "What day", "What time"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜What time 問幾點", "explanation": "【句型】What time…? 問「幾點」，回答用 at + 時刻 / about + 時刻。\n【分析】Willy 回答 About six（大約六點），是時刻，用 What time。\n【其他選項】(A) How often 問頻率；(B) How old 問年紀，且 How old does she get up 不合文法；(C) What day 問星期幾。\n【例句】A: What time does the movie start? B: At seven thirty.（七點半。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1298, "question": "Ann: ______ do you usually go to bed?\nBob: At ten thirty.", "options": ["What time", "What day", "How long", "How often"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "At ten thirty 是時刻，用 What time。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1299, "question": "Lisa: ______ is it today?\nJohn: It's Friday.", "options": ["What time", "What date", "What day", "How long"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "Friday 是星期，用 What day。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1300, "question": "Tourist: ______ does the last train leave?\nClerk: At 11:45 p.m.", "options": ["How soon", "What time", "How often", "Which day"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "回答具體時刻，用 What time。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1301, "question": "Son: Mom, ______ are my glasses?\nMom: Aren't they on the table in the living room?", "options": ["what", "when", "where", "how"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜會考歷屆｜Where 問地點", "explanation": "【句型】Where + be + S?：問「……在哪裡」。\n【分析】媽媽回答 on the table in the living room（在客廳桌上），是位置，用 where。\n【其他選項】(A) what 問事物；(B) when 問時間；(D) how 問方式或狀況，都不合回答。\n【例句】A: Where is my backpack? B: It's behind the door.（在門後面。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1302, "question": "Dad: ______ is your brother?\nMia: He's in his room.", "options": ["Where", "Who", "How", "When"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "回答 in his room 是地點，用 Where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1303, "question": "Joe: ______ did you buy this cap?\nRay: At the night market.", "options": ["When", "Where", "Why", "Which"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "At the night market 是地點，用 Where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1304, "question": "Lucy: Excuse me. ______ is the nearest bank?\nWoman: It's across from the park.", "options": ["What", "When", "Where", "How"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "問位置，回答 across from the park，用 Where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1305, "question": "Alan works hard in his new job, and he wants to know ______ his boss feels about him.", "options": ["how", "that", "whether", "why"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜115會考｜間接問句 how + S + V（how … feels about）", "explanation": "【句型】know + 疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞（間接問句當受詞）；How do you feel about…? → how + S + feels about…（對……的看法／感受如何）。\n【分析】Alan 努力工作，想知道老闆「怎麼看」他 → how his boss feels about him。\n【其他選項】(B) that：引導已知事實，且 feels about him 缺少「感受內容」；(C) whether：whether 子句須是完整句，his boss feels about him 缺少 feels 的補語（feels good/bad），句子不完整；(D) why：還不知道老闆的感受，就無從問原因，語意不合。\n【例句】I want to know how my parents feel about my new haircut.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1306, "question": "Jenny asked me ______ I thought about the new teacher.", "options": ["how", "what", "that", "why"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "think about 後缺受詞，用 what 問「想法是什麼」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1307, "question": "Please tell me ______ you like your new school.", "options": ["what", "which", "how", "that"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "How do you like…? 問「覺得如何」，間接問句用 how + S + V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1308, "question": "Nobody knows ______ Leo was absent today. He didn't call the teacher.", "options": ["why", "how much", "which", "that"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "沒人知道他缺席的「原因」，用 why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1309, "question": "Jill: Have you decided ______ you will celebrate your 30th birthday?\nSue: Yeah, I'm going to have a big barbecue party.", "options": ["how", "where", "what", "when"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜WH 名詞子句：how（方式）", "explanation": "【句型】decide + 疑問詞 + S + V（名詞子句當受詞）。\n【分析】Sue 回答「要辦一場大型烤肉派對」（have a big barbecue party），說的是慶祝的「方式」，用 how。\n【其他選項】(B) where 問地點，答句沒有提到地點；(C) what 用於子句中缺受詞時，這裡 celebrate 已有受詞 your 30th birthday；(D) when 問時間，答句未提。\n【例句】I don't know how my brother fixed the old bike.\n備註：講義 p.275", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1310, "question": "Ann: Do you know ______ the school trip will be?\nTom: It'll be next Friday.", "options": ["where", "how", "when", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "答句說時間 next Friday，用 when。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1311, "question": "Leo: Can you tell me ______ you bought this cap?\nMay: At the night market near my house.", "options": ["where", "when", "what", "how"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "答句說地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1312, "question": "I'm not sure ______ Grandma wants for her birthday. Maybe a new scarf?", "options": ["how", "what", "when", "why"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "wants 缺受詞，用 what 當子句受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1313, "question": "Drew: Do you know ______ as the team leader?\nWendy: It may be Jane.", "options": ["who will our teacher pick", "our teacher will pick", "who will be picked", "who is picking our teacher"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜間接問句：who 當主詞＋被動 will be picked", "explanation": "【句型】間接問句用直述句語序：疑問詞 + (S) + V；疑問詞當主詞時直接接動詞。\n【分析】空格後接 as the team leader，問「誰會被選為隊長」，who 當主詞且是「被選」，用被動 who will be picked。\n【其他選項】(A) 間接問句不可倒裝（will our teacher pick 錯）；(B) 缺少疑問詞，know 後不合語意；(D) 變成「誰在挑我們的老師」，不合理。\n【例句】Do you know who will be invited to the party?\n備註：講義 p.276", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1314, "question": "Can you tell me ______?", "options": ["where is the post office", "where the post office is", "the post office is where", "is where the post office"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "間接問句用直述句語序：where + S + V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1315, "question": "I wonder ______ the window in our classroom yesterday.", "options": ["who broke", "who did break", "did who break", "who was broken"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "who 當主詞，直接接動詞 broke，主動語意。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1316, "question": "Nobody knows ______ to the school party next week.", "options": ["who will invite", "will who be invited", "who will be invited", "who invited"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "who 當主詞且是「被邀請」，用被動 will be invited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1317, "question": "I wasn't able to decide ______ and ended up buying both of them.", "options": ["to buy which of the two skirts", "which of the two skirts should I buy", "which of the two skirts to buy", "I should buy which of the two skirts"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜疑問詞 + to V（which of… to buy）", "explanation": "【句型】decide / know / tell + 疑問詞(片語) + to V。\n【分析】「無法決定要買兩件裙子中的哪一件」= decide which of the two skirts to buy，結果兩件都買了（ended up buying both of them）。\n【其他選項】(A)(D) 疑問詞片語必須放在前面；(B) 間接問句不可倒裝，應為 which of the two skirts I should buy。\n【例句】Could you tell me which bus to take to the zoo?\n備註：講義 p.276", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1318, "question": "Lucy doesn't know ______ for her mother's birthday.", "options": ["to buy what", "what to buy", "what should she buy", "she to buy what"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "疑問詞 + to V：what to buy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1319, "question": "The new student asked me ______ to the library.", "options": ["how to get", "how get", "how did he get", "to get how"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "how to get 表「如何到達」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1320, "question": "We haven't decided ______ for our class trip.", "options": ["where should we go", "we should go where", "to go where", "where to go"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "疑問詞 + to V：where to go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1321, "question": "Of the three parks, ______ do you think is the best for us to camp?", "options": ["that", "what", "which", "where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜疑問詞 which（有限範圍選擇）＋插入語 do you think", "explanation": "【句型】疑問詞 + do you think + (主詞) + V？（do you think 為插入語，疑問詞放句首）；在限定範圍內選一個用 which\n【分析】Of the three parks 表示「三座公園中」，是有限範圍的選擇 → which；which 當 is the best 的主詞。\n【其他選項】(A) that 不是疑問詞；(B) what 用於範圍不限定的「什麼」；(D) where 是副詞，不能當 is 的主詞。\n【例句】Of these two jackets, which do you think looks better?\n備註：講義 p.291", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1322, "question": "Of all the subjects, ______ do you think is the most useful?", "options": ["that", "which", "where", "when"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "在所有科目中選一個，用 which 當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1323, "question": "______ do you think will win the game, the Lions or the Monkeys?", "options": ["Which team", "What", "Where", "How"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "兩隊之中選一隊，用 Which team 當 will win 的主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1324, "question": "There are four cakes here. ______ do you think Mom will like most?", "options": ["Where", "That", "Which", "How"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "四個蛋糕中選一個，且當 like 的受詞，用 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1325, "question": "______ everybody dies is a fact, so live at the moment.", "options": ["It", "That", "Why", "What"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜That 子句當主詞", "explanation": "【句型】That + 完整句子 + V…（that 子句當主詞，表「…這件事」）\n【分析】everybody dies 是完整句子，整個子句當 is 的主詞，句意「人都會死是個事實」→ That。\n【其他選項】(A) It 是代名詞，不能連接兩個動詞 dies 和 is；(C) Why 表「為什麼…」，語意不合；(D) What 須在子句中當主詞或受詞，後不能接完整句。\n【例句】That he lied to us made me angry.\n備註：講義 p.334", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1326, "question": "______ Amy won the speech contest surprised everyone in our class.", "options": ["What", "It", "That", "Which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "Amy won the speech contest 為完整句，當主詞用 That。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1327, "question": "______ he said at the meeting made his boss happy.", "options": ["What", "That", "It", "Because"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "he said 缺受詞，用 What 當子句受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1328, "question": "______ exercise is good for our health is true.", "options": ["What", "That", "Why", "It"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "exercise is good for our health 為完整句，用 That 引導主詞子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1329, "question": "Each of the items on the menu looked so delicious that I had a hard time deciding ______.", "options": ["which one should I order", "that one I should order", "which one to order", "which one I have ordered"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜疑問詞 + to V（which one to order）", "explanation": "【句型】decide/know/learn + 疑問詞 + to V ＝ 疑問詞 + S + should + V\n【分析】每道菜都很好吃，難以決定「要點哪一道」→ which one to order。\n【其他選項】(A) 間接問句要用直述句語序 which one I should order；(B) that one 不是疑問詞，語意不完整；(D) 已點過就不用再決定，時態語意不合。\n【例句】I don't know what to buy for Dad's birthday.\n備註：講義 p.337", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1330, "question": "I'm new here. Can you tell me ______?", "options": ["where to go", "where should I go", "where I went", "to go where"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "疑問詞 + to V：where to go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1331, "question": "Ken can't decide ______ for the school trip, the blue bag or the black one.", "options": ["which should he bring", "which bag to bring", "that bag to bring", "which bag he brought"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "兩者擇一，用 which bag to bring。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1332, "question": "Our teacher showed us ______ the robot by using a computer.", "options": ["how do we control", "what to control", "how to control", "how controlled"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "教我們「如何」操控，用 how to control。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1333, "question": "Could you give me some ideas about ______ so that I know what to expect?", "options": ["you will carry out the plan", "will you carry out the plan", "how will you carry out the plan", "how you will carry out the plan"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜講義錯題｜間接問句語序（疑問詞 + S + V）", "explanation": "【句型】介系詞/動詞 + 疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞（間接問句用直述句語序）\n【分析】about 後接名詞子句，問「你要如何執行計畫」→ how you will carry out the plan。\n【其他選項】(A) 缺疑問詞，句子不能直接接在介系詞後；(B)(C) 是直接問句的倒裝語序，不能放在句中。\n【例句】I'm thinking about where we should go this weekend.\n備註：講義 p.338", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1334, "question": "Do you know ______?", "options": ["when does the movie start", "when the movie starts", "the movie starts when", "when will the movie start"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "間接問句用疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1335, "question": "We talked about ______ for Teacher's Day.", "options": ["what we should prepare", "what should we prepare", "we should prepare what", "should we prepare"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "about 後接間接問句，用直述句語序。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1336, "question": "Can you tell me ______ to the train station?", "options": ["how can I get", "how do I get", "how I can get", "I can get how"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "間接問句語序為 how I can get。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "疑問詞、WH名詞子句、that名詞子句"}, {"id": 1337, "question": "John felt much better ______ he took the medicine the doctor gave him.", "options": ["if", "so", "than", "after"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜時間連接詞 after", "explanation": "【句型】S + V + after + S + V（在……之後）；after 引導時間副詞子句。\n【分析】先吃藥，「之後」才覺得好多了 → after。\n【其他選項】(A) if 如果，felt 為過去事實，不合條件語意；(B) so 所以，因果顛倒（應是吃藥所以好轉）；(C) than 前雖有比較級 better，但「比他吃藥更好」語意不通。\n【例句】I always brush my teeth after I eat breakfast.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1338, "question": "Wash your hands ______ you eat dinner.", "options": ["before", "so", "than", "but"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "吃飯「之前」洗手 → before。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1339, "question": "Mark was tired, ______ he went to bed early.", "options": ["because", "so", "after", "if"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "因為累，「所以」早睡 → so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1340, "question": "Kelly felt happy ______ she heard the good news.", "options": ["than", "unless", "after", "so"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "聽到好消息「之後」覺得開心 → after。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1341, "question": "Shirley: How's your new English teacher? She looks friendly.\nLauren: She is nice! ______, she's the nicest person I've ever seen.", "options": ["Even so", "In fact", "Also", "However"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜轉折語 In fact（事實上，更進一步）", "explanation": "【句型】In fact = 事實上；用來補充、加強前一句的說法。\n【分析】She is nice! 之後補充更強烈的說法「她是我見過最好的人」→ In fact。\n【其他選項】(A) Even so 即使如此，表讓步，前後應相反；(C) Also 也，用於追加另一件不同的事，此處是加強同一點；(D) However 然而，表轉折，前後語意應相反。\n【例句】Tim isn't lazy. In fact, he is the hardest-working boy in class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1342, "question": "I like dogs. ______, I have three of them at home.", "options": ["However", "In fact", "Even so", "Instead"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "補充加強「喜歡狗」→ In fact。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1343, "question": "The test was very hard. ______, Peter got a perfect score.", "options": ["In fact", "Also", "However", "So"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "很難卻考滿分 → 轉折 However。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1344, "question": "Kate can play the violin. She can ______ play the piano.", "options": ["however", "ever", "also", "yet"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "追加另一項才能 → also（也）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1345, "question": "I walked to school every day ______ my dad bought me a bike last month. It's really fun and convenient to go to school by bike.", "options": ["after", "because", "if", "until"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜連接詞 until 直到", "explanation": "【句型】A until B：A 持續到 B 發生為止\n【分析】以前每天走路上學，「直到」上個月爸爸買了腳踏車，現在改騎車上學，用 until。\n【其他選項】(A) after 在…之後，變成買車後才走路，與後句騎車矛盾；(B) because 因為，因果不合；(C) if 如果，不用於已發生的過去事實。\n【例句】We waited in the classroom until the rain stopped.\n備註：此題考連接詞，與副詞無關，建議改歸「連接詞」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1346, "question": "Please stay in your seat ______ the bus stops.", "options": ["until", "because", "though", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "「直到」公車停下前都要坐好，用 until。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1347, "question": "Kevin didn't know how to swim ______ he took lessons last summer.", "options": ["because", "until", "so", "but"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "not…until「直到…才」，直到去年夏天上課才會游泳。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1348, "question": "I'll wait here ______ you come back. Don't be too long.", "options": ["before", "but", "until", "or"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "等到你回來為止，用 until。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1349, "question": "It was an exciting moment for Mr. and Mrs. Wang ______ they learned that they were going to have a baby.", "options": ["what", "when", "whether", "why"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜時間連接詞 when（…的時候）", "explanation": "【句型】S ＋ V ..., when ＋ S ＋ V（when 引導時間副詞子句：當…時）\n【分析】「當」王先生夫婦得知要有寶寶的時候，那是興奮的時刻；前句結構完整，空格引導時間子句，用 when。\n【其他選項】(A) what 引導名詞子句且須缺主詞／受詞，此處子句完整；(C) whether 是否；(D) why 為什麼，皆不合語意。\n【例句】Everyone cheered when the team scored the winning goal.\n備註：本題 when 引導時間副詞子句（亦可視為修飾 moment 的關係副詞），並非疑問詞名詞子句，建議改歸「連接詞」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1350, "question": "I was taking a shower ______ the phone rang.", "options": ["when", "what", "whether", "which"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "「當」電話響時，when 引導時間子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1351, "question": "Rita felt very proud ______ she got first place in the speech contest.", "options": ["what", "whether", "when", "who"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "「當」她得第一名時很驕傲，when 引導時間子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1352, "question": "Please turn off the lights ______ you leave the classroom.", "options": ["whether", "when", "what", "why"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "離開教室「的時候」關燈，when 引導時間子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1353, "question": "Patty spent several days planning to invite Charlie to dinner, ______ she couldn't say a word when they met.", "options": ["but", "if", "or", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜but 表轉折（但是）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V, but + S + V：前後語意相反，用 but。\n【分析】前句「花好幾天計畫邀 Charlie 吃飯」，後句「見面時卻一句話都說不出來」，前後語意相反，用 but。\n【其他選項】(B) if 表條件「如果」，語意不通；(C) or 表「否則／或者」，不合；(D) so 表結果「所以」，花時間計畫不會導致說不出話。\n【例句】I studied hard, but I didn't pass the test.（我很用功，但考試沒過。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1354, "question": "Jason practiced the song many times, ______ he still forgot the words on stage.", "options": ["so", "but", "or", "because"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "練習很多次卻還是忘詞，前後轉折用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1355, "question": "The restaurant is small, ______ its food is famous all over Tainan.", "options": ["or", "so", "if", "but"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "店小但食物有名，語意相反用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1356, "question": "Wendy wanted to call her friend, ______ her phone was out of battery.", "options": ["but", "so", "or", "if"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "想打電話卻沒電，轉折用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1357, "question": "______ machines have been used to pick fruits for a long time, they were not used on strawberry farms until several years ago.", "options": ["Although", "Because", "Before", "If"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜Although 雖然（讓步）", "explanation": "【句型】Although + S + V, S + V：「雖然……，（但）……」，although 與 but 不可並用。\n【分析】前句「機器用來採水果已經很久了」，後句「直到幾年前才用在草莓園」，前後語意相反，用 Although 表讓步。\n【其他選項】(B) Because 表原因，語意不通；(C) Before 表時間「在……之前」，與現在完成式 have been used 不搭且語意不合；(D) If 表條件，不合過去事實。\n【例句】Although it was raining, we still went to the beach.（雖然下雨，我們還是去了海邊。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1358, "question": "______ Ryan is only ten, he can speak three languages.", "options": ["Because", "Although", "If", "Until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "年紀小卻會三種語言，語意轉折用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1359, "question": "______ the test was difficult, most students got good grades.", "options": ["Though", "Because", "Unless", "Since"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "考試難但多數人考好，用 Though 表讓步。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1360, "question": "______ my grandpa is over eighty, he still goes jogging every morning.", "options": ["If", "Because", "Although", "When"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "年紀大卻仍慢跑，用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1361, "question": "Jimmy would not get up for breakfast, ______ his dad had already tried to pull him from his bed several times.", "options": ["although", "because", "if", "until"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜although 雖然（子句在後）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V, although + S + V：「……，雖然……」，although 子句可放句後。\n【分析】「Jimmy 就是不起床吃早餐」，「雖然爸爸已經試著把他拉下床好幾次」，前後語意相反，用 although。\n【其他選項】(B) because：爸爸拉他不會是他不起床的原因；(C) if 表條件，與過去完成式事實不合；(D) until「直到」，語意不通（不是到爸爸拉他才不起床）。\n【例句】She went to school, although she had a cold.（她去上學了，雖然她感冒了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1362, "question": "Ivy kept walking in the rain, ______ she had an umbrella in her bag.", "options": ["because", "although", "until", "if"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "有傘卻淋雨走，語意相反用 although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1363, "question": "Leo didn't say sorry to his sister, ______ he knew he was wrong.", "options": ["although", "so", "because", "if"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "知道錯卻不道歉，用 although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1364, "question": "The baby kept crying, ______ his mom fed him and sang to him.", "options": ["because", "unless", "though", "since"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "媽媽餵奶唱歌卻仍哭，用 though 表讓步。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1365, "question": "Da-fa is cleaning the house ______ some of his friends are coming for dinner.", "options": ["because", "but", "if", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜because 因為（原因）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V + because + S + V：說明原因。\n【分析】「朋友要來吃晚餐」是 Da-fa「正在打掃房子」的原因，用 because。\n【其他選項】(B) but 表轉折，前後並不相反；(C) if 表條件，但他已經在打掃，朋友要來是確定的；(D) so 表結果，順序顛倒（打掃不會導致朋友來）。\n【例句】Amy went to bed early because she was tired.（Amy 很早睡，因為她累了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1366, "question": "Mom is making a big cake ______ it's my sister's birthday today.", "options": ["but", "because", "or", "until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "今天是妹妹生日是做蛋糕的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1367, "question": "Andy wore a coat ______ it was very cold outside.", "options": ["because", "so", "but", "or"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "天冷是穿外套的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1368, "question": "The students are cheering ______ their team just won the game.", "options": ["but", "or", "if", "because"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "球隊贏球是歡呼的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1369, "question": "Ms. Liu usually gives us a lot of homework, ______ she didn't give us any today.", "options": ["but", "if", "or", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜but 表轉折（但是）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V, but + S + V：前後語意相反。\n【分析】「劉老師通常給很多功課」，「今天卻一點都沒給」，usually 與 today 對比、語意相反，用 but。\n【其他選項】(B) if 表條件；(C) or 表「否則／或」；(D) so 表結果，常給功課不會導致今天沒給。\n【例句】Ben usually walks to school, but he took a bus today.（Ben 通常走路上學，但今天搭公車。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1370, "question": "My dad usually drinks coffee in the morning, ______ he had tea today.", "options": ["so", "or", "but", "because"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "usually 與 today 對比，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1371, "question": "Kevin is usually very quiet, ______ he talked a lot at the party last night.", "options": ["but", "so", "if", "or"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "平常安靜、昨晚卻很多話，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1372, "question": "It usually rains a lot in Keelung in winter, ______ it was sunny all week.", "options": ["so", "but", "because", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "平常多雨卻整週晴天，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1373, "question": "Sue is very sick and has to stop working for several weeks. But ______ she feels better, she will get back to work.", "options": ["so far", "since then", "because", "as soon as"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜as soon as 一……就……", "explanation": "【句型】as soon as + S + 現在式, S + will V：「一……就……」（時間副詞子句用現在式代替未來）。\n【分析】「她一覺得好一點，就會回去工作」，she feels better 用現在式表未來，主句 will get back，用 as soon as。\n【其他選項】(A) so far「到目前為止」，是副詞片語，不能接子句，且配完成式；(B) since then「從那時起」，副詞片語，不能連接兩個子句；(C) because「因為」，語意上不是原因而是時間點，且與 But 搭配不自然。\n【例句】I'll call you as soon as I get home.（我一到家就打給你。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1374, "question": "Please text me ______ you arrive at the airport.", "options": ["as soon as", "so far", "because of", "since then"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "「一到機場就傳訊息」，用 as soon as + 現在式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1375, "question": "______ the bell rang, the students ran out of the classroom.", "options": ["So far", "As soon as", "Because of", "Since then"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "鐘一響學生就跑出去，as soon as 連接兩子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1376, "question": "We will start the meeting ______ Mr. Chang gets here.", "options": ["so far", "since then", "as soon as", "because of"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "張先生一到就開會，時間子句用現在式 gets。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1377, "question": "______ Joe looks strong, in fact he gets sick easily.", "options": ["Because", "If", "Though", "When"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜Though 雖然（讓步）", "explanation": "【句型】Though/Although + S + V, S + V：「雖然……，（但）……」。\n【分析】「Joe 看起來很強壯」，「事實上卻很容易生病」，in fact 提示前後相反，用 Though。\n【其他選項】(A) Because：看起來壯不是容易生病的原因；(B) If 表條件，語意不通；(D) When 表時間，語意不合。\n【例句】Though the room is small, it is very comfortable.（雖然房間小，但很舒服。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1378, "question": "______ the bag looks cheap, it actually costs a lot.", "options": ["Because", "Though", "If", "Since"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "看起來便宜實際很貴，前後相反用 Though。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1379, "question": "______ Nina seems shy, she is actually very outgoing with friends.", "options": ["Though", "When", "Because", "If"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "看似害羞實則外向，用 Though。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1380, "question": "______ the question looks easy, few students got it right.", "options": ["Because", "Unless", "When", "Although"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "看起來簡單卻很少人答對，用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1381, "question": "My grandmother believes that young children in big cities get sick easily ______ the air is dirty.", "options": ["because", "before", "but", "whether"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜because 因為（原因）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V + because + S + V：說明原因。\n【分析】「空氣髒」是「大城市孩子容易生病」的原因，用 because。\n【其他選項】(B) before「在……之前」，語意不通；(C) but 表轉折，前後並不相反；(D) whether「是否」，不用來連接原因。\n【例句】We stayed at home because it was raining hard.（因為雨下很大，我們待在家。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1382, "question": "Many people like living in the countryside ______ it is quiet there.", "options": ["but", "because", "before", "whether"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "安靜是喜歡住鄉下的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1383, "question": "The plants died ______ nobody watered them for weeks.", "options": ["because", "but", "until", "whether"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "沒人澆水是植物死掉的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1384, "question": "Dr. Lin says some students can't focus in class ______ they sleep too late.", "options": ["but", "before", "because", "or"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "太晚睡是不專心的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1385, "question": "I've wanted to read The Diary of a Young Girl for months, ______ today I finally borrowed the book from the library.", "options": ["and", "since", "so", "until"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜so 所以（結果）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V (原因), so + S + V (結果)：「……，所以……」。\n【分析】「想讀這本書好幾個月了」（原因），「所以今天終於從圖書館借來了」（結果），用 so。\n【其他選項】(A) and 只表並列，無法表達「想讀很久→終於借」的因果；(B) since「因為／自從」，放在結果前語意顛倒；(D) until「直到」，與 have wanted 及 finally 搭配不自然（應為 until today 而非 until today I finally…）。\n【例句】I was very hungry, so I ate two bowls of rice.（我很餓，所以吃了兩碗飯。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1386, "question": "Jill missed the last bus, ______ she had to take a taxi home.", "options": ["but", "so", "because", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "錯過公車導致要搭計程車，結果用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1387, "question": "Bill has saved money for a year, ______ now he can buy the new bike.", "options": ["so", "because", "until", "or"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "存錢一年的結果是能買新車，用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1388, "question": "It was my first time in Tainan, ______ I asked a local for directions.", "options": ["because", "until", "but", "so"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "第一次來台南所以問路，結果用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1389, "question": "It was very hot when we got to Kenting National Park, ______ we still had a good time there.", "options": ["or", "so", "but", "because"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜but 表轉折（但是）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V, but + S + V：前後語意相反；still 常提示轉折。\n【分析】「到墾丁時很熱」，「我們仍然玩得很開心」，still 提示前後相反，用 but。\n【其他選項】(A) or 表「否則／或」；(B) so 表結果，天熱不會「導致」玩得開心；(D) because 表原因，語意不通。\n【例句】The bag was heavy, but she still carried it up the stairs.（袋子很重，但她還是提上樓了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1390, "question": "It rained all day, ______ we still enjoyed the trip to Yilan.", "options": ["so", "because", "but", "or"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "下雨卻仍玩得開心，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1391, "question": "The line was very long, ______ Rick still waited to buy the ice cream.", "options": ["but", "so", "or", "if"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "隊伍長卻仍排隊，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1392, "question": "Lucy was very tired, ______ she still finished her homework.", "options": ["because", "but", "or", "so"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "很累卻仍寫完功課，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1393, "question": "My sister wants to buy a car ______ she doesn't have enough money.", "options": ["because", "but", "if", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜but 表轉折（但是）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V + but + S + V：前後語意相反。\n【分析】「姊姊想買車」，「但她錢不夠」，前後語意相反，用 but。\n【其他選項】(A) because：錢不夠不是想買車的原因；(C) if：「如果錢不夠就想買車」不合理；(D) or 表「或／否則」，語意不通。\n【例句】I want to go to the concert, but I don't have a ticket.（我想去演唱會，但沒有票。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1394, "question": "Tony wants to play outside ______ he has to finish his homework first.", "options": ["but", "because", "or", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "想出去玩卻得先寫功課，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1395, "question": "Grace likes the dress very much, ______ it is too expensive for her.", "options": ["because", "so", "but", "if"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "喜歡但太貴，前後相反用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1396, "question": "We wanted to see the sunrise, ______ the sky was too cloudy.", "options": ["so", "but", "because", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "想看日出但天空多雲，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1397, "question": "This dress is pretty, ______ it does not look good on me.", "options": ["so", "but", "or", "if"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜but 表轉折（但是）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V, but + S + V：前後語意相反。\n【分析】「這件洋裝很漂亮」，「但穿在我身上不好看」，前後相反，用 but。\n【其他選項】(A) so 表結果，漂亮不會導致不好看；(C) or 表「或／否則」；(D) if 表條件，語意不通。\n【例句】The soup smells good, but it tastes too salty.（湯聞起來香，但喝起來太鹹。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1398, "question": "These shoes are cheap, ______ they are not comfortable.", "options": ["so", "or", "but", "if"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "便宜但不舒服，轉折用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1399, "question": "The movie was long, ______ it wasn't boring at all.", "options": ["but", "so", "because", "or"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "片長但不無聊，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1400, "question": "The phone looks nice, ______ it breaks easily.", "options": ["so", "or", "because", "but"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "外觀好但容易壞，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1401, "question": "I have to catch the bus right now, ______ I'll miss my brother's birthday party.", "options": ["and", "because", "or", "until"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜祈使/義務句, or 否則", "explanation": "【句型】S + have to/must V..., or + S + will V：「……，否則……」。\n【分析】「我現在必須趕上公車」，「否則會錯過弟弟的生日派對」，用 or 表「否則」。\n【其他選項】(A) and 表「然後／而且」，搭公車然後錯過派對不合理；(B) because：錯過派對不是趕公車的原因（語意顛倒）；(D) until「直到」，語意不通。\n【例句】Hurry up, or you'll be late for school.（快點，否則你上學會遲到。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1402, "question": "You should wear a jacket, ______ you'll catch a cold.", "options": ["and", "or", "so", "because"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "穿外套，否則會感冒，用 or。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1403, "question": "We must leave now, ______ we'll miss the first part of the show.", "options": ["or", "and", "but", "since"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "必須現在走，否則錯過開場，用 or。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1404, "question": "Study hard, ______ you'll pass the exam.", "options": ["or", "but", "and", "until"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "祈使句 + and 表「……，就會……」（正面結果），用 and。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1405, "question": "______ Annie knows fast food is not good for her health, she still eats it.", "options": ["Although", "Because", "If", "When"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜Although 雖然（讓步）", "explanation": "【句型】Although + S + V, S + still V：「雖然……，還是……」。\n【分析】「Annie 知道速食對健康不好」，「她還是吃」，still 提示前後語意相反，用 Although。\n【其他選項】(B) Because：知道不健康不會是她吃的原因；(C) If 表條件，語意不合；(D) When 表時間，無法表達讓步。\n【例句】Although Ben was tired, he still helped his mom wash the dishes.（雖然 Ben 很累，他還是幫媽媽洗碗。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1406, "question": "______ Kevin knows the answer, he doesn't want to raise his hand.", "options": ["Because", "If", "Although", "When"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "知道答案卻不舉手，語意相反用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1407, "question": "______ it was late, the children were still playing in the park.", "options": ["Although", "Because", "If", "Until"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "很晚了孩子還在玩，用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1408, "question": "______ Judy was afraid of dogs, she still fed her neighbor's dog.", "options": ["If", "Although", "Because", "Unless"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "怕狗卻還是餵狗，用 Although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1409, "question": "Dad: Are you going out? It's really late now.\nMitch: I know, but it's the last day to buy tickets to the World Cup games, ______ I must go.", "options": ["if", "or", "so", "though"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜so 所以（結果）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V (原因), so + S + V (結果)。\n【分析】「今天是買世足賽門票的最後一天」（原因），「所以我一定得去」（結果），用 so。\n【其他選項】(A) if 表條件，語意不通；(B) or 表「否則」，不合；(D) though「雖然」，前後不是相反關係。\n【例句】The store will close soon, so we have to hurry.（店快關了，所以我們得快點。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1410, "question": "Tomorrow is the deadline for the art contest, ______ I have to finish my painting tonight.", "options": ["though", "so", "or", "if"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "明天截止，所以今晚得畫完，用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1411, "question": "The MRT was out of service, ______ we took a bus to the concert.", "options": ["though", "or", "if", "so"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "捷運停駛導致改搭公車，結果用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1412, "question": "It's Mom's birthday today, ______ we're going to cook dinner for her.", "options": ["so", "or", "though", "if"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "今天媽媽生日所以要煮晚餐，用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1413, "question": "Mr. Hu speaks good English ______ he lived in the U.S. for many years.", "options": ["because", "but", "so", "whether"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜because 因為（原因）", "explanation": "【句型】S + V + because + S + V：說明原因。\n【分析】「住在美國很多年」是「胡先生英文說得好」的原因，用 because。\n【其他選項】(B) but 表轉折，前後並不相反；(C) so 表結果，因果顛倒（說英文好不會導致住美國多年）；(D) whether「是否」，不能表原因。\n【例句】Lily can play the piano well because she has practiced since she was five.（Lily 鋼琴彈得好，因為她從五歲就練習。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1414, "question": "Carl knows a lot about animals ______ his mother is a vet.", "options": ["but", "so", "because", "whether"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "媽媽是獸醫是他懂動物的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1415, "question": "Jenny is good at cooking ______ she often helps her grandma in the kitchen.", "options": ["because", "but", "or", "so"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "常幫忙下廚是會煮菜的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1416, "question": "Owen got a high score on the math test ______ he studied every night.", "options": ["but", "because", "or", "whether"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "每晚讀書是考高分的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1417, "question": "I can't find my history book, ______ I know it's somewhere in the living room.", "options": ["because", "but", "since", "until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜對等連接詞 but（語氣轉折）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V1, but + S2 + V2.（前後語意相反、轉折）\n【分析】前句「找不到歷史課本」，後句「知道它就在客廳某處」，兩句語意相對，用 but「但是」連接。\n【其他選項】(A) because「因為」、(C) since「既然；因為」皆表原因，但「知道書在客廳」不是找不到的原因；(D) until「直到」表時間，語意不通。\n【例句】I wanted to go to the concert, but the tickets were sold out.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1418, "question": "Kevin studied hard for the test, ______ he still didn't pass it.", "options": ["so", "because", "but", "if"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "「努力讀書」與「還是沒過」語意相反，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1419, "question": "It was raining heavily, ______ we stayed at home and watched a movie.", "options": ["so", "but", "though", "until"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "下雨是原因、待在家是結果，用 so「所以」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1420, "question": "Ivy is only ten years old, ______ she can speak three languages.", "options": ["because", "but", "so", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "「才十歲」與「會講三種語言」形成對比，用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1421, "question": "Elsa hates going shopping, ______ she went last night when her grandpa asked her to buy some medicine for him.", "options": ["because", "but", "if", "so"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜對等連接詞 but（語氣轉折）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V1, but + S2 + V2.（前後語意相反）\n【分析】前句「Elsa 討厭逛街購物」，後句「昨晚她還是去了（因為爺爺請她買藥）」，語意轉折，用 but。\n【其他選項】(A) because 表原因，「討厭購物」不是她去的原因；(C) if 表條件，與過去發生的事實不合；(D) so 表結果，「討厭購物所以去了」不合邏輯。\n【例句】Tom doesn't like vegetables, but he ate all the salad today.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1422, "question": "My brother is afraid of dogs, ______ he played with my neighbor's puppy yesterday.", "options": ["so", "because", "or", "but"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "怕狗卻和小狗玩，語意相反用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1423, "question": "Mia was very tired, ______ she went to bed early.", "options": ["but", "so", "though", "or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "累是原因、早睡是結果，用 so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1424, "question": "Leo doesn't like math, ______ he got a perfect score on the math test.", "options": ["but", "so", "because", "and"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "不喜歡數學卻考滿分，語意轉折用 but。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1425, "question": "Enya got up early this morning ______ she did not want to be late for her trip.", "options": ["if", "but", "though", "because"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜從屬連接詞 because（表原因）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V1 + because + S2 + V2.（because 引導原因副詞子句）\n【分析】「早起」的原因是「不想旅行遲到」，後句說明原因，用 because「因為」。\n【其他選項】(A) if「如果」表條件，與已發生的事實不合；(B) but「但是」、(C) though「雖然」皆表轉折，前後語意並不相反。\n【例句】Ben stayed home because he had a bad cold.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1426, "question": "We took a taxi ______ we missed the last bus.", "options": ["because", "though", "until", "but"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "錯過末班公車是搭計程車的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1427, "question": "______ it was cold outside, the kids still played in the park.", "options": ["Because", "If", "Though", "So"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "天冷但孩子仍在外玩，語意讓步用 though。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1428, "question": "Jenny turned on the light ______ the room was too dark to read in.", "options": ["but", "until", "though", "because"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "房間太暗是開燈的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1429, "question": "Mr. Green was very angry with his daughter ______ she always put her dirty socks on the dining table.", "options": ["although", "because", "but", "until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜從屬連接詞 because（表原因）", "explanation": "【句型】S1 + V1 + because + S2 + V2.（because 引導原因）\n【分析】Mr. Green 生氣的原因是女兒「總是把髒襪子放在餐桌上」，後句為原因，用 because。\n【其他選項】(A) although「雖然」、(C) but「但是」表讓步／轉折，前後並非相反；(D) until「直到」表時間，語意不通。\n【例句】The teacher was happy because all the students passed the test.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1430, "question": "Grandma was worried ______ Peter didn't come home after school.", "options": ["because", "although", "until", "or"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "彼得沒回家是奶奶擔心的原因，用 because。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1431, "question": "Please wait here ______ I come back.", "options": ["because", "though", "until", "so"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "「在這裡等直到我回來」，用 until 表時間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1432, "question": "______ Lily practiced the piano every day, she didn't win the contest.", "options": ["Because", "Although", "If", "Until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "每天練琴卻沒贏，語意讓步用 although。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1433, "question": "Still, the heavy price Munich paid does not worry the cities that are in the race to get the 2022 Winter Olympics. ___41___, they are happy that Munich said no to the Olympics—their chances of getting the Games have become higher.\n41. ______", "options": ["In fact", "If so", "However", "Finally"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜會考歷屆｜轉折語 In fact（事實上，補充並加強前句）", "explanation": "【句型】轉折語（副詞片語）In fact「事實上」：用來進一步補充、加強前句的說法\n【分析】前句說「慕尼黑付出的代價沒讓其他競爭城市擔心」，後句更進一步說「事實上它們很高興慕尼黑退出，因為獲選機會變高了」，屬於同方向的加強說明 → In fact。\n【其他選項】(B) If so「如果是這樣」表條件，前句不是假設；(C) However「然而」表轉折，但前後語意同方向，不相反；(D) Finally「最後」表順序，不合文意。\n【例句】Kevin isn't lazy. In fact, he works harder than anyone in our class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1434, "question": "Jenny doesn't hate vegetables. ______, she eats a big salad every day.", "options": ["However", "In fact", "If so", "Finally"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "「不討厭蔬菜」→「事實上每天吃沙拉」，同方向加強用 In fact。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1435, "question": "Leo practiced very hard. ______, he didn't win the race.", "options": ["However", "In fact", "For example", "Besides"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "努力練習卻沒贏，語意相反用 However。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1436, "question": "Are you going to the night market? ______, can you buy me some stinky tofu?", "options": ["However", "Finally", "If so", "In fact"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "「如果你要去的話」用 If so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1437, "question": "______ you ______ your brother can go out before you finish tidying your bedrooms. So, you'd better do it right now.", "options": ["Both; and", "Either; or", "Neither; nor", "No only; but also"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜講義錯題｜Neither A nor B（兩者皆不）", "explanation": "【句型】Neither A nor B（A 和 B 都不）；Both A and B（兩者都）；Either A or B（兩者之一）\n【分析】before you finish tidying 和後句 you'd better do it right now 表示整理完前「兩人都不能」出去 → Neither … nor。\n【其他選項】(A) 兩人都可以出去，與後句矛盾；(B) 其中一人可出去，語意不合；(D) 應為 Not only，且語意也不合。\n【例句】Neither Tom nor I like spicy food.\n備註：講義 p.317；選項 (D) 原書拼為 No only，應為 Not only，照原文保留。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1438, "question": "______ Jenny ______ Mark was at home, so I left a note on the door.", "options": ["Both; and", "Neither; nor", "Not only; but also", "Either; or"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "沒人在家才留紙條，用 Neither…nor。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1439, "question": "You can have ______ juice ______ milk, but not both.", "options": ["either; or", "neither; nor", "both; and", "not only; but also"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "but not both 表二選一，用 either…or。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1440, "question": "______ my mom ______ my dad came to my graduation. I was so happy to see them both.", "options": ["Either; or", "Neither; nor", "Both; and", "Not; but"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "連接詞｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "see them both 表兩人都來，用 Both…and。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "連接詞"}, {"id": 1441, "question": "Sam: Sorry, I'm late.\nBen: Here you are! I waited for you for one hour and ______ you wouldn't come.", "options": ["forgot", "found", "noticed", "thought"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜thought + 子句「原本以為」(搭配 would)", "explanation": "【句型】S + thought (that) + S + would/wouldn't + V:「(當時)以為…會/不會…」。\n【分析】Ben 等了一小時,當時「以為」Sam 不會來了,後面 you wouldn't come 是當時的猜想 → thought。\n【其他選項】(A) forgot「忘記」+ 子句語意不合;(B) found「發現」表事實,但 Sam 最後還是來了;(C) noticed「注意到」也表事實,與 Sam 已到不合。\n【例句】I thought you wouldn't be able to finish it today.\n備註：參考解答(4f68a85b.txt)為改編版(雙空格 thought; wouldn't);截圖原題為單空格動詞選擇,答案 D thought 一致。本題主要考動詞語意判斷,故建議歸入詞彙題。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1442, "question": "Mom: You're home early!\nKen: The meeting was canceled. I ______ it would take all afternoon.", "options": ["thought", "found", "forgot", "noticed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "原本以為會很久(結果沒有)→ thought。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1443, "question": "I ______ the test would be hard, but it was easier than I expected.", "options": ["noticed", "forgot", "thought", "found"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "原本以為難,實際上簡單 → thought。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1444, "question": "When I opened the box, I ______ that the cup inside was broken.", "options": ["thought", "forgot", "wondered", "found"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "打開箱子「發現」杯子破了(事實)→ found。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1445, "question": "The little girl was ______ by a truck on her way home and was badly hurt.", "options": ["hit", "led", "lost", "paid"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜被動句中的動詞詞彙 be hit by", "explanation": "【句型】be hit by + 交通工具「被…撞到」。\n【分析】選項皆為 p.p.，考字義：被卡車「撞」到才會 badly hurt（受重傷）→ hit。\n【其他選項】(B) led 被帶領；(C) lost 被弄丟；(D) paid 被付錢，皆與 by a truck、受傷語意不合。\n【例句】The dog was hit by a car, but it's OK now.\n備註：四個選項皆為被動 p.p.，實際考的是動詞字義。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1446, "question": "The boy was ______ by a dog while he was walking in the park. His leg was bleeding.", "options": ["bitten", "bought", "built", "borrowed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "被狗「咬」才會流血，bite 的 p.p. 為 bitten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1447, "question": "The thief was ______ by the police when he was running out of the store.", "options": ["taught", "caught", "brought", "thought"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "小偷被警察「抓到」→ caught。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1448, "question": "Many houses were ______ by the strong typhoon last summer.", "options": ["planted", "invited", "destroyed", "followed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "房子被強颱「摧毀」→ destroyed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1449, "question": "John: What's wrong with Wendy?\nJean: Her knees hurt. She was ______ by a motorcycle this afternoon.\nJohn: Oh, that's too bad!", "options": ["caught", "hit", "killed", "saved"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜被動句中的動詞詞彙 be hit by", "explanation": "【句型】be hit by + 交通工具「被…撞到」。\n【分析】Her knees hurt 膝蓋受傷，且還能對話 → 被機車「撞到」hit。\n【其他選項】(A) caught 被抓住；(C) killed 被撞死，與膝蓋痛、還活著不合；(D) saved 被救，與受傷不合，且 That's too bad 表示壞事。\n【例句】My uncle was hit by a bike when he was crossing the street.\n備註：四個選項皆為被動 p.p.，實際考的是動詞字義。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1450, "question": "Henry: Why is Jane crying?\nAmy: She was ______ by a bee in the garden.", "options": ["stung", "sung", "sold", "shown"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "被蜜蜂「螫」→ stung（sting 的 p.p.）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1451, "question": "The window was ______ by a baseball, and now there's glass all over the floor.", "options": ["cleaned", "opened", "closed", "broken"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "地上都是玻璃，窗戶被棒球「打破」→ broken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1452, "question": "Ben was ______ in a car accident, but luckily he wasn't seriously hurt.", "options": ["invited", "included", "injured", "excited"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "在車禍中「受傷」→ be injured。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1453, "question": "Jean is crazy about the color purple. The walls of her house are all ______ purple.", "options": ["built", "dug", "painted", "shown"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜被動句中的動詞詞彙 be painted", "explanation": "【句型】S + be painted + 顏色「被漆成…色」。\n【分析】Jean 很喜歡紫色，所以牆壁都被「漆」成紫色 → painted。\n【其他選項】(A) built 被建造；(B) dug 被挖；(D) shown 被展示，後面都不能直接接顏色。\n【例句】The door was painted red last year.\n備註：四個選項皆為被動 p.p.，實際考的是動詞字義。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1454, "question": "The old house was ______ more than 100 years ago, but it still looks strong.", "options": ["built", "drawn", "grown", "cooked"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "房子「被建造」→ built。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1455, "question": "The letters were ______ in English, so Grandma couldn't read them.", "options": ["spoken", "written", "painted", "sung"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "信是用英文「寫」的 → written。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1456, "question": "The gift was ______ in beautiful paper with a red ribbon.", "options": ["hidden", "dropped", "washed", "wrapped"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "禮物被漂亮的紙「包裝」→ wrapped。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1457, "question": "Ms. Wang thought she lost her ring last night. But this morning she found that it was on the table and was ______ by a book.", "options": ["covered", "moved", "packed", "stopped"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜被動句中的動詞詞彙 be covered by", "explanation": "【句型】be covered by/with「被…蓋住」。\n【分析】戒指其實在桌上，只是「被書蓋住」才以為弄丟了 → covered。\n【其他選項】(B) moved 被移動，與 on the table 找到的情境不合；(C) packed 被打包；(D) stopped 被阻止，皆不合語意。\n【例句】The ground was covered with snow.\n備註：四個選項皆為被動 p.p.，實際考的是動詞字義。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1458, "question": "The mountain was ______ with snow, so everything looked white.", "options": ["filled", "covered", "made", "moved"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "山「被雪覆蓋」→ be covered with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1459, "question": "The bottle was ______ with water, so it was very heavy.", "options": ["filled", "covered", "dressed", "mixed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "瓶子「裝滿」水 → be filled with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1460, "question": "My keys were ______ under the sofa, so I couldn't find them all morning.", "options": ["heard", "hurt", "hidden", "hit"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "鑰匙「被藏／落」在沙發下所以找不到 → hidden。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1461, "question": "Jessie felt sad because she was not ______ to the party. She really wanted to go.", "options": ["invited", "scared", "followed", "impressed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜被動句中的動詞詞彙 be invited to", "explanation": "【句型】be invited to + 活動「被邀請參加…」。\n【分析】她很想去卻很難過 → 因為沒有「被邀請」去派對 → invited。\n【其他選項】(B) scared 害怕；(C) followed 被跟隨；(D) impressed 印象深刻，皆不合語意。\n【例句】All the students were invited to the school concert.\n備註：四個選項皆為被動 p.p.，實際考的是動詞字義。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1462, "question": "Dan was ______ to join the school team because he runs very fast.", "options": ["worried", "chosen", "bored", "closed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "跑得快所以「被選中」加入校隊 → chosen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1463, "question": "The students were ______ by the teacher for being late again.", "options": ["praised", "thanked", "blamed", "welcomed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "又遲到所以「被責備」→ blamed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1464, "question": "The new student was warmly ______ by everyone in the class on her first day.", "options": ["punished", "forgotten", "laughed", "welcomed"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "新同學第一天受到熱情「歡迎」→ welcomed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1465, "question": "It is hard for trees to ______ along this beach because of the strong winds from the sea.", "options": ["blow", "build", "follow", "grow"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞詞彙 grow", "explanation": "【句型】It is + adj. + for 人/物 + to V；本題考動詞字義：grow 生長。\n【分析】主詞是 trees，又提到 because of the strong winds「因為海上強風」，所以樹木很難在海邊「生長」，grow 最合理。\n【其他選項】(A) blow 吹（樹不會吹）；(B) build 建造；(C) follow 跟隨，都不符合語意。\n【例句】Rice grows well in warm and wet places.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1466, "question": "These flowers need a lot of sun to ______ well. Please put them by the window.", "options": ["grow", "cook", "throw", "sell"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "花需要陽光才能「生長」，用 grow。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1467, "question": "The wind ______ so hard last night that many trees fell down.", "options": ["built", "blew", "grew", "followed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "風「吹」得很強，用 blow 的過去式 blew。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1468, "question": "It took the workers two years to ______ the new library.", "options": ["follow", "blow", "build", "grow"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "工人花兩年「建造」圖書館，用 build。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1469, "question": "It is ______ to sell fake CDs and watches. You will be caught by the police.", "options": ["illegal", "important", "convenient", "comfortable"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞詞彙 illegal", "explanation": "【句型】It is + adj. + to V（虛主詞 it 代替後面的不定詞）；考形容詞字義 illegal 違法的。\n【分析】後句 You will be caught by the police「你會被警察抓」，可知賣假 CD 和手錶是「違法的」，用 illegal。\n【其他選項】(B) important 重要的；(C) convenient 方便的；(D) comfortable 舒服的，都與「被警察抓」無關。\n【例句】It is illegal to ride a scooter without a license.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1470, "question": "It is ______ to drive after drinking. Many people get hurt because of it.", "options": ["comfortable", "dangerous", "convenient", "popular"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "酒後開車會讓人受傷，是「危險的」dangerous。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1471, "question": "In Taiwan, it is ______ to smoke in restaurants. You may have to pay a lot of money.", "options": ["important", "comfortable", "illegal", "convenient"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "會被罰錢，表示在餐廳抽菸是「違法的」illegal。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1472, "question": "It is ______ to drink enough water every day. It keeps you healthy.", "options": ["important", "illegal", "terrible", "boring"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "喝足夠的水讓你健康，是「重要的」important。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1473, "question": "It is ______ for me to go to work by bus. My office is very near the bus stop.", "options": ["convenient", "dangerous", "difficult", "special"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞詞彙 convenient", "explanation": "【句型】It is + adj. + for 人 + to V；考形容詞字義 convenient 方便的。\n【分析】後句說 My office is very near the bus stop「辦公室離公車站很近」，所以搭公車上班很「方便」，用 convenient。\n【其他選項】(B) dangerous 危險的；(C) difficult 困難的，與「很近」的線索矛盾；(D) special 特別的，語意不合。\n【例句】It is convenient to live near an MRT station.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1474, "question": "It is ______ for Grandma to go shopping now. There is a supermarket right next to her house.", "options": ["difficult", "convenient", "dangerous", "boring"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "超市就在隔壁，購物很「方便」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1475, "question": "It is ______ for kids to play near the busy road. Cars drive very fast there.", "options": ["dangerous", "convenient", "special", "healthy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "車子開很快，在路邊玩很「危險」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1476, "question": "It was ______ for Tim to read the small words without his glasses.", "options": ["convenient", "special", "difficult", "careful"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "沒戴眼鏡看小字很「困難」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1477, "question": "There are more and more cars in our city, so ______ has become a serious problem.", "options": ["jumping", "learning", "parking", "smoking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動名詞詞彙 parking", "explanation": "【句型】Ving 當主詞；考字義 parking 停車。\n【分析】前句 There are more and more cars「車子越來越多」，所以「停車」變成嚴重的問題，用 parking。\n【其他選項】(A) jumping 跳；(B) learning 學習；(D) smoking 抽菸，都與「車子多」沒有因果關係。\n【例句】Parking near the night market is not easy.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1478, "question": "More and more people use cellphones in bed, so ______ problems are getting serious.", "options": ["parking", "sleeping", "cooking", "dancing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "睡前用手機造成「睡眠」問題。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1479, "question": "The road is full of cars in the morning, so ______ to work takes a long time.", "options": ["driving", "jumping", "smoking", "parking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "車多導致「開車」上班很久。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1480, "question": "______ is not allowed in this building. Please put out your cigarette.", "options": ["Parking", "Swimming", "Smoking", "Learning"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "put out your cigarette 表示「抽菸」是禁止的。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1481, "question": "It's great that we can buy train tickets over the phone without going out. It ______ us a lot of time.", "options": ["lends", "prepares", "saves", "takes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜save + 人 + 時間（為某人節省時間）", "explanation": "【句型】save + 人 + 時間／金錢（為某人省下時間／錢）。\n【分析】前句說「不用出門就能用電話買車票」，所以是「替我們省下很多時間」，選 saves。\n【其他選項】(A) lends 借出，語意不合；(B) prepares 準備，不能接「人＋時間」；(D) takes 花費（It takes us time to V），與「不用出門很方便」語意相反，且後面缺 to V。\n【例句】Riding the MRT saves me twenty minutes every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1482, "question": "Online shopping is convenient. It ______ people the trouble of going to the store.", "options": ["spends", "saves", "costs", "borrows"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "save sb the trouble 替某人省去麻煩，符合「方便」的語意。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1483, "question": "Taking the High Speed Rail ______ us two hours. We got to Kaohsiung before lunch.", "options": ["saved", "lent", "paid", "spent"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "save + 人 + 時間 表示幫某人省下時間；spent 主詞須為人。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1484, "question": "The new road is very long and full of traffic lights. It ______ me more time to get to school now.", "options": ["saves", "spends", "takes", "pays"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "It takes + 人 + 時間 + to V 表示花費時間；路變遠所以花更多時間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1485, "question": "Joyce tells her brother everything. She never ______ anything from him.", "options": ["covers", "believes", "hides", "takes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜hide sth from sb（對某人隱瞞某事）", "explanation": "【句型】hide + 事物 + from + 人（對某人隱藏／隱瞞某事）。\n【分析】前句「Joyce 什麼都告訴哥哥」，所以「她從不對他隱瞞任何事」，選 hides。\n【其他選項】(A) covers 覆蓋，不搭配 from 人表隱瞞；(B) believes 相信，語意不合；(D) takes anything from him 是「從他那裡拿東西」，與前句不呼應。\n【例句】Tom hid the broken cup from his mom.\n備註：此題考動詞詞彙，非 spend/cost/take 等特殊動詞句型。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1486, "question": "Kelly and Ann are best friends. They never ______ secrets from each other.", "options": ["hide", "borrow", "believe", "find"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "hide sth from sb 對某人隱瞞，符合「好朋友」的語意。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1487, "question": "The boy ______ his bad test score from his parents, but they found out later.", "options": ["showed", "told", "hid", "gave"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "後句「但父母後來發現了」，表示他原本隱瞞，選 hid。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1488, "question": "Sam is honest. He always ______ his teacher the truth.", "options": ["hides", "tells", "says", "speaks"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "tell + 人 + the truth 告訴某人實話；say / speak 不接人當間接受詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1489, "question": "There are online videos that teach you exercises you can do at home. They'll ______ you a trip to the gym, and some money too.", "options": ["cost", "give", "keep", "save"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜save + 人 + 事物（替某人省下）", "explanation": "【句型】save + 人 + 事物（替某人省下某事物，如時間、錢、一趟路）。\n【分析】在家看影片就能運動，所以「替你省下跑健身房的一趟路，也省錢」，選 save。\n【其他選項】(A) cost 花費，語意相反；(B) give you a trip 給你一趟旅程，不合；(C) keep 保留，不接「人＋事物」表此意。\n【例句】Cooking at home saves us a lot of money.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1490, "question": "Doing your homework at school will ______ you a lot of time at night.", "options": ["cost", "save", "spend", "lend"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "save + 人 + 時間 替某人省下時間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1491, "question": "Buying things online can ______ you a trip to the mall.", "options": ["save", "take", "pay", "borrow"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "save you a trip 替你省下跑一趟。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1492, "question": "Taking a taxi will ______ you more money than taking the MRT.", "options": ["save", "spend", "cost", "pay"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "事物 + cost + 人 + 金錢，搭計程車花較多錢。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1493, "question": "\"Bad traffic\" is perhaps the ______ excuse for being late when your boss knows it only takes you five minutes to walk to work.", "options": ["easiest", "oldest", "smartest", "worst"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜最高級形容詞語意 worst", "explanation": "【句型】the + 最高級形容詞 + N；本題考形容詞語意判斷。\n【分析】走路上班只要五分鐘，用「塞車」當遲到藉口最站不住腳 → the worst excuse（最糟的藉口）。\n【其他選項】(A) easiest 最容易的、(B) oldest 最老舊的、(C) smartest 最聰明的，皆與「老闆知道你走路五分鐘就到」的語意不符。\n【例句】That was the worst movie I have ever seen.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1494, "question": "Leo forgot his mom's birthday again. That was the ______ thing he did this year.", "options": ["worst", "best", "kindest", "happiest"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "忘記媽媽生日 → 最糟的事 → worst。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1495, "question": "Lisa got 100 on every test. She is the ______ student in our class.", "options": ["laziest", "best", "worst", "busiest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "每次考一百分 → 最優秀 → best。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1496, "question": "Winter is the ______ season in Hehuan Mountain; it sometimes snows there.", "options": ["hottest", "wettest", "coldest", "driest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "會下雪 → 最冷的季節 → coldest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1497, "question": "It is ______ to go out on a typhoon day. The sky is dark and the wind is strong.", "options": ["careful", "fashionable", "dangerous", "convenient"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞語意 dangerous", "explanation": "【句型】It is + adj. + to V（做……是……的）；本題考形容詞語意。\n【分析】颱風天天色暗、風很強 → 出門「很危險」→ dangerous。\n【其他選項】(A) careful 小心的，形容人，It is careful to… 不合；(B) fashionable 時髦的；(D) convenient 方便的；皆與颱風天語意不符。\n【例句】It is dangerous to swim in the river after heavy rain.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1498, "question": "It is ______ to ride a bike at night without lights.", "options": ["safe", "dangerous", "healthy", "cheap"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "夜間騎車無燈 → 危險。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1499, "question": "It is ______ to live near an MRT station. You can go anywhere quickly.", "options": ["convenient", "noisy", "careful", "lonely"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "到哪都很快 → 方便 → convenient。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1500, "question": "Please be ______ when you cross the street.", "options": ["dangerous", "famous", "careful", "popular"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "過馬路要小心 → careful（形容人）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1501, "question": "With the new bus line, it is much more ______ for Fanny to go to school. It saves her a lot of time now.", "options": ["useful", "possible", "interesting", "convenient"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞語意 convenient", "explanation": "【句型】it is + adj. + for sb. + to V；much + 比較級；本題考形容詞語意。\n【分析】新公車路線「幫她省很多時間」→ 上學更「方便」→ convenient。\n【其他選項】(A) useful 有用的，通常形容物品，it is useful for her to go to school 語意怪；(B) possible 可能的，much more possible 不自然；(C) interesting 有趣的，與省時無關。\n【例句】It is convenient to buy snacks at a convenience store.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1502, "question": "My home is next to the MRT station, so it is very ______ for me to go downtown.", "options": ["convenient", "dangerous", "careful", "lonely"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "住捷運旁 → 進城很方便。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1503, "question": "A dictionary is very ______ when you learn new words.", "options": ["lucky", "useful", "honest", "sleepy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "字典學單字「有用」→ useful。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1504, "question": "Is it ______ for you to finish the report by tomorrow?", "options": ["famous", "friendly", "possible", "honest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "問「是否可能」明天前完成 → possible。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1505, "question": "The knife doesn't cut very well. It's not as ______ as before.", "options": ["bright", "heavy", "quick", "sharp"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜as + 形容詞原級 + as；sharp 語意", "explanation": "【句型】not as + 形容詞原級 + as =「不如……」；本題考形容詞語意。\n【分析】刀子切不好 → 不像以前那麼「鋒利」→ sharp。\n【其他選項】(A) bright 明亮的；(B) heavy 重的；(C) quick 快速的；皆與「切不好」無直接因果。\n【例句】My pencil isn't as sharp as yours.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1506, "question": "This street is not as ______ as before. Many shops have closed.", "options": ["busy", "sharp", "honest", "careful"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "很多店關了 → 不像以前熱鬧 → busy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1507, "question": "You need a ______ knife to cut the beef.", "options": ["sharp", "bright", "soft", "quiet"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "切牛肉需要鋒利的刀 → sharp。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1508, "question": "My old phone is not as ______ as my new one. It takes a long time to open an app.", "options": ["heavy", "fast", "dark", "cheap"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "開 app 很慢 → 不如新手機快 → fast。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1509, "question": "After winning money in the card game, Jay decided to try again. He felt that he might also be ______ a second time.", "options": ["famous", "interested", "lucky", "ready"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞語意 lucky", "explanation": "【句型】be + 形容詞；本題考形容詞語意，lucky = 幸運的。\n【分析】玩牌贏了錢想再試一次 → 覺得第二次可能也會「幸運」→ lucky。\n【其他選項】(A) famous 有名的；(B) interested 感興趣的（需接 in）；(D) ready 準備好的；與「再贏一次」的語意不符。\n【例句】You are lucky to have such a nice teacher.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1510, "question": "Ella found a NT$1,000 bill on the street. What a ______ day!", "options": ["lucky", "boring", "sad", "busy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "撿到錢 → 幸運的一天。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1511, "question": "Are you ______ for the test tomorrow?", "options": ["lucky", "ready", "famous", "honest"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "準備好考試了嗎 → ready for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1512, "question": "Andy is very ______ in science. He reads science books every night.", "options": ["interesting", "famous", "interested", "lucky"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "be interested in = 對……感興趣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1513, "question": "In the past, people thought it was a ______ idea to send e-mails and read news online, but now it is part of our everyday life.", "options": ["simple", "popular", "good", "fresh"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞語意 fresh（新穎的）", "explanation": "【句型】a + adj. + idea；fresh idea =「新奇、新穎的想法」；本題考形容詞語意。\n【分析】In the past … but now it is part of our everyday life → 以前覺得是「新鮮」的點子，現在已是日常 → fresh。\n【其他選項】(A) simple 簡單的、(B) popular 受歡迎的、(C) good 好的，都無法與「但現在已成日常」形成對比。\n【例句】Using robots to teach English is a fresh idea.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1514, "question": "Ten years ago, paying with a cell phone was a ______ idea, but now everyone does it.", "options": ["fresh", "boring", "usual", "old"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "以前新奇、現在普遍 → fresh。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1515, "question": "The fish is ______. It was caught this morning.", "options": ["fresh", "dark", "sharp", "honest"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "今早剛捕的魚 → 新鮮。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1516, "question": "Bubble tea is very ______ in Taiwan. You can find it on almost every street.", "options": ["lonely", "popular", "careful", "quiet"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "到處都有 → 很受歡迎 → popular。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1517, "question": "The paint on the wall is not as ______ as it was ten years ago. It has changed from white to gray.", "options": ["bright", "heavy", "sure", "young"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜not as + 形容詞 + as；bright 語意", "explanation": "【句型】not as + 形容詞原級 + as；本題考形容詞語意，bright = 明亮的（顏色鮮亮）。\n【分析】牆漆由白變灰 → 不像十年前那樣「明亮」→ bright。\n【其他選項】(B) heavy 重的；(C) sure 確定的，形容人；(D) young 年輕的，形容人或生物；皆不合油漆顏色。\n【例句】The sun is very bright today.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1518, "question": "Turn on the light. The room is not ______ enough for reading.", "options": ["bright", "heavy", "sharp", "loud"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "房間不夠亮 → bright。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1519, "question": "My grandfather is eighty, but he still feels ______.", "options": ["bright", "young", "sure", "sharp"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "八十歲仍覺得年輕 → young。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1520, "question": "This box is too ______ for me to carry. Can you help me?", "options": ["heavy", "bright", "young", "sure"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "搬不動 → 太重 → heavy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1521, "question": "You've had the same food for breakfast for one week. Do you want something ______ for a change?", "options": ["bright", "different", "helpful", "round"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜something + 形容詞；different 語意", "explanation": "【句型】something / anything / nothing + 形容詞（形容詞放後面）；本題考形容詞語意。\n【分析】同樣早餐吃了一週 → for a change（換換口味）→ 想要「不一樣的」東西 → different。\n【其他選項】(A) bright 明亮的；(C) helpful 有幫助的；(D) round 圓的；皆與 the same / for a change 的對比無關。\n【例句】Let's do something different this weekend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1522, "question": "Your idea is ______ from mine, but I think both are good.", "options": ["same", "different", "helpful", "bright"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "be different from = 與……不同。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1523, "question": "Is there anything ______ in today's newspaper?", "options": ["interesting", "interest", "interested", "interestingly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "anything + 形容詞（後置）；形容事物「有趣的」→ interesting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1524, "question": "My twin brother and I look the ______, but we like different things.", "options": ["different", "same", "round", "similar"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "look the same = 看起來一樣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1525, "question": "Ms. Lee is a(n) ______ businesswoman. Just now in her shop, she gave me back the wallet I left on the table last week.", "options": ["famous", "honest", "important", "smart"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞語意 honest", "explanation": "【句型】a(n) + adj. + N；本題考形容詞語意，honest = 誠實的。\n【分析】她把我上週遺留的錢包還給我 → 她是「誠實的」商人 → an honest businesswoman。\n【其他選項】(A) famous 有名的、(C) important 重要的、(D) smart 聰明的，都無法由「歸還錢包」推知。\n【例句】Please be honest and tell me the truth.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1526, "question": "Tina always tells the truth. She is an ______ girl.", "options": ["honest", "angry", "awful", "empty"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "總說實話 → honest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1527, "question": "Andy can solve any math problem in one minute. He is really ______.", "options": ["honest", "smart", "lazy", "shy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "一分鐘解數學題 → 聰明 → smart。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1528, "question": "Jay Chou is a ______ singer. Almost everyone in Taiwan knows him.", "options": ["shy", "honest", "famous", "lazy"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "大家都認識 → 有名的 → famous。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1529, "question": "I can't believe you ate the ______ piece of pizza and didn't even leave one bite for me.", "options": ["last", "least", "less", "most"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜last（最後的）vs. least", "explanation": "【句型】the last + 單數名詞 =「最後一個……」。\n【分析】didn't even leave one bite for me（連一口都沒留）→ 你吃了「最後一片」披薩 → the last piece。\n【其他選項】(B) the least 最少的，修飾不可數名詞或表程度，the least piece 不通；(C) less 為比較級，不與 the…piece 搭配；(D) the most 最多的，piece 為單數，不合。\n【例句】Kevin was the last person to leave the classroom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1530, "question": "December is the ______ month of the year.", "options": ["least", "last", "latest", "less"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "一年的最後一個月 → last。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1531, "question": "Who drank the ______ bottle of milk? I wanted it for breakfast.", "options": ["last", "least", "less", "most"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "最後一瓶 → last。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1532, "question": "Of the three boys, Ray spends the ______ money. He always saves it.", "options": ["last", "least", "less", "latter"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "money 不可數 + 三者中最少 → the least。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1533, "question": "The ______ is so strong today that my hair keeps blowing in the air.", "options": ["rain", "snow", "sun", "wind"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞詞義 wind（so…that 句意線索）", "explanation": "【句型】so ＋ adj. ＋ that 子句：如此…以致於…\n【分析】that 子句說「頭髮一直在空中飄」，可知是「風」太強，用 wind。\n【其他選項】(A) rain 雨；(B) snow 雪；(C) sun 太陽，都不會讓頭髮飄起來。\n【例句】The rain was so heavy that we couldn't see the road.\n備註：空格考名詞詞義，so…that 僅為句意線索，建議歸「詞彙題」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1534, "question": "The ______ is so hot today that the ice cream melted in a minute.", "options": ["moon", "sun", "cloud", "wind"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "冰淇淋一下就融化，是「太陽」很熱。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1535, "question": "The ______ was so heavy last night that the streets were full of water.", "options": ["rain", "sun", "sky", "air"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "街道淹水，是「雨」下得很大，heavy rain。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1536, "question": "The ______ was so thick this morning that drivers couldn't see the cars in front.", "options": ["sun", "wind", "fog", "heat"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "看不到前車，是「霧」很濃，thick fog。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1537, "question": "When I was a teenager, I was very ______. But now, it's easier for me to talk to people.", "options": ["happy", "lazy", "popular", "shy"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞 shy 害羞的", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：形容詞語意判斷 shy「害羞的」\n【分析】後句說「但現在比較容易和人說話了」，表示以前不敢和人說話，故為 shy。\n【其他選項】(A) happy「快樂的」、(B) lazy「懶惰的」、(C) popular「受歡迎的」都與「現在較容易跟人說話」的對比無關。\n【例句】Amy is too shy to sing in front of the class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1538, "question": "Danny never says hello to new classmates. He's just a little ______.", "options": ["shy", "loud", "rude", "brave"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "不敢打招呼表示害羞 shy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1539, "question": "Kelly always does her homework at the last minute and sleeps all weekend. She is so ______.", "options": ["honest", "lazy", "polite", "careful"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "拖到最後一刻且整個週末睡覺，表示懶惰 lazy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1540, "question": "Everyone in our class likes Ray. He's very ______ with his classmates.", "options": ["angry", "quiet", "popular", "strange"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "大家都喜歡他，表示受歡迎 popular with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1541, "question": "Lena doesn't want to go ______ with John because she is afraid of water.", "options": ["dancing", "hiking", "sailing", "shopping"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 sailing 航行／go + Ving 活動", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：go + Ving（從事某活動），依語意選 sailing「航行；駕帆船」\n【分析】線索 afraid of water「怕水」，所以不想去和水有關的活動 → go sailing。\n【其他選項】(A) dancing「跳舞」、(B) hiking「健行」、(D) shopping「購物」都與水無關，不是怕水而不去的理由。\n【例句】My uncle likes to go sailing on the lake in summer.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1542, "question": "Kevin is afraid of heights, so he never goes ______ with his friends.", "options": ["swimming", "shopping", "climbing", "fishing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "怕高所以不去爬山 climbing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1543, "question": "Let's go ______ at the mall. I need a new pair of shoes.", "options": ["shopping", "camping", "hiking", "skating"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "在購物中心買鞋 → go shopping。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1544, "question": "Dad bought a new fishing pole, and he wants to go ______ by the river this Sunday.", "options": ["dancing", "fishing", "jogging", "bowling"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "買了釣竿要去河邊 → go fishing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1545, "question": "There are so many new ______ in the office. It'll take me some time to remember who is who.", "options": ["faces", "ideas", "rules", "tools"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 face 臉孔（new faces 新面孔）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：new faces「新面孔＝新來的人」\n【分析】後句「要花時間記住誰是誰」(who is who)，表示辦公室有很多新來的人，用 faces。\n【其他選項】(B) ideas「點子」、(C) rules「規定」、(D) tools「工具」都不是「人」，與 who is who 不合。\n【例句】There are a lot of new faces in our class this year.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1546, "question": "I can't remember her name, but I'll never forget her ______. She has big eyes and a sweet smile.", "options": ["voice", "face", "hair", "hand"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "大眼睛和甜美笑容描述的是臉 face。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1547, "question": "Our school has some new ______ this year. For example, we can't use cellphones in class.", "options": ["faces", "rules", "tools", "hobbies"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "不能在課堂用手機是規定 rules。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1548, "question": "Peter always has great ______ for our class parties, so everyone asks him for help.", "options": ["ideas", "faces", "noises", "mistakes"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "大家請他幫忙辦派對，因為他有好點子 ideas。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1549, "question": "I feel like a ______. I was looking for my keys for hours but they have been in my pocket the whole time.", "options": ["fool", "ghost", "king", "stranger"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 fool 傻瓜（feel like a fool）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：feel like a fool「覺得自己像個傻瓜」\n【分析】找鑰匙找了好幾個小時，結果一直在自己口袋裡，覺得自己很蠢 → fool。\n【其他選項】(B) ghost「鬼」、(C) king「國王」、(D) stranger「陌生人」都無法說明這種糊塗的感受。\n【例句】Don't be a fool. Nobody can finish all that homework in one hour.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1550, "question": "I'm new in this town and I don't know anyone here. I feel like a ______.", "options": ["king", "stranger", "fool", "hero"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "不認識任何人，覺得像陌生人 stranger。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1551, "question": "Grace laughed at herself. She wore her T-shirt inside out all day and felt like a ______.", "options": ["fool", "king", "ghost", "leader"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "衣服整天穿反，覺得自己像傻瓜 fool。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1552, "question": "Everyone gave Andy flowers after he saved the little girl from the river. He is a real ______.", "options": ["stranger", "fool", "hero", "ghost"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "救了落水女孩是英雄 hero。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1553, "question": "You may have a long drive because of the terrible ______. There are usually a lot of cars and buses during this time.", "options": ["experience", "machine", "service", "traffic"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 traffic 交通", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：terrible/heavy traffic「糟糕／擁擠的交通」\n【分析】後句「這段時間通常有很多汽車和公車」，所以開車會很久是因為交通很塞 → traffic。\n【其他選項】(A) experience「經驗」、(B) machine「機器」、(C) service「服務」都與車多造成車程久無關。\n【例句】The traffic is always heavy on Friday evenings.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1554, "question": "We were late for the movie because of the heavy ______ on the highway.", "options": ["traffic", "weather", "service", "machine"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "高速公路上車很多→交通 traffic。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1555, "question": "The ______ at this restaurant is great. The waiters are always polite and fast.", "options": ["traffic", "service", "experience", "price"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "服務生有禮又快速，指服務 service。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1556, "question": "Living in Japan for a year was a wonderful ______ for me. I learned a lot.", "options": ["machine", "traffic", "experience", "service"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "在日本住一年學到很多，是一段經驗 experience。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1557, "question": "My ______ hurts so much that I cannot even turn my head.", "options": ["arm", "knee", "neck", "stomach"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 neck 脖子（身體部位）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：身體部位 neck「脖子」\n【分析】線索 cannot even turn my head「連頭都不能轉」，轉頭要用脖子 → neck。\n【其他選項】(A) arm「手臂」、(B) knee「膝蓋」、(D) stomach「胃；肚子」都與轉頭無關。\n【例句】Giraffes have very long necks.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1558, "question": "I ate too much ice cream, and now my ______ hurts.", "options": ["neck", "stomach", "knee", "ear"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "吃太多冰淇淋會肚子痛 stomach。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1559, "question": "Ken fell off his bike and hurt his ______. Now he can't bend his leg.", "options": ["knee", "neck", "nose", "shoulder"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "不能彎腿是膝蓋受傷 knee。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1560, "question": "Please raise your ______ if you know the answer.", "options": ["neck", "foot", "hand", "head"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "舉手回答 raise your hand。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1561, "question": "Tomorrow is Sam's last day in the office. Nobody knows why he decided to ______.", "options": ["hide", "leave", "pack", "walk"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 leave 離開（離職）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：decide to + V；leave「離開（工作）」\n【分析】線索 last day in the office「在辦公室的最後一天」，表示他決定離職 → leave。\n【其他選項】(A) hide「躲藏」、(C) pack「打包」、(D) walk「走路」都不能表達離開這份工作。\n【例句】My sister decided to leave her job and study abroad.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1562, "question": "It's getting late. I have to ______ now, or I'll miss the last train.", "options": ["stay", "leave", "hide", "wait"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "不然會錯過末班車，所以得離開 leave。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1563, "question": "The cat always ______ under the bed when there's a typhoon.", "options": ["hides", "leaves", "packs", "walks"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "颱風時貓會躲在床下 hides。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1564, "question": "We're going to Kenting tomorrow. Don't forget to ______ your swimsuit tonight.", "options": ["hide", "leave", "pack", "wash"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "出遊前一晚要打包 pack 泳衣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1565, "question": "It's not a good idea to go mountain climbing in this bad ______. We should wait until the typhoon goes away.", "options": ["chance", "dream", "habit", "weather"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 weather 天氣", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：bad weather「惡劣的天氣」\n【分析】線索 typhoon「颱風」，表示天氣不好，不適合爬山 → weather。\n【其他選項】(A) chance「機會」、(B) dream「夢想」、(C) habit「習慣」都與颱風無關。\n【例句】The weather in Taipei is often rainy in spring.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1566, "question": "Eating breakfast every day is a good ______. It keeps you healthy.", "options": ["habit", "weather", "dream", "chance"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "每天吃早餐是好習慣 habit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1567, "question": "Becoming a pilot has been Henry's ______ since he was a little boy.", "options": ["habit", "weather", "dream", "traffic"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "從小想當飛行員是夢想 dream。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1568, "question": "The ______ is so nice today. Let's have a picnic in the park.", "options": ["chance", "habit", "dream", "weather"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "天氣好適合野餐 weather。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1569, "question": "The new guy at the help desk answers calls like a ______. There are no ups and downs in his voice and you can't tell if he is happy or sad.", "options": ["father", "foreigner", "radio", "robot"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 robot 機器人（like a robot）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：like a robot「像機器人一樣（沒有感情）」\n【分析】線索「聲音沒有高低起伏」、「聽不出他是開心或難過」，表示說話毫無感情，像機器人 → robot。\n【其他選項】(A) father「父親」、(B) foreigner「外國人」、(C) radio「收音機」都不能表達「沒有情緒」的特徵。\n【例句】He walks like a robot because his new shoes are too tight.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1570, "question": "Mr. Lin speaks English with an accent, so people often think he's a ______.", "options": ["robot", "foreigner", "radio", "teacher"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "說話有口音被以為是外國人 foreigner。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1571, "question": "The ______ in this factory can work 24 hours a day without getting tired.", "options": ["robots", "foreigners", "fathers", "radios"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "不會累、24 小時工作的是機器人 robots。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1572, "question": "Grandpa likes to listen to the news on the ______ every morning.", "options": ["robot", "camera", "radio", "printer"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "聽新聞用收音機 radio。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1573, "question": "Jasmine planned to spend her summer in the country, but right after she got there, she started to ______ the noise in the city.", "options": ["enjoy", "mind", "miss", "notice"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 miss 想念", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：miss + N「想念…」\n【分析】她計畫在鄉下過暑假，但 but 表轉折，一到鄉下（很安靜）就開始想念城市的吵鬧 → miss。\n【其他選項】(A) enjoy「享受」：鄉下沒有城市噪音，無從享受；(B) mind「介意」：與 but 的轉折語意不合；(D) notice「注意到」：人在鄉下聽不到城市噪音。\n【例句】I miss my grandma's cooking when I'm away from home.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1574, "question": "Yuki moved to Taiwan last year. She sometimes ______ her friends in Japan.", "options": ["minds", "misses", "notices", "hates"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "離開日本會想念朋友 misses。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1575, "question": "Do you ______ if I open the window? It's hot in here.", "options": ["miss", "enjoy", "mind", "notice"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "Do you mind if...「你介意…嗎」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1576, "question": "Did you ______ anything strange about Ted today? He didn't say a word all morning.", "options": ["notice", "miss", "mind", "enjoy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "有沒有注意到什麼奇怪的事 notice。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1577, "question": "Don't let the children swim in the river. We don't know how ______ it is. It could be dangerous.", "options": ["deep", "far", "long", "thick"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞 deep 深的（how deep）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：how + adj. 問程度；deep「深的」\n【分析】不讓孩子在河裡游泳，因為不知道河有多「深」，可能很危險 → how deep。\n【其他選項】(B) far「遠」、(C) long「長」、(D) thick「厚」都不是游泳時危險的關鍵（水深）。\n【例句】How deep is this swimming pool?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1578, "question": "How ______ is it from your home to the MRT station? —About ten minutes on foot.", "options": ["deep", "far", "thick", "high"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "問距離用 how far。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1579, "question": "This dictionary is so ______ that it's too heavy for me to carry.", "options": ["thick", "deep", "far", "short"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "字典很厚所以很重 thick。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1580, "question": "How ______ did you stay in Tainan? —For a week.", "options": ["far", "deep", "long", "often"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "問待多久用 how long。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1581, "question": "Ben always uses his birthday as a(n) ______ to ask Dad to buy him something expensive.", "options": ["action", "excuse", "prize", "rule"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 excuse 藉口", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：use sth as an excuse to V「把…當作藉口去做…」\n【分析】Ben 總是拿生日「當藉口」要爸爸買貴的東西給他 → excuse。題目有 a(n)，excuse 開頭為母音，用 an。\n【其他選項】(A) action「行動」、(C) prize「獎品」、(D) rule「規定」放入 use...as a(n) ___ to ask... 語意都不通。\n【例句】Don't use the rain as an excuse to skip PE class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1582, "question": "Tim was late again, and his ______ was that his alarm clock didn't ring.", "options": ["prize", "excuse", "rule", "habit"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "遲到的理由（藉口）excuse。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1583, "question": "The first ______ in our classroom is: no eating during class.", "options": ["rule", "excuse", "prize", "action"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "上課不准吃東西是規定 rule。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1584, "question": "Nina won first ______ in the drawing contest and got a new bike.", "options": ["excuse", "rule", "prize", "action"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "比賽第一名 first prize。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1585, "question": "Tom's voice ______ when he talks about his neighbors. He speaks faster, his face becomes redder and you can almost see fire in his eyes.", "options": ["appears", "drops", "grows", "rises"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 rise 升高（聲音提高）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：one's voice rises「聲音提高（變大聲）」\n【分析】後句說他講話變快、臉變紅、眼睛冒火，表示他很生氣，聲音會「提高」→ rises。\n【其他選項】(A) appears「出現」，聲音一直都在，不合；(B) drops「降低」與生氣相反；(C) grows「成長、變大」不用來形容音量提高。\n【例句】The price of vegetables always rises after a typhoon.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1586, "question": "The sun ______ in the east every morning.", "options": ["drops", "rises", "grows", "appears"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "太陽從東方升起 rises。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1587, "question": "The temperature ______ to 10°C last night, so we all wore jackets.", "options": ["rose", "grew", "dropped", "appeared"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "大家穿外套，表示氣溫下降 dropped。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1588, "question": "A rainbow ______ in the sky after the rain stopped.", "options": ["appeared", "dropped", "rose", "grew"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "雨停後彩虹出現 appeared。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1589, "question": "See the ruler on your right? Please ______ it to me. I need to draw a line.", "options": ["check", "collect", "hand", "turn"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 hand 遞交（hand sth to sb）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：hand + 物 + to + 人「把某物遞給某人」\n【分析】「看到你右邊的尺嗎？請把它遞給我，我要畫線」→ hand it to me。\n【其他選項】(A) check「檢查」、(B) collect「收集」、(D) turn「轉動」都不接 it to me 表「遞給我」的意思。\n【例句】Could you hand me the salt, please?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1590, "question": "The teacher asked us to ______ our homework to the class leader before 8 a.m.", "options": ["hand", "check", "turn", "fold"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "把作業交給班長 hand...to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1591, "question": "Please ______ your answers carefully before you hand in the test.", "options": ["collect", "check", "hand", "turn"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "交卷前檢查答案 check。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1592, "question": "My cousin likes to ______ stamps from different countries.", "options": ["hand", "turn", "collect", "check"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "收集郵票 collect。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1593, "question": "Mark: We can't enter the house. I can't find my key!\nBilly: Is it possible that you ______ it in the car?", "options": ["caught", "changed", "found", "left"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 leave 遺留（leave sth in/at 地點）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：leave + 物 + 地點「把某物遺忘在某處」\n【分析】Mark 找不到鑰匙，Billy 問「有沒有可能你把它留在車上了？」→ left it in the car。\n【其他選項】(A) caught「抓到」、(B) changed「改變」不合語意；(C) found「找到」與「找不到鑰匙」矛盾。\n【例句】Oh no! I left my umbrella on the bus.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1594, "question": "I can't find my cellphone. Maybe I ______ it at school.", "options": ["left", "found", "caught", "changed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "把物品遺留在某地用 leave，left it at school。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1595, "question": "Jason ______ a big fish in the river last Sunday.", "options": ["left", "changed", "caught", "lost"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "釣到大魚 caught。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1596, "question": "Good news! I ______ my lost wallet under the sofa.", "options": ["left", "found", "changed", "caught"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "在沙發下找到錢包 found。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1597, "question": "Jim always forgets my birthday. He has asked me many times and still can't ______ it.", "options": ["answer", "celebrate", "remember", "understand"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 remember 記得", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：remember「記得」（與 forget 相反）\n【分析】線索 always forgets「總是忘記」、問了很多次還是「記不住」→ can't remember it。\n【其他選項】(A) answer「回答」、(B) celebrate「慶祝」、(D) understand「理解」都與「忘記生日」的語意無關。\n【例句】I can't remember where I put my glasses.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1598, "question": "Please ______ to bring your PE clothes tomorrow.", "options": ["remember", "answer", "understand", "celebrate"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "記得帶體育服 remember to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1599, "question": "We'll ______ Grandpa's 80th birthday with a big dinner.", "options": ["understand", "celebrate", "answer", "remember"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "慶祝生日 celebrate。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1600, "question": "The teacher explained the question three times, but I still don't ______ it.", "options": ["celebrate", "answer", "understand", "forget"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "解釋三次仍不懂 understand。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1601, "question": "My sister was very ______ with me because I broke her new pencil box.", "options": ["popular", "shy", "honest", "angry"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜形容詞 angry 生氣的（angry with sb）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：be angry with + 人「對某人生氣」\n【分析】因為我弄壞她的新鉛筆盒，所以姊姊（妹妹）對我很生氣 → angry with me。\n【其他選項】(A) popular with「受…歡迎」、(B) shy「害羞」、(C) honest with「對…誠實」都不是弄壞東西後的反應。\n【例句】Mom was angry with me because I came home late.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1602, "question": "You should be ______ with your parents and tell them the truth.", "options": ["angry", "honest", "shy", "busy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "說實話 → 對父母誠實 honest with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1603, "question": "Coach Chen is ______ with the students. Everyone loves his classes.", "options": ["angry", "shy", "popular", "honest"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "大家都愛他的課，受歡迎 popular with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1604, "question": "Dad was ______ with my brother because he lied about his grades.", "options": ["proud", "popular", "happy", "angry"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "說謊所以爸爸生氣 angry with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1605, "question": "You can't ______ Tasty Bakery's meat pie! It's so delicious that even some restaurants in town order it.", "options": ["cook", "cut", "hit", "miss"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 miss 錯過（You can't miss...）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：You can't miss + N.「你絕不能錯過…」\n【分析】後句說肉派好吃到連餐廳都向他們訂，所以是「千萬別錯過」→ miss。\n【其他選項】(A) cook「烹煮」、(B) cut「切」、(C) hit「打」放入句中都無法表達推薦的語意。\n【例句】You can't miss the night markets when you visit Taipei.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1606, "question": "Hurry up, or we'll ______ the school bus.", "options": ["hit", "miss", "catch", "cut"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "快點不然會錯過校車 miss。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1607, "question": "Be careful with the knife when you ______ the onions.", "options": ["cut", "miss", "hit", "cook"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "用刀切洋蔥 cut。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1608, "question": "The typhoon is going to ______ southern Taiwan tomorrow night.", "options": ["miss", "cook", "hit", "cut"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "颱風侵襲 hit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1609, "question": "Mark studies very hard and never ______ classes. He goes to school even when he is sick.", "options": ["loses", "misses", "changes", "forgets"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 miss 錯過（miss classes 缺課）", "explanation": "【句型】詞彙題：miss classes / school「缺課」\n【分析】後句說他「連生病都去上學」，所以從不缺課 → never misses classes。\n【其他選項】(A) loses「遺失」、(C) changes「改變」、(D) forgets「忘記」都不能與 classes 搭配表示缺課。\n【例句】Try not to miss any classes before the final exam.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1610, "question": "Ted got a cold and ______ school for two days.", "options": ["lost", "missed", "forgot", "changed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "感冒缺課 missed school。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1611, "question": "I ______ my umbrella on the MRT, so I had to buy a new one.", "options": ["missed", "changed", "lost", "failed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "雨傘弄丟 lost。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1612, "question": "Mom often ______ where she parks her car at the mall.", "options": ["misses", "loses", "changes", "forgets"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "忘記車停哪裡 forgets。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1613, "question": "If you are not afraid of talking to strangers, you'll have more ______ to make friends.", "options": ["languages", "opportunities", "prescriptions", "problems"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 opportunity 機會", "explanation": "【句型】have opportunities to V＝有機會做某事。\n【分析】不害怕和陌生人說話，就會有更多「機會」交朋友，opportunities 正確。\n【其他選項】(A) languages 語言；(C) prescriptions 處方箋；(D) problems 問題，皆不合「交朋友」的語意。\n【例句】Joining the club gives students more opportunities to practice English.（參加社團讓學生有更多機會練英文。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1614, "question": "Studying abroad gave Lily a great ______ to learn about other cultures.", "options": ["problem", "opportunity", "reason", "language"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "出國讀書給她「機會」認識其他文化，opportunity。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1615, "question": "The doctor wrote a ______ for some medicine for my cough.", "options": ["prescription", "chance", "message", "program"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "醫生開藥用的是「處方箋」，prescription。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1616, "question": "Math is hard for Tom. He has many ______ with his homework every day.", "options": ["opportunities", "languages", "problems", "hobbies"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "數學很難，作業上有很多「問題」，problems。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1617, "question": "Some songs are forgotten very quickly. A really good song can pass the test of ______ and be remembered for many, many years.", "options": ["knowledge", "sound", "time", "weather"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜the test of time 時間的考驗", "explanation": "【句型】pass / stand the test of time＝經得起時間考驗。\n【分析】前句說有些歌很快被遺忘，後面說好歌能被記住「很多很多年」，所以是通過「時間」的考驗，選 time。\n【其他選項】(A) knowledge 知識；(B) sound 聲音；(D) weather 天氣，都與「被記住很多年」無關。\n【例句】This old bridge has passed the test of time.（這座老橋經得起時間的考驗。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1618, "question": "Ms. Lin's ______ of history is amazing. She can answer any question about the past.", "options": ["weather", "knowledge", "sound", "season"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "能回答任何歷史問題，代表她的歷史「知識」豐富，knowledge。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1619, "question": "Turn down the ______ of the TV, please. The baby is sleeping.", "options": ["sound", "time", "test", "knowledge"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "嬰兒在睡覺，要把電視「聲音」轉小，sound。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1620, "question": "The ______ is getting colder. Remember to wear a jacket when you go out.", "options": ["knowledge", "sound", "weather", "habit"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "變冷又要穿外套，指「天氣」，weather。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1621, "question": "Roy: Why didn't you eat your cake?\nKay: I'm still full. Can I ______ it for later?\nRoy: Sure.", "options": ["pass", "save", "share", "stop"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜save sth for later 留到之後", "explanation": "【句型】save + 物 + for later＝把…留到之後。\n【分析】Kay 還很飽，想把蛋糕「留著」晚點吃，for later 是線索，選 save。\n【其他選項】(A) pass 傳遞；(C) share 分享；(D) stop 停止，都和 for later「留到之後」不搭。\n【例句】I'll save this chocolate for tomorrow.（我要把這塊巧克力留到明天。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1622, "question": "Ivy wants to buy a new camera, so she ______ some money every month.", "options": ["spends", "saves", "stops", "passes"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "為買相機每月「存」錢，save。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1623, "question": "Could you ______ me the salt, please? I can't reach it.", "options": ["save", "stop", "pass", "share"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "請別人「遞」鹽，pass。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1624, "question": "It's dangerous to cross now. Please ______ and wait for the green light.", "options": ["save", "pass", "share", "stop"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "危險要「停下」等綠燈，stop。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1625, "question": "John has finished his studies at music school. Now with his good ______ of music, he can teach at school.", "options": ["future", "habit", "knowledge", "language"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜knowledge of 對…的知識", "explanation": "【句型】knowledge of + N＝對…的知識。\n【分析】John 讀完音樂學校，具備良好的音樂「知識」，所以能教書，選 knowledge。\n【其他選項】(A) future 未來；(B) habit 習慣；(D) language 語言，與「能教音樂」的原因不符。\n【例句】Mr. Wu has a lot of knowledge of Taiwanese history.（吳老師很懂台灣歷史。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1626, "question": "Getting up early is a good ______. It helps you start the day well.", "options": ["knowledge", "habit", "future", "language"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "早起是好「習慣」，habit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1627, "question": "Nina reads a lot of science books, so she has good ______ of nature.", "options": ["future", "language", "habit", "knowledge"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "讀很多科學書，具備自然方面的「知識」，knowledge。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1628, "question": "Jacob wants to be a doctor in the ______, so he studies very hard now.", "options": ["future", "knowledge", "habit", "past"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "將來想當醫生，in the future「未來」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1629, "question": "Tim: Can you see what the word is? The first ______ is not clear.\nAnn: Oh, it's \"r.\" The word is \"ring.\"", "options": ["idea", "lesson", "letter", "sound"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 letter 字母", "explanation": "【句型】letter＝字母（亦可指「信」）。\n【分析】Ann 回答「是 r」，r 是一個「字母」，所以第一個字母看不清楚，選 letter。\n【其他選項】(A) idea 想法；(B) lesson 課；(D) sound 聲音，題目問的是「看」不清楚的字，不是聲音。\n【例句】The word \"apple\" begins with the letter \"a.\"（apple 這個字以字母 a 開頭。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1630, "question": "There are twenty-six ______ in the English alphabet.", "options": ["letters", "words", "lessons", "sounds"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "英文字母表有 26 個「字母」，letters。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1631, "question": "I have a good ______. Let's have a picnic by the river this Sunday.", "options": ["letter", "idea", "lesson", "sound"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "提出野餐的「點子」，idea。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1632, "question": "Did you hear that strange ______ outside? It was like a cat crying.", "options": ["letter", "idea", "sound", "lesson"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "聽到奇怪的「聲音」，sound。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1633, "question": "Tom: Jack, put the letter in the ______ and send it to Mr. Wu, please.\nJack: Sure.", "options": ["closet", "envelope", "tunnel", "corner"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 envelope 信封", "explanation": "【句型】put the letter in the envelope＝把信放進信封。\n【分析】要把信寄給吳先生，信要放進「信封」，選 envelope。\n【其他選項】(A) closet 衣櫥；(C) tunnel 隧道；(D) corner 角落，皆不是寄信時裝信的東西。\n【例句】Don't forget to write the address on the envelope.（別忘了在信封上寫地址。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1634, "question": "Please hang your coat in the ______ before you sit down.", "options": ["envelope", "closet", "tunnel", "stamp"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "外套掛在「衣櫥」裡，closet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1635, "question": "Grandma put some red ______ under her pillow for us on Lunar New Year's Eve.", "options": ["closets", "corners", "envelopes", "tunnels"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "除夕的「紅包」為 red envelope。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1636, "question": "The train is going through a long ______, so it is dark outside.", "options": ["envelope", "closet", "corner", "tunnel"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "火車穿過長「隧道」，外面很暗，tunnel。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1637, "question": "I want to buy a cell phone. Which ______ is better?", "options": ["art", "fake", "light", "brand"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 brand 品牌", "explanation": "【句型】Which brand ...?＝哪個品牌…？\n【分析】要買手機，問哪個「品牌」比較好，選 brand。\n【其他選項】(A) art 藝術；(B) fake 假的／假貨，Which fake is better 不合理；(C) light 燈／光，皆不合買手機的情境。\n【例句】This brand of shoes is very popular with students.（這個品牌的鞋子很受學生歡迎。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1638, "question": "My dad only drinks coffee from one ______. He says it tastes the best.", "options": ["art", "brand", "light", "fake"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "只喝某一「品牌」的咖啡，brand。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1639, "question": "Don't buy that bag at the night market. It may be a ______.", "options": ["brand", "light", "fake", "art"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "夜市的包包可能是「假貨」，fake。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1640, "question": "It's too dark in here. Can you turn on the ______?", "options": ["light", "brand", "art", "fake"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "太暗了，打開「燈」，light。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1641, "question": "House prices are ______, so you can buy a house at a lower price than before.", "options": ["moving", "growing", "dropping", "climbing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜dropping 下跌", "explanation": "【句型】prices are dropping / going down＝價格正在下跌。\n【分析】後句說可以用「比以前低的價格」買房，表示房價正在「下跌」，選 dropping。\n【其他選項】(A) moving 移動；(B) growing 成長／上升；(D) climbing 攀升，(B)(D) 皆表上漲，與「較低價格」矛盾。\n【例句】The temperature is dropping quickly tonight.（今晚氣溫快速下降。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1642, "question": "Oil prices keep ______, so it costs more to drive a car now.", "options": ["dropping", "climbing", "falling", "moving"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "開車花費更多，表示油價「攀升」，climbing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1643, "question": "The number of students in the village is ______ because many families moved to the city.", "options": ["dropping", "growing", "climbing", "rising"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "家庭搬到城市，學生人數「減少」，dropping。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1644, "question": "This little tree is ______ fast. It is already taller than me.", "options": ["dropping", "moving", "growing", "falling"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "樹已比我高，表示「長」得快，growing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1645, "question": "Alice doesn't take medicine when she has a cold. She believes the body is able to ______ the cold by itself.", "options": ["catch", "fight", "hunt", "pass"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 fight 對抗", "explanation": "【句型】fight (against) + 疾病＝對抗…。\n【分析】她感冒不吃藥，因為相信身體能自己「對抗」感冒，選 fight。\n【其他選項】(A) catch a cold 是「得到」感冒，不合語意；(C) hunt 獵捕；(D) pass 傳遞／通過，皆不合。\n【例句】Eating vegetables helps your body fight sickness.（吃蔬菜幫助身體對抗疾病。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1646, "question": "Wear a jacket, or you'll ______ a cold.", "options": ["fight", "catch", "hunt", "pass"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "不穿外套會「得到」感冒，catch a cold。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1647, "question": "Doctors around the world are working together to ______ the disease.", "options": ["catch", "pass", "fight", "hunt"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "醫生合作「對抗」疾病，fight。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1648, "question": "Lions usually ______ for food in groups.", "options": ["fight", "pass", "catch", "hunt"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "獅子成群「獵食」，hunt for food。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1649, "question": "It is not safe to swim in the sea, so Susan's mother asked her to ______ it.", "options": ["invite", "draw", "avoid", "join"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 avoid 避免", "explanation": "【句型】ask sb to V＝要求某人做…；avoid＝避免、避開。\n【分析】在海裡游泳不安全，所以媽媽要她「避免」這件事，選 avoid。\n【其他選項】(A) invite 邀請；(B) draw 畫；(D) join 加入，皆與「不安全」的語意相反或無關。\n【例句】You should avoid eating too much fried food.（你應該避免吃太多油炸食物。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1650, "question": "The road is very busy at eight. Let's leave earlier to ______ the traffic.", "options": ["join", "avoid", "invite", "follow"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "提早出門「避開」車潮，avoid。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1651, "question": "Mark wants to ______ the school band because he loves playing the drums.", "options": ["avoid", "draw", "join", "invite"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "喜歡打鼓想「加入」樂隊，join。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1652, "question": "Helen is going to ______ all her classmates to her birthday party.", "options": ["avoid", "join", "draw", "invite"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "「邀請」同學參加生日派對，invite。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1653, "question": "The movie star does not like his family to ______ in public places with him; he does not want people to know who they are.", "options": ["agree", "appear", "cheat", "decide"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 appear 出現", "explanation": "【句型】appear (in public)＝（公開）出現、露面。\n【分析】他不想讓別人知道家人是誰，所以不喜歡家人和他一起在公共場所「出現」，選 appear。\n【其他選項】(A) agree 同意；(C) cheat 欺騙／作弊；(D) decide 決定，都無法說明「不想被認出」。\n【例句】The singer appeared on TV last night.（那位歌手昨晚上了電視。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1654, "question": "A rainbow ______ in the sky after the rain stopped.", "options": ["decided", "appeared", "agreed", "cheated"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "雨停後彩虹「出現」，appear。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1655, "question": "It's wrong to ______ on a test. You should study hard instead.", "options": ["appear", "agree", "cheat", "decide"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "考試「作弊」是錯的，cheat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1656, "question": "Nora couldn't ______ which dress to wear, so she asked her sister for help.", "options": ["decide", "appear", "cheat", "agree"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "無法「決定」穿哪件，decide。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1657, "question": "The ______ of the house is too high. My parents do not have enough money to buy it.", "options": ["price", "size", "space", "wall"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜名詞 price 價格", "explanation": "【句型】The price is high / low＝價格高／低。\n【分析】父母錢不夠買，表示房子的「價格」太高，選 price。\n【其他選項】(B) size 大小；(C) space 空間；(D) wall 牆，雖可說「高」，但與「錢不夠」沒有因果關係。\n【例句】The price of this jacket is too high for me.（這件外套的價格對我來說太高了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1658, "question": "These shoes are on sale. The ______ is fifty percent lower than last week.", "options": ["size", "price", "space", "wall"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "特價比上週低一半，指「價格」，price。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1659, "question": "This T-shirt is too small. Do you have a bigger ______?", "options": ["price", "space", "size", "wall"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "衣服太小要大一點的「尺寸」，size。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1660, "question": "There isn't enough ______ in my room for a piano.", "options": ["price", "size", "wall", "space"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "房間沒有足夠「空間」放鋼琴，space。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1661, "question": "Christmas is coming. Jane and her brother are busy ______ their house with a Christmas tree and some flowers.", "options": ["visiting", "building", "cleaning", "decorating"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜動詞 decorate 裝飾（be busy Ving）", "explanation": "【句型】be busy + Ving＝忙著做…；decorate A with B＝用 B 裝飾 A。\n【分析】用「聖誕樹和花」來布置房子，是「裝飾」，with a Christmas tree and some flowers 是線索，選 decorating。\n【其他選項】(A) visiting 拜訪；(B) building 建造；(C) cleaning 打掃，都不會「用聖誕樹和花」來做。\n【例句】We decorated the classroom with balloons for the party.（我們用氣球布置教室準備派對。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1662, "question": "Before Lunar New Year, everyone in my family is busy ______ the house. We wash windows and floors.", "options": ["decorating", "visiting", "cleaning", "building"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "洗窗戶和地板是「打掃」，be busy cleaning。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1663, "question": "Ruby decorated her room ______ pictures of her favorite singers.", "options": ["for", "with", "by", "in"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "decorate A with B，用照片「裝飾」房間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1664, "question": "During the summer vacation, we ______ our grandparents in Hualien and stayed there for a week.", "options": ["visited", "decorated", "built", "cleaned"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "放假去花蓮「拜訪」祖父母並住了一週，visit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1665, "question": "Joe: Where was Mary last weekend? I ______ her, but no one answered the phone.\nTom: I don't know. Why not try again?", "options": ["asked", "called", "found", "talked to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜call 打電話給某人", "explanation": "【句型】call + 人 = 打電話給某人（及物動詞，後面直接接受詞）。\n【分析】後句 no one answered the phone（沒人接電話）→ 表示「我打電話給她」，用 called。\n【其他選項】(A) asked 詢問，與接電話無關；(C) found 找到，若找到她就不會沒人接；(D) talked to 和…說話，沒人接電話就無法交談。\n【例句】I called Grandma last night, but she was asleep.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1666, "question": "Kevin: Did you ______ Amy about the party?\nJill: Yes, but her phone was busy, so I sent her a message.", "options": ["call", "visit", "meet", "write"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "her phone was busy（電話占線）表示有打電話給她，用 call。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1667, "question": "Nobody ______ the phone when I called the store, so I went there myself.", "options": ["called", "answered", "asked", "heard"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "answer the phone 接電話；沒人接，所以親自去。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1668, "question": "Please ______ me when you get to the train station. I'll pick you up.", "options": ["take", "find", "call", "answer"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "到站時「打電話給我」，我去接你，用 call me。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1669, "question": "Soccer is a kind of ______ sport. That means you cannot play it by yourself.", "options": ["team", "popular", "funny", "boring"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜team sport 團隊運動", "explanation": "【句型】team sport = 團隊運動（需要多人一起進行的運動）。\n【分析】後句 you cannot play it by yourself（無法一個人玩）→ 是需要隊友的「團隊」運動。\n【其他選項】(B) popular 受歡迎的、(C) funny 好笑的、(D) boring 無聊的，都無法解釋「不能一個人玩」。\n【例句】Basketball is a team sport, but swimming is not.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1670, "question": "You need eleven players to play baseball because it is a ______ sport.", "options": ["dangerous", "team", "cheap", "quiet"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "需要十一個人 → 團隊運動 team sport。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1671, "question": "Ken likes running because he can do it ______. He doesn't need anyone else.", "options": ["by himself", "with a team", "in a group", "for others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "不需要別人 → 自己一個人 by himself。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1672, "question": "Our class has a volleyball ______, and we practice together every Friday.", "options": ["game", "ball", "team", "player"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "一起練習的團體 → team 隊伍。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1673, "question": "Our teacher ______ the old lessons before starting a new one.", "options": ["reviewed", "noticed", "previewed", "remembered"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜會考歷屆｜review 複習", "explanation": "【句型】review = 複習（舊的）；preview = 預習（新的）。\n【分析】the old lessons（舊課）+ before starting a new one（開始新課前）→ 先複習舊課，用 reviewed。\n【其他選項】(B) noticed 注意到，語意不合；(C) previewed 預習，對象應是新課；(D) remembered 記得，老師「記得舊課」不合理。\n【例句】I review my notes every night before the test.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1674, "question": "Before the final exam, Joy ______ all the words she learned this term.", "options": ["previewed", "reviewed", "noticed", "invited"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "考前把學過的單字再看一次 → 複習 reviewed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1675, "question": "It's a good idea to ______ the next lesson so you know what the teacher will talk about tomorrow.", "options": ["preview", "review", "repeat", "return"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "明天要上的新課 → 預習 preview。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1676, "question": "Mr. Chen asked us to ______ Units 1 to 3 again because the test is on Monday.", "options": ["notice", "forget", "review", "preview"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "Units 1–3 已學過且要考試 → 複習 review。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1677, "question": "[圖：學校操場上，幾位學生正在運動：兩人在打羽毛球、一人在跳繩，另有幾位學生坐在長椅上休息；正在運動的三位學生都戴著眼鏡]\nLook at the picture. All of the students who are exercising are wearing ______.", "options": ["caps", "glasses", "jackets", "pants"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜看圖選字：衣著配件 glasses", "explanation": "【句型】wear + 衣物／配件（戴著、穿著）；看圖找出「所有正在運動的學生」的共同點。\n【分析】線索 All of the students who are exercising：圖中打羽毛球、跳繩的學生都戴著眼鏡，故選 glasses（眼鏡）。\n【其他選項】(A) caps 帽子、(C) jackets 夾克、(D) pants 長褲：並非每位運動中的學生都有穿戴，不是共同點。\n【例句】My grandpa wears glasses when he reads the newspaper.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1678, "question": "[圖：三個小孩在雪地裡堆雪人，每個人都戴著手套，只有一人戴帽子]\nLook at the picture. All of the kids who are making the snowman are wearing ______.", "options": ["hats", "gloves", "shorts", "sunglasses"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "三個堆雪人的小孩都戴手套，只有一人戴帽子，故選 gloves。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1679, "question": "[圖：公園裡四個人在跑步，四人都穿著短褲，其中兩人戴帽子]\nLook at the picture. Everyone who is running in the park is wearing ______.", "options": ["caps", "jackets", "shorts", "scarves"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "四位跑者共同穿著短褲；帽子只有兩人戴，故選 shorts。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1680, "question": "[圖：教室裡有五位學生，坐著寫字的三位學生都戴著口罩，站著的兩位沒有]\nLook at the picture. All of the students who are sitting and writing are wearing ______.", "options": ["masks", "glasses", "coats", "boots"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "坐著寫字的學生共同點是戴口罩，故選 masks。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1681, "question": "Rita ______ her dogs many times a day. That's why they're too fat.", "options": ["feeds", "kisses", "walks", "washes"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜動詞辨義 feed（餵食）", "explanation": "【句型】feed + 動物（餵食）；由後句結果推回原因。\n【分析】線索 That's why they're too fat：狗太胖是因為一天被餵很多次，故選 feeds（餵食）。\n【其他選項】(B) kisses 親吻、(D) washes 幫…洗澡：與變胖無關；(C) walks 遛（狗）：反而會讓狗消耗熱量變瘦。\n【例句】Please feed the fish before you go to school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1682, "question": "Ben forgot to ______ his plants for two weeks, so they all died.", "options": ["water", "feed", "plant", "cut"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "植物兩週沒澆水而枯死，water 當動詞為「澆水」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1683, "question": "My cat looks thin. Maybe we should ______ her more food every day.", "options": ["take", "give", "bring", "make"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "give + 人／動物 + 東西：給牠更多食物。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1684, "question": "Mr. Lin ______ his dog in the park every evening, so the dog is very healthy.", "options": ["feeds", "washes", "walks", "kisses"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "每晚在公園「遛狗」讓狗健康，walk the dog 為遛狗。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1685, "question": "You can ask Sophia anything about butterflies and bees. She has great ______ of insects.", "options": ["chances", "knowledge", "news", "power"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜名詞辨義 knowledge（have great knowledge of）", "explanation": "【句型】have (great) knowledge of + 名詞：對……有豐富的知識。\n【分析】線索 You can ask Sophia anything about butterflies and bees：什麼都能問她，表示她對昆蟲懂很多，故選 knowledge（知識）。\n【其他選項】(A) chances 機會、(C) news 新聞／消息、(D) power 力量：都不能表達「懂得很多」，語意不合。\n【例句】Mr. Wang has great knowledge of Taiwanese history.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1686, "question": "Amy has read many books about stars. She has a lot of ______ about space.", "options": ["knowledge", "weather", "money", "noise"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "讀了很多星星的書，對太空有很多「知識」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1687, "question": "If you have any ______ about the homework, you can ask Ms. Chen after class.", "options": ["answers", "questions", "stories", "colors"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "對作業有「問題」可以下課問老師。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1688, "question": "Kevin can fix almost any computer. He has great ______ in this area.", "options": ["luck", "pain", "skill", "fear"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "什麼電腦都能修，表示他在這方面很有「技術」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1689, "question": "Adam slept ______ last night because he kept waking up from bad dreams.", "options": ["deeply", "early", "terribly", "quickly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜副詞辨義 terribly（睡得很糟）", "explanation": "【句型】一般動詞 + 情態副詞（修飾動作的方式）：sleep well / badly / terribly。\n【分析】線索 kept waking up from bad dreams：一直從惡夢中驚醒，表示睡得很糟，故選 terribly（很糟地）。\n【其他選項】(A) deeply 熟睡地：與一直驚醒矛盾；(B) early 早地：與惡夢無因果關係；(D) quickly 很快地：sleep quickly 不合語意。\n【例句】Lily sang terribly because she had a bad cold.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1690, "question": "The baby slept ______ after drinking her milk. She didn't wake up until morning.", "options": ["badly", "deeply", "loudly", "late"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "直到早上才醒，表示「熟睡地」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1691, "question": "Jason did ______ on the math test because he didn't study at all.", "options": ["poorly", "carefully", "happily", "well"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "完全沒讀書，所以考得「很差」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1692, "question": "The old man walked ______ because his leg hurt.", "options": ["quickly", "proudly", "slowly", "quietly"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "腳痛所以走得「很慢」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1693, "question": "Tara enjoys being with all kinds of animals; she even ______ a snake as a pet.", "options": ["drops", "gives", "keeps", "makes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜keep + 動物 + as a pet（飼養）", "explanation": "【句型】keep + 動物 + as a pet：把……當寵物飼養。\n【分析】線索 enjoys being with all kinds of animals、even：喜歡各種動物，甚至「養」了一條蛇當寵物，故選 keeps。\n【其他選項】(A) drops 掉落、(B) gives 給予、(D) makes 製作：都無法和 as a pet 搭配表示飼養。\n【例句】My cousin keeps two rabbits as pets.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1694, "question": "Lisa ______ a turtle as a pet because it is quiet and easy to take care of.", "options": ["keeps", "takes", "finds", "feels"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "keep ... as a pet 為「飼養當寵物」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1695, "question": "Our apartment is too small, so we can't ______ a big dog.", "options": ["make", "have", "give", "drop"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "have a dog 也可表示「養狗」；公寓太小養不了大狗。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1696, "question": "Tom wants to ______ care of the stray cat until it finds a new home.", "options": ["keep", "get", "take", "look"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "take care of 為固定片語「照顧」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1697, "question": "After four hours of mountain climbing, Rosa's legs got ______, so she took a rest on the top of the mountain.", "options": ["dirty", "sick", "sore", "strong"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜形容詞辨義 sore（痠痛的）＋連綴動詞 get", "explanation": "【句型】連綴動詞 get + 形容詞（變得……）；sore 痠痛的。\n【分析】線索 four hours of mountain climbing、took a rest：爬了四小時山，腿變得痠痛所以休息，故選 sore。\n【其他選項】(A) dirty 髒的：不需因此休息；(B) sick 生病的：通常形容人，不形容腿；(D) strong 強壯的：腿變強壯不會需要休息，因果不合。\n【例句】My arms got sore after I moved all the boxes.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1698, "question": "I talked for three hours at the party, and now my throat is ______.", "options": ["sore", "wet", "cheap", "empty"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "講話太久喉嚨「痛」，sore throat 喉嚨痛。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1699, "question": "After the long trip, everyone got ______ and went to bed early.", "options": ["hungry", "tired", "rich", "loud"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "長途旅行後大家「累了」所以早睡。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1700, "question": "Andy ate too much ice cream, and his stomach began to ______.", "options": ["smell", "laugh", "hurt", "sleep"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "吃太多冰淇淋肚子開始「痛」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1701, "question": "Joe is happy he is not at the ______ of the class now. His grades are better than half of his classmates' this school year.", "options": ["side", "front", "center", "bottom"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜名詞辨義 bottom（at the bottom of the class 班上墊底）", "explanation": "【句型】at the bottom of the class：在班上墊底；at the top of the class：班上頂尖。\n【分析】線索 His grades are better than half of his classmates'：成績贏過一半同學，表示不再是「墊底」，所以很開心 → bottom。\n【其他選項】(A) side 旁邊、(B) front 前面、(C) center 中間：都只是位置，無法表達成績排名的高低，語意不合。\n【例句】Mia studied hard and is now at the top of her class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1702, "question": "Wendy got the highest score on every test. She is at the ______ of her class.", "options": ["top", "bottom", "side", "back"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "每次考最高分 → 班上頂尖 at the top。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1703, "question": "The ball rolled down the hill and stopped at the ______ of it.", "options": ["top", "bottom", "middle", "front"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "球滾下山停在山「底」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1704, "question": "Sam was last in the race, but he was happy he finished it. He came in ______.", "options": ["first", "second", "last", "early"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "比賽最後一名 came in last。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1705, "question": "On windy days, the flowers in my garden ______ like shy children with their heads down.", "options": ["bow", "fall", "rise", "smell"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜115會考｜動詞辨義 bow（低頭、鞠躬）", "explanation": "【句型】bow：彎腰、低頭、鞠躬；本句用 like 把花比喻成低頭的害羞小孩。\n【分析】線索 like shy children with their heads down：風吹時花「低著頭」像害羞小孩，故選 bow。\n【其他選項】(B) fall 掉落／跌倒：不是低頭的樣子；(C) rise 上升：與 heads down 相反；(D) smell 聞起來：與低頭動作無關。\n【例句】The students bowed to their teacher at the end of the class.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1706, "question": "In Japan, people often ______ to say hello or thank you.", "options": ["bow", "shout", "cry", "jump"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "日本人打招呼或道謝時常「鞠躬」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1707, "question": "In fall, the leaves turn yellow and ______ from the trees.", "options": ["rise", "fall", "grow", "bow"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "秋天葉子變黃從樹上「掉落」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1708, "question": "Every morning, the sun ______ in the east.", "options": ["sets", "falls", "rises", "bows"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "太陽從東方「升起」用 rises。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1709, "question": "The math homework today is to do all the ______ on pages 11 to 13.", "options": ["answers", "exercises", "numbers", "subjects"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜講義錯題｜exercise（可數）= 習題、練習", "explanation": "【句型】do exercises = 做習題；exercise 當可數名詞指「練習題」。\n【分析】數學作業是做第 11 到 13 頁（on pages 11 to 13）的所有習題，用 exercises。\n【其他選項】(A) answers 答案，不能說「做答案」；(C) numbers 數字，不合；(D) subjects 科目，不會在某幾頁上。\n【例句】Please finish the exercises at the end of Lesson 3.\n備註：講義 p.60", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1710, "question": "Math, English, and science are my favorite school ______.", "options": ["subjects", "exercises", "answers", "numbers"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "數學、英文、自然是「科目」subjects。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1711, "question": "Teacher: Check your ______ on the board after you finish the test.", "options": ["questions", "answers", "pages", "subjects"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "考完後對「答案」answers。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1712, "question": "Doing some ______ every day, like jogging or swimming, keeps you healthy.", "options": ["homework", "subject", "exercise", "number"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "exercise 不可數時表「運動」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1713, "question": "If you don't want to be wet, just get out of the rain. Though the bad experience may be like ______ hanging over your head, believe there is always bright light ahead.", "options": ["a bright sun", "a dark cloud", "a rainy day", "a light wind"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜講義錯題｜a dark cloud（比喻壞事、陰影）", "explanation": "【句型】be like + 名詞（像…一樣）；a dark cloud hanging over sb.'s head 比喻揮之不去的壞事\n【分析】the bad experience 是壞經驗，又「掛在頭上」（hanging over your head），且和後句 bright light ahead 對比 → a dark cloud（烏雲）。\n【其他選項】(A) 太陽代表好事，與 bad 矛盾；(C) 下雨天不能「掛在頭上」；(D) 微風不代表壞事。\n【例句】The test is like a dark cloud over my weekend.\n備註：講義 p.335", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1714, "question": "After the long rainy week, the warm ______ finally came out and dried the streets.", "options": ["cloud", "sun", "storm", "snow"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 1（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "讓街道變乾的是太陽 sun。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1715, "question": "Her smile was like ______ on a cold winter day; it made everyone feel warm.", "options": ["a dark cloud", "a heavy rain", "a strong wind", "a ray of sunshine"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 2（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "讓人溫暖的比喻是 a ray of sunshine。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1716, "question": "The big exam next week is like a dark cloud ______ over Tim; he can't relax at all.", "options": ["hanging", "shining", "smiling", "dancing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "詞彙題｜類似題 3（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "烏雲籠罩頭上用 hanging over。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "詞彙題"}, {"id": 1717, "question": "______ exercise after work is a good way for me to forget the troubles in the office.", "options": ["Playing", "Making", "Going", "Doing"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜do exercise（動詞搭配詞）＋Ving 主詞", "explanation": "【句型】Ving 片語當主詞；動詞搭配：do exercise＝做運動。\n【分析】四個選項都是 Ving，可當主詞；關鍵在搭配詞，exercise「運動」要搭配動詞 do，Doing exercise after work「下班後做運動」。\n【其他選項】(A) play 搭配球類（play basketball）；(B) make 不和 exercise 搭配；(C) go 搭配 Ving（go swimming），不接 exercise。\n【例句】Doing exercise every morning keeps my grandpa healthy.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1718, "question": "______ yoga before bed helps me sleep well.", "options": ["Making", "Doing", "Taking", "Going"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "do yoga 為固定搭配。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1719, "question": "______ jogging in the park is my dad's habit.", "options": ["Going", "Doing", "Making", "Playing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "go jogging 為固定搭配。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1720, "question": "______ badminton with my sister is fun on weekends.", "options": ["Doing", "Going", "Playing", "Making"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "球類運動用 play，play badminton。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1721, "question": "Gina has always been ______ writing. In fact, she likes writing so much that she has decided to be a writer.", "options": ["embarrassed by", "fond of", "safe in", "worried about"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be fond of 喜歡", "explanation": "【句型】be fond of + N / Ving「喜歡…」\n【分析】後句 she likes writing so much「她非常喜歡寫作」以 In fact 補充前句，所以前句是「一直很喜歡寫作」→ fond of。\n【其他選項】(A) embarrassed by「因…感到尷尬」、(D) worried about「擔心…」與「喜歡寫作、想當作家」相反；(C) safe in 非此用法，語意不通。\n【例句】My little brother is fond of playing video games.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1722, "question": "Amy is ______ animals. She has two cats, a dog, and three rabbits.", "options": ["worried about", "afraid of", "fond of", "tired of"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "養很多動物表示喜歡動物 fond of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1723, "question": "Ryan is ______ his math test. He didn't study at all last night.", "options": ["fond of", "worried about", "proud of", "good at"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "沒讀書所以擔心考試 worried about。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1724, "question": "I was ______ my mistake when everyone laughed at me in class.", "options": ["embarrassed by", "fond of", "good at", "interested in"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "大家笑我，因錯誤感到尷尬 embarrassed by。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1725, "question": "Our school basketball team won the national game last night. We are so ______ them.", "options": ["popular with", "proud of", "sorry for", "worried about"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be proud of 以…為榮", "explanation": "【句型】be proud of + N「以…為榮」\n【分析】校隊昨晚贏得全國比賽，大家當然以他們為榮 → proud of。\n【其他選項】(A) popular with「受…歡迎」主詞應為被喜愛者，we 不合；(C) sorry for「為…感到難過」、(D) worried about「擔心」都與贏球的喜悅不合。\n【例句】Mom is proud of me because I got first place in the speech contest.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1726, "question": "Mr. Wu is very ______ his students. They all listen to him and love his classes.", "options": ["sorry for", "worried about", "popular with", "afraid of"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "學生都喜歡他 → 他受學生歡迎 popular with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1727, "question": "I feel ______ the old man. He lost his wallet and can't go home.", "options": ["proud of", "sorry for", "popular with", "fond of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "老人掉錢包回不了家，為他難過 sorry for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1728, "question": "Tina won the singing contest. Her parents are very ______ her.", "options": ["worried about", "sorry for", "tired of", "proud of"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "女兒得獎，父母以她為榮 proud of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1729, "question": "Henry does well at school and is always polite to his teachers. His friends like him, and his parents are ______ him.", "options": ["good at", "interesting to", "proud of", "worried about"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be proud of 以…為榮", "explanation": "【句型】be proud of + N「以…為榮」\n【分析】Henry 成績好、有禮貌、朋友喜歡他，父母當然以他為榮 → proud of。\n【其他選項】(A) good at「擅長」後接事物或技能，不接人；(B) interesting to「對…來說有趣」語意不合；(D) worried about「擔心」與前面正面描述矛盾。\n【例句】We are proud of our school's baseball team.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1730, "question": "Lisa is ______ drawing. She has won many art contests.", "options": ["proud of", "good at", "worried about", "sorry for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "得過很多美術比賽，擅長畫畫 good at。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1731, "question": "Mom is ______ Dad because he hasn't come home yet and it's already midnight.", "options": ["worried about", "proud of", "good at", "fond of"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "半夜還沒回家所以擔心 worried about。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1732, "question": "Coach Lee is ______ his players. They practiced hard and won the game.", "options": ["afraid of", "tired of", "proud of", "bad at"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "球員努力並贏球，教練以他們為榮 proud of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1733, "question": "The factory has been throwing trash into the river for years. Now ______ must be taken to stop this.", "options": ["action", "chances", "exercise", "notes"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜take action 採取行動（被動 action must be taken）", "explanation": "【句型】搭配詞 take action「採取行動」；被動語態 action must be taken\n【分析】工廠多年來把垃圾丟入河中，現在必須「採取行動」來阻止 → action must be taken (to V)。\n【其他選項】(B) take chances「冒險」、(D) take notes「做筆記」雖可搭配 take，但語意不合；(C) exercise 搭配 do/get exercise，且語意不通。\n【例句】We should take action to save the earth.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1734, "question": "Please ______ notes during the class. They will help you review.", "options": ["make", "take", "do", "have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "做筆記 take notes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1735, "question": "The government must ______ action to stop air pollution.", "options": ["make", "do", "take", "get"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "採取行動 take action。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1736, "question": "Don't take ______ when you ride a scooter. Always wear a helmet.", "options": ["notes", "action", "exercise", "chances"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "不要冒險 take chances。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1737, "question": "The beach party tonight ______ the end of our summer vacation. Tomorrow we are all going back home and getting ready for school.", "options": ["changes", "marks", "passes", "saves"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜mark the end of 標誌…的結束", "explanation": "【句型】搭配詞 mark the end/beginning of...「標誌著…的結束／開始」\n【分析】今晚的海灘派對之後，明天就要回家準備上學，表示派對「標誌著」暑假結束 → marks。\n【其他選項】(A) changes「改變」、(C) passes「通過、傳遞」、(D) saves「拯救、節省」都不能和 the end of 搭配成合理語意。\n【例句】The graduation ceremony marks the end of our junior high school life.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1738, "question": "Lunar New Year ______ the beginning of a new year in Taiwan.", "options": ["saves", "passes", "marks", "changes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "農曆新年標誌新一年開始 marks。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1739, "question": "Turning off the lights when you leave the room ______ energy.", "options": ["marks", "saves", "passes", "changes"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "隨手關燈節省能源 saves。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1740, "question": "Time ______ quickly when you are having fun.", "options": ["passes", "marks", "saves", "changes"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "時光飛逝 time passes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1741, "question": "Amy's father is very sick. The doctors can do nothing for him, so Amy went to the temple to ______ for him.", "options": ["care", "count", "look", "pray"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜pray for 為…祈禱", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 pray for + 人「為某人祈禱」\n【分析】爸爸病重、醫生束手無策，所以 Amy 去廟裡「為他祈禱」→ pray for him。線索 temple「廟」。\n【其他選項】(A) care for「照顧」：應在身邊照顧，不必去廟裡；(B) count for 非此語意；(C) look for「尋找」：爸爸不需要尋找。\n【例句】Let's pray for the people hurt in the earthquake.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1742, "question": "Nancy stays home every day to ______ her sick grandma.", "options": ["pray for", "care for", "look for", "wait for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "在家照顧生病的奶奶 care for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1743, "question": "I'm ______ my glasses. Have you seen them?", "options": ["praying for", "caring for", "looking for", "asking for"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "找眼鏡 look for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1744, "question": "Many people go to the temple to ______ good luck before the big exam.", "options": ["pray for", "look after", "care about", "pay for"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "去廟裡祈求好運 pray for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1745, "question": "The baby birds were still hungry so their parents had to fly out to ______ more food.", "options": ["get off", "give up", "look for", "put on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜look for 尋找", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 look for + N「尋找…」\n【分析】小鳥還餓，所以鳥爸媽得飛出去「尋找」更多食物 → look for more food。\n【其他選項】(A) get off「下車」、(B) give up「放棄」、(D) put on「穿上」都與找食物語意不合。\n【例句】I'm looking for my cat. Have you seen her?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1746, "question": "Please ______ the bus at the next stop. The museum is right there.", "options": ["look for", "get off", "give up", "put on"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "在下一站下車 get off。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1747, "question": "It's cold outside. ______ your coat before you go out.", "options": ["Put on", "Look for", "Give up", "Get off"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "天冷先穿外套 put on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1748, "question": "Mr. Chen lost his job, so he is ______ a new one now.", "options": ["giving up", "getting off", "looking for", "putting on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "失業後在找新工作 look for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1749, "question": "Sally got angry because her little brother ______ the fan when she was still working on the computer.", "options": ["cheated", "closed", "got off", "turned off"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜turn off 關掉（電器）", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 turn off + 電器「關掉（電器、開關）」\n【分析】Sally 還在用電腦時，弟弟把電扇「關掉」，所以她生氣 → turned off the fan。\n【其他選項】(A) cheated「欺騙」語意不合；(B) closed「關（門窗等）」，電器開關要用 turn off；(C) got off「下（車）」不合。\n【例句】Please turn off the lights when you leave the classroom.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1750, "question": "It's too dark in here. Can you ______ the light?", "options": ["turn on", "turn off", "close", "get off"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "太暗要開燈 turn on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1751, "question": "Please ______ the window. It's raining outside.", "options": ["turn off", "get off", "close", "put on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "關窗戶用 close。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1752, "question": "Don't forget to ______ the TV before you go to bed.", "options": ["get off", "turn off", "close down", "put off"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "睡前關電視 turn off。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1753, "question": "I told you this road went the wrong way, but you just wouldn't listen. Now we have to ______ and take another road.", "options": ["go ahead", "move away", "pass by", "turn back"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜turn back 折返、往回走", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 turn back「往回走、折返」\n【分析】走錯路了，現在得「折返」改走另一條路 → turn back and take another road。\n【其他選項】(A) go ahead「繼續前進」與換路矛盾；(B) move away「搬走」；(C) pass by「經過」都不合語意。\n【例句】It started to rain, so we turned back and went home.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1754, "question": "Our family will ______ to Kaohsiung next month because Dad got a new job there.", "options": ["turn back", "move away", "pass by", "go ahead"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "因工作搬離（到高雄）move away。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1755, "question": "Can I ask you a question? —Sure, ______.", "options": ["go ahead", "turn back", "pass by", "move away"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "「請說」go ahead。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1756, "question": "I ______ the bookstore every day on my way to school.", "options": ["turn back", "go ahead", "pass by", "move away"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "上學途中經過書店 pass by。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1757, "question": "Though Jack was poor and sick, he never ______ any chance to write. That is why he finally became a successful writer.", "options": ["agreed to", "gave up", "looked for", "thought of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜give up 放棄", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 give up + N/Ving「放棄…」\n【分析】雖然又窮又病（Though），他從不「放棄」任何寫作的機會，因此最後成為成功作家 → never gave up any chance。\n【其他選項】(A) agreed to「同意」、(C) looked for「尋找」、(D) thought of「想到」放入 never ___ any chance 都無法說明他成功的原因。\n【例句】Don't give up your dream just because it's hard.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1758, "question": "Grandpa ______ smoking last year because it was bad for his health.", "options": ["gave up", "looked for", "agreed to", "put on"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "為健康戒菸 give up smoking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1759, "question": "Mom finally ______ let us keep a dog.", "options": ["gave up", "agreed to", "looked for", "thought of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "終於同意讓我們養狗 agreed to + V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1760, "question": "Have you ______ a good name for your new puppy?", "options": ["given up", "agreed to", "thought of", "taken off"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "想到好名字 think of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1761, "question": "Lexie ______ reading maps. Even with a map, she still cannot find her way when she is in a foreign city.", "options": ["is careful about", "is good at", "has fun", "has trouble"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜have trouble (in) Ving 做…有困難", "explanation": "【句型】have trouble (in) + Ving「做…有困難」\n【分析】後句「就算有地圖，在外國城市還是找不到路」，表示她看地圖有困難 → has trouble reading maps。\n【其他選項】(A) is careful about「對…很小心」、(B) is good at「擅長」與找不到路矛盾；(C) has fun (Ving)「做…很開心」也不合語意。\n【例句】Many students have trouble remembering new words.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1762, "question": "Joe ______ singing. He won first place in the school singing contest.", "options": ["has trouble", "is good at", "is afraid of", "is tired of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "得歌唱比賽冠軍表示擅長唱歌 good at。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1763, "question": "My grandma ______ hearing, so please speak louder to her.", "options": ["has trouble", "has fun", "is good at", "is fond of"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "要大聲說話，表示她聽力有困難 has trouble hearing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1764, "question": "We ______ playing in the snow on our trip to Japan last winter.", "options": ["had trouble", "were careful", "had fun", "were worried"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "在雪地玩得很開心 had fun Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1765, "question": "Joseph was painting the wall when the phone rang. He quickly ______ his brush and ran to answer it.", "options": ["gave up", "handed in", "put down", "took away"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜put down 放下", "explanation": "【句型】動詞片語 put down + N「放下…」\n【分析】油漆牆壁時電話響了，他很快「放下」刷子跑去接電話 → put down his brush。\n【其他選項】(A) gave up「放棄」、(B) handed in「繳交」、(D) took away「拿走」都不符合接電話前的動作。\n【例句】Please put down your pencils. The test is over.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1766, "question": "Please ______ your reports before Friday.", "options": ["put down", "hand in", "take away", "give up"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "週五前交報告 hand in。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1767, "question": "The waiter ______ our plates after we finished eating.", "options": ["took away", "put down", "handed in", "gave up"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "吃完後服務生收走盤子 took away。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1768, "question": "When the teacher came in, the students ______ their phones and opened their books.", "options": ["handed in", "gave up", "took away", "put down"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "老師進來，學生放下手機 put down。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1769, "question": "Jack likes to ______. He always tells his friends that he has many beautiful girlfriends.", "options": ["get off", "give up", "shut up", "show off"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜show off 炫耀", "explanation": "【句型】show off 炫耀、賣弄。\n【分析】後句說他總是告訴朋友自己有很多漂亮女友，這是在「炫耀」，故選 show off。\n【其他選項】(A) get off 下車；(B) give up 放棄；(C) shut up 閉嘴，皆與「到處誇耀」語意不符。\n【例句】Tina likes to show off her new phone at school.（Tina 喜歡在學校炫耀她的新手機。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1770, "question": "Kevin got a new bike, and he rode it around the park to ______ to everyone.", "options": ["show off", "take off", "put off", "turn off"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "到處騎給大家看是在「炫耀」，show off 為正解。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1771, "question": "I'm tired. Please ______ the TV and let me sleep.", "options": ["show off", "give up", "turn off", "get off"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "想睡覺要「關掉」電視，turn off。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1772, "question": "Don't ______ trying. You will learn to swim if you keep practicing.", "options": ["get off", "show off", "put on", "give up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "勸人持續練習，即「不要放棄」，give up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1773, "question": "Jim grew up with many animals at home and knows well how to ______ pets.", "options": ["belong to", "get away from", "take care of", "wake up"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜take care of 照顧", "explanation": "【句型】take care of + 人／動物＝照顧。\n【分析】Jim 從小和許多動物一起長大，所以很懂得如何「照顧」寵物，選 take care of。\n【其他選項】(A) belong to 屬於；(B) get away from 逃離；(D) wake up 醒來／叫醒，皆不合語意。\n【例句】Amy takes care of her little brother after school.（Amy 放學後照顧弟弟。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1774, "question": "When my parents are away, my grandma ______ me and my sister.", "options": ["looks for", "takes care of", "belongs to", "gets along"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "父母不在時由奶奶「照顧」我們，take care of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1775, "question": "This old bike ______ my uncle. He rode it to school when he was young.", "options": ["takes care of", "wakes up", "belongs to", "looks after"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "「屬於」叔叔的腳踏車，belong to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1776, "question": "Ben must ______ early tomorrow because his train leaves at six.", "options": ["take care of", "get away from", "belong to", "wake up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "火車六點開，要「早起」，wake up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1777, "question": "This restaurant is ______ for its chicken soup. Many people come to eat it.", "options": ["crazy", "delicious", "famous", "sharp"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be famous for 以…聞名", "explanation": "【句型】be famous for + N＝因…而有名。\n【分析】空格後接 for its chicken soup，且「很多人來吃」，可知是「以雞湯聞名」，選 famous。\n【其他選項】(A) be crazy about 才是「熱愛」，且 crazy for 不符語意；(B) delicious 美味的，不接 for；(D) sharp 尖銳的，不合語意。\n【例句】Tainan is famous for its delicious snacks.（台南以美味小吃聞名。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1778, "question": "Yilan is ______ for its hot springs. Many visitors go there in winter.", "options": ["famous", "afraid", "proud", "full"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "冬天很多遊客去泡溫泉，宜蘭「以溫泉聞名」，be famous for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1779, "question": "My brother is ______ about baseball. He watches every CPBL game.", "options": ["famous", "afraid", "crazy", "able"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "每場比賽都看，表示他「熱愛」棒球，be crazy about。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1780, "question": "Be careful with that knife. It's very ______.", "options": ["famous", "sharp", "delicious", "serious"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "刀子要小心，因為很「鋒利」，sharp。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1781, "question": "The driving test is not very difficult, and most people are ______ to pass it.", "options": ["able", "afraid", "correct", "serious"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be able to V 能夠", "explanation": "【句型】be able to + 原形 V＝能夠做…。\n【分析】前句說駕照考試不難，所以大部分人都「能夠」通過，選 able。\n【其他選項】(B) be afraid to V 害怕去做，與「考試不難」矛盾；(C) correct 正確的，不接 to V；(D) serious 嚴肅的，不合語意。\n【例句】After practicing for a month, Leo was able to ride a bike.（練了一個月後，Leo 能騎腳踏車了。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1782, "question": "The box is too heavy. I'm not ______ to carry it by myself.", "options": ["afraid", "able", "sure", "famous"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "箱子太重，我「無法」自己搬，be able to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1783, "question": "Mia is ______ to speak in front of the class because she is very shy.", "options": ["able", "famous", "afraid", "correct"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "她很害羞，所以「害怕」在全班面前說話，be afraid to V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1784, "question": "Please check your answers again. Make sure they are all ______.", "options": ["correct", "able", "afraid", "serious"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "檢查答案確保都「正確」，correct。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1785, "question": "The turtle is the animal my sister is most ______ of. She cries and runs away even when she sees a picture of one.", "options": ["sure", "shy", "proud", "afraid"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be afraid of 害怕", "explanation": "【句型】be afraid of + N＝害怕…。\n【分析】看到烏龜圖片就哭著跑開，表示最「害怕」烏龜；空格後有 of，選 afraid。\n【其他選項】(A) be sure of 確定；(B) shy 害羞的，常接 with/about；(C) be proud of 以…為傲，皆與「哭著跑開」不符。\n【例句】Many children are afraid of the dark.（許多小孩怕黑。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1786, "question": "Lucy won first prize in the speech contest. Her parents are very ______ of her.", "options": ["afraid", "proud", "tired", "full"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "得獎讓父母「以她為傲」，be proud of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1787, "question": "Ken never goes near the water because he is ______ of swimming in deep places.", "options": ["afraid", "proud", "famous", "full"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "不靠近水是因為「害怕」，be afraid of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1788, "question": "Are you ______ of the time of the meeting? I don't want to be late.", "options": ["proud", "afraid", "sure", "tired"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "確認開會時間，be sure of「確定」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1789, "question": "When I heard my baby girl say her first word, my heart was ______ with joy.", "options": ["filled", "marked", "prepared", "shown"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be filled with 充滿", "explanation": "【句型】be filled with + N＝充滿…（= be full of）。\n【分析】聽到女兒說出第一個字，心中「充滿」喜悅；空格後接 with joy，選 filled。\n【其他選項】(B) marked 被標記；(C) prepared 被準備；(D) shown 被展示，都不能和 with joy 搭配成合理語意。\n【例句】The classroom was filled with laughter.（教室裡充滿笑聲。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1790, "question": "After the concert, the streets were ______ with happy fans.", "options": ["shown", "filled", "marked", "covered by"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "街上「擠滿」歌迷，be filled with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1791, "question": "The bottle is ______ of water. Don't put any more in it.", "options": ["full", "filled", "empty", "made"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "空格後接 of，be full of「裝滿」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1792, "question": "The mountain is ______ with snow in winter, so it looks white.", "options": ["filled", "full", "covered", "made"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "山「被雪覆蓋」，be covered with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1793, "question": "Jean: Thanks for driving me to the station. You didn't have to.\nSam: But I wanted to. It's my ______. And I had a good time talking with you.", "options": ["bus", "homework", "pleasure", "problem"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜It's my pleasure. 我的榮幸／不客氣", "explanation": "【句型】回應道謝：It's my pleasure. / My pleasure.＝不客氣、這是我的榮幸。\n【分析】Jean 道謝，Sam 說「是我想做的」，又說和她聊得很開心，故回答「這是我的榮幸」，選 pleasure。\n【其他選項】(A) bus 公車；(B) homework 作業；(D) problem 問題，It's my problem 意思為「是我的問題」，不合道謝情境。\n【例句】A: Thank you for helping me. B: It's my pleasure.（A：謝謝你幫我。B：不客氣。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1794, "question": "Ann: Thanks for lending me your umbrella.\nBob: ______ I'm glad I could help.", "options": ["My pleasure.", "That's too bad.", "Not at all bad.", "Good luck."], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "回應道謝用 My pleasure.「不客氣」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1795, "question": "Eric: I'm sorry I broke your pencil.\nDora: ______ I have another one.", "options": ["My pleasure.", "Congratulations!", "Never mind.", "Help yourself."], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "回應道歉用 Never mind.「沒關係」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1796, "question": "Grace: Can I have some cookies?\nHenry: Sure. ______", "options": ["Never mind.", "It's my problem.", "No way.", "Help yourself."], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "請對方自己取用：Help yourself.", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1797, "question": "Denny: I guess Alice likes you. Her face always turns red when you talk to her.\nDavid: ______ She's just shy with boys.", "options": ["Why not?", "I'm really surprised!", "That's right!", "I don't think so."], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜對話回應語 I don't think so.", "explanation": "【句型】表達不同意：I don't think so.＝我不這麼認為。\n【分析】David 接著說「她只是對男生害羞」，表示他不同意 Alice 喜歡他的說法，選 I don't think so.\n【其他選項】(A) Why not? 為何不（表贊成邀約）；(B) 真驚訝，但後句是在解釋否定；(C) That's right! 表同意，與後句矛盾。\n【例句】A: Is it going to rain today? B: I don't think so. The sky is clear.（A：今天會下雨嗎？B：我不這麼認為，天空很晴朗。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1798, "question": "Olivia: Let's go to the night market tonight.\nPeter: ______ I'm hungry, too.", "options": ["I don't think so.", "Why not?", "Never mind.", "That's too bad."], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "接受邀約可說 Why not?「好啊」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1799, "question": "Rita: I think the test is very easy.\nSteve: ______ I couldn't finish half of it.", "options": ["That's right!", "Why not?", "I don't think so.", "Me too."], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "後句說寫不完一半，表示不同意，I don't think so。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1800, "question": "Tony: Paris is the capital of France, right?\nUma: ______ I went there last year.", "options": ["That's right!", "I don't think so.", "No way.", "Why not?"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "陳述正確，表示同意：That's right!", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1801, "question": "At the end of the baseball game, all the players ______ the fans to thank them for coming to the game.", "options": ["agreed with", "arrived with", "bowed to", "checked out"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜bow to 向…鞠躬", "explanation": "【句型】bow to + 人＝向某人鞠躬。\n【分析】比賽結束後，球員為了「感謝」球迷到場而向球迷「鞠躬」，選 bowed to。\n【其他選項】(A) agreed with 同意；(B) arrived with 與…一起抵達；(D) checked out 退房／查看，皆不合「致謝」的動作。\n【例句】The students bowed to their teacher on Teachers' Day.（學生在教師節向老師鞠躬。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1802, "question": "After the show, the dancers ______ the audience and walked off the stage.", "options": ["agreed with", "bowed to", "checked out", "belonged to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "表演結束向觀眾「鞠躬」，bow to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1803, "question": "I don't ______ you. I think the movie was boring.", "options": ["bow to", "check out", "arrive at", "agree with"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "後句表達不同看法，「同意」agree with 的否定。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1804, "question": "We have to ______ of the hotel before eleven tomorrow morning.", "options": ["check out", "bow to", "agree with", "arrive at"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "離開飯店要「退房」，check out of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1805, "question": "We don't have enough toys for each child, so they will have to ______ them with each other.", "options": ["follow", "prepare", "repeat", "share"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜share A with B 與…分享", "explanation": "【句型】share + 物 + with + 人＝和某人分享某物。\n【分析】玩具不夠每個孩子各一個，所以要彼此「分享」；空格後有 with each other，選 share。\n【其他選項】(A) follow 跟隨；(B) prepare 準備；(C) repeat 重複，都不合「玩具不夠」的語意。\n【例句】Kelly shared her lunch with her new classmate.（Kelly 和新同學分享午餐。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1806, "question": "There's only one umbrella, so Lisa ______ it with her brother on the way home.", "options": ["shared", "followed", "repeated", "prepared"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "只有一把傘，和弟弟「共用」，share A with B。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1807, "question": "Mom is in the kitchen ______ dinner for the family.", "options": ["sharing", "preparing", "repeating", "following"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "在廚房「準備」晚餐，prepare。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1808, "question": "I didn't hear you clearly. Could you ______ the question, please?", "options": ["share", "prepare", "repeat", "follow"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "沒聽清楚，請對方「重複」問題，repeat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1809, "question": "You have been in front of the computer for more than five hours. It's time for you to ______ and relax.", "options": ["get up early", "show off", "shut up", "get some exercise"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜get some exercise 做些運動", "explanation": "【句型】get / do some exercise＝做點運動；It's time for sb to V＝該是某人做…的時候了。\n【分析】已經在電腦前五小時以上，應該起來「做點運動」放鬆一下，and relax 是線索，選 get some exercise。\n【其他選項】(A) get up early 早起，與「坐太久」無關；(B) show off 炫耀；(C) shut up 閉嘴，都不合語意。\n【例句】Let's get some exercise in the park after dinner.（晚餐後我們去公園運動一下吧。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1810, "question": "You look tired after studying all day. Why don't you go out and ______?", "options": ["show off", "get some exercise", "shut up", "give up"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "讀書一整天很累，建議出去「運動一下」，get some exercise。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1811, "question": "If you want to catch the first bus, you have to ______ tomorrow.", "options": ["get up early", "show off", "get some exercise", "shut up"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "要趕第一班公車就要「早起」，get up early。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1812, "question": "The movie has started. Could you please ______? I can't hear anything.", "options": ["get up early", "get some exercise", "show off", "shut up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "電影開始還在講話，請對方「閉嘴」，shut up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1813, "question": "I need a quiet place to study in, because I am going to ______ tomorrow.", "options": ["take a test", "take a seat", "have a bath", "have a dialogue"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜take a test 參加考試", "explanation": "【句型】take a test / an exam＝參加考試。\n【分析】需要安靜地方「讀書」，因為明天要「考試」，選 take a test。\n【其他選項】(B) take a seat 坐下；(C) have a bath 洗澡；(D) have a dialogue 對話，都和「需要讀書」沒有因果關係。\n【例句】We will take a math test next Monday.（我們下週一要考數學。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1814, "question": "Please ______. The doctor will see you in a few minutes.", "options": ["take a test", "take a seat", "take a bath", "take a walk"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "請病人先「坐下」等候，take a seat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1815, "question": "Owen studied hard all week because he had to ______ on Friday.", "options": ["take a seat", "take a bath", "take a test", "take a picture"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "整週用功是因為週五要「考試」，take a test。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1816, "question": "After playing basketball, Ray felt dirty, so he went home to ______.", "options": ["take a test", "take a seat", "take a walk", "take a bath"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "打完球很髒，回家「洗澡」，take a bath。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1817, "question": "(On the cell phone)\nStacy: Where are you? I can't see you here at the theater.\nGreg: ______. I'm just one block away.", "options": ["Nice talking to you", "I'm coming", "Hurry up", "Hope to see you soon"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜電話用語 I'm coming. 我馬上到", "explanation": "【句型】I'm coming.＝我就來了／我快到了（現在進行式表即將發生）。\n【分析】Stacy 找不到 Greg，Greg 說他只差一個街區，表示「我快到了」，選 I'm coming。\n【其他選項】(A) 很高興和你聊天，用於結束對話；(C) Hurry up 快點，應是等人的 Stacy 說的話；(D) 希望很快見到你，語氣像道別，不合情境。\n【例句】A: Dinner is ready! B: I'm coming!（A：晚餐好了！B：我來了！）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1818, "question": "Mom: Kevin, it's time for school. Where are you?\nKevin: ______ I'm putting on my shoes.", "options": ["Hurry up!", "I'm coming!", "Nice to meet you.", "Help yourself."], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "媽媽在催，Kevin 回答「我來了」，I'm coming。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1819, "question": "Wendy: The bus will leave in two minutes. ______\nZack: OK, I'm running!", "options": ["Hurry up!", "I'm coming!", "Take your time.", "Never mind."], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "公車快開了，催對方「快點」，Hurry up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1820, "question": "Ivy: I have to go now. Bye!\nJoe: Bye! ______", "options": ["I'm coming.", "Hurry up.", "Nice talking to you.", "Who's calling?"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "結束對話道別時說「很高興和你聊天」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1821, "question": "Ms. Smith is ______ at telling stories, so all of her students enjoy story time in her class very much.", "options": ["convenient", "excellent", "lucky", "ready"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be excellent at 擅長", "explanation": "【句型】be excellent at + N / Ving＝擅長…（= be good at）。\n【分析】學生都很喜歡她的說故事時間，因為她「很會」說故事；空格後接 at telling，選 excellent。\n【其他選項】(A) convenient 方便的；(C) lucky 幸運的；(D) be ready for/to 準備好，都不接 at Ving 表擅長。\n【例句】Paul is excellent at playing the piano.（Paul 很擅長彈鋼琴。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1822, "question": "Ella is ______ at drawing. Her pictures often win prizes.", "options": ["excellent", "ready", "lucky", "convenient"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "畫作常得獎，表示她「擅長」畫畫，be excellent at。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1823, "question": "The MRT station is near my home, so it's very ______ for me to go downtown.", "options": ["excellent", "ready", "convenient", "lucky"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "捷運站在附近，去市區很「方便」，convenient。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1824, "question": "Are you ______ for the trip? We're leaving in ten minutes.", "options": ["excellent", "convenient", "lucky", "ready"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "十分鐘後出發，問是否「準備好」，be ready for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1825, "question": "Michael: Mom, I got the best grade on the English test today.\nMrs. Lee: Good job, son. I'm ______ of you.", "options": ["sure", "sick", "afraid", "proud"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜be proud of 以…為傲", "explanation": "【句型】be proud of + 人／事＝以…為榮。\n【分析】兒子英文考最高分，媽媽說 Good job，表示「以你為傲」，選 proud。\n【其他選項】(A) be sure of 確定；(B) be sick of 厭倦；(C) be afraid of 害怕，都不合稱讚的語氣。\n【例句】Taiwanese people are proud of their baseball team.（台灣人以他們的棒球隊為傲。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1826, "question": "I'm ______ of eating instant noodles every day. I want something different.", "options": ["proud", "sick", "sure", "afraid"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "每天吃泡麵想換口味，表示「厭倦」，be sick of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1827, "question": "Mr. Chen is very ______ of his daughter because she helped many old people.", "options": ["afraid", "sick", "proud", "sure"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "女兒幫助許多老人，爸爸「以她為傲」，be proud of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1828, "question": "Are you ______ of your answer? You can still change it.", "options": ["sure", "proud", "sick", "afraid"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "問對方是否「確定」答案，be sure of。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1829, "question": "When we stayed at the country house, we had only enough water for drinking. That's why we did not take a ______ for two days.", "options": ["bath", "rest", "vacation", "walk"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜take a bath 洗澡", "explanation": "【句型】take a bath＝洗澡；take a rest／walk／vacation 分別為休息／散步／度假。\n【分析】水只夠喝，所以兩天沒「洗澡」，選 bath。\n【其他選項】(B) rest 休息；(C) vacation 度假；(D) walk 散步，都不需要用水，與「水只夠喝」沒有因果關係。\n【例句】Linda takes a hot bath before going to bed.（Linda 睡前洗熱水澡。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1830, "question": "You've been working for hours. Sit down and take a ______.", "options": ["bath", "rest", "vacation", "test"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "工作好幾小時，坐下來「休息」一下，take a rest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1831, "question": "It's a nice evening. Let's take a ______ along the river.", "options": ["bath", "test", "rest", "walk"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "天氣好去河邊「散步」，take a walk。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1832, "question": "Mr. Huang worked hard all year, so he is going to take a ______ in Japan.", "options": ["walk", "bath", "vacation", "seat"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "辛苦一年去日本「度假」，take a vacation。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1833, "question": "The noise those boys are making is giving me a(n) ______. Can you do anything about it?", "options": ["break", "excuse", "hand", "headache"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜give sb a headache 讓人頭痛", "explanation": "【句型】give sb a headache＝讓某人頭痛（可指真的頭痛或很煩）。\n【分析】男孩們製造的噪音讓我「頭痛」，所以請對方處理，選 headache。\n【其他選項】(A) give sb a break 讓某人休息／饒了某人；(B) excuse 藉口；(C) give sb a hand 幫忙，都不是噪音造成的結果。\n【例句】This math problem is giving me a headache.（這道數學題讓我很頭痛。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1834, "question": "This box is heavy. Can you give me a ______?", "options": ["hand", "headache", "break", "excuse"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "箱子很重請人「幫忙」，give sb a hand。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1835, "question": "You've been studying for three hours. Give yourself a ______ and have some tea.", "options": ["hand", "headache", "break", "chance"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "讀了三小時，讓自己「休息一下」，give yourself a break。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1836, "question": "Sam was late again, and he gave the teacher another ______ about missing the bus.", "options": ["break", "hand", "headache", "excuse"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "又遲到並說沒趕上公車，是「藉口」，excuse。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1837, "question": "Everyone ______ mistakes in his or her life. The important thing is not to repeat them.", "options": ["does", "forgets", "makes", "takes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜make mistakes 犯錯", "explanation": "【句型】make a mistake / mistakes＝犯錯（固定搭配動詞為 make）。\n【分析】每個人一生中都會「犯錯」，重要的是不要重蹈覆轍，mistakes 搭配 make。\n【其他選項】(A) do 不與 mistakes 搭配；(B) forget mistakes 忘記錯誤，與後句「不要重複」邏輯不合；(D) take 不與 mistakes 搭配。\n【例句】Don't be afraid to make mistakes when you speak English.（說英文時別怕犯錯。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1838, "question": "Please check your homework again. You ______ three mistakes in it.", "options": ["did", "made", "took", "had"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "犯錯固定用 make mistakes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1839, "question": "Jenny always ______ her homework right after dinner.", "options": ["makes", "takes", "does", "gives"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "做功課固定用 do homework。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1840, "question": "Let's ______ a picture in front of Taipei 101.", "options": ["make", "do", "give", "take"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "拍照固定用 take a picture。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1841, "question": "Jane: Ned hasn't talked to me for two days because I laughed at his hair color. What should I do?\nLois: You should go and tell him that you're sorry. He's nice, and I'm sure he'll give you another ______.", "options": ["chance", "excuse", "headache", "lesson"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜give sb another chance 再給某人一次機會", "explanation": "【句型】give sb another chance＝再給某人一次機會。\n【分析】勸 Jane 去道歉，Ned 人很好，一定會「再給妳一次機會」，選 chance。\n【其他選項】(B) excuse 藉口；(C) headache 頭痛；(D) lesson 課／教訓，皆不合「原諒」的語意。\n【例句】I failed the test, but my teacher gave me another chance.（我考不及格，但老師再給我一次機會。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1842, "question": "I'm sorry I broke your cup. Please give me another ______. I'll be more careful.", "options": ["chance", "lesson", "headache", "letter"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "請求原諒並保證小心，「再給一次機會」，chance。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1843, "question": "Losing the game taught us an important ______: we need more practice.", "options": ["chance", "excuse", "lesson", "headache"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "比賽輸了學到「教訓」，lesson。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1844, "question": "Bill always has an ______ for not doing his homework.", "options": ["lesson", "chance", "headache", "excuse"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "沒做功課總有「藉口」，excuse。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1845, "question": "Mike: I always forget what I want to buy when I go to the market.\nOscar: Well, you can make a ______ of things you want to buy.", "options": ["habit", "list", "pack", "wish"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜make a list 列清單", "explanation": "【句型】make a list of + N＝列出…的清單。\n【分析】Mike 總是忘記要買什麼，Oscar 建議他把要買的東西「列成清單」，選 list。\n【其他選項】(A) make a habit of 養成…習慣，不合；(C) pack 包裹；(D) make a wish 許願，都無法解決「忘記要買什麼」。\n【例句】Mom made a list of things to buy for the party.（媽媽列了派對要買的東西清單。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1846, "question": "Before the trip, Rose made a ______ of everything she needed to bring.", "options": ["wish", "list", "habit", "noise"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "旅行前把要帶的東西「列成清單」，make a list。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1847, "question": "Close your eyes and make a ______ before you blow out the candles.", "options": ["list", "habit", "wish", "mistake"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "吹蠟燭前「許願」，make a wish。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1848, "question": "Ted wants to make a ______ of reading for twenty minutes every night.", "options": ["habit", "wish", "list", "pack"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "每晚讀書成為「習慣」，make a habit of Ving。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1849, "question": "The weather is nice and cool today. Let's go for a ______ on the grass and enjoy some food and drinks.", "options": ["drive", "picnic", "swim", "vacation"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜go for a picnic 去野餐", "explanation": "【句型】go for a picnic / go on a picnic＝去野餐。\n【分析】在「草地上」享用「食物和飲料」，就是「野餐」，選 picnic。\n【其他選項】(A) go for a drive 兜風，不會在草地上；(C) go for a swim 游泳，不在草地上；(D) vacation 度假，與「在草地上吃東西」不符。\n【例句】We went for a picnic in Daan Forest Park last Sunday.（上週日我們去大安森林公園野餐。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1850, "question": "It's too hot today. Let's go for a ______ in the pool.", "options": ["picnic", "drive", "swim", "walk"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "天氣熱去泳池「游泳」，go for a swim。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1851, "question": "Dad bought a new car, and he took us for a ______ along the coast.", "options": ["drive", "swim", "picnic", "bath"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "開新車沿海岸「兜風」，go for a drive。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1852, "question": "We brought sandwiches and juice and had a ______ under a big tree.", "options": ["drive", "swim", "vacation", "picnic"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "帶三明治果汁在樹下「野餐」，have a picnic。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1853, "question": "When the teacher was not in the classroom, the students talked loudly and made a lot of ______.", "options": ["excuses", "heat", "languages", "noise"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜make noise 製造噪音", "explanation": "【句型】make (a lot of) noise＝製造（很多）噪音；noise 為不可數名詞。\n【分析】學生大聲講話，「製造很多噪音」，talked loudly 是線索，選 noise。\n【其他選項】(A) make excuses 找藉口，與大聲講話無關；(B) heat 熱；(C) languages 語言，皆不合。\n【例句】Please don't make any noise in the library.（在圖書館請勿製造噪音。）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1854, "question": "The dogs next door make a lot of ______ at night, so I can't sleep well.", "options": ["noise", "heat", "excuses", "language"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "狗吵得睡不著，make noise。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1855, "question": "Stop making ______. Just tell me why you didn't come.", "options": ["noise", "heat", "excuses", "mistakes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "叫對方別再「找藉口」，make excuses。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1856, "question": "The sun gives us light and ______.", "options": ["noise", "excuses", "languages", "heat"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "太陽提供光和「熱」，heat。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1857, "question": "Mark: I've got a lot of exercise these days, but still can't lose weight.\nDoris: Exercise is not enough. You should also ______. Eating the right foods is very important for weight control.", "options": ["quit eating", "start an exercise class", "take some medicine", "go on a diet"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜go on a diet 節食", "explanation": "【句型】go on a diet = 節食、控制飲食。\n【分析】後句 Eating the right foods is very important（吃對食物很重要）→ 要控制飲食，選 go on a diet。also 表示「除了運動之外還要」。\n【其他選項】(A) quit eating 停止進食，不合理也不健康；(B) start an exercise class 仍是運動，與 Exercise is not enough 矛盾；(C) take some medicine 吃藥，與「吃對食物」無關。\n【例句】My sister went on a diet and stopped eating fried chicken.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1858, "question": "Ben: I want to lose some weight before summer.\nAmy: Then you should ______ and stop drinking soda.", "options": ["go on a diet", "go on a trip", "take a rest", "take a bath"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "想減重且不喝汽水 → 節食 go on a diet。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1859, "question": "The doctor told Mr. Lin to ______ because he was too heavy and ate too much meat.", "options": ["take a walk", "go shopping", "go on a diet", "make a wish"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "太重又吃太多肉 → 醫生要他節食。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1860, "question": "Lisa is ______ a diet, so she only eats vegetables and fruit for dinner.", "options": ["in", "at", "with", "on"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "be on a diet 正在節食，介系詞用 on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1861, "question": "You will become a good learner if you ______ the tips your teachers talk about.", "options": ["do", "ask", "answer", "follow"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜follow the tips 遵循建議", "explanation": "【句型】follow + 建議/規則/指示（tips, advice, rules）= 遵守、照著做。\n【分析】「如果你照著老師說的 tips（訣竅）去做，就會成為好學習者」→ follow the tips。\n【其他選項】(A) do the tips 不是正確搭配；(B) ask 詢問，tips 是老師說的不是你要問的；(C) answer 回答，tips 不是問題。\n【例句】If you follow the doctor's advice, you will get better soon.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1862, "question": "Please ______ the rules when you swim in the pool.", "options": ["follow", "make", "break", "watch"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "遵守規則 follow the rules；break 是違反，語意不合。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1863, "question": "Amy didn't ______ her mom's advice, so she got lost on the way.", "options": ["give", "take", "say", "keep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "take one's advice 接受建議；沒聽建議所以迷路。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1864, "question": "Just ______ the steps on the box, and you can make the cake easily.", "options": ["ask", "answer", "follow", "forget"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "照著盒子上的步驟做 follow the steps。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1865, "question": "I feel it great to take ______ in the hot springs in Yangmingshan.", "options": ["an interest", "a bath", "a trip", "some medicine"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜take a bath 泡澡", "explanation": "【句型】take a bath = 洗澡、泡澡。\n【分析】in the hot springs（在溫泉裡）→ 在溫泉裡做的事是泡澡 take a bath。\n【其他選項】(A) take an interest 對…產生興趣（須接 in），不能「在溫泉裡」；(C) take a trip 去旅行，不會在溫泉「裡面」旅行；(D) take some medicine 吃藥，不合語意。\n【例句】After the long hike, we took a bath in the hot springs.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1866, "question": "It's cold today. Let's ______ in the hot springs in Beitou.", "options": ["take a bath", "take a picture", "take a seat", "take a walk"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "在溫泉裡 → 泡澡 take a bath。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1867, "question": "Ted always ______ before he goes to bed, so he feels clean and relaxed.", "options": ["takes a trip", "takes a test", "takes a shower", "takes a look"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "睡前讓自己乾淨 → 洗澡 take a shower。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1868, "question": "We plan to ______ to Hualien this summer vacation.", "options": ["take a bath", "take a nap", "take a rest", "take a trip"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "去花蓮 → 旅行 take a trip to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1869, "question": "I have no ______ in cooking so I always ask my brother to cook for me.", "options": ["rule", "point", "example", "interest"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜會考歷屆｜have no interest in 對…沒興趣", "explanation": "【句型】have (no) interest in + N/Ving = 對…（沒）有興趣。\n【分析】後句 always ask my brother to cook for me（總是叫哥哥煮）→ 自己對烹飪沒興趣，空格後的 in 是 interest 的搭配介系詞。\n【其他選項】(A) rule 規則、(B) point 重點、(C) example 例子，都不與 in cooking 搭配成合理語意。\n【例句】Tom has no interest in sports; he prefers reading.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1870, "question": "Kelly has a strong ______ in music, so she plays the piano every day.", "options": ["interest", "reason", "chance", "habit"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "have an interest in 對…有興趣，所以天天彈琴。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1871, "question": "My grandpa is interested ______ old movies.", "options": ["at", "with", "in", "on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "be interested in 對…感興趣。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1872, "question": "Joe showed no interest ______ the game, so he left early.", "options": ["for", "in", "of", "to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "show interest in 對…有興趣；沒興趣所以早走。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1873, "question": "Look! There is not a cloud in the sky. I think the chances of getting some rain today are really ______.", "options": ["far", "good", "possible", "small"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜115會考｜搭配詞：the chances of … are small / good", "explanation": "【句型】the chances of + Ving + are small / good（機會小／大）；chance 常搭配 good、small、high、low。\n【分析】線索 There is not a cloud in the sky：萬里無雲，下雨的機會「很小」→ small。\n【其他選項】(A) far 遠的：不能形容機會；(B) good：機會大，與萬里無雲矛盾；(C) possible：主詞應為「事情」（It is possible that…），不說 chances are possible。\n【例句】The chances of seeing snow in Taipei are very small.\n※ 本題亦可歸「詞彙題」。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1874, "question": "Our team has the best players this year. The chances of winning the game are ______.", "options": ["good", "far", "easy", "possible"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "球員最好 → 贏的機會「大」，chances are good。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1875, "question": "Ted didn't study at all, so his chances of passing the test are ______.", "options": ["big", "low", "high", "tall"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "沒讀書 → 及格機會「低」，chance 搭配 low。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1876, "question": "It's ______ that it will rain this afternoon. The sky is getting dark.", "options": ["chance", "small", "possible", "far"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "It is possible that… 「有可能……」，possible 的主詞是事情。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1877, "question": "Alex fell down in the race and hurt his leg. When he got up and ran to the finish line, everybody ______.", "options": ["gave him a hand", "gave him a big hand", "put themselves in his shoes", "had it both ways"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜give sb. a big hand（為某人熱烈鼓掌）", "explanation": "【句型】give sb. a big hand = 為某人熱烈鼓掌；give sb. a hand = 幫某人忙。\n【分析】Alex 受傷後仍跑到終點（ran to the finish line），大家為他熱烈鼓掌，選 gave him a big hand。\n【其他選項】(A) 幫他忙，但他已自己跑到終點；(C) put oneself in one's shoes 是「設身處地」，不合情境；(D) have it both ways 是「兩者兼得」，不合語意。\n【例句】After the speech, the students gave the principal a big hand.\n備註：講義 p.60", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1878, "question": "This box is too heavy for me. Could you ______?", "options": ["give me a big hand", "give me a hand", "make me a hand", "take my hand"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "give sb. a hand 是「幫某人忙」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1879, "question": "When the little girl finished playing the piano, the audience ______ her ______.", "options": ["gave; a big hand", "took; a hand", "made; a big hand", "had; a hand"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "表演結束為她熱烈鼓掌，用 give sb. a big hand。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1880, "question": "Before you get angry at Ben, try to ______. He just lost his dog.", "options": ["give him a big hand", "have it both ways", "put yourself in his shoes", "keep an eye on him"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "put yourself in his shoes 是「設身處地為他著想」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1881, "question": "Helen: How often do I need to water this plant? Do I need to do it every day?\nWendy: No. Watering it ______ will be quite enough. About three or four times a week.", "options": ["once in a while", "every other day", "twice a day", "every three days"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜every other day（每隔一天）", "explanation": "【句型】every other day = 每隔一天；every three days = 每三天一次。\n【分析】Wendy 說「一週大約三到四次」（About three or four times a week），正好是每隔一天澆一次。\n【其他選項】(A) once in a while 是「偶爾」，次數不明確；(C) twice a day 一天兩次，比每天更多；(D) every three days 一週只有兩次多。\n【例句】I go jogging every other day, so I run about three times a week.\n備註：講義 p.60", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1882, "question": "Mr. Lin has English class on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. He has it ______.", "options": ["every day", "once a week", "every other day", "twice a day"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "一、三、五上課是每隔一天。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1883, "question": "Kim doesn't eat fast food often. She only has it ______, maybe once or twice a month.", "options": ["once in a while", "every day", "every other day", "three times a day"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "一個月一兩次是「偶爾」once in a while。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1884, "question": "Take this medicine ______: after breakfast, after lunch, and after dinner.", "options": ["every other day", "three times a day", "once a week", "every three days"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "三餐飯後各一次是一天三次。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1885, "question": "No one loses ______ in playing with the gift toy through the party.", "options": ["to interest", "interests", "interested", "interesting"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜lose interest in（對…失去興趣），interest 當名詞", "explanation": "【句型】lose interest in + N／Ving = 對…失去興趣；lose 是及物動詞，後接名詞當受詞。\n【分析】空格是 loses 的受詞，又接 in playing…，需名詞 interest；選項中只有 (B) interests 是名詞形式。\n【其他選項】(A) to interest 是不定詞，lose 不接 to V；(C) interested、(D) interesting 是形容詞，不能當受詞。\n【例句】Many kids lose interest in a new toy after a few days.\n備註：講義 p.258；一般用法多為不可數 lose interest in，但本題選項中只有 (B) 為名詞，故答案保留 (B)。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1886, "question": "Ben used to love comic books, but he has lost ______ in them now.", "options": ["interest", "interesting", "interested", "to interest"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "lose interest in，lose 後接名詞 interest。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1887, "question": "Sara is very ______ in Japanese culture, so she is learning Japanese.", "options": ["interest", "interests", "interesting", "interested"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "be interested in 表人「對…感興趣」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1888, "question": "The science museum is so ______ that we stayed there all day.", "options": ["interest", "interesting", "interested", "interests"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "形容事物「有趣的」用 interesting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1889, "question": "Look at the picture. The girl is ______. [圖：戴派對帽的女孩雙手合十、閉眼，面前有插著蠟燭的生日蛋糕]", "options": ["making a wish", "blowing out the candles", "putting on a hat", "eating a cake"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜make a wish（許願）", "explanation": "【句型】make a wish = 許願；blow out the candles = 吹熄蠟燭。\n【分析】圖中女孩雙手合十、閉著眼睛，蠟燭仍點著，表示她正在許願。\n【其他選項】(B) 蠟燭還亮著，沒有在吹；(C) 帽子已經戴好了，不是正在戴；(D) 她沒有在吃蛋糕。\n【例句】Close your eyes and make a wish before you blow out the candles.\n備註：講義 p.260", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1890, "question": "Before blowing out the candles on the cake, Joe closed his eyes and ______.", "options": ["made a wish", "took a wish", "did a wish", "had a wish"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "「許願」的固定搭配是 make a wish。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1891, "question": "After making a wish, Linda ______ the candles with one breath.", "options": ["put on", "blew out", "took off", "turned on"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "吹熄蠟燭是 blow out the candles。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1892, "question": "It's cold outside. ______ your jacket before you go out.", "options": ["Take off", "Make", "Put on", "Blow out"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "put on 是「穿上、戴上」。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1893, "question": "When I was walking past the store, I saw that beautiful dress in the window and couldn't help stopping to ______ it.", "options": ["put on", "try on", "pick up", "look at"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜look at vs. 可分片語動詞 try on（代名詞置中）", "explanation": "【句型】可分片語動詞（V + adv.）受詞為代名詞時要放中間：try it on；look at（V + prep.）受詞放介系詞後：look at it\n【分析】走過商店、看到櫥窗（in the window）裡的洋裝，忍不住停下來「看」它 → look at it。\n【其他選項】(A) put on、(B) try on、(C) pick up 受詞是 it 時須寫成 put it on / try it on / pick it up；且人在店外也不會穿上或拿起櫥窗裡的衣服。\n【例句】This hat looks nice. Can I try it on?\n備註：講義 p.319", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1894, "question": "It's cold outside. Your jacket is on the chair. Please ______.", "options": ["put on it", "put it on", "put on them", "put them on it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "put on 為可分片語，代名詞 it 放中間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1895, "question": "The baby was crying, so Dad walked over to ______ her.", "options": ["look at", "try on", "pick up", "put on"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "受詞 her 在後，只有 look at 可接；pick up 須寫 pick her up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1896, "question": "There's some trash on the floor. Could you ______?", "options": ["pick up it", "look it at", "try it on", "pick it up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "撿起垃圾用 pick up，代名詞 it 放中間。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1897, "question": "We are feeling down. Let's go shopping to ______ ourselves ______!", "options": ["look; up", "give; up", "pick; up", "cheer; up"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜講義錯題｜cheer sb. up（使振作）", "explanation": "【句型】cheer sb. up 使某人振作、高興起來\n【分析】feeling down（心情低落）→ 去購物讓自己振作 → cheer ourselves up。\n【其他選項】(A) look up 查詢；(B) give up 放棄；(C) pick up 撿起、接人，皆不合語意。\n【例句】Grandpa told funny stories to cheer me up.\n備註：講義 p.319", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1898, "question": "Sara lost the game and looked sad, so we bought her ice cream to ______.", "options": ["give her up", "cheer her up", "look her up", "pick her out"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 1（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "讓難過的人開心用 cheer sb. up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1899, "question": "Don't ______ your dream just because it's hard. Keep trying!", "options": ["give up", "cheer up", "look up", "pick up"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 2（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "不要放棄夢想，用 give up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1900, "question": "If you don't know this word, you can ______ in the dictionary.", "options": ["cheer it up", "give it up", "look it up", "pick it up"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "片語與搭配詞｜類似題 3（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "查字典用 look sth. up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "片語與搭配詞"}, {"id": 1901, "question": "The temple sits alone in the mountains at a height of 3,000m ______ sea level.", "options": ["above", "at", "below", "in"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜above sea level 海拔以上", "explanation": "【句型】above sea level = 海平面以上（海拔）。\n【分析】in the mountains（在山上）+ 3,000m → 高於海平面三千公尺，用 above。\n【其他選項】(B) at sea level 在海平面高度，與 3,000m 矛盾；(C) below 在…之下，山上的廟不會在海平面下；(D) in sea level 無此用法。\n【例句】Yushan is about 3,952 meters above sea level.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1902, "question": "The plane is flying high ______ the clouds.", "options": ["under", "above", "between", "into"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "飛得很高 → 在雲層之上 above。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1903, "question": "Some fish live deep ______ the sea where there is no light.", "options": ["above", "over", "below", "on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "深海沒有光 → 在海面之下 below。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1904, "question": "Hehuanshan is more than 3,000 meters ______ sea level, so it often snows there in winter.", "options": ["above", "below", "in", "at"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "高山海拔 3,000 公尺以上 → above sea level。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1905, "question": "Beverly eats lots of snacks ______ meals. That's why she is often too full to eat anything at mealtimes.", "options": ["after", "between", "during", "from"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜between meals 兩餐之間", "explanation": "【句型】between meals = 兩餐之間（正餐以外的時間）。\n【分析】因為她在「兩餐之間」吃很多零食，所以到吃飯時間 at mealtimes 吃不下。\n【其他選項】(A) after meals 飯後吃零食，不會造成正餐時吃不下；(C) during meals 用餐時吃零食，與 at mealtimes 吃不下矛盾；(D) from meals 無此用法。\n【例句】Try not to drink soda between meals.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1906, "question": "Don't eat cookies ______ lunch and dinner, or you won't be hungry at dinnertime.", "options": ["between", "during", "after", "among"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "午餐和晚餐兩者之間 → between。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1907, "question": "Please turn off your phone ______ the movie.", "options": ["between", "from", "during", "since"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "在電影進行期間 → during。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1908, "question": "Remember to take this medicine three times a day ______ meals.", "options": ["between", "after", "among", "into"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "藥通常飯後吃 → after meals；吃三次 between 只有兩個間隔，不合。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1909, "question": "Mr. Yang has worked in this factory ______ 1968.", "options": ["before", "for", "in", "since"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜since + 過去時間點（現在完成式）", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 have/has + p.p. + since + 過去時間點 = 自從…（到現在）。\n【分析】has worked（現在完成式）+ 1968（時間點）→ 自從 1968 年至今，用 since。\n【其他選項】(A) before 1968 表 1968 年以前，與現在完成式持續到現在不合；(B) for 接一段時間（如 for 50 years）；(C) in 1968 表過去某時，應配過去式 worked。\n【例句】Lily has lived in Tainan since 2015.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1910, "question": "We have known each other ______ we were in elementary school.", "options": ["for", "since", "in", "until"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "since + 子句（過去時間點）配現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1911, "question": "Mr. Huang has taught English ______ twenty years.", "options": ["since", "in", "for", "at"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "twenty years 是一段時間 → for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1912, "question": "My aunt moved to Kaohsiung ______ 2019.", "options": ["in", "since", "for", "during"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "moved 過去式 + 年份 → in 2019。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1913, "question": "Lucy and her boyfriend, Daniel, came to Taiwan ______ July 10, 1999.", "options": ["at", "in", "with", "on"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜on + 特定日期", "explanation": "【句型】on + 特定某一天（日期、星期、節日當天）；in + 月/年/季節；at + 時刻。\n【分析】July 10, 1999 有「日」→ 是特定的一天，用 on。\n【其他選項】(A) at 用於時刻（at 7:00）；(B) in 用於只有月或年（in July / in 1999）；(C) with 和…一起，不表時間。\n【例句】My birthday party is on May 5.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1914, "question": "The school sports day will be held ______ October 24.", "options": ["in", "on", "at", "for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "October 24 是特定日期 → on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1915, "question": "Ivy's family moved to Taichung ______ 2018.", "options": ["in", "on", "at", "by"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "只有年份 → in。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1916, "question": "The movie starts ______ 7:30 tonight.", "options": ["on", "in", "at", "since"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "時刻 → at。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1917, "question": "I write down everything about work in my pink notebook; ______ it, I'd forget the things I should do.", "options": ["before", "except", "outside", "without"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜without 沒有（若沒有…）", "explanation": "【句型】without + N = 沒有…（的話），常接 would + V 表假設結果。\n【分析】it = my pink notebook；I'd forget（我會忘記）→ 「沒有這本筆記本的話」我會忘記，用 without。\n【其他選項】(A) before it 在它之前，語意不通；(B) except it 除了它，不合；(C) outside it 在它外面，不合。\n【例句】Without your help, I couldn't finish the work.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1918, "question": "I can't see the words on the board ______ my glasses.", "options": ["with", "without", "except", "beside"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "沒戴眼鏡看不清楚 → without。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1919, "question": "______ water, plants can't grow.", "options": ["Without", "With", "Before", "Except"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "沒有水植物無法生長 → Without。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1920, "question": "Nina always goes to school ______ her umbrella in the rainy season.", "options": ["without", "except", "with", "from"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "雨季帶著傘 → with；without 不合常理。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1921, "question": "I love sports and enjoy playing baseball with friends ______ the school team.", "options": ["about", "at", "on", "to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜on the team 在隊上", "explanation": "【句型】be on a team = 是某隊的成員；friends on the school team = 校隊上的朋友。\n【分析】空格修飾 friends，表示「校隊裡的朋友」，隊伍的成員用介系詞 on。\n【其他選項】(A) about 關於；(B) at 表地點或時間點，不表隊伍成員；(D) to 表方向，均不與 team 搭配。\n【例句】My brother is on the basketball team.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1922, "question": "Is your sister ______ the school volleyball team?", "options": ["at", "on", "to", "about"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "身為隊員 be on the team。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1923, "question": "There are fifteen players ______ our baseball team.", "options": ["on", "at", "to", "of"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "隊伍裡的球員 players on the team。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1924, "question": "Leo practices every day because he wants to play ______ the school soccer team next year.", "options": ["at", "to", "about", "on"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "在校隊上踢球 play on the team。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1925, "question": "Everyone in the class enjoys playing chess ______ Bill; he thinks the game is boring.", "options": ["except", "for", "like", "of"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜except 除了…之外（排除）", "explanation": "【句型】everyone / nobody / all + except + 人 = 除了某人以外（排除在外）。\n【分析】後句 he thinks the game is boring（Bill 覺得無聊）→ Bill 被排除在「大家都喜歡」之外，用 except。\n【其他選項】(B) for 為了；(C) like 像，Bill 不喜歡下棋所以不像大家；(D) of 的，均不表排除。\n【例句】All my friends came to the party except Sam.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1926, "question": "All the students passed the test ______ Mark. He has to take it again.", "options": ["with", "except", "like", "for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "Mark 要重考 → 他被排除 except。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1927, "question": "The store is open every day ______ Monday.", "options": ["except", "on", "with", "of"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "除了星期一以外每天營業 → except。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1928, "question": "Nobody ______ Grace knew the answer, so the teacher praised her.", "options": ["with", "of", "except", "like"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "只有 Grace 知道答案 → nobody except Grace。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1929, "question": "Look at the picture. The dog is sitting ______.\n[圖：女子開敞篷車，狗坐在她旁邊的座位，包包放在後方]", "options": ["on the bag", "next to the woman", "inside the bag", "between the woman and the bag"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜next to 在…旁邊（看圖）", "explanation": "【句型】位置介系詞：next to 在旁邊；between A and B 在 A 與 B 之間；on 在上面；inside 在裡面。\n【分析】圖中女子在開車，狗坐在她身旁的座位上，包包在後座 → 狗在女子旁邊 next to the woman。\n【其他選項】(A) 狗沒坐在包包上；(C) 狗不在包包裡；(D) 包包在女子後方，狗並不在女子和包包中間。\n【例句】My cat likes to sleep next to the window.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1930, "question": "In the classroom, Tim sits ______ Amy and Ben. Amy is on his left, and Ben is on his right.", "options": ["next to", "between", "behind", "across"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "左右各一人 → 在兩者之間 between。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1931, "question": "The bank is ______ the post office. They are side by side.", "options": ["next to", "under", "inside", "above"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "side by side 並排 → next to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1932, "question": "I can't find my keys. Oh, they're ______ my bag, under my books.", "options": ["on", "between", "inside", "next to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "在包包裡、書下面 → inside。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1933, "question": "I enjoy drinking a cup of black coffee ______ Friday nights.", "options": ["at", "by", "in", "on"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜on + 星期（Friday nights）", "explanation": "【句型】on + 星期幾／特定某天的早上、晚上（on Friday nights, on Sunday morning）。\n【分析】Friday nights 是特定星期的晚上 → 用 on。\n【其他選項】(A) at night 可以，但有 Friday 時要用 on；(B) by 在…之前；(C) in the evening 可以，但加上星期時改用 on。\n【例句】We usually watch movies on Saturday evenings.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1934, "question": "My family goes hiking ______ Sunday mornings.", "options": ["in", "at", "on", "by"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "星期 + 早上 → on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1935, "question": "I always read a book ______ night before I sleep.", "options": ["at", "on", "in", "for"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "at night 固定用法。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1936, "question": "Ms. Lee takes a walk ______ the evening after dinner.", "options": ["on", "in", "at", "by"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "in the evening；沒有指定星期時用 in。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1937, "question": "Bob: When is Mr. Wang going to Japan?\nTim: On ______.", "options": ["June", "June fourth", "the year 2010", "June, 2010"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜On + 日期（on June fourth）", "explanation": "【句型】on 只接特定某一天；只有月份或年份要用 in。\n【分析】Tim 用 On 開頭 → 後面必須是具體日期，只有 June fourth 符合。\n【其他選項】(A) June 只有月份，應說 In June；(C) the year 2010 是年份，應用 in；(D) June, 2010 仍無「日」，應用 in。\n【例句】The concert is on March 3.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1938, "question": "Amy: When were you born?\nTom: In ______.", "options": ["May 2", "Monday", "2011", "the morning of May 2"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "In + 年份 → 2011；有日期或星期要用 on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1939, "question": "Kim: When is the school trip?\nJoe: It's on ______.", "options": ["November", "the twelfth of November", "2026", "winter"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "on + 特定日期 the twelfth of November。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1940, "question": "We will have the English contest ______ December.", "options": ["in", "on", "at", "for"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "只有月份 → in December。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1941, "question": "Judy moved to France and has lived there ______ two years. I miss her very much.", "options": ["before", "for", "in", "since"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜for + 一段時間（現在完成式）", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 + for + 一段時間（for two years）；since + 時間點。\n【分析】has lived（現在完成式）+ two years（一段時間）→ 住了兩年，用 for。\n【其他選項】(A) before 之前，before two years 不合文法；(C) in two years 表「兩年後」，用於未來；(D) since 接時間點，不接一段時間。\n【例句】I have studied English for six years.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1942, "question": "Andy has played the guitar ______ he was ten.", "options": ["for", "since", "in", "during"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間點子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1943, "question": "The Lins have lived in Hsinchu ______ more than ten years.", "options": ["since", "in", "for", "on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "more than ten years 是一段時間 → for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1944, "question": "I'll finish the report ______ two days. Please wait.", "options": ["in", "for", "since", "before"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "in + 一段時間 表「…之後」（未來）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1945, "question": "______ going shopping, Dad asked me if Mom would eat at home tonight. He wanted to know what he should buy for the dinner.", "options": ["Without", "Until", "By", "Before"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜Before + Ving（在…之前）", "explanation": "【句型】Before + Ving = 在做…之前（介系詞 + 動名詞）。\n【分析】後句 He wanted to know what he should buy（想知道要買什麼）→ 是「去購物之前」先問，用 Before。\n【其他選項】(A) Without going shopping 沒去購物，但問題是為了買菜；(B) Until 直到，句子語意不通；(C) By + Ving 表「藉由…方式」，不合。\n【例句】Before eating, wash your hands.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1946, "question": "______ leaving the classroom, please turn off the lights.", "options": ["Before", "Without", "Since", "During"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "離開教室前關燈 → Before。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1947, "question": "You can improve your English ______ reading English books every day.", "options": ["before", "by", "until", "without"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "by + Ving 藉由…方式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1948, "question": "Ruby went to school ______ eating breakfast, so she was hungry all morning.", "options": ["before", "by", "without", "after"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "整個早上都餓 → 沒吃早餐 without eating。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1949, "question": "I live ______ my office, so I walk to work every morning.", "options": ["along", "between", "near", "out of"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜near 在…附近", "explanation": "【句型】near + 地點 = 在…附近。\n【分析】so I walk to work（所以走路上班）→ 住在辦公室附近，用 near。\n【其他選項】(A) along 沿著，接路、河；(B) between 需要兩個對象 A and B；(D) out of 從…出來，不合。\n【例句】There is a park near my school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1950, "question": "Mia lives far ______ school, so she takes the MRT every day.", "options": ["from", "near", "along", "with"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "far from 離…遠，所以搭捷運。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1951, "question": "Is there a convenience store ______ here? I need to buy some water.", "options": ["along", "near", "between", "out of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "near here 這附近。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1952, "question": "We rode our bikes ______ the river and enjoyed the view.", "options": ["near", "between", "along", "out of"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "沿著河騎車 → along。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1953, "question": "Allan: Want to try Uncle Joe's pumpkin pie? I heard it's quite good.\nJamie: No, thank you. I think nobody ______ my mom can make good pies.", "options": ["with", "than", "for", "except"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜nobody except 除了…沒有人", "explanation": "【句型】nobody / no one + except + 人 = 除了某人以外沒有人。\n【分析】Jamie 拒絕吃 Joe 叔叔的派，因為他認為「除了我媽以外沒人做得出好派」→ except。\n【其他選項】(A) with 和…一起，語意不合；(B) than 用於比較級（better than），本句無比較級；(C) for 為了，不合。\n【例句】No one except Kevin got full marks.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1954, "question": "Nobody ______ Linda remembered to bring an umbrella, so we all got wet.", "options": ["except", "with", "for", "than"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "只有 Linda 帶傘 → nobody except Linda。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1955, "question": "My grandma cooks better ______ anyone else in our family.", "options": ["except", "than", "with", "of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "比較級 better than。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1956, "question": "I like all kinds of fruit ______ bananas. I never eat them.", "options": ["with", "for", "except", "about"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "從不吃香蕉 → 除了香蕉 except。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1957, "question": "March is the third month of the year. It comes ______ February and April.", "options": ["about", "before", "during", "between"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜between A and B", "explanation": "【句型】between A and B = 在 A 和 B 之間。\n【分析】三月在二月和四月中間，且空格後有 February and April 兩個對象 → between。\n【其他選項】(A) about 關於；(B) before 在…之前，三月不在四月和二月「之前」；(C) during 在…期間，接一段期間而非兩個月份。\n【例句】Wednesday comes between Tuesday and Thursday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1958, "question": "The letter C comes ______ B and D.", "options": ["between", "before", "after", "among"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "兩者之間 between B and D。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1959, "question": "Sunday comes ______ Monday. It's the day before Monday.", "options": ["after", "before", "between", "during"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "the day before Monday → before。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1960, "question": "Our school is ______ the library and the hospital.", "options": ["among", "near to", "between", "during"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "兩個地點之間 between A and B。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1961, "question": "My dog, Lucy, was lying on the sofa ______ the fan on the wall. So when the fan fell, she was hit right on the head.", "options": ["under", "off", "from", "down"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜under 在…正下方", "explanation": "【句型】under + N = 在…的正下方。\n【分析】電扇掉下來正好打到她的頭 → 狗躺在電扇的正下方，用 under。\n【其他選項】(B) off 離開（某表面）；(C) from 從…；(D) down 向下（副詞/介系詞，down the stairs），都無法表示「在電扇下方」的位置。\n【例句】The cat is sleeping under the table.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1962, "question": "Don't stand ______ the tree when it's raining with thunder. It's dangerous.", "options": ["above", "under", "off", "from"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "雷雨時別站在樹下 → under。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1963, "question": "The picture is hanging on the wall ______ the clock.", "options": ["below", "down", "off", "from"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "掛在時鐘下方 → below（在下方，牆面上）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1964, "question": "Please take your feet ______ the desk. It's not polite.", "options": ["under", "down", "off", "below"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "把腳從桌上移開 → take ... off。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1965, "question": "Linda: Jenny, will you still be here this afternoon?\nJenny: Yeah, I think I'll stay ______ five. Then I'll leave for dinner.", "options": ["at", "for", "since", "until"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜until 直到…（持續動作）", "explanation": "【句型】持續性動詞（stay, wait, sleep）+ until + 時間點 = 一直…直到某時。\n【分析】stay（待著）是持續動作，Then I'll leave（然後離開）→ 待到五點，用 until。\n【其他選項】(A) at five 表在五點這一刻，與「待著」持續動作不合；(B) for 接一段時間（for two hours）；(C) since 用於現在完成式，表自從。\n【例句】Please wait here until I come back.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1966, "question": "Last night I studied ______ midnight, so I'm very tired now.", "options": ["since", "until", "for", "at"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "持續讀書直到午夜 → until。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1967, "question": "The shop is open ______ 9 p.m. Let's go after dinner.", "options": ["until", "since", "for", "during"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "營業到晚上九點 → until。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1968, "question": "We waited for the bus ______ thirty minutes, but it didn't come.", "options": ["until", "since", "for", "at"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "thirty minutes 一段時間 → for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1969, "question": "Tina is getting married to a man she has known only ______ a month.", "options": ["for", "in", "on", "since"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜for + 一段時間（has known for）", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 + for + 一段時間。\n【分析】has known（現在完成式）+ a month（一段時間）→ 才認識一個月，用 for。\n【其他選項】(B) in a month 表一個月後（未來）；(C) on 接日期；(D) since 接時間點（since last month）。\n【例句】I have had this bike for three years.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1970, "question": "Sam has known Peter ______ they were in kindergarten.", "options": ["for", "since", "in", "on"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "since + 過去時間點子句。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1971, "question": "Mrs. Wu has worked at this hospital ______ ten years.", "options": ["for", "since", "in", "at"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "ten years 一段時間 → for。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1972, "question": "The new MRT line will open ______ two months.", "options": ["for", "since", "in", "on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "in + 時間 表「…之後」（未來）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1973, "question": "There's something wrong ______ Gina and Greg. They haven't talked to each other for over one month.", "options": ["beside", "between", "during", "under"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜會考歷屆｜between 兩人之間", "explanation": "【句型】between A and B = 在 A 與 B（兩者）之間；something wrong between A and B 兩人之間有問題。\n【分析】Gina and Greg 兩人一個多月沒說話 → 兩人「之間」出了問題，用 between。\n【其他選項】(A) beside 在旁邊，表位置；(C) during 在…期間，接一段時間；(D) under 在…下面，均不合。\n【例句】There is a secret between Ann and me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1974, "question": "The match ______ Taiwan and Japan was very exciting.", "options": ["among", "between", "during", "beside"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "兩隊之間的比賽 between A and B。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1975, "question": "The teacher divided the cake ______ the five students.", "options": ["between", "during", "with", "among"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "三者以上之間 → among。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1976, "question": "Kate and Ella are good friends. There are no secrets ______ them.", "options": ["between", "beside", "under", "during"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "兩人之間沒有秘密 between them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1977, "question": "Little Eric chose the doll ______ big brown eyes because it was the cutest in the store.", "options": ["at", "in", "on", "with"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜115會考｜介係詞 with 表「帶有（特徵）」", "explanation": "【句型】名詞 + with + 特徵：帶有……的（人／物）。\n【分析】the doll ______ big brown eyes：大棕眼是娃娃的特徵，用 with 修飾 the doll，表示「有著大棕眼的娃娃」，故選 with。\n【其他選項】(A) at 在（某點）、(B) in 在……裡面、(C) on 在……上面：都表位置，不能表示「具有某特徵」。\n【例句】The girl with long hair is my sister.\n※注意：描述人穿著時也可用 in，如 the man in a black coat，但「身體特徵」要用 with。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1978, "question": "Do you see the boy ______ curly hair? He is the new student.", "options": ["in", "with", "at", "of"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "表示身體特徵「有著捲髮」用 with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1979, "question": "I want to buy the bag ______ two big pockets on the front.", "options": ["with", "at", "by", "for"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "「有兩個大口袋」的包包，with 表具有。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1980, "question": "The woman ______ a red dress is our new English teacher.", "options": ["with", "on", "in", "at"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "表示穿著衣服用 in：穿紅洋裝的女士。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1981, "question": "Flora: Do you know that cute-looking boy over there?\nTeresa: There are three of them. Which one?\nFlora: The one ______ a white T-shirt and blue jeans.", "options": ["at", "on", "with", "in"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "介係詞｜講義錯題｜in + 衣物（穿著…），介系詞片語後位修飾", "explanation": "【句型】N + in + 衣物／顏色 = 穿著…的人；介系詞片語放在名詞後修飾。\n【分析】The one in a white T-shirt and blue jeans = 穿著白 T 恤和藍色牛仔褲的那位。\n【其他選項】(A) at 表地點或時間點；(B) on 表在…上面，不表穿著；(C) with 用於配件或身體特徵（with glasses, with long hair），不用於穿衣服。\n【例句】The woman in the red dress is my English teacher.\n備註：講義 p.287", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1982, "question": "The man ______ glasses is our new science teacher.", "options": ["in", "with", "at", "on"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "配件（眼鏡）用 with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1983, "question": "Who is the girl ______ the yellow raincoat?", "options": ["on", "at", "in", "by"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "穿著衣物用 in。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1984, "question": "The boy ______ long hair and a big smile is my cousin.", "options": ["with", "in", "on", "at"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "介係詞｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "身體特徵（長髮）用 with。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "介係詞"}, {"id": 1985, "question": "At dinner time, I often enjoy telling Mom everything ______ at school.", "options": ["happened", "was happening", "that happened", "which happening"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜everything＋that＋V（關代 that 作主詞不可省）", "explanation": "【句型】N（everything）＋ that ＋ V，關係代名詞 that 在子句中當主詞時不可省略。\n【分析】telling Mom everything 後要用關係子句修飾 everything，且子句缺主詞，需用 that happened「在學校發生的每件事」。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 缺關係代名詞，句中會出現兩個主要動詞；(D) which 後需接完整動詞，happening 不行，且 everything 通常用 that。\n【例句】Please tell me everything that you saw.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1986, "question": "I'll never forget the people ______ helped me during the trip.", "options": ["who", "which", "they", "whom they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 people 是人，關代當主詞用 who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1987, "question": "Is there anything ______ wrong with your computer?", "options": ["is", "that is", "which being", "it is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "anything 後接關係子句，關代 that 當主詞不能省，用 that is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1988, "question": "This is the bus ______ to the airport.", "options": ["goes", "going to it", "that goes", "which go"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 the bus 單數，關代當主詞不可省，用 that goes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1989, "question": "Fiona loves listening to her children sing songs ______ at school.", "options": ["are learned", "that learned", "they learned", "that they are learned"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜關係代名詞省略（受格）＋主動", "explanation": "【句型】N + (that/which) + S + V：受格關係代名詞可省略。\n【分析】songs (that) they learned at school「他們在學校學的歌」，they 是學歌的人，songs 是 learned 的受詞，that 被省略 → they learned。\n【其他選項】(A) 少了關係代名詞，句中出現兩個動詞；(B) songs that learned 表示「歌學了…」，主動語意錯；(D) they are learned 表「孩子們被學」，語意錯。\n【例句】This is the bike my dad bought for me.\n備註：考點主要是關係代名詞省略（主動），非被動語態。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1990, "question": "The cake ______ for my birthday was delicious.", "options": ["Mom made", "that made", "was made", "Mom was made"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "the cake (that) Mom made，省略受格關代 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1991, "question": "The book ______ last week is very interesting.", "options": ["borrowed I", "I borrowed", "that borrowed", "was borrowed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "the book (that) I borrowed，省略受格關代，語序為 S + V。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1992, "question": "Do you like the songs ______ in music class?", "options": ["are sung", "that sang", "we sang", "that we are sung"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "the songs (that) we sang，省略受格關代 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1993, "question": "The medicine I ______ you this morning should be taken three times a day.", "options": ["to give", "given", "giving", "gave"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜關係代名詞省略＋過去式主動 gave", "explanation": "【句型】N + (that) + S + V...：受格關係代名詞省略後，子句仍需有完整動詞。\n【分析】The medicine (that) I gave you this morning，主詞 I 是「給」的人 → 主動；this morning 已發生 → 過去式 gave。整句主要動詞是 should be taken。\n【其他選項】(A)(C) 不定詞、現在分詞不能當子句的動詞；(B) given 是 p.p.，I given 缺 be/have，且語意應為主動。\n【例句】The shoes I bought last week are too small.\n備註：本題選項考主動/被動判斷，但句構重點是關係代名詞省略。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1994, "question": "The pictures you ______ me last week were beautiful.", "options": ["send", "sent", "sending", "to send"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "the pictures (that) you sent me，last week 用過去式 sent。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1995, "question": "The movie we ______ last night was really scary.", "options": ["watched", "watching", "were watched", "to watch"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "the movie (that) we watched，主動過去式 watched。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1996, "question": "The sweater my grandma ______ for me last winter is still warm.", "options": ["making", "to make", "was made", "made"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "the sweater (that) my grandma made，奶奶「做」毛衣 → 主動過去式 made。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1997, "question": "All the excuses Nick made ______ a lot about how much he hates to do the job.", "options": ["say", "saying", "which say", "to say"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜省略關代的形容詞子句 + 主詞動詞一致", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞 + (that/which) + S + V（受格關代可省略）；整句主詞仍是先行詞，要接主要動詞。\n【分析】Nick made 是省略 that 的形容詞子句，修飾 All the excuses；句子還缺主要動詞，主詞 excuses 是複數，所以用 say。\n【其他選項】(B) saying、(D) to say 不能當主要動詞；(C) which say 會變成另一個形容詞子句，整句仍缺主要動詞。\n【例句】The books my aunt gave me are very interesting.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1998, "question": "The cookies Linda baked yesterday ______ really delicious.", "options": ["tasting", "taste", "tastes", "to taste"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "Linda baked yesterday 為省略關代的子句，主詞 cookies 複數，用 taste。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 1999, "question": "The boy you met at the party ______ my cousin.", "options": ["is", "are", "being", "who is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "主詞 The boy 單數，主要動詞用 is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2000, "question": "The questions the teacher asked today ______ too hard for most of us.", "options": ["was", "being", "were", "which were"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "主詞 questions 複數，過去式用 were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2001, "question": "Students ______ to go on the school trip should ask their parents first.", "options": ["who want", "want", "who they want", "what they want"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜主格關代 who + 複數動詞", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（人）+ who + V（主格關代，動詞與先行詞一致）。\n【分析】句子主要動詞是 should ask，空格須是修飾 Students 的形容詞子句 → who want（想去校外教學的學生）；Students 複數，用 want。\n【其他選項】(B) want 會造成一句兩個動詞；(C) who 已當主詞，不可再加 they；(D) what 不能有先行詞，且後面多了 they。\n【例句】People who like music often go to concerts.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2002, "question": "The boy ______ is talking to Ms. Lin is my cousin.", "options": ["he", "who", "which", "what"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "先行詞人 + 主格 who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2003, "question": "Kids ______ eat too much candy may have bad teeth.", "options": ["who", "which", "they", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 Kids 是人 → who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2004, "question": "Anyone who ______ to join the club can sign up today.", "options": ["want", "wanting", "wants", "to want"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "anyone 視為單數 → wants。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2005, "question": "Actor David Piper became tired of talking about the movie ______ after he was interviewed about it many times.", "options": ["he is famous", "that he is famous", "that is famous for", "he is famous for"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜受格關代省略（the movie he is famous for）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞 + (that/which) + S + V + 介系詞；受格關代可省略。be famous for + N = 因…而出名。\n【分析】原意為 he is famous for the movie → the movie (that) he is famous for，省略受格關代 that，介系詞 for 留在句尾。\n【其他選項】(A) 少了 for，the movie 無法成為 famous 的受詞；(B) 同樣少了 for；(C) that is famous for 表「電影因…出名」，for 後缺受詞且主詞不對。\n【例句】This is the snack Tainan is famous for.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2006, "question": "This is the song ______ I told you about yesterday.", "options": ["that", "who", "what", "it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "先行詞物 + 受格關代 that，about 留句尾。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2007, "question": "The girl ______ Sam is talking with is my sister.", "options": ["which", "she", "who", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "先行詞人 + 受格 who/that，with 留句尾。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2008, "question": "Is this the dictionary ______?", "options": ["you are looking", "you are looking for", "you are looking for it", "that you are looking it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "look for the dictionary → 關係子句保留 for，不重複 it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2009, "question": "The tall man ______ at the bookstore is my high school teacher.", "options": ["you saw", "who saw", "you saw him", "that you saw him"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜受格關代省略（the man you saw）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞 + (who/whom/that) + S + V；受格關代可省略，子句中不再重複受詞。\n【分析】you saw the man → the man (whom) you saw，省略受格關代；主要動詞是 is。\n【其他選項】(B) who saw 表「看到（別人）的男人」，缺受詞且語意不完整；(C)(D) him 與先行詞 the man 重複，錯誤。\n【例句】The book I bought yesterday is very interesting.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2010, "question": "The cake ______ was delicious.", "options": ["Mom made", "Mom made it", "that Mom made it", "which made Mom"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "Mom made the cake → the cake (that) Mom made，不重複 it。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2011, "question": "The girl ______ in the park was my classmate.", "options": ["we met her", "that we met her", "we met", "who met we"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "受格關代省略，不重複 her。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2012, "question": "The shoes ______ last week are too small for me.", "options": ["bought them", "I bought", "I bought them", "who I bought"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "the shoes (that) I bought，不重複 them。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2013, "question": "I like to read comic books ______ me laugh.", "options": ["made", "to have made", "that make", "which makes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜主格關代 that + 動詞一致", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（物）+ that/which + V；動詞單複數與先行詞一致。\n【分析】先行詞 comic books 是複數 → that make me laugh（讓我發笑的漫畫書）。\n【其他選項】(A) made 缺關代，且時態不合；(B) to have made 不定詞語意不通；(D) which makes 動詞單數，與複數 comic books 不一致。\n【例句】I like movies that have happy endings.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2014, "question": "Tom has a dog ______ very fast.", "options": ["that run", "who run", "runs", "that runs"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "a dog 單數 → that runs。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2015, "question": "These are the photos ______ me of my childhood.", "options": ["that remind", "which reminds", "remind", "that reminds"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "photos 複數 → that remind。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2016, "question": "She bought a bag ______ a lot of pockets.", "options": ["that have", "which has", "it has", "who has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "a bag 單數物 → which has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2017, "question": "The movie is about a true story ______ happened in Korea in 1945.", "options": ["it", "that", "what", "when"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜主格關代 that（事物）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（物）+ that/which + V（主格關代）。\n【分析】空格修飾 a true story，且後面直接接動詞 happened → 需主格關代 that。\n【其他選項】(A) it 是代名詞，不能連接兩個子句；(C) what 不可接先行詞；(D) when 是關係副詞，先行詞要是時間。\n【例句】This is a house that was built 100 years ago.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2018, "question": "I read a book ______ was written by a Taiwanese writer.", "options": ["what", "who", "which", "where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "先行詞物 + 主格 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2019, "question": "Do you remember the day ______ we first met?", "options": ["when", "what", "who", "it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "先行詞時間 the day → 關係副詞 when。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2020, "question": "It is a story ______ makes everyone cry.", "options": ["who", "that", "what", "it"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "先行詞物 + 主格 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2021, "question": "James: Do you see the street vendor over there?\nPhilip: Which one?\nJames: The one ______ is wearing a hat.", "options": ["it", "he", "who", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜主格關代 who（人）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（人）+ who + V。\n【分析】The one 指 the street vendor（小販，人），後接動詞 is wearing → 主格關代 who。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) it、he 是代名詞，不能連接子句；(D) which 用於事物，不用於人。\n【例句】The one who is singing is my sister.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2022, "question": "Amy: Which girl is your sister?\nBen: The one ______ has long hair.", "options": ["which", "she", "who", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "人 → who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2023, "question": "Which bike is yours? — The one ______ is next to the tree.", "options": ["who", "that", "it", "what"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "物 → that/which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2024, "question": "The man ______ helped me find my wallet was very kind.", "options": ["who", "which", "he", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "人 + 主格 who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2025, "question": "Do you remember the girl ______ looked worried at the train station yesterday?", "options": ["who", "where", "which", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜會考歷屆｜主格關代 who（人）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（人）+ who + V。\n【分析】先行詞 the girl 是人，後接動詞 looked → 主格關代 who。\n【其他選項】(B) where 關係副詞，先行詞須是地點；(C) which 用於事物；(D) what 不接先行詞。\n【例句】I know the boy who won the race.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2026, "question": "Do you know the woman ______ is standing at the door?", "options": ["which", "who", "where", "what"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "人 → who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2027, "question": "This is the restaurant ______ we had dinner last week.", "options": ["who", "which", "what", "where"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "地點 + 完整子句 → where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2028, "question": "I found the key ______ I lost yesterday.", "options": ["who", "where", "which", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "物 → which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2029, "question": "I thought the girl ______ was Kate, but it was her sister, Candy. They sounded almost the same.", "options": ["answered the phone", "she answered the phone", "who answered the phone", "and answered the phone"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜115會考｜主格關係代名詞 who（the girl who answered the phone）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞（人）+ who + 動詞……（形容詞子句修飾前面的名詞）。\n【分析】主要句是 I thought the girl ... was Kate，空格要修飾 the girl，說明是「接電話的那個女孩」，用主格關代 who → the girl who answered the phone。\n【其他選項】(A) 少了關代，一句出現 answered 和 was 兩個動詞；(B) 多了主詞 she，無法連接兩句；(D) and 連接對等動作，the girl and answered… was 結構錯誤。\n【例句】The boy who sits next to me is good at drawing.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2030, "question": "The man ______ is talking to my dad is our new neighbor.", "options": ["he", "who", "which", "and"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 the man 是人，主格關代用 who。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2031, "question": "I like the song ______ won first prize in the contest.", "options": ["which", "who", "it", "and it"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 the song 是物，主格關代用 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2032, "question": "The students ______ in the gym are practicing for the dance show.", "options": ["they are", "and are", "who are", "who is"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "先行詞 the students 為複數人，用 who are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2033, "question": "The Great Wall of China ______ is said to be the only man-made building able to be seen from space, is visited by hundreds of thousands of people from around the world.", "options": ["that", "×", ", which", ", what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜非限定用法：, which（專有名詞不可用 that）", "explanation": "【句型】專有名詞（獨一無二的先行詞）+ , which / , who…, + 主要動詞（非限定用法，前後加逗號）。\n【分析】長城只有一個，後面是補充說明，要用非限定用法「, which」；space 後面的逗號與之呼應，主要動詞是 is visited。\n【其他選項】(A) 非限定用法不能用 that；(B) 不填則 is said 與 is visited 兩個動詞沒有連接；(D) what 本身含先行詞，不能接在先行詞後面。\n【例句】Taipei 101, which is in Taipei, was once the tallest building in the world.\n備註：講義 p.289", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2034, "question": "Mr. Chen, ______ teaches us math, is going to retire next year.", "options": ["that", "which", "who", "whom"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "專有名詞（人）當先行詞，非限定用法用 , who，且在子句中當主詞。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2035, "question": "Sun Moon Lake, ______ is in Nantou, attracts many visitors every year.", "options": ["which", "that", "what", "where"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "非限定用法、先行詞是物，用 , which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2036, "question": "The book ______ I borrowed from the library is very interesting.", "options": ["what", "who", ", which", "that"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "限定用法（無逗號）、先行詞是物，可用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2037, "question": "Vivian is trying to save the cat ______ leg is broken.", "options": ["who", "that", "which", "whose"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜關係代名詞所有格 whose", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞 + whose + 名詞 + V（whose 表「…的」，所有格關代，人、物皆可用）\n【分析】空格後直接接名詞 leg，leg is broken 已有主詞和動詞，缺的是「誰的腿」→ the cat's leg，用所有格 whose。\n【其他選項】(A) who 指人，且後面要缺主詞或受詞；(B) that、(C) which 後面要接缺主詞或受詞的子句，不能直接接名詞表所有。\n【例句】I have a friend whose father is a pilot.\n備註：講義 p.291", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2038, "question": "The boy ______ bike was stolen yesterday went to the police station.", "options": ["who", "whose", "which", "that"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "空格後接名詞 bike，表「男孩的腳踏車」，用所有格 whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2039, "question": "We stayed in a hotel ______ windows face the sea.", "options": ["whose", "which", "where", "that"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "windows face the sea 是完整句子，表「飯店的窗戶」，用 whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2040, "question": "Mr. Lin is the teacher ______ class won first prize in the singing contest.", "options": ["who", "which", "whom", "whose"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "class 前要表「老師的班級」，用所有格關代 whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2041, "question": "Jerry, name a park ______ we can camp safely and comfortably.", "options": ["that", "what", "which", "where"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜關係副詞 where（後接完整句）", "explanation": "【句型】地點先行詞 + where（= in/at which）+ 完整句子\n【分析】we can camp safely and comfortably 有主詞、動詞，不缺主詞或受詞（camp 是不及物動詞），缺的是地點 in the park → 用 where。\n【其他選項】(A) that、(C) which 後要接缺名詞的子句；(B) what 不能接在先行詞後面。\n【例句】This is the town where my grandma grew up.\n備註：講義 p.291", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2042, "question": "Do you know a restaurant ______ we can have a quiet dinner?", "options": ["which", "where", "what", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "we can have a quiet dinner 是完整句，缺地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2043, "question": "Tainan is the city ______ Amy visited last summer.", "options": ["where", "what", "which", "whose"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "visited 缺受詞，用關代 which，不能用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2044, "question": "The library ______ I often study on weekends is near my house.", "options": ["where", "which", "that", "what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "I often study on weekends 是完整句，缺地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2045, "question": "I think the park ______ lies across from the police station is the best.", "options": ["whose", "what", "which", "where"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜關係代名詞 which 當主詞（vs. where）", "explanation": "【句型】事物先行詞 + which/that + V（關代當子句主詞）\n【分析】___ lies across from the police station 缺主詞，先行詞 the park 是物 → which。\n【其他選項】(A) whose 後要接名詞；(B) what 不接先行詞；(D) where 是關係副詞，後接完整句，不能當主詞。\n【例句】The bookstore which opened last week sells comic books.\n備註：講義 p.291", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2046, "question": "The museum ______ stands next to the station is free on Sundays.", "options": ["where", "which", "what", "whose"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "___ stands 缺主詞，先行詞是物，用 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2047, "question": "The beach ______ we went swimming last week was very clean.", "options": ["where", "which", "what", "that"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "we went swimming 是完整句，缺地點，用 where。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2048, "question": "The road ______ leads to the night market is always crowded.", "options": ["where", "whose", "that", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "___ leads 缺主詞，先行詞是物，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2049, "question": "This is the sofa on ______ Grandpa used to sit while watching TV.", "options": ["who", "that", "which", "what"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜介系詞＋which（不可用 that）", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞 + 介系詞 + which（物）/ whom（人）+ 子句；介系詞後不可用 that\n【分析】Grandpa used to sit on the sofa → 介系詞 on 提前，先行詞 the sofa 是物 → on which。\n【其他選項】(A) who 指人且不放在介系詞後；(B) that 不能放在介系詞後；(D) what 不接先行詞。\n【例句】This is the box in which I keep my letters.\n備註：講義 p.292", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2050, "question": "That is the desk at ______ my brother does his homework every night.", "options": ["that", "which", "where", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "介系詞 at 後接事物關代用 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2051, "question": "Ms. Chen is the person to ______ you should give this letter.", "options": ["who", "that", "whom", "which"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "介系詞 to 後接人用 whom。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2052, "question": "The hill ______ we had a picnic is not far from here.", "options": ["on which", "on that", "which", "on what"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "we had a picnic on the hill → on which；介系詞後不能接 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2053, "question": "The man and his pet ______ were interviewed by many reporters are famous in this country.", "options": ["which", "that", "who", "whose"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜先行詞「人＋動物」用 that", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞同時有人和動物/物 → 關代只能用 that\n【分析】先行詞 the man and his pet 包含人和動物，且 ___ were interviewed 缺主詞 → that。\n【其他選項】(A) which 只指物；(C) who 只指人；(D) whose 後要接名詞。\n【例句】Look at the girl and her dog that are running in the park.\n備註：講義 p.293", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2054, "question": "The farmer and his cows ______ live on the hill appeared on TV.", "options": ["who", "which", "that", "whose"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "先行詞為人＋動物，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2055, "question": "We talked about the singers and the songs ______ we liked best.", "options": ["that", "who", "which", "whom"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "先行詞為人＋物，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2056, "question": "The old woman ______ cat is lost is crying.", "options": ["that", "whose", "which", "who"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "cat 前表「老婦人的貓」，用所有格 whose。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2057, "question": "We make sure both the pets and their owners ______ come to stay at our hotel will be taken the best care of.", "options": ["who", "which", "that", "they"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "關係代名詞｜講義錯題｜先行詞「動物＋人」用 that", "explanation": "【句型】先行詞同時有人和動物/物 → 關代用 that\n【分析】先行詞 the pets and their owners 包含動物和人，___ come 缺主詞 → that。\n【其他選項】(A) who 只指人；(B) which 只指物或動物；(D) they 是代名詞，不能連接子句，會造成句中兩個動詞 come、will be 無連接。\n【例句】We saw the boy and his horse that won the race.\n備註：講義 p.337", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2058, "question": "The kids and the dogs ______ were playing on the grass looked happy.", "options": ["who", "which", "they", "that"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "先行詞為人＋動物，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2059, "question": "The cat ______ is sleeping on the sofa belongs to my aunt.", "options": ["who", "which", "whose", "where"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "先行詞只有動物 cat，缺主詞，用 which。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2060, "question": "The writer and the books ______ he talked about are popular among teens.", "options": ["that", "who", "whose", "they"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "關係代名詞｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "先行詞為人＋物，用 that。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "關係代名詞"}, {"id": 2061, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Usually I wouldn't cross the park at this time of night. ... Soon after I walked into the park, I saw a man under a tree up ahead. My heart fell. The stories I'd heard about the park __38__ into my head at this moment. ... I did __39__ stupid thing: I decided to hurry past him. ... I had hoped the trees would keep some rain off. And they __40__. But they also made the park look even darker. ... \"What? I __41__ to give back your bag! You dropped it,\" the man gave me my bag.\n\n38. The stories I'd heard about the park ______ into my head at this moment.\n\n▶ 請選出第 38 格的答案", "options": ["are all coming", "have all come", "were all coming", "would all come"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 38 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中描述「當時正在發生」的動作 → 過去進行式 was/were + Ving。\n【分析】全文用過去式敘事（saw, fell），at this moment 指故事當下 → 那些故事「當時正湧進腦海」，用 were all coming。\n【其他選項】(A) are coming 現在進行式，與過去敘事不合；(B) have come 現在完成式，不合過去敘事；(D) would come 表過去的未來或習慣，不是當下正在發生。\n【例句】When I opened the door, my brothers were all watching TV.\n備註：克漏字題組（同一張圖含 38–41 四題）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2062, "question": "When the teacher walked in, the students ______ loudly.", "options": ["are talking", "were talking", "have talked", "will talk"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "過去某時正在進行 → were talking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2063, "question": "I saw a strange man at the gate. Many scary thoughts ______ through my mind at that moment.", "options": ["were running", "are running", "have run", "run"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事當下正在發生 → were running。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2064, "question": "At eight last night, my dad ______ dinner in the kitchen.", "options": ["cooks", "has cooked", "was cooking", "is cooking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 1 題）", "explanation": "過去特定時間正在做 → was cooking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2065, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Usually I wouldn't cross the park at this time of night. ... Soon after I walked into the park, I saw a man under a tree up ahead. My heart fell. The stories I'd heard about the park __38__ into my head at this moment. ... I did __39__ stupid thing: I decided to hurry past him. ... I had hoped the trees would keep some rain off. And they __40__. But they also made the park look even darker. ... \"What? I __41__ to give back your bag! You dropped it,\" the man gave me my bag.\n\n39. But me? No. I did ______ stupid thing: I decided to hurry past him.\n\n▶ 請選出第 39 格的答案", "options": ["another", "one", "the last", "the other"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 39 格｜名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞", "explanation": "【句型】another + 單數名詞 = 另一個、又一個（不特定，數量未限定）。\n【分析】第一段已說 And that was the first stupid thing I did tonight，此處是「又做了一件」蠢事 → another。\n【其他選項】(B) one stupid thing 沒有「又」的意思，與前文連結不上；(C) the last 最後一件，但文末還有 the stupidest thing；(D) the other 用於「兩者中的另一個」，此處並非只有兩件。\n【例句】I ate one cookie, and then I ate another.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2066, "question": "This cup is dirty. Can I have ______ one?", "options": ["other", "another", "the others", "others"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "另一個（不特定）單數 → another。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2067, "question": "I have two pens. One is red, and ______ is blue.", "options": ["another", "other", "the other", "others"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "兩者中的另一個 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2068, "question": "Joe made a mistake on the test, and then he made ______ one.", "options": ["another", "the other", "other", "the others"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 5 題）", "explanation": "又一個錯誤 → another。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2069, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Usually I wouldn't cross the park at this time of night. ... Soon after I walked into the park, I saw a man under a tree up ahead. My heart fell. The stories I'd heard about the park __38__ into my head at this moment. ... I did __39__ stupid thing: I decided to hurry past him. ... I had hoped the trees would keep some rain off. And they __40__. But they also made the park look even darker. ... \"What? I __41__ to give back your bag! You dropped it,\" the man gave me my bag.\n\n40. I had hoped the trees would keep some rain off. And they ______. But they also made the park look even darker.\n\n▶ 請選出第 40 格的答案", "options": ["have", "did", "had", "would"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 40 格｜省略句（助動詞／be動詞）", "explanation": "【句型】為避免重複，用助動詞代替前面的一般動詞片語：they did = they kept some rain off。\n【分析】And they ___ 表「樹也真的擋了雨」，是過去的事實，用 did 代替 kept some rain off；後句 made 也是過去式。\n【其他選項】(A) have 現在式不合過去敘事；(C) had 會變成 had kept，表更早的過去，不合；(D) would 表推測或過去的未來，不表已發生的事實。\n【例句】I hoped my mom would buy me a cake, and she did.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2070, "question": "Tim said he would call me last night, and he ______.", "options": ["does", "did", "has", "is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "did = called，表過去確實做了。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2071, "question": "I don't like spicy food, but my brother ______.", "options": ["does", "is", "did", "doesn't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "現在式肯定 → does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2072, "question": "Amy can swim fast, and her sister ______, too.", "options": ["does", "is", "can", "did"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 9 題）", "explanation": "前面助動詞 can → 用 can 代替。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2073, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Usually I wouldn't cross the park at this time of night. ... Soon after I walked into the park, I saw a man under a tree up ahead. My heart fell. The stories I'd heard about the park __38__ into my head at this moment. ... I did __39__ stupid thing: I decided to hurry past him. ... I had hoped the trees would keep some rain off. And they __40__. But they also made the park look even darker. ... \"What? I __41__ to give back your bag! You dropped it,\" the man gave me my bag.\n\n41. \"What? I ______ to give back your bag! You dropped it,\" the man gave me my bag.\n\n▶ 請選出第 41 格的答案", "options": ["was trying", "try", "would try", "will try"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 41 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去進行式 was/were + Ving 表示過去某段時間正在進行的動作。\n【分析】男子說「我（剛才追你時）一直在試著把包包還給你」，且 You dropped it 用過去式 → was trying。\n【其他選項】(B) try 現在式，表習慣，不合；(C) would try 表假設或過去的未來；(D) will try 表未來，但他已經把包包拿給我了。\n【例句】Sorry, I didn't hear you. I was listening to music.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2074, "question": "\"Why didn't you answer the phone?\" \"I ______ a shower.\"", "options": ["take", "was taking", "will take", "have taken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "打電話當時正在洗澡 → was taking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2075, "question": "Sorry for shouting. I ______ to tell you that your bus was coming.", "options": ["was trying", "try", "will try", "would try"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "剛才一直試著告訴你 → was trying。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2076, "question": "While I ______ my homework, the lights went out.", "options": ["do", "will do", "was doing", "have done"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 13 題）", "explanation": "While + 過去進行式，被過去式動作打斷。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2077, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Elizabeth Alexandra Mary Windsor was born in London on April 21, 1926. No one thought one day she __38__ the queen of the UK. After her grandfather, King George V, died in 1936, Elizabeth's uncle, Prince Edward, became King Edward VIII. Edward __39__ in love with a married American woman long before, and he decided to marry her after he became the king. However, Edward was asked to choose between the throne and his love. Finally, he decided to give up the throne.\n__40__. After Edward VIII gave up the throne, Elizabeth's father became King George VI. As the oldest child without any brothers, Elizabeth became next in line to the throne. She needed to say goodbye to her good old life and prepare to be a queen. After her father died in 1952, she became Queen Elizabeth II.\nEver since she became head of her country, Queen Elizabeth II __41__: She has held meetings with important people in the UK, and has visited many foreign countries. In the few hours she keeps to herself, however, she reads and enjoys horseback riding. (throne 王位)\n\n38. No one thought one day she ______ the queen of the UK.\n\n▶ 請選出第 38 格的答案", "options": ["has become", "became", "had become", "would become"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 38 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去式主要子句（thought）+ that 子句中表「當時看來的未來」→ would + V（過去未來式）。\n【分析】No one thought（過去）+ one day（將來有一天）→ 當時沒人想到她「將會」成為女王，用 would become。\n【其他選項】(A) has become 現在完成式，不配 thought 的過去敘事；(B) became 表已成為的事實，與 one day（將來）不合；(C) had become 表更早已完成，與 one day 矛盾。\n【例句】I never thought I would win the contest.\n備註：克漏字題組（同一張圖含 38–41 四題）", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2078, "question": "When Tom was little, he never thought he ______ a doctor someday.", "options": ["will be", "would be", "has been", "is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "過去觀點的未來 → would be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2079, "question": "My mom said she ______ me a new bike for my birthday.", "options": ["would buy", "buys", "has bought", "will have bought"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "said（過去）+ 未來 → would buy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2080, "question": "Nobody knew the little shop ______ so famous ten years later.", "options": ["becomes", "has become", "would become", "had become"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 17 題）", "explanation": "過去當時看來的未來 → would become。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2081, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Elizabeth Alexandra Mary Windsor was born in London on April 21, 1926. No one thought one day she __38__ the queen of the UK. After her grandfather, King George V, died in 1936, Elizabeth's uncle, Prince Edward, became King Edward VIII. Edward __39__ in love with a married American woman long before, and he decided to marry her after he became the king. However, Edward was asked to choose between the throne and his love. Finally, he decided to give up the throne.\n__40__. After Edward VIII gave up the throne, Elizabeth's father became King George VI. As the oldest child without any brothers, Elizabeth became next in line to the throne. She needed to say goodbye to her good old life and prepare to be a queen. After her father died in 1952, she became Queen Elizabeth II.\nEver since she became head of her country, Queen Elizabeth II __41__: She has held meetings with important people in the UK, and has visited many foreign countries. In the few hours she keeps to herself, however, she reads and enjoys horseback riding. (throne 王位)\n\n39. Edward ______ in love with a married American woman long before, and he decided to marry her after he became the king.\n\n▶ 請選出第 39 格的答案", "options": ["has fallen", "is falling", "had fallen", "would fall"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 39 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去完成式 had + p.p. 表示「比過去某時間更早」發生的事。\n【分析】long before（早在之前）指在他成為國王（過去）之前，就已經愛上她 → had fallen。\n【其他選項】(A) has fallen 現在完成式，不用於過去敘事；(B) is falling 現在進行式不合；(D) would fall 表過去的未來，與 long before 矛盾。\n【例句】When I got to the station, the train had left.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2082, "question": "By the time we arrived, the movie ______.", "options": ["has started", "had started", "starts", "would start"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "比 arrived 更早發生 → had started。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2083, "question": "Lily ______ Japanese for three years before she moved to Tokyo.", "options": ["had studied", "has studied", "studies", "would study"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "搬家前已學 → 過去完成式 had studied。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2084, "question": "I didn't watch the show because I ______ it before.", "options": ["see", "have seen", "would see", "had seen"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 21 題）", "explanation": "比 didn't watch 更早看過 → had seen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2085, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Elizabeth Alexandra Mary Windsor was born in London on April 21, 1926. No one thought one day she __38__ the queen of the UK. After her grandfather, King George V, died in 1936, Elizabeth's uncle, Prince Edward, became King Edward VIII. Edward __39__ in love with a married American woman long before, and he decided to marry her after he became the king. However, Edward was asked to choose between the throne and his love. Finally, he decided to give up the throne.\n__40__. After Edward VIII gave up the throne, Elizabeth's father became King George VI. As the oldest child without any brothers, Elizabeth became next in line to the throne. She needed to say goodbye to her good old life and prepare to be a queen. After her father died in 1952, she became Queen Elizabeth II.\nEver since she became head of her country, Queen Elizabeth II __41__: She has held meetings with important people in the UK, and has visited many foreign countries. In the few hours she keeps to herself, however, she reads and enjoys horseback riding. (throne 王位)\n\n40. ______. After Edward VIII gave up the throne, Elizabeth's father became King George VI. ...\n\n▶ 請選出第 40 格的答案", "options": ["This changed Elizabeth's life", "It was not easy to give up the throne", "It was good news to Elizabeth and her family", "This part of history made the UK a strong country"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 40 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】段落主題句：空格在段首，需概括本段內容並承接上一段。\n【分析】上段末 Edward 放棄王位；本段說伊莉莎白因此成為王位繼承人、要告別舊生活準備當女王 → 這件事「改變了伊莉莎白的人生」。\n【其他選項】(B) 本段沒有談放棄王位有多難；(C) 文中說她需 say goodbye to her good old life，看不出是好消息；(D) 本段沒有談英國變強大。\n【例句】Moving to Taipei changed my life. I made many new friends there.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2086, "question": "______. After Ken's family got a dog, he started to walk it every morning and became much healthier.", "options": ["The dog changed Ken's life", "Ken didn't like dogs", "Dogs are expensive", "Ken's family moved away"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "後文描述 Ken 生活改變 → 主題句為狗改變了他的生活。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2087, "question": "______. Mia practiced the piano for three hours every day and finally won first prize.", "options": ["Mia gave up the piano", "Hard work brought Mia success", "Mia didn't like music", "The contest was canceled"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "努力練習後得獎 → 努力帶來成功。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2088, "question": "______. Because of the typhoon, all the schools were closed, and the trains stopped running.", "options": ["The weather was nice", "People went to the beach", "The typhoon changed everyone's plans", "Students had a test"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 25 題）", "explanation": "颱風導致停課停駛 → 颱風改變大家的計畫。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2089, "question": "(38–41) [克漏字] Elizabeth Alexandra Mary Windsor was born in London on April 21, 1926. No one thought one day she __38__ the queen of the UK. After her grandfather, King George V, died in 1936, Elizabeth's uncle, Prince Edward, became King Edward VIII. Edward __39__ in love with a married American woman long before, and he decided to marry her after he became the king. However, Edward was asked to choose between the throne and his love. Finally, he decided to give up the throne.\n__40__. After Edward VIII gave up the throne, Elizabeth's father became King George VI. As the oldest child without any brothers, Elizabeth became next in line to the throne. She needed to say goodbye to her good old life and prepare to be a queen. After her father died in 1952, she became Queen Elizabeth II.\nEver since she became head of her country, Queen Elizabeth II __41__: She has held meetings with important people in the UK, and has visited many foreign countries. In the few hours she keeps to herself, however, she reads and enjoys horseback riding. (throne 王位)\n\n41. Ever since she became head of her country, Queen Elizabeth II ______: She has held meetings with important people in the UK, and has visited many foreign countries.\n\n▶ 請選出第 41 格的答案", "options": ["has worked hard for the UK", "has been popular with the people of the UK", "has been the queen of the UK for a long time", "has brought the people of the UK much closer"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 41 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】冒號（:）後的內容是對前句的說明或舉例，前句須能概括後面的細節。\n【分析】冒號後說她與重要人士開會、出訪許多國家，都是「為國家努力工作」的例子；下一句 however 提到她少數的私人時間，也呼應她很忙 → has worked hard for the UK。\n【其他選項】(B) 冒號後沒有提到人民喜愛她；(C) 雖為事實，但開會、出訪無法說明「在位很久」；(D) 沒有提到拉近人民的距離。\n【例句】My dad works very hard: he gets up at six and comes home at ten every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2090, "question": "Coach Wang ______: he gets to school at 6 a.m. and practices with the team every day.", "options": ["works very hard", "is very rich", "likes music", "is new at school"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "冒號後舉早到和天天練習 → 很努力。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2091, "question": "Our town ______: there are many parks, and the streets are always clean.", "options": ["is very old", "is a nice place to live", "is very noisy", "has many factories"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "公園多、街道乾淨 → 宜居的好地方。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2092, "question": "Grandma ______: she grows vegetables, cooks for us, and walks the dog every day.", "options": ["is always tired", "doesn't like animals", "keeps herself busy", "lives alone in the city"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 29 題）", "explanation": "種菜、煮飯、遛狗 → 讓自己保持忙碌。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2093, "question": "(19-21)\nIf you cannot live without your car, Zurich might be the last city you would like to visit. In Zurich, people are welcome, but cars are not! Over the past 20 years, this city has used smart ways ______(19). One is to keep the same total number of parking spaces. For example, if 50 new parking spaces are built in one part of the city, then 50 old spaces in other parts are taken away for other uses. So the total number does not change. Some are unhappy that there are never enough spaces. That is just what the city has in mind: If people find parking more difficult, they will drive less.\n__(20)__, the total number of cars in the city is counted. Over 3,500 little computers are put under Zurich roads to check the number of cars that enter the city. If the number is higher than the city can deal with, the traffic lights on the roads that enter the city will be kept red. So drivers who are traveling into Zurich have to stop and wait until there are fewer cars in the city. Now, you may wonder __(21)__. The answer is simple: The city wants to make more space for its people.\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["to make traffic lighter", "to invite people to visit", "to make itself a famous city", "to build more parking spaces"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】smart ways + to V（表目的）；克漏字須依全文主旨判斷。\n【分析】全文說蘇黎世「歡迎人、不歡迎車」，後面舉例「停車位總數不變」「車太多就亮紅燈」，又說 If people find parking more difficult, they will drive less，目的都是減少車流 → to make traffic lighter。\n【其他選項】(B) 邀請人來玩，文中沒提；(C) 讓城市出名，與內容無關；(D) 文中說停車位總數不變，並沒有蓋更多。\n【例句】Our school uses many ways to keep the classrooms clean.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2094, "question": "The city closed some roads on weekends ______. Now people can walk and ride bikes there safely.", "options": ["to sell more cars", "to make the streets safer for people", "to build more parking lots", "to invite more drivers"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "後句說人們可安全步行騎車，目的是讓街道對人更安全。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2095, "question": "Mr. Lin turns off the lights when he leaves the room ______. He wants to pay less every month.", "options": ["to save money", "to make the room brighter", "to wake up early", "to visit his friends"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "後句「每月想付少一點」→ 目的是省錢。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2096, "question": "Our school started a \"No Plastic Day\" ______. On that day, students bring their own cups and bags.", "options": ["to sell more drinks", "to win a sports game", "to use less plastic", "to buy new bags"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 33 題）", "explanation": "自備杯袋 → 目的是少用塑膠。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2097, "question": "(19-21)\nIf you cannot live without your car, Zurich might be the last city you would like to visit. In Zurich, people are welcome, but cars are not! Over the past 20 years, this city has used smart ways __(19)__. One is to keep the same total number of parking spaces. For example, if 50 new parking spaces are built in one part of the city, then 50 old spaces in other parts are taken away for other uses. So the total number does not change. Some are unhappy that there are never enough spaces. That is just what the city has in mind: If people find parking more difficult, they will drive less.\n______(20), the total number of cars in the city is counted. Over 3,500 little computers are put under Zurich roads to check the number of cars that enter the city. If the number is higher than the city can deal with, the traffic lights on the roads that enter the city will be kept red. So drivers who are traveling into Zurich have to stop and wait until there are fewer cars in the city. Now, you may wonder __(21)__. The answer is simple: The city wants to make more space for its people.\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["This way", "However", "For example", "Also"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜連接詞", "explanation": "【句型】轉承語：Also（此外）表「再補充一點」；However 表轉折；For example 表舉例；This way 表「這樣一來」(結果)。\n【分析】第一段已說 One is to keep the same total number of parking spaces（第一個方法），第二段開頭介紹「計算車輛總數」是第二個方法 → Also，補充另一種做法。\n【其他選項】(A) This way 表前面做法帶來的結果，但第二段是新做法；(B) However 表相反，前後並不對立；(C) For example 用來舉例，而第二段不是第一個方法的例子。\n【例句】Eat more vegetables. Also, try to go to bed early.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2098, "question": "There are two ways to get to the zoo. One is to take the MRT. ______, you can take a bus from the train station.", "options": ["However", "Also", "For example", "This way"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "第二個方法，用 Also 補充。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2099, "question": "Kevin studied hard every day. ______, he still failed the math test.", "options": ["Also", "For example", "However", "This way"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "努力卻不及格，前後相反 → However。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2100, "question": "Many animals sleep during the day. ______, owls hunt at night and rest when the sun is up.", "options": ["For example", "However", "Also", "Besides that way"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 37 題）", "explanation": "貓頭鷹是「白天睡覺的動物」的例子 → For example。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2101, "question": "(19-21)\nIf you cannot live without your car, Zurich might be the last city you would like to visit. In Zurich, people are welcome, but cars are not! Over the past 20 years, this city has used smart ways __(19)__. One is to keep the same total number of parking spaces. For example, if 50 new parking spaces are built in one part of the city, then 50 old spaces in other parts are taken away for other uses. So the total number does not change. Some are unhappy that there are never enough spaces. That is just what the city has in mind: If people find parking more difficult, they will drive less.\n__(20)__, the total number of cars in the city is counted. Over 3,500 little computers are put under Zurich roads to check the number of cars that enter the city. If the number is higher than the city can deal with, the traffic lights on the roads that enter the city will be kept red. So drivers who are traveling into Zurich have to stop and wait until there are fewer cars in the city. Now, you may wonder ______(21). The answer is simple: The city wants to make more space for its people.\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["why Zurich is doing this", "what all this has cost Zurich", "if Zurich should try other ways", "if Zurich can deal with angry drivers"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】you may wonder + 疑問詞子句（why + S + V）；由下句 The answer is… 反推問題。\n【分析】下一句 The answer is simple: The city wants to make more space for its people. 回答的是「為什麼」，所以前面問的是 why Zurich is doing this。\n【其他選項】(B) 花了多少錢，答案沒談費用；(C) 是否該試別的方法，答案不是 yes/no；(D) 能否應付生氣的駕駛，答案沒提。\n【例句】You may wonder why the store is closed. The owner is on vacation.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2102, "question": "You may ask ______. The answer is easy: she wants to be a nurse in the future.", "options": ["where Amy lives", "why Amy studies so hard", "when Amy got up", "how old Amy is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "答案說「她想當護士」是原因 → why。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2103, "question": "People often wonder ______. Well, the trip takes about three hours by train.", "options": ["how long it takes to get to Hualien", "who Mark is traveling with", "why Mark likes trains", "what Mark bought"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "答案講「花三小時」→ how long it takes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2104, "question": "Many students want to know ______. The answer: the teacher will tell them next Monday.", "options": ["why the test is hard", "where the test is", "when they will get their test scores", "what the test is about"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 41 題）", "explanation": "答案是「下週一」→ when。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2105, "question": "(34-37)\nJerry Stevens has been unhappy these months. He ______(34) a proud businessman of a successful shaved ice shop. His highest sales numbers were 1,899 plates a week; people called him \"Ice King.\" But all this changed when the cookie shop across the street started selling ice cream cookies. It took away half of his business.\nAnd __(35)__ when Dan, his dead sister's only son, came to work for him.\nDan was a nice young man with a simple mind, too simple, maybe. He always let people try some shaved ice for free, but he never learned to see when \"some\" became \"too much.\" Many people came, but few bought. When the sales did not grow with the heat, Jerry started to worry. He wanted to send Dan home. But how could he? Dan had no family except him.\nThen, one day, __(36)__. And it was from across the street. The cookie shop __(37)__ a clerk. For Jerry, it was a great chance to get Dan out of his store without sending him home. After taking the shopkeeper to several nice dinners, Jerry got Dan the job.\nNow Jerry could finally try and save his store. And maybe Dan would help by sending him a few people who are thirsty from eating too many cookies.\n(shaved ice 刨冰)\n\n▶ 請選出第 34 格的答案", "options": ["is", "has been", "used to be", "was going to be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 34 格｜used to", "explanation": "【句型】used to + 原形V：過去曾經……（現在已不是）。\n【分析】首句 has been unhappy these months 表示他現在不開心；後面 But all this changed when the cookie shop… 說明情況已改變 → 他「過去曾是」驕傲的老闆 → used to be。\n【其他選項】(A) is 表現在仍是，與 all this changed 矛盾；(B) has been 表一直到現在都是，也矛盾；(D) was going to be 表「過去本來要成為」，但他確實已經是，且有銷售紀錄。\n【例句】This park used to be a parking lot.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2106, "question": "My grandpa ______ a bus driver, but now he stays home and grows vegetables.", "options": ["is", "has been", "used to be", "is going to be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "現在在家種菜 → 過去曾是 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2107, "question": "Tina ______ afraid of dogs. Now she has two dogs at home.", "options": ["used to be", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "現在養兩隻狗 → 以前怕狗 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2108, "question": "There ______ a big tree in front of our school, but it was cut down last year.", "options": ["is", "has been", "will be", "used to be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 45 題）", "explanation": "樹去年被砍 → 以前有 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2109, "question": "(34-37)\nJerry Stevens has been unhappy these months. He __(34)__ a proud businessman of a successful shaved ice shop. His highest sales numbers were 1,899 plates a week; people called him \"Ice King.\" But all this changed when the cookie shop across the street started selling ice cream cookies. It took away half of his business.\nAnd ______(35) when Dan, his dead sister's only son, came to work for him.\nDan was a nice young man with a simple mind, too simple, maybe. He always let people try some shaved ice for free, but he never learned to see when \"some\" became \"too much.\" Many people came, but few bought. When the sales did not grow with the heat, Jerry started to worry. He wanted to send Dan home. But how could he? Dan had no family except him.\nThen, one day, __(36)__. And it was from across the street. The cookie shop __(37)__ a clerk. For Jerry, it was a great chance to get Dan out of his store without sending him home. After taking the shopkeeper to several nice dinners, Jerry got Dan the job.\nNow Jerry could finally try and save his store. And maybe Dan would help by sending him a few people who are thirsty from eating too many cookies.\n(shaved ice 刨冰)\n\n▶ 請選出第 35 格的答案", "options": ["things didn't get better", "he was ready to give up", "the sales of shaved ice finally started to rise", "the cookie shop was not successful for long"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 35 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】克漏字文意題：選項須與前後文的情節方向一致。\n【分析】前段說生意被搶走一半，後段說 Dan 讓人免費試吃、Many people came, but few bought、Jerry started to worry → 情況「沒有變好」→ things didn't get better。\n【其他選項】(B) 他並沒有放棄，最後還 try and save his store；(C) 業績上升與 few bought 矛盾；(D) 餅乾店沒有失敗，後來還要徵店員。\n【例句】We changed the plan, but things didn't get better.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2110, "question": "Amy lost her wallet in the morning. And ______ when it started to rain and she had no umbrella.", "options": ["her day got worse", "she found her wallet", "the sun came out", "she felt very happy"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "掉錢包又淋雨 → 一天更糟。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2111, "question": "Leo practiced English every day. And ______ when he got an A on the final exam.", "options": ["he gave up", "his hard work paid off", "he forgot everything", "he felt bored"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "拿到 A → 努力有回報。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2112, "question": "The store had few customers. And ______ when a new supermarket opened next door. Soon the store closed.", "options": ["things got better", "the owner got rich", "business got even worse", "more people came"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 49 題）", "explanation": "後來關店 → 生意更糟。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2113, "question": "(34-37)\nJerry Stevens has been unhappy these months. He __(34)__ a proud businessman of a successful shaved ice shop. His highest sales numbers were 1,899 plates a week; people called him \"Ice King.\" But all this changed when the cookie shop across the street started selling ice cream cookies. It took away half of his business.\nAnd __(35)__ when Dan, his dead sister's only son, came to work for him.\nDan was a nice young man with a simple mind, too simple, maybe. He always let people try some shaved ice for free, but he never learned to see when \"some\" became \"too much.\" Many people came, but few bought. When the sales did not grow with the heat, Jerry started to worry. He wanted to send Dan home. But how could he? Dan had no family except him.\nThen, one day, ______(36). And it was from across the street. The cookie shop __(37)__ a clerk. For Jerry, it was a great chance to get Dan out of his store without sending him home. After taking the shopkeeper to several nice dinners, Jerry got Dan the job.\nNow Jerry could finally try and save his store. And maybe Dan would help by sending him a few people who are thirsty from eating too many cookies.\n(shaved ice 刨冰)\n\n▶ 請選出第 36 格的答案", "options": ["his only hope died", "good news arrived", "worse trouble came", "the hard time passed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 36 格｜綜合", "explanation": "【句型】克漏字文意題：從後文推出空格內容。\n【分析】後文 And it was from across the street. The cookie shop was looking for a clerk… it was a great chance → 從對面傳來的是「好消息」→ good news arrived。\n【其他選項】(A) 唯一的希望破滅，與 great chance 相反；(C) 更大的麻煩，同樣相反；(D) 困難時期過去，但下文說的是「一個機會」，且 it was from across the street 指的是一則消息，不是時期。\n【例句】Then, one day, good news arrived: Mom got a new job.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2114, "question": "Kevin waited for weeks. Then, one day, ______. It was a letter from the school: he got in!", "options": ["bad news came", "good news arrived", "his dog ran away", "the letter got lost"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "錄取了 → 好消息來了。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2115, "question": "Everything was going well. Then, one day, ______. The typhoon broke all the windows of the shop.", "options": ["good luck came", "a gift arrived", "trouble came", "the sun came out"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "颱風打破窗戶 → 麻煩來了。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2116, "question": "Lily felt nervous all week. Then, ______: the doctor said her mother was fine.", "options": ["the hard news came", "the good news came", "her test began", "the rain started"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 53 題）", "explanation": "醫生說媽媽沒事 → 好消息。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2117, "question": "(34-37)\nJerry Stevens has been unhappy these months. He __(34)__ a proud businessman of a successful shaved ice shop. His highest sales numbers were 1,899 plates a week; people called him \"Ice King.\" But all this changed when the cookie shop across the street started selling ice cream cookies. It took away half of his business.\nAnd __(35)__ when Dan, his dead sister's only son, came to work for him.\nDan was a nice young man with a simple mind, too simple, maybe. He always let people try some shaved ice for free, but he never learned to see when \"some\" became \"too much.\" Many people came, but few bought. When the sales did not grow with the heat, Jerry started to worry. He wanted to send Dan home. But how could he? Dan had no family except him.\nThen, one day, __(36)__. And it was from across the street. The cookie shop ______(37) a clerk. For Jerry, it was a great chance to get Dan out of his store without sending him home. After taking the shopkeeper to several nice dinners, Jerry got Dan the job.\nNow Jerry could finally try and save his store. And maybe Dan would help by sending him a few people who are thirsty from eating too many cookies.\n(shaved ice 刨冰)\n\n▶ 請選出第 37 格的答案", "options": ["used to look for", "has looked for", "was looking for", "had looked for"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 37 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去進行式 was/were + Ving：表過去某時正在進行的事。\n【分析】故事用過去式敘述（got Dan the job），當時餅乾店「正在找」店員 → was looking for；之後 Jerry 才幫 Dan 得到工作。\n【其他選項】(A) used to 表過去習慣，現已不再，不合情境；(B) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事；(D) had looked for 表更早以前找過（已結束），則不需要 Dan 了。\n【例句】When I called Anna, she was looking for her keys.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2118, "question": "When I got to the shop, the owner ______ a new cook.", "options": ["looks for", "was looking for", "has looked for", "will look for"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "過去某時正在找 → 過去進行式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2119, "question": "At eight last night, my brother ______ a movie in his room.", "options": ["watches", "has watched", "was watching", "is watching"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "last night 某時正在 → was watching。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2120, "question": "While Ben ______ for the bus, it started to rain.", "options": ["was waiting", "waits", "has waited", "will wait"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 57 題）", "explanation": "while + 過去進行式，下雨插入。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2121, "question": "(35-38)\nIt was 11 p.m. and Molly walked out of her bakery. She turned and looked at her store one last time. She wanted to remember what it ______(35) at the moment. A few hours later, people would come and clean out everything in the store. A young man had bought it. He __(36)__ it into a flower shop.\nBefore it was a bakery, this place __(37)__ a small coffee shop. Molly worked in the shop as a waitress. But taking orders was never Molly's dream; baking was. When she knew her boss planned to sell the shop, she borrowed money and bought it.\nHer bakery had been open for thirty years. Thirty very wonderful years. However, it would all come to an end tonight. Molly __(38)__ the bakery to be a family business. But her daughter was never interested in baking. Molly did not want her business in a stranger's hands, so after some serious thinking, she decided to close it.\n\"Goodbye, my dear old friend,\" Molly looked at the store, whispering.\n(whisper 低語)\n\n▶ 請選出第 35 格的答案", "options": ["had looked like", "looked like", "would look like", "has looked like"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 35 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去式敘事中，描述「當時」的狀態用過去簡單式。\n【分析】全文以過去式敘事（It was 11 p.m.… walked out），she wanted to remember what it looked like at the moment，at the moment 指當時那一刻 → looked like。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去完成式表更早以前的樣子，不是「此刻」；(C) would look like 表未來的樣子（之後會變花店）；(D) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事。\n【例句】I took a photo to remember what the old house looked like.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2122, "question": "Before we moved, I walked around my room. I wanted to remember what it ______ then.", "options": ["looked like", "has looked like", "will look like", "looks like"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事中的當時 → looked like。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2123, "question": "Grandma showed me a photo. It showed what our town ______ fifty years ago.", "options": ["looks like", "was looked like", "looked like", "will look like"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "fifty years ago → 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2124, "question": "It was dark, and I couldn't see what the man ______.", "options": ["looks like", "looked like", "has looked like", "will look like"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 61 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事 → 子句也用過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2125, "question": "(35-38)\nIt was 11 p.m. and Molly walked out of her bakery. She turned and looked at her store one last time. She wanted to remember what it __(35)__ at the moment. A few hours later, people would come and clean out everything in the store. A young man had bought it. He ______(36) it into a flower shop.\nBefore it was a bakery, this place __(37)__ a small coffee shop. Molly worked in the shop as a waitress. But taking orders was never Molly's dream; baking was. When she knew her boss planned to sell the shop, she borrowed money and bought it.\nHer bakery had been open for thirty years. Thirty very wonderful years. However, it would all come to an end tonight. Molly __(38)__ the bakery to be a family business. But her daughter was never interested in baking. Molly did not want her business in a stranger's hands, so after some serious thinking, she decided to close it.\n\"Goodbye, my dear old friend,\" Molly looked at the store, whispering.\n(whisper 低語)\n\n▶ 請選出第 36 格的答案", "options": ["had changed", "changed", "was going to change", "has changed"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 36 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】was/were going to + V：站在過去時間點說「打算／將要」做的事。\n【分析】店才剛被買下，A few hours later, people would come and clean out everything，表示改成花店是「之後才要做」的事 → was going to change。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 表已經改了，但當時店還是麵包店；(D) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事。\n【例句】Dad bought some wood. He was going to build a doghouse.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2126, "question": "Mr. Wu bought the old house last week. He ______ it into a small café, but he hasn't started yet.", "options": ["turned", "has turned", "was going to turn", "had turned"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "尚未開始，是過去打算的事 → was going to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2127, "question": "Jenny bought some flour and eggs yesterday. She ______ a cake for her mom's birthday.", "options": ["was going to make", "made", "has made", "had made"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "買材料是為了之後要做 → was going to make。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2128, "question": "I packed my bag last night because I ______ to Tainan this morning.", "options": ["went", "have gone", "was going", "had gone"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 65 題）", "explanation": "昨晚打包，為了今早要出發 → was going。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2129, "question": "(35-38)\nIt was 11 p.m. and Molly walked out of her bakery. She turned and looked at her store one last time. She wanted to remember what it __(35)__ at the moment. A few hours later, people would come and clean out everything in the store. A young man had bought it. He __(36)__ it into a flower shop.\nBefore it was a bakery, this place ______(37) a small coffee shop. Molly worked in the shop as a waitress. But taking orders was never Molly's dream; baking was. When she knew her boss planned to sell the shop, she borrowed money and bought it.\nHer bakery had been open for thirty years. Thirty very wonderful years. However, it would all come to an end tonight. Molly __(38)__ the bakery to be a family business. But her daughter was never interested in baking. Molly did not want her business in a stranger's hands, so after some serious thinking, she decided to close it.\n\"Goodbye, my dear old friend,\" Molly looked at the store, whispering.\n(whisper 低語)\n\n▶ 請選出第 37 格的答案", "options": ["used to be", "would be", "has been", "is"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 37 格｜used to", "explanation": "【句型】used to + V：過去曾經是（現在不是）。\n【分析】Before it was a bakery 指出在當麵包店之前，這地方「曾經是」咖啡店，現在已不是 → used to be。\n【其他選項】(B) would be 表過去的未來，時間反了；(C) has been 表到現在仍是；(D) is 表現在，與 Before it was a bakery 矛盾。\n【例句】This bookstore used to be a movie theater.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2130, "question": "Before it became a museum, this building ______ a train station.", "options": ["is", "used to be", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "以前是車站，現在是博物館 → used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2131, "question": "My little brother ______ shy, but now he talks to everyone.", "options": ["used to be", "is", "has been", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "現在不害羞 → 以前是 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2132, "question": "There ______ many fish in this river. Now it is too dirty.", "options": ["are", "have been", "used to be", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 69 題）", "explanation": "現在很髒沒魚 → 以前有 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2133, "question": "(35-38)\nIt was 11 p.m. and Molly walked out of her bakery. She turned and looked at her store one last time. She wanted to remember what it __(35)__ at the moment. A few hours later, people would come and clean out everything in the store. A young man had bought it. He __(36)__ it into a flower shop.\nBefore it was a bakery, this place __(37)__ a small coffee shop. Molly worked in the shop as a waitress. But taking orders was never Molly's dream; baking was. When she knew her boss planned to sell the shop, she borrowed money and bought it.\nHer bakery had been open for thirty years. Thirty very wonderful years. However, it would all come to an end tonight. Molly ______(38) the bakery to be a family business. But her daughter was never interested in baking. Molly did not want her business in a stranger's hands, so after some serious thinking, she decided to close it.\n\"Goodbye, my dear old friend,\" Molly looked at the store, whispering.\n(whisper 低語)\n\n▶ 請選出第 38 格的答案", "options": ["had wanted", "has wanted", "would want", "will want"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 38 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去完成式 had + p.p.：表比過去某時間更早就存在的狀態。\n【分析】故事在「關店的今晚」（過去），Molly 早就一直希望麵包店成為家族事業（比決定關店更早）→ had wanted；後句 But her daughter was never interested 說明願望沒實現。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事；(C) would want 表過去的未來，不合；(D) will want 是未來式。\n【例句】Ken had wanted a dog for years before he finally got one.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2134, "question": "Before she moved to Japan, Amy ______ to learn Japanese for a long time.", "options": ["has wanted", "had wanted", "wants", "will want"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "移居前早就想 → had wanted。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2135, "question": "When the store closed, Mr. Lee was sad. He ______ it for twenty years.", "options": ["has run", "runs", "had run", "will run"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "關店之前已經營二十年 → had run。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2136, "question": "By the time we got to the station, the train ______.", "options": ["had left", "has left", "leaves", "will leave"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 73 題）", "explanation": "到站前車已開走 → had left。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2137, "question": "(19-21)\nDear Sir,\nI'm sorry that I have to write this letter, but if I ______(19), you'll never see what your problem is.\nOn Saturday evening, my family and I went to your restaurant for my birthday. Many people __(20)__ in the restaurant. We were very hungry and didn't want to wait, but your waiter said we __(21)__ served in twenty minutes. We believed him, but we ended up waiting for ONE HOUR!\nI have to say the steak was delicious, but it was still wrong to keep people waiting for so long.\nJulia Wu\n(serve 服務)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["didn't", "don't", "hadn't", "haven't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜省略句（助動詞／be動詞）", "explanation": "【句型】If + 現在式, S + will + V（條件句）；助動詞後可省略重複的動詞：if I don't (write this letter)。\n【分析】主要子句 you'll never see 是未來式，if 子句用現在式代替未來 → if I don't（= don't write this letter），省略前面出現過的 write this letter。\n【其他選項】(A) didn't 過去式，與 you'll 不搭（若是假設語氣應為 would）；(C) hadn't 是過去完成式；(D) haven't 須接 p.p.（written），且不合條件句。\n【例句】Take an umbrella. If you don't, you'll get wet.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2138, "question": "Finish your homework now. If you ______, you won't be able to watch TV tonight.", "options": ["didn't", "don't", "haven't", "won't"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "if 子句現在式代替未來，省略 finish your homework。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2139, "question": "I'll call Grandma tonight. If I ______, she will worry about me.", "options": ["don't", "didn't", "won't", "haven't"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "條件句 if 子句用現在式 don't。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2140, "question": "You should ask the teacher. If you ______, you will never know the answer.", "options": ["didn't", "haven't", "don't", "won't"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 77 題）", "explanation": "if + 現在式 + 省略原動詞 ask。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2141, "question": "(19-21)\nDear Sir,\nI'm sorry that I have to write this letter, but if I __(19)__, you'll never see what your problem is.\nOn Saturday evening, my family and I went to your restaurant for my birthday. Many people ______(20) in the restaurant. We were very hungry and didn't want to wait, but your waiter said we __(21)__ served in twenty minutes. We believed him, but we ended up waiting for ONE HOUR!\nI have to say the steak was delicious, but it was still wrong to keep people waiting for so long.\nJulia Wu\n(serve 服務)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["were already", "are already", "have already been", "will already be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】描述過去某時的狀態用過去式；already 放 be 動詞後。\n【分析】On Saturday evening… went（過去），當時餐廳裡已經有很多人 → were already。\n【其他選項】(B) are 是現在式；(C) 現在完成式不和過去時間 On Saturday evening 連用；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】When we got to the beach, many people were already there.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2142, "question": "When I got to the classroom, most of my classmates ______ there.", "options": ["are already", "were already", "have already been", "will already be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "過去某時已在 → were already。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2143, "question": "Last night when Dad came home, we ______ asleep.", "options": ["were already", "are already", "have already been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "last night → 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2144, "question": "At the concert yesterday, the seats ______ full when we arrived.", "options": ["are", "will be", "were already", "have been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 81 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → were already。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2145, "question": "(19-21)\nDear Sir,\nI'm sorry that I have to write this letter, but if I __(19)__, you'll never see what your problem is.\nOn Saturday evening, my family and I went to your restaurant for my birthday. Many people __(20)__ in the restaurant. We were very hungry and didn't want to wait, but your waiter said we ______(21) served in twenty minutes. We believed him, but we ended up waiting for ONE HOUR!\nI have to say the steak was delicious, but it was still wrong to keep people waiting for so long.\nJulia Wu\n(serve 服務)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["were", "would be", "have been", "are going to be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜主動與被動語態", "explanation": "【句型】過去時間的間接引述：said (that) S + would + V（過去的未來）；被動：would be + p.p.。\n【分析】服務生當時說「我們二十分鐘內會被服務」，是過去說的「未來」→ would be served（被動，因為我們是被服務的人）。\n【其他選項】(A) were served 表已經被服務了，與後面等了一小時矛盾；(C) have been 現在完成式不合過去敘事；(D) are going to be 是現在角度的未來，主要動詞 said 是過去式，應改為 would。\n【例句】The teacher said the tests would be returned on Friday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2146, "question": "The man at the counter said our pizza ______ ready in ten minutes.", "options": ["is", "has been", "would be", "was being"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "said 之後表過去的未來 → would be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2147, "question": "Mom told me the package ______ sent the next day.", "options": ["would be", "is", "has been", "was"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "過去的未來＋被動 → would be sent。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2148, "question": "The news said the road ______ closed until Sunday.", "options": ["will be", "would be", "has been", "is"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 85 題）", "explanation": "主句 said 過去式 → would be closed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2149, "question": "(57-60) Reader's Story\nIt's never comfortable to take a bus during rush hour on a hot summer day. All my friends hate it. And I..., well, I ______(57) it too.\nThe story happened two months ago. I was on a bus that was packed with almost everyone in the city. I __(58)__ my friend Neal to see a show. And then he called and said he couldn't come. \"This is not what I planned for Friday!\" I thought. The air on the bus was terrible; the man in front of me smelled like dead fish. While I was feeling sorry for myself, a girl called my name. I didn't recognize her at first. Then I was surprised to find that she was Hui-ting, my old neighbor. I __(59)__ Hui-ting in years. We used to play together every day when we were kids. We were happy to see each other, so we decided to have dinner together. And that was the start of many dinners after.\nWith Hui-ting, the bus ride __(60)__ something I love. The bus is still packed with people, but I enjoy the ride every day.\n(Xiang Chang, Taipei)\n(rush hour 尖峰時間　recognize 認出)\n\n▶ 請選出第 57 格的答案", "options": ["hate", "have hated", "used to hate", "would hate"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 57 格｜used to", "explanation": "【句型】used to + 原形V：過去曾經……，現在已不是。\n【分析】「And I…, well, I」的猶豫語氣，加上文末 the bus ride has become something I love，表示作者「以前」也討厭，現在不了 → used to hate。\n【其他選項】(A) hate 表現在仍討厭，與結尾矛盾；(B) have hated 表一直討厭到現在，也矛盾；(D) would hate 表假設或過去的未來，不合。\n【例句】I used to hate vegetables, but now I eat them every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2150, "question": "Jack ______ swimming, but after his summer class he loves it.", "options": ["used to hate", "hates", "has hated", "will hate"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "現在喜歡 → 以前討厭 used to hate。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2151, "question": "Mia ______ late for school, but now she always arrives early.", "options": ["is", "has been", "used to be", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "現在準時 → 以前常遲到 used to be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2152, "question": "My dad ______ coffee every morning. Now he only drinks tea.", "options": ["drinks", "used to drink", "has drunk", "is drinking"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 89 題）", "explanation": "現在只喝茶 → 以前喝咖啡。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2153, "question": "(57-60) Reader's Story\nIt's never comfortable to take a bus during rush hour on a hot summer day. All my friends hate it. And I..., well, I __(57)__ it too.\nThe story happened two months ago. I was on a bus that was packed with almost everyone in the city. I ______(58) my friend Neal to see a show. And then he called and said he couldn't come. \"This is not what I planned for Friday!\" I thought. The air on the bus was terrible; the man in front of me smelled like dead fish. While I was feeling sorry for myself, a girl called my name. I didn't recognize her at first. Then I was surprised to find that she was Hui-ting, my old neighbor. I __(59)__ Hui-ting in years. We used to play together every day when we were kids. We were happy to see each other, so we decided to have dinner together. And that was the start of many dinners after.\nWith Hui-ting, the bus ride __(60)__ something I love. The bus is still packed with people, but I enjoy the ride every day.\n(Xiang Chang, Taipei)\n(rush hour 尖峰時間　recognize 認出)\n\n▶ 請選出第 58 格的答案", "options": ["used to meet", "was going to meet", "have met", "had met"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 58 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】was/were going to + V：過去原本打算……（常暗示沒有實現）。\n【分析】作者在公車上，「本來要」去見 Neal 看表演，And then he called and said he couldn't come，計畫沒實現 → was going to meet。\n【其他選項】(A) used to meet 表過去習慣，不合單次計畫；(C) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事；(D) had met 表已經見過了，但後來對方說不能來，並沒見到。\n【例句】I was going to call you, but my phone died.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2154, "question": "We ______ a picnic last Sunday, but it rained all day.", "options": ["had", "were going to have", "have had", "used to have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "原本計畫但下雨沒辦 → were going to have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2155, "question": "Sam ______ his grandparents yesterday, but his car broke down.", "options": ["was going to visit", "visited", "has visited", "visits"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "本來要拜訪但車壞了。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2156, "question": "I ______ you a birthday card, but I forgot.", "options": ["sent", "have sent", "was going to send", "send"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 93 題）", "explanation": "本來要寄但忘了 → was going to send。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2157, "question": "(57-60) Reader's Story\nIt's never comfortable to take a bus during rush hour on a hot summer day. All my friends hate it. And I..., well, I __(57)__ it too.\nThe story happened two months ago. I was on a bus that was packed with almost everyone in the city. I __(58)__ my friend Neal to see a show. And then he called and said he couldn't come. \"This is not what I planned for Friday!\" I thought. The air on the bus was terrible; the man in front of me smelled like dead fish. While I was feeling sorry for myself, a girl called my name. I didn't recognize her at first. Then I was surprised to find that she was Hui-ting, my old neighbor. I ______(59) Hui-ting in years. We used to play together every day when we were kids. We were happy to see each other, so we decided to have dinner together. And that was the start of many dinners after.\nWith Hui-ting, the bus ride __(60)__ something I love. The bus is still packed with people, but I enjoy the ride every day.\n(Xiang Chang, Taipei)\n(rush hour 尖峰時間　recognize 認出)\n\n▶ 請選出第 59 格的答案", "options": ["won't see", "wouldn't see", "haven't seen", "hadn't seen"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 59 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去完成式 had (not) + p.p.：到過去某時為止已經（沒有）……；常和 in years / for + 時間 連用。\n【分析】重逢發生在兩個月前（過去），到那時為止「已經好幾年沒見到」Hui-ting → hadn't seen … in years。\n【其他選項】(A)(B) 表未來，不合；(C) haven't seen 以「現在」為基準，但重逢是過去的事，且他們現在每天見面。\n【例句】When I met Tom at the station, I hadn't seen him in five years.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2158, "question": "Grace was so happy at the party. She ______ her cousins in three years.", "options": ["hasn't seen", "hadn't seen", "won't see", "doesn't see"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "過去的派對之前多年未見 → hadn't seen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2159, "question": "When I opened the box last week, I found a toy I ______ for a long time.", "options": ["hadn't played with", "haven't played with", "won't play with", "don't play with"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "過去某時之前一直沒玩 → 過去完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2160, "question": "Ray ______ his old teacher for ten years, so he didn't recognize her yesterday.", "options": ["hasn't seen", "won't see", "hadn't seen", "didn't see"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 97 題）", "explanation": "昨天之前十年沒見 → hadn't seen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2161, "question": "(57-60) Reader's Story\nIt's never comfortable to take a bus during rush hour on a hot summer day. All my friends hate it. And I..., well, I __(57)__ it too.\nThe story happened two months ago. I was on a bus that was packed with almost everyone in the city. I __(58)__ my friend Neal to see a show. And then he called and said he couldn't come. \"This is not what I planned for Friday!\" I thought. The air on the bus was terrible; the man in front of me smelled like dead fish. While I was feeling sorry for myself, a girl called my name. I didn't recognize her at first. Then I was surprised to find that she was Hui-ting, my old neighbor. I __(59)__ Hui-ting in years. We used to play together every day when we were kids. We were happy to see each other, so we decided to have dinner together. And that was the start of many dinners after.\nWith Hui-ting, the bus ride ______(60) something I love. The bus is still packed with people, but I enjoy the ride every day.\n(Xiang Chang, Taipei)\n(rush hour 尖峰時間　recognize 認出)\n\n▶ 請選出第 60 格的答案", "options": ["has become", "had become", "will become", "would become"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 60 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 have/has + p.p.：過去開始的變化，結果延續到現在。\n【分析】後句 The bus is still packed… but I enjoy the ride every day（現在式），表示公車之旅「已經變成」作者現在所愛 → has become。\n【其他選項】(B) had become 以過去為基準，不合「現在」；(C) will become 表還沒發生，但他現在已每天享受；(D) would become 表假設或過去的未來。\n【例句】Since I joined the team, basketball has become my favorite sport.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2162, "question": "Since Lisa moved to Tainan, the city ______ her second home.", "options": ["became", "has become", "will become", "had become"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "到現在已成為 → 現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2163, "question": "Thanks to his new friends, school ______ much more fun for Eric. He loves going there now.", "options": ["has become", "had become", "will become", "would become"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "now → 結果延續到現在。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2164, "question": "Over the years, this small shop ______ very famous. Now people wait in line every day.", "options": ["becomes", "will become", "has become", "would become"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 101 題）", "explanation": "over the years 到現在 → has become。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2165, "question": "(57-60) Sports News\nMaria Sharapova is a world-famous tennis player. She was born in Russia in 1987. At the age of four, she started her first tennis lesson. From then on, she ______(57) that she's one of the best tennis players ever. Tennis fans all over the world enjoy watching her play.\nAlthough her family had little money, Sharapova moved to America with her father in 1994. Soon after they arrived, Sharapova's father brought her to a famous tennis school in Florida. Back in Russia, her father __(58)__ a great future ahead of little Sharapova. He wanted to do his best to help her, and an American tennis school would be a good start. Now the seven-year-old girl __(59)__ at the school and would start to make her dream come true.\nThe little girl surprised the teachers when she knocked off the hat of one teacher with a strong serve. They told her father that she __(60)__ a scholarship when she was old enough to enter the school in 1995.\nThat is where it all began. Sharapova has since caught the eye of the world with her excellent tennis skills.\n(serve 發球　scholarship 獎學金　skill 技巧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 57 格的答案", "options": ["has shown", "had shown", "showed", "will show"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 57 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】from then on / since then + 現在完成式：從過去某時起一直到現在。\n【分析】From then on（從四歲起）一直到現在，她「已經展現出」自己是最好的選手之一，後句 Tennis fans… enjoy（現在式）也顯示延續至今 → has shown。\n【其他選項】(B) had shown 以過去為基準，不合；(C) showed 只講過去，無法表示延續到現在；(D) will show 表未來，但她已是世界知名選手。\n【例句】Tim joined the club in 2020. From then on, he has made many friends.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2166, "question": "Amy started playing piano at five. Since then, she ______ in many concerts.", "options": ["played", "has played", "had played", "will play"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "since then → 現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2167, "question": "Our school built a new library last year. From then on, more students ______ books there.", "options": ["have read", "had read", "read", "will read"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "from then on 到現在 → 現在完成式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2168, "question": "Ken moved to Taichung in 2019. He ______ there since then.", "options": ["lived", "lives", "has lived", "will live"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 105 題）", "explanation": "since then → has lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2169, "question": "(57-60) Sports News\nMaria Sharapova is a world-famous tennis player. She was born in Russia in 1987. At the age of four, she started her first tennis lesson. From then on, she __(57)__ that she's one of the best tennis players ever. Tennis fans all over the world enjoy watching her play.\nAlthough her family had little money, Sharapova moved to America with her father in 1994. Soon after they arrived, Sharapova's father brought her to a famous tennis school in Florida. Back in Russia, her father ______(58) a great future ahead of little Sharapova. He wanted to do his best to help her, and an American tennis school would be a good start. Now the seven-year-old girl __(59)__ at the school and would start to make her dream come true.\nThe little girl surprised the teachers when she knocked off the hat of one teacher with a strong serve. They told her father that she __(60)__ a scholarship when she was old enough to enter the school in 1995.\nThat is where it all began. Sharapova has since caught the eye of the world with her excellent tennis skills.\n(serve 發球　scholarship 獎學金　skill 技巧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 58 格的答案", "options": ["has seen", "had seen", "sees", "would see"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 58 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去完成式 had + p.p.：比另一個過去動作更早發生。\n【分析】Back in Russia（還在俄國時），比 1994 年搬到美國更早，父親「早已看到」女兒的大好前途 → had seen。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式不用於過去敘事；(C) sees 現在式不合；(D) would see 表過去的未來，但「看出潛力」發生在搬家前。\n【例句】Before they moved to Taipei, the Chens had lived in Kaohsiung for ten years.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2170, "question": "Back in elementary school, Jay ______ that he wanted to be a chef.", "options": ["has decided", "decides", "had decided", "will decide"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "比後來的過去事件更早 → had decided。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2171, "question": "When I got to the theater, the movie ______.", "options": ["had started", "has started", "starts", "will start"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "我到之前電影已開始 → had started。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2172, "question": "Linda wasn't hungry at the party because she ______ dinner at home.", "options": ["has eaten", "had eaten", "eats", "would eat"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 109 題）", "explanation": "派對前已吃過 → had eaten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2173, "question": "(57-60) Sports News\nMaria Sharapova is a world-famous tennis player. She was born in Russia in 1987. At the age of four, she started her first tennis lesson. From then on, she __(57)__ that she's one of the best tennis players ever. Tennis fans all over the world enjoy watching her play.\nAlthough her family had little money, Sharapova moved to America with her father in 1994. Soon after they arrived, Sharapova's father brought her to a famous tennis school in Florida. Back in Russia, her father __(58)__ a great future ahead of little Sharapova. He wanted to do his best to help her, and an American tennis school would be a good start. Now the seven-year-old girl ______(59) at the school and would start to make her dream come true.\nThe little girl surprised the teachers when she knocked off the hat of one teacher with a strong serve. They told her father that she __(60)__ a scholarship when she was old enough to enter the school in 1995.\nThat is where it all began. Sharapova has since caught the eye of the world with her excellent tennis skills.\n(serve 發球　scholarship 獎學金　skill 技巧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 59 格的答案", "options": ["has been", "had been", "was", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 59 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事裡的 Now 指「故事當時」，仍用過去式。\n【分析】後半句 and would start to make her dream come true 用 would（過去的未來），可知敘事時間在過去；Now 指當時（1994 年）她「在」那所學校 → was。\n【其他選項】(A) has been 以現在為基準；(B) had been 表更早以前已在那裡，不合剛到學校的時間點；(D) will be 是現在角度的未來，與 would 不一致。\n【例句】It was 1990. Now my mother was in high school and would soon meet my father.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2174, "question": "In 2010, Mr. Lin moved to Tainan. Now he ______ a teacher there and would work there for ten years.", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事中的 Now → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2175, "question": "After a long trip, the family finally arrived in the new town. Now they ______ ready to start a new life.", "options": ["are", "have been", "were", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "故事為過去 → were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2176, "question": "The tired boy got home at last. Now he ______ safe and could finally rest.", "options": ["was", "is", "has been", "had been"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 113 題）", "explanation": "與 could 一致 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2177, "question": "(57-60) Sports News\nMaria Sharapova is a world-famous tennis player. She was born in Russia in 1987. At the age of four, she started her first tennis lesson. From then on, she __(57)__ that she's one of the best tennis players ever. Tennis fans all over the world enjoy watching her play.\nAlthough her family had little money, Sharapova moved to America with her father in 1994. Soon after they arrived, Sharapova's father brought her to a famous tennis school in Florida. Back in Russia, her father __(58)__ a great future ahead of little Sharapova. He wanted to do his best to help her, and an American tennis school would be a good start. Now the seven-year-old girl __(59)__ at the school and would start to make her dream come true.\nThe little girl surprised the teachers when she knocked off the hat of one teacher with a strong serve. They told her father that she ______(60) a scholarship when she was old enough to enter the school in 1995.\nThat is where it all began. Sharapova has since caught the eye of the world with her excellent tennis skills.\n(serve 發球　scholarship 獎學金　skill 技巧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 60 格的答案", "options": ["has got", "had got", "got", "would get"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 60 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】told/said (that) S + would + V：過去說的「未來」。\n【分析】老師們（過去）告訴她父親，她「將會得到」獎學金 when she was old enough to enter the school in 1995 → 從 1994 看 1995 是未來 → would get。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式不合；(B)(C) 表已經得到，但要等到 1995 年才入學。\n【例句】The coach told us we would get new uniforms next month.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2178, "question": "Mom said she ______ me a bike when I turned twelve.", "options": ["bought", "would buy", "has bought", "buys"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "過去說的未來 → would buy。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2179, "question": "The teacher told us that we ______ a test the next day.", "options": ["would have", "had", "have had", "have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "told + the next day → would have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2180, "question": "Tom promised that he ______ back by six.", "options": ["has come", "came", "would come", "comes"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 117 題）", "explanation": "promised 過去式＋未來 → would come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2181, "question": "(21-23)\nDear Jean,\nHow have you been? I'm writing this to say I'm sorry that ______(21) your birthday. These days I felt there was something wrong, but I just couldn't think of what it was. Yesterday afternoon on the bus, I __(22)__ remembered what it was. Your birthday is this month, and it was two weeks ago! I feel so bad. I picked out a gift for you. I hope you like it.\nBy the way, __(23)__ a great time on your birthday? I can't wait to hear about it.\nLove,\nLinda\n(by the way 順便一提)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["I forget", "I forgot", "I'm forgetting", "I've forgotten"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】說明過去發生的事用過去式；I'm sorry that + S + 過去式。\n【分析】生日 was two weeks ago，而且作者昨天已經 remembered，所以「忘記」是過去的事 → I forgot。\n【其他選項】(A) forget 現在式表現在仍忘記，不合；(C) 進行式不合；(D) I've forgotten 表到現在仍忘記，但她已想起來了。\n【例句】I'm sorry that I forgot to call you last night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2182, "question": "I'm sorry that I ______ your book at home yesterday.", "options": ["leave", "left", "am leaving", "will leave"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2183, "question": "Ben ______ his homework at home this morning, so the teacher was not happy.", "options": ["forgets", "forgot", "is forgetting", "will forget"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "this morning 已過去 → forgot。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2184, "question": "Ann said sorry because she ______ to bring my umbrella back last week.", "options": ["forgets", "has forgotten", "forgot", "will forget"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 121 題）", "explanation": "last week → forgot。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2185, "question": "(21-23)\nDear Jean,\nHow have you been? I'm writing this to say I'm sorry that __(21)__ your birthday. These days I felt there was something wrong, but I just couldn't think of what it was. Yesterday afternoon on the bus, I ______(22) remembered what it was. Your birthday is this month, and it was two weeks ago! I feel so bad. I picked out a gift for you. I hope you like it.\nBy the way, __(23)__ a great time on your birthday? I can't wait to hear about it.\nLove,\nLinda\n(by the way 順便一提)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["also", "finally", "only", "still"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜詞彙題", "explanation": "【句型】finally + V：經過一段時間後「終於」。\n【分析】前句 These days I felt there was something wrong, but I just couldn't think of what it was（一直想不起來），昨天在公車上「終於」想起來 → finally。\n【其他選項】(A) also 也，前面沒有可呼應的事；(C) only 只有，語意不通；(D) still 仍然，與「想起來了」不搭。\n【例句】After waiting for an hour, we finally saw the bus.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2186, "question": "Joe looked for his keys all morning, and he ______ found them under the sofa.", "options": ["also", "still", "finally", "only"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "找了一早上，終於找到。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2187, "question": "It's ten o'clock, but Amy is ______ sleeping. She is going to be late.", "options": ["finally", "still", "also", "only"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "十點了「仍然」在睡 → still。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2188, "question": "My brother likes dogs. I ______ like dogs, so we want to get one.", "options": ["also", "finally", "still", "only"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 125 題）", "explanation": "我也喜歡 → also。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2189, "question": "(21-23)\nDear Jean,\nHow have you been? I'm writing this to say I'm sorry that __(21)__ your birthday. These days I felt there was something wrong, but I just couldn't think of what it was. Yesterday afternoon on the bus, I __(22)__ remembered what it was. Your birthday is this month, and it was two weeks ago! I feel so bad. I picked out a gift for you. I hope you like it.\nBy the way, ______(23) a great time on your birthday? I can't wait to hear about it.\nLove,\nLinda\n(by the way 順便一提)\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["have you had", "are you having", "would you have", "did you have"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】問過去發生的事：Did + S + 原形V…?\n【分析】生日 was two weeks ago，已經過去，詢問當時是否玩得愉快 → did you have a great time。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式不和特定過去事件（on your birthday，兩週前）連用；(B) 進行式表正在；(C) would 表假設或意願，不合。\n【例句】Did you have a good time at the party last night?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2190, "question": "______ a nice trip to Kenting last weekend?", "options": ["Do you have", "Did you have", "Will you have", "Are you having"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "last weekend → Did you have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2191, "question": "Your test was yesterday. ______ well?", "options": ["Did you do", "Do you do", "Will you do", "Have you do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → Did you do。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2192, "question": "How ______ your summer vacation? Tell me about it.", "options": ["is", "will be", "was", "are"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 129 題）", "explanation": "暑假已過 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2193, "question": "(21-24)\nMy mother likes to tell me the story about my name, Stella. She ______(21) about it many times.\nI was born on a night full of stars. My mom __(22)__ a hard time when the doctor said I was too big to be pulled out. At that moment, Mom looked into the sky, making a wish with all her heart, \"Let the baby live, please, even if I may die!\"\nJust then, a very bright star __(23)__ from the sky. All her troubles were soon gone, and my little head came out of her body.\nWith the falling of a star came a new life. That's how I __(24)__ the name \"Stella,\" which means \"star.\"\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["talked", "is talking", "has talked", "will talk"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 have/has + p.p. + 次數（many times / twice）：到目前為止的經驗。\n【分析】前句 My mother likes to tell me…（現在式），到現在為止她「已經講了很多次」→ has talked … many times。\n【其他選項】(A) talked 只表過去，無法表示到現在的累積經驗；(B) 進行式不和 many times 連用；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】I have watched this movie three times.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2194, "question": "Grandpa loves this story. He ______ it to us many times.", "options": ["told", "has told", "is telling", "will tell"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "到現在講了很多次 → has told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2195, "question": "Mrs. Wang ______ to Japan five times. She really loves it there.", "options": ["has been", "went", "is going", "will go"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "經驗次數 → has been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2196, "question": "I ______ this song so many times that I can sing it by heart.", "options": ["hear", "will hear", "have heard", "am hearing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 133 題）", "explanation": "累積次數 → have heard。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2197, "question": "(21-24)\nMy mother likes to tell me the story about my name, Stella. She __(21)__ about it many times.\nI was born on a night full of stars. My mom ______(22) a hard time when the doctor said I was too big to be pulled out. At that moment, Mom looked into the sky, making a wish with all her heart, \"Let the baby live, please, even if I may die!\"\nJust then, a very bright star __(23)__ from the sky. All her troubles were soon gone, and my little head came out of her body.\nWith the falling of a star came a new life. That's how I __(24)__ the name \"Stella,\" which means \"star.\"\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["was having", "has", "has had", "will have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去進行式 was/were + Ving + when + 過去式：某事正在進行時，另一事發生。\n【分析】作者出生是過去的事；醫生說話（said）那時，媽媽「正在經歷」難產的辛苦 → was having a hard time。\n【其他選項】(B) has 現在式、(C) 現在完成式、(D) 未來式都與過去敘事 I was born / said 不合。\n【例句】I was having dinner when the phone rang.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2198, "question": "We ______ a hard time finding the hotel when a kind man helped us.", "options": ["have", "were having", "have had", "will have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "when 子句過去式，主句正在進行 → were having。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2199, "question": "Tina ______ a shower when the lights went out.", "options": ["was taking", "takes", "has taken", "will take"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "停電時正在洗澡。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2200, "question": "When the teacher came in, the students ______ loudly.", "options": ["talk", "have talked", "were talking", "will talk"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 137 題）", "explanation": "老師進來時正在講話。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2201, "question": "(21-24)\nMy mother likes to tell me the story about my name, Stella. She __(21)__ about it many times.\nI was born on a night full of stars. My mom __(22)__ a hard time when the doctor said I was too big to be pulled out. At that moment, Mom looked into the sky, making a wish with all her heart, \"Let the baby live, please, even if I may die!\"\nJust then, a very bright star ______(23) from the sky. All her troubles were soon gone, and my little head came out of her body.\nWith the falling of a star came a new life. That's how I __(24)__ the name \"Stella,\" which means \"star.\"\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["would fall", "fell", "falls", "is falling"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】Just then（就在那時）+ 過去簡單式，描述過去發生的一個動作。\n【分析】故事以過去式敘述（looked, came out），一顆星「就在那時落下」→ fell（fall 的過去式）。\n【其他選項】(A) would fall 表過去的未來或假設；(C)(D) 現在式／現在進行式與過去敘事不一致。\n【例句】Just then, a cat jumped out of the box.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2202, "question": "I was about to leave. Just then, my phone ______.", "options": ["rings", "rang", "is ringing", "would ring"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "Just then + 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2203, "question": "We were walking home. Suddenly, a big dog ______ toward us.", "options": ["runs", "is running", "ran", "will run"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事中突然發生 → ran。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2204, "question": "At that moment, the door ______ open and Dad walked in.", "options": ["opened", "opens", "has opened", "will open"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 141 題）", "explanation": "與 walked 一致 → opened。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2205, "question": "(21-24)\nMy mother likes to tell me the story about my name, Stella. She __(21)__ about it many times.\nI was born on a night full of stars. My mom __(22)__ a hard time when the doctor said I was too big to be pulled out. At that moment, Mom looked into the sky, making a wish with all her heart, \"Let the baby live, please, even if I may die!\"\nJust then, a very bright star __(23)__ from the sky. All her troubles were soon gone, and my little head came out of her body.\nWith the falling of a star came a new life. That's how I ______(24) the name \"Stella,\" which means \"star.\"\n\n▶ 請選出第 24 格的答案", "options": ["got", "get", "am getting", "will get"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 24 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】That's how + S + 過去式：說明過去某事「就是這樣」發生的。\n【分析】名字是出生時取得的（過去），That's how I got the name \"Stella\"。\n【其他選項】(B) get 現在式、(C) 現在進行式、(D) 未來式，都不符合「出生時已得到名字」。\n【例句】That's how I met my best friend.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2206, "question": "I fell off my bike when I was six. That's how I ______ this scar.", "options": ["get", "got", "am getting", "will get"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "過去得到 → got。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2207, "question": "We sat next to each other on the first day of school. That's how we ______ friends.", "options": ["become", "will become", "are becoming", "became"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "過去成為朋友 → became。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2208, "question": "My uncle worked in Japan for ten years. That's how he ______ Japanese.", "options": ["learned", "learns", "is learning", "will learn"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 145 題）", "explanation": "過去學會 → learned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2209, "question": "(21-24)\nLong long time ago, a girl named Doris lost her ring. She felt so bad that she could not sleep well. When Doris turned over in her bed, she found the black horse in the picture on the wall ______(21). She was very surprised, so she got out of bed to have a closer look. When Doris touched the head of the horse, she __(22)__ into the picture!\nNow Doris was sitting on the back of the running horse! It was so exciting to be riding a horse in the beautiful sky, but Doris did not know where the horse __(23)__ her. Finally, they stopped in front of an old church. There Doris found a gift bag. She opened the bag and saw her ring inside. Doris was very happy. When she put on the ring, she woke up from her dream. At that moment, Doris could not believe her eyes – the ring __(24)__ there back on her finger!\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["is moving", "has moved", "was moving", "will move"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中描述「當時正在進行」的動作用過去進行式。\n【分析】她 turned over 時發現（found）畫裡的馬「正在動」，所以她才 very surprised → was moving。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在進行式與過去敘事不一致；(B) 現在完成式不合；(D) will move 表未來，不能解釋她當下的驚訝。\n【例句】When I looked out, I saw that the leaves were moving in the wind.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2210, "question": "When I opened the door, I found that my cat ______ on my bed.", "options": ["is sleeping", "was sleeping", "has slept", "will sleep"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "過去某時正在睡 → was sleeping。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2211, "question": "Mike looked up and saw that the plane ______ over the mountain.", "options": ["was flying", "flies", "has flown", "will fly"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "當時正在飛。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2212, "question": "When we got home, we heard that the baby ______.", "options": ["cries", "has cried", "was crying", "will cry"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 149 題）", "explanation": "當時正在哭 → was crying。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2213, "question": "(21-24)\nLong long time ago, a girl named Doris lost her ring. She felt so bad that she could not sleep well. When Doris turned over in her bed, she found the black horse in the picture on the wall __(21)__. She was very surprised, so she got out of bed to have a closer look. When Doris touched the head of the horse, she ______(22) into the picture!\nNow Doris was sitting on the back of the running horse! It was so exciting to be riding a horse in the beautiful sky, but Doris did not know where the horse __(23)__ her. Finally, they stopped in front of an old church. There Doris found a gift bag. She opened the bag and saw her ring inside. Doris was very happy. When she put on the ring, she woke up from her dream. At that moment, Doris could not believe her eyes – the ring __(24)__ there back on her finger!\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["is pulled", "was pulled", "has been pulled", "would be pulled"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜主動與被動語態", "explanation": "【句型】被動語態 be + p.p.；過去式被動 was/were + p.p.。\n【分析】Doris 是「被拉進」畫中（她不是自己拉），且故事為過去 → was pulled into the picture。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式被動與過去敘事不合；(C) 現在完成式被動不合；(D) would be pulled 表過去的未來或假設，但事情當下就發生了。\n【例句】The boy was pulled out of the water by his father.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2214, "question": "The little dog fell into the river, but it ______ out by a kind man.", "options": ["pulls", "was pulled", "is pulled", "has pulled"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "被拉出來，過去 → was pulled。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2215, "question": "My bike ______ last night, so I walked to school today.", "options": ["was stolen", "stole", "is stolen", "steals"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "腳踏車被偷，過去被動。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2216, "question": "These photos ______ by my uncle during his trip to Japan last year.", "options": ["take", "took", "were taken", "are taking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 153 題）", "explanation": "照片被拍，過去被動 → were taken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2217, "question": "(21-24)\nLong long time ago, a girl named Doris lost her ring. She felt so bad that she could not sleep well. When Doris turned over in her bed, she found the black horse in the picture on the wall __(21)__. She was very surprised, so she got out of bed to have a closer look. When Doris touched the head of the horse, she __(22)__ into the picture!\nNow Doris was sitting on the back of the running horse! It was so exciting to be riding a horse in the beautiful sky, but Doris did not know where the horse ______(23) her. Finally, they stopped in front of an old church. There Doris found a gift bag. She opened the bag and saw her ring inside. Doris was very happy. When she put on the ring, she woke up from her dream. At that moment, Doris could not believe her eyes – the ring __(24)__ there back on her finger!\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["took", "is taking", "has taken", "would take"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中提到「接下來會發生」的事，用 would + V（過去的未來）。\n【分析】騎馬當下 Doris 不知道馬「將會」帶她去哪裡（之後才停在教堂前）→ where the horse would take her。\n【其他選項】(A) took 表已帶到某地，但當時還在飛；(B) 現在進行式時態不一致；(C) 現在完成式不合。\n【例句】We didn't know what would happen next.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2218, "question": "On the first day of school, Ben didn't know who ______ his new teacher.", "options": ["is", "would be", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "過去不知道未來的事 → would be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2219, "question": "When we got on the boat, we had no idea where it ______ us.", "options": ["would take", "takes", "has taken", "took"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "過去的未來 → would take。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2220, "question": "Amy wasn't sure if her mom ______ her go to the party.", "options": ["lets", "has let", "would let", "let"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 157 題）", "explanation": "過去不確定未來 → would let。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2221, "question": "(21-24)\nLong long time ago, a girl named Doris lost her ring. She felt so bad that she could not sleep well. When Doris turned over in her bed, she found the black horse in the picture on the wall __(21)__. She was very surprised, so she got out of bed to have a closer look. When Doris touched the head of the horse, she __(22)__ into the picture!\nNow Doris was sitting on the back of the running horse! It was so exciting to be riding a horse in the beautiful sky, but Doris did not know where the horse __(23)__ her. Finally, they stopped in front of an old church. There Doris found a gift bag. She opened the bag and saw her ring inside. Doris was very happy. When she put on the ring, she woke up from her dream. At that moment, Doris could not believe her eyes – the ring ______(24) there back on her finger!\n\n▶ 請選出第 24 格的答案", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "would be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 24 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中描述當時的狀態用過去式。\n【分析】At that moment, Doris could not believe her eyes（過去）——戒指「當時」就在她手指上 → was。\n【其他選項】(A) is 現在式、(C) 現在完成式與過去敘事不合；(D) would be 表過去的未來，但戒指已經在那裡了。\n【例句】When I woke up, my phone was still in my hand.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2222, "question": "When I got home, my keys ______ on the table.", "options": ["are", "were", "have been", "would be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事 → were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2223, "question": "Kevin opened the box. A little puppy ______ inside!", "options": ["was", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2224, "question": "When the sun came up, the snow ______ still on the ground.", "options": ["is", "will be", "was", "has been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 161 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2225, "question": "(21-23)\nMonica ______(21) the thin old man who lives next to her must be very poor and lonely. She often saw him wearing old clothes and sitting in the park by himself.\nLast Christmas, when Monica was jogging in the park, the old man came up to her with a large bag on his shoulder. Monica guessed the old man __(22)__ her for some money or help. But she was surprised to find many children following him. The old man took out a box from his bag and said to her with a big smile, \"Merry Christmas! I bought presents for everybody. This one is for you.\" At that moment, Monica understood her mistake and changed her idea about the old man. Since then, she __(23)__ not to judge people by how they look. She now knows how people look is not the same as what they really are.\n(judge 判斷)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["used to think", "is thinking", "thinks", "will think"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜used to", "explanation": "【句型】used to + 原形V：過去曾經……（現在不再）。\n【分析】下文 Monica understood her mistake and changed her idea about the old man，表示她「以前認為」老人很窮很孤單，現在不這麼想了 → used to think。\n【其他選項】(B)(C) 現在式表現在仍這麼想，與 changed her idea 矛盾；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】I used to think math was boring, but now I love it.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2226, "question": "Kelly ______ that cats were unfriendly. After she got one, she changed her mind.", "options": ["thinks", "used to think", "is thinking", "will think"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "後來改變想法 → used to think。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2227, "question": "People ______ the earth was flat. Now we know it is round.", "options": ["used to believe", "believe", "are believing", "will believe"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "過去的想法 → used to believe。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2228, "question": "Max ______ that English was too hard for him. Now he is the best in his class.", "options": ["thinks", "will think", "used to think", "is thinking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 165 題）", "explanation": "現在不同 → used to think。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2229, "question": "(21-23)\nMonica __(21)__ the thin old man who lives next to her must be very poor and lonely. She often saw him wearing old clothes and sitting in the park by himself.\nLast Christmas, when Monica was jogging in the park, the old man came up to her with a large bag on his shoulder. Monica guessed the old man ______(22) her for some money or help. But she was surprised to find many children following him. The old man took out a box from his bag and said to her with a big smile, \"Merry Christmas! I bought presents for everybody. This one is for you.\" At that moment, Monica understood her mistake and changed her idea about the old man. Since then, she __(23)__ not to judge people by how they look. She now knows how people look is not the same as what they really are.\n(judge 判斷)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["asked", "would ask", "is asking", "has asked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】主要動詞為過去式（guessed / thought / said）時，子句中表「將要」用 would + V。\n【分析】Monica guessed（過去）老人「會」向她要錢，但事實上並沒有發生 → would ask。\n【其他選項】(A) asked 表老人真的要了錢，與後文矛盾；(C) 現在進行式時態不一致；(D) 現在完成式不合。\n【例句】I thought it would rain, so I took an umbrella.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2230, "question": "When Ann saw the dark clouds, she guessed it ______ soon.", "options": ["rains", "would rain", "has rained", "is raining"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "guessed 過去 → would rain。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2231, "question": "Tom thought his parents ______ angry, but they just smiled.", "options": ["would be", "are", "have been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "過去的猜測 → would be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2232, "question": "We believed the bus ______ on time, but it was thirty minutes late.", "options": ["comes", "has come", "would come", "is coming"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 169 題）", "explanation": "believed 過去 → would come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2233, "question": "(21-23)\nMonica __(21)__ the thin old man who lives next to her must be very poor and lonely. She often saw him wearing old clothes and sitting in the park by himself.\nLast Christmas, when Monica was jogging in the park, the old man came up to her with a large bag on his shoulder. Monica guessed the old man __(22)__ her for some money or help. But she was surprised to find many children following him. The old man took out a box from his bag and said to her with a big smile, \"Merry Christmas! I bought presents for everybody. This one is for you.\" At that moment, Monica understood her mistake and changed her idea about the old man. Since then, she ______(23) not to judge people by how they look. She now knows how people look is not the same as what they really are.\n(judge 判斷)\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["tried", "is trying", "has tried", "will try"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】since then（從那時起）+ 現在完成式 have/has + p.p.。\n【分析】Since then 表從去年聖誕節起一直到現在，後句 She now knows… 也是現在 → has tried。\n【其他選項】(A) tried 只表過去，不能和 since then 表延續；(B) 進行式不和 since then 連用；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】I broke my leg last year. Since then, I have been careful on the stairs.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2234, "question": "Peter got a cold last month. Since then, he ______ warm clothes every day.", "options": ["wore", "has worn", "wears", "will wear"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "since then → has worn。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2235, "question": "My aunt moved to Canada in 2018. Since then, I ______ her only twice.", "options": ["have seen", "saw", "see", "will see"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "since then → have seen。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2236, "question": "Joy lost her phone at the MRT station. Since then, she ______ more careful with her things.", "options": ["was", "is being", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 173 題）", "explanation": "since then → has been。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2237, "question": "(17-20)\nPeople in Quiet Town are very sad that their old friend, Time River, is facing the end of its life next October. The river ______(17) a lot to the people in the town. They all grow up and live with it all their lives.\nIn the old times, people in the town __(18)__ their houses on both sides of the river. The houses in each block shared a public washing room. On Mondays, people came and washed their clothes together there. They hung their clothes at the back of each house. Those clothes with different colors __(19)__ a beautiful picture along the river.\nNow Time River is going to be filled in to make more land to build on. People are happy that they __(20)__ more living space. But at the same time, they feel sorry that they must say good-bye to their old friend. So they have decided to give a party one day a year to remember the river.\n(hung（原形為hang） 懸掛)\n\n▶ 請選出第 17 格的答案", "options": ["means", "is meaning", "will mean", "meant"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 17 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在簡單式表示現在的狀態／事實；mean（對…很重要）是狀態動詞，不用進行式。\n【分析】前後句都是現在式（are very sad, grow up and live），河流「現在」對居民意義重大 → means a lot。\n【其他選項】(B) mean 為狀態動詞，不用進行式；(C) will mean 表未來，但現在就很重要；(D) meant 表過去，不合現在情境。\n【例句】This old watch means a lot to my grandpa.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2238, "question": "This letter from my best friend ______ a lot to me. I keep it in my desk.", "options": ["is meaning", "means", "meant", "will mean"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "現在的狀態 → means。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2239, "question": "My dog ______ the world to me. I take him everywhere.", "options": ["means", "is meaning", "has meant", "will mean"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "現在事實 → means。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2240, "question": "Lisa ______ the new phone very much. She uses it all the time.", "options": ["is liking", "will like", "likes", "liked"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 177 題）", "explanation": "like 狀態動詞，現在 → likes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2241, "question": "(17-20)\nPeople in Quiet Town are very sad that their old friend, Time River, is facing the end of its life next October. The river __(17)__ a lot to the people in the town. They all grow up and live with it all their lives.\nIn the old times, people in the town ______(18) their houses on both sides of the river. The houses in each block shared a public washing room. On Mondays, people came and washed their clothes together there. They hung their clothes at the back of each house. Those clothes with different colors __(19)__ a beautiful picture along the river.\nNow Time River is going to be filled in to make more land to build on. People are happy that they __(20)__ more living space. But at the same time, they feel sorry that they must say good-bye to their old friend. So they have decided to give a party one day a year to remember the river.\n(hung（原形為hang） 懸掛)\n\n▶ 請選出第 18 格的答案", "options": ["build", "are building", "have built", "built"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 18 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去時間 In the old times / long ago + 過去簡單式。\n【分析】In the old times 表示過去，後文 came, washed, hung 都是過去式 → built。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式、(B) 現在進行式、(C) 現在完成式都不能和明確的過去時間 In the old times 連用。\n【例句】In the old times, people built their houses with wood.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2242, "question": "In the old days, people ______ letters to keep in touch.", "options": ["write", "have written", "wrote", "are writing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "In the old days → 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2243, "question": "Long ago, my great-grandparents ______ rice on this land.", "options": ["grew", "grow", "have grown", "are growing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "Long ago → grew。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2244, "question": "Many years ago, there ______ no MRT in Taipei.", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 181 題）", "explanation": "Many years ago → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2245, "question": "(17-20)\nPeople in Quiet Town are very sad that their old friend, Time River, is facing the end of its life next October. The river __(17)__ a lot to the people in the town. They all grow up and live with it all their lives.\nIn the old times, people in the town __(18)__ their houses on both sides of the river. The houses in each block shared a public washing room. On Mondays, people came and washed their clothes together there. They hung their clothes at the back of each house. Those clothes with different colors ______(19) a beautiful picture along the river.\nNow Time River is going to be filled in to make more land to build on. People are happy that they __(20)__ more living space. But at the same time, they feel sorry that they must say good-bye to their old friend. So they have decided to give a party one day a year to remember the river.\n(hung（原形為hang） 懸掛)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["make", "are making", "have made", "made"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】描述過去的習慣或情景，前後時態一致用過去式。\n【分析】同段 came, washed, hung 都是過去式，描寫以前的景象：五顏六色的衣服「形成」美麗畫面 → made。\n【其他選項】(A)(B)(C) 現在式、進行式、完成式都與「以前的景象」不一致。\n【例句】On holidays, the lanterns made the old street look beautiful.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2246, "question": "Back then, the children played in the street, and their laughter ______ the town lively.", "options": ["makes", "made", "has made", "is making"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "描述過去景象 → made。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2247, "question": "When I was young, my grandma ______ dumplings for us every weekend.", "options": ["made", "makes", "has made", "is making"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "When I was young → 過去式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2248, "question": "Years ago, the old trees along the road ______ shade for people walking by.", "options": ["give", "have given", "gave", "are giving"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 185 題）", "explanation": "Years ago → gave。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2249, "question": "(17-20)\nPeople in Quiet Town are very sad that their old friend, Time River, is facing the end of its life next October. The river __(17)__ a lot to the people in the town. They all grow up and live with it all their lives.\nIn the old times, people in the town __(18)__ their houses on both sides of the river. The houses in each block shared a public washing room. On Mondays, people came and washed their clothes together there. They hung their clothes at the back of each house. Those clothes with different colors __(19)__ a beautiful picture along the river.\nNow Time River is going to be filled in to make more land to build on. People are happy that they ______(20) more living space. But at the same time, they feel sorry that they must say good-bye to their old friend. So they have decided to give a party one day a year to remember the river.\n(hung（原形為hang） 懸掛)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["have", "have had", "will have", "had"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】未來式 will + V：表將來會發生的事。\n【分析】Now Time River is going to be filled in…（尚未填平），居民高興他們「將會有」更多居住空間 → will have。\n【其他選項】(A) have 表現在已有；(B) have had 表已經有了；(D) had 表過去，都與「河還沒填」不合。\n【例句】When the new park opens, we will have more places to play.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2250, "question": "The new MRT line is going to open next year. People are glad that they ______ an easier way to get to work.", "options": ["have", "will have", "had", "have had"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "明年才開 → will have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2251, "question": "Our school is going to build a new gym. Students are happy that they ______ more space to play basketball.", "options": ["will have", "had", "have had", "are having"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "尚未蓋好 → will have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2252, "question": "The bookstore is moving to a bigger place next month. The owner says he ______ more room for books.", "options": ["had", "has had", "will have", "have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 189 題）", "explanation": "next month → will have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2253, "question": "(19-21)\nMr. Hutman owns a restaurant. One day, one of his two cooks ran away with some money. Mr. Hutman was sad and worried because the next day was Saturday, and the restaurant ______(19) very busy then. So that night he called his friends, but could not find anyone to help.\nOn Saturday, many people came to the restaurant for lunch. __(20)__ cook got so busy that he wanted to leave, too. __(21)__, one of the waiters, Henry, told Mr. Hutman that he could help in the kitchen. People who had lunch in the restaurant that day enjoyed the food Henry cooked. Mr. Hutman was very happy and made Henry a new cook of the restaurant.\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["would be", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中提到「之後會發生」的事，用 would + V。\n【分析】故事為過去（was sad and worried），而 the next day（隔天週六）餐廳「將會」很忙 → would be。\n【其他選項】(B) is 現在式、(C) has been 現在完成式與過去敘事不合；(D) will be 是以現在為基準的未來，過去敘事中應改為 would。\n【例句】Amy was nervous because the test would be on the next day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2254, "question": "Ben went to bed early because the next day ______ his first day of school.", "options": ["is", "would be", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事中的隔天 → would be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2255, "question": "The farmers were worried. The weather report said a typhoon ______ the next morning.", "options": ["would come", "comes", "has come", "will come"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "said 過去 → would come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2256, "question": "We bought a lot of food, because ten friends ______ to our house that night.", "options": ["come", "have come", "were coming", "will come"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 193 題）", "explanation": "過去預定之事 → were coming（過去的未來）。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2257, "question": "(19-21)\nMr. Hutman owns a restaurant. One day, one of his two cooks ran away with some money. Mr. Hutman was sad and worried because the next day was Saturday, and the restaurant __(19)__ very busy then. So that night he called his friends, but could not find anyone to help.\nOn Saturday, many people came to the restaurant for lunch. ______(20) cook got so busy that he wanted to leave, too. __(21)__, one of the waiters, Henry, told Mr. Hutman that he could help in the kitchen. People who had lunch in the restaurant that day enjoyed the food Henry cooked. Mr. Hutman was very happy and made Henry a new cook of the restaurant.\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["One", "Each", "Another", "The only"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜名詞、冠詞、代名詞、數量詞", "explanation": "【句型】the only + N：唯一的……。\n【分析】文首說他有兩位廚師，one of his two cooks ran away，所以只剩一位 → The only cook got so busy…, too（too 表示他也想走）。\n【其他選項】(A) One cook 表「某一位」，但只剩一人；(B) Each cook 指每一位，但只剩一位；(C) Another cook 指「另一位（新的）」，不合語意。\n【例句】Tom is the only student who finished the test early.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2258, "question": "Lily has two cats. One ran away last week, so now Kitty is ______ cat she has.", "options": ["another", "the only", "each", "one"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "兩隻跑一隻，只剩一隻 → the only。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2259, "question": "There were two cookies on the plate. I ate one, and my brother ate ______ one.", "options": ["the other", "another", "each", "one"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "兩者中的另一個 → the other。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2260, "question": "All the other students went home. Jack was ______ person left in the classroom.", "options": ["another", "each", "the only", "one"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 197 題）", "explanation": "只剩他 → the only。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2261, "question": "(19-21)\nMr. Hutman owns a restaurant. One day, one of his two cooks ran away with some money. Mr. Hutman was sad and worried because the next day was Saturday, and the restaurant __(19)__ very busy then. So that night he called his friends, but could not find anyone to help.\nOn Saturday, many people came to the restaurant for lunch. __(20)__ cook got so busy that he wanted to leave, too. ______(21), one of the waiters, Henry, told Mr. Hutman that he could help in the kitchen. People who had lunch in the restaurant that day enjoyed the food Henry cooked. Mr. Hutman was very happy and made Henry a new cook of the restaurant.\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["Also", "In fact", "Luckily", "For example"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜詞彙題", "explanation": "【句型】轉承副詞 Luckily：幸運地、幸好（困境後出現好結果）。\n【分析】前句廚師忙到也想離開，餐廳陷入困境；接著服務生 Henry 說他能幫忙，是好事 → Luckily。\n【其他選項】(A) Also 表補充，不合；(B) In fact 表「事實上」，用來補充或更正前面說法；(D) For example 表舉例，不合。\n【例句】I missed the bus. Luckily, my dad drove me to school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2262, "question": "I forgot my lunch at home. ______, my friend shared her sandwich with me.", "options": ["Also", "Luckily", "For example", "In fact"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "困境後的好事 → Luckily。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2263, "question": "Tom is not lazy. ______, he is the hardest-working student in our class.", "options": ["In fact", "Luckily", "For example", "Also"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "更正、強調 → In fact。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2264, "question": "There are many ways to stay healthy. ______, you can jog or swim every day.", "options": ["Luckily", "In fact", "For example", "Also"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 201 題）", "explanation": "舉例 → For example。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2265, "question": "(20-22)\nShu-mei is in the third year of senior high school. She is very good at singing and ______(20) many prizes in the past few years with her beautiful voice. Although Shu-mei always gets good grades at school, she does not want to spend too much time studying. She __(21)__ singing more than studying. Her biggest dream is to become a great singer in the future. Shu-mei's parents have sent her to a music teacher to learn singing, and Shu-mei __(22)__ hard every day. She hopes she can get into a music school to study singing after she finishes high school.\n(prize 獎賞)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["wins", "was winning", "has won", "is going to win"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】in the past/last + 時間（在過去幾年來）+ 現在完成式。\n【分析】in the past few years 表從幾年前到現在的累積成果 → has won many prizes。\n【其他選項】(A) wins 現在式不和 in the past few years 連用；(B) 過去進行式不合；(D) 未來式不合「過去幾年」。\n【例句】Our team has won three games in the past two weeks.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2266, "question": "Mr. Chen ______ five books in the past ten years.", "options": ["writes", "has written", "wrote", "is writing"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "in the past ten years → has written。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2267, "question": "In the last few months, Ivy ______ a lot of weight.", "options": ["has lost", "loses", "is losing", "will lose"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "in the last few months → has lost。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2268, "question": "This shop ______ more and more customers in the past year.", "options": ["gets", "will get", "has gotten", "is getting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 205 題）", "explanation": "in the past year → has gotten。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2269, "question": "(20-22)\nShu-mei is in the third year of senior high school. She is very good at singing and __(20)__ many prizes in the past few years with her beautiful voice. Although Shu-mei always gets good grades at school, she does not want to spend too much time studying. She ______(21) singing more than studying. Her biggest dream is to become a great singer in the future. Shu-mei's parents have sent her to a music teacher to learn singing, and Shu-mei __(22)__ hard every day. She hopes she can get into a music school to study singing after she finishes high school.\n(prize 獎賞)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["loves", "loved", "is loving", "will love"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在簡單式表現在的喜好／狀態；love 為狀態動詞，一般不用進行式。\n【分析】前後句皆為現在式（does not want, Her biggest dream is），她「現在」喜愛唱歌勝過讀書 → loves。\n【其他選項】(B) loved 過去式不合；(C) love 為狀態動詞不用進行式；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】My sister loves drawing more than playing games.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2270, "question": "My brother ______ basketball more than baseball.", "options": ["likes", "is liking", "liked", "will like"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "現在的喜好 → likes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2271, "question": "Jenny ______ cats. She has three of them at home.", "options": ["is loving", "loves", "loved", "will love"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "現在事實 → loves。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2272, "question": "Mark ______ reading comics more than doing homework.", "options": ["is preferring", "preferred", "prefers", "will prefer"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 209 題）", "explanation": "現在偏好 → prefers。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2273, "question": "(20-22)\nShu-mei is in the third year of senior high school. She is very good at singing and __(20)__ many prizes in the past few years with her beautiful voice. Although Shu-mei always gets good grades at school, she does not want to spend too much time studying. She __(21)__ singing more than studying. Her biggest dream is to become a great singer in the future. Shu-mei's parents have sent her to a music teacher to learn singing, and Shu-mei ______(22) hard every day. She hopes she can get into a music school to study singing after she finishes high school.\n(prize 獎賞)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["practices", "practiced", "has practiced", "is going to practice"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在簡單式＋every day：表現在的習慣動作。\n【分析】every day 表示現在的習慣，主詞 Shu-mei 第三人稱單數 → practices。\n【其他選項】(B) 過去式不合現在情境；(C) 現在完成式不和 every day 表習慣連用；(D) 未來式不合每天的習慣。\n【例句】Ken jogs in the park every morning.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2274, "question": "Tim ______ the piano for an hour every day.", "options": ["practiced", "practices", "has practiced", "is going to practice"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "every day → 現在簡單式。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2275, "question": "My mom ______ to work by bus every morning.", "options": ["goes", "went", "has gone", "is going to go"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "習慣 → goes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2276, "question": "Linda usually ______ her homework before dinner.", "options": ["did", "has done", "does", "will do"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 213 題）", "explanation": "usually → does。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2277, "question": "(21-23)\nKaren: Good morning, Sheryl. You look different today.\nSheryl: Really? Do I look thinner? I just ______(21) doing some work on my apartment.\nKaren: I see. What did you do?\nSheryl: I __(22)__ the apartment myself and got a new couch and coffee table for the living room.\nKaren: It sounds like a big job. What colors did you paint your apartment?\nSheryl: Several different ones. Let me see . . . white, yellow, green, blue and pink.\nKaren: So that's why you __(23)__ all those colors on your hair?\nSheryl: Oh, no!\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["finish", "will finish", "finished", "would finish"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】just + 過去式（或 have just p.p.）：剛剛做完某事；finish + Ving。\n【分析】下一句 Karen 問 What did you do?（過去式），可知整理公寓已經「剛做完」→ just finished doing。\n【其他選項】(A) finish 現在式不合；(B) will finish 表還沒做完，與 What did you do? 矛盾；(D) would finish 表假設或過去的未來。\n【例句】I just finished cleaning my room.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2278, "question": "A: You look tired. B: I just ______ running ten kilometers.", "options": ["finish", "finished", "will finish", "would finish"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "剛跑完 → just finished。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2279, "question": "A: Are you free now? B: Yes, I just ______ my homework.", "options": ["finished", "finish", "will finish", "am finishing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "剛完成 → just finished。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2280, "question": "A: Why is the floor wet? B: Mom just ______ it.", "options": ["washes", "will wash", "washed", "would wash"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 217 題）", "explanation": "剛洗過 → washed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2281, "question": "(21-23)\nKaren: Good morning, Sheryl. You look different today.\nSheryl: Really? Do I look thinner? I just __(21)__ doing some work on my apartment.\nKaren: I see. What did you do?\nSheryl: I ______(22) the apartment myself and got a new couch and coffee table for the living room.\nKaren: It sounds like a big job. What colors did you paint your apartment?\nSheryl: Several different ones. Let me see . . . white, yellow, green, blue and pink.\nKaren: So that's why you __(23)__ all those colors on your hair?\nSheryl: Oh, no!\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["paint", "painted", "was painting", "would paint"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】對等連接詞 and 連接的動詞時態一致。\n【分析】Karen 問 What did you do?；後半句 and got a new couch 是過去式，前面並列動詞也用過去式 → painted。\n【其他選項】(A) paint 現在式與 got 不一致；(C) 過去進行式表某時正在做，不合「已完成的事」；(D) would paint 表假設。\n【例句】Last weekend I cleaned my room and washed my clothes.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2282, "question": "A: What did you do last night? B: I ______ a movie and went to bed early.", "options": ["watch", "watched", "was watching", "would watch"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "與 went 一致 → watched。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2283, "question": "Yesterday Dad ______ the car and cooked dinner for us.", "options": ["washed", "washes", "was washing", "would wash"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "與 cooked 一致 → washed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2284, "question": "A: How was your trip? B: Great! We ______ the night market and ate a lot.", "options": ["visit", "would visit", "visited", "are visiting"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 221 題）", "explanation": "與 ate 一致 → visited。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2285, "question": "(21-23)\nKaren: Good morning, Sheryl. You look different today.\nSheryl: Really? Do I look thinner? I just __(21)__ doing some work on my apartment.\nKaren: I see. What did you do?\nSheryl: I __(22)__ the apartment myself and got a new couch and coffee table for the living room.\nKaren: It sounds like a big job. What colors did you paint your apartment?\nSheryl: Several different ones. Let me see . . . white, yellow, green, blue and pink.\nKaren: So that's why you ______(23) all those colors on your hair?\nSheryl: Oh, no!\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["have", "will have", "had", "would have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】have（擁有）表現在狀態用現在簡單式。\n【分析】對話發生在現在，Karen 看著 Sheryl 說「這就是為什麼你頭髮上（現在）有這些顏色？」→ have。\n【其他選項】(B) will have 表未來；(C) had 表過去，但顏色現在還在頭髮上；(D) would have 表假設。\n【例句】Why do you have paint on your shirt?", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2286, "question": "A: Why ______ mud on your shoes? B: I just played soccer in the rain.", "options": ["do you have", "will you have", "did you have", "would you have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "現在鞋上有泥 → do you have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2287, "question": "So that's why Jimmy ______ a smile on his face. He got a new bike!", "options": ["had", "has", "will have", "would have"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "現在臉上有笑容 → has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2288, "question": "Look! Your dog ______ something in its mouth.", "options": ["had", "would have", "has", "will have"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 225 題）", "explanation": "現在 → has。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2289, "question": "(18-20)\nOne Thursday morning in Blue Town, I noticed a lot of people going to the church. Later, all the people in the streets stopped and just stood where they were. All of them ______(18) quiet for two minutes. Everyone looked serious.\nI found this strange and asked a woman what was happening. She said that they were commemorating the birthday of St. George, who __(19)__ for helping the farmers of the town to get back their land from the king. Later, I saw some people wearing and selling flowers on the streets. They told me the money would be used to help poor farmers.\nSince that trip, I __(20)__ about Blue Town a lot. I often tell my friends about this experience and show them some pictures I took there.\n(commemorate 紀念)\n\n▶ 請選出第 18 格的答案", "options": ["are", "have been", "were", "would be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 18 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事中描述當時狀態用過去式；主詞 All of them 為複數 → were。\n【分析】前後句 stopped, stood, looked 都是過去式，所有人「當時」安靜兩分鐘 → were quiet。\n【其他選項】(A) are 現在式、(B) have been 現在完成式與過去敘事不合；(D) would be 表過去的未來或假設。\n【例句】During the test, all of the students were quiet.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2290, "question": "When the movie started, everyone in the theater ______ quiet.", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "would be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "過去敘事 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2291, "question": "Last night all of us ______ tired after the long hike.", "options": ["were", "are", "have been", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "last night → were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2292, "question": "At the meeting yesterday, the students ______ very excited about the trip.", "options": ["are", "have been", "were", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 229 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2293, "question": "(18-20)\nOne Thursday morning in Blue Town, I noticed a lot of people going to the church. Later, all the people in the streets stopped and just stood where they were. All of them __(18)__ quiet for two minutes. Everyone looked serious.\nI found this strange and asked a woman what was happening. She said that they were commemorating the birthday of St. George, who ______(19) for helping the farmers of the town to get back their land from the king. Later, I saw some people wearing and selling flowers on the streets. They told me the money would be used to help poor farmers.\nSince that trip, I __(20)__ about Blue Town a lot. I often tell my friends about this experience and show them some pictures I took there.\n(commemorate 紀念)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["has been killed", "was killed", "would be killed", "is going to be killed"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜主動與被動語態", "explanation": "【句型】被動語態 be + p.p.；過去發生的事用 was/were + p.p.。\n【分析】St. George 是「被殺」（被動），而且是很久以前的歷史事件（現在在紀念他的生日）→ was killed。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式不用於明確的歷史事件；(C) would be killed 表過去的未來或假設；(D) is going to be 表未來，不合。\n【例句】The old temple was built two hundred years ago.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2294, "question": "The man ______ by a car while he was crossing the street last night.", "options": ["is hit", "was hit", "has hit", "hits"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "過去被動 → was hit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2295, "question": "This bridge ______ in 1990.", "options": ["was built", "built", "is built", "has built"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "1990 年被建 → was built。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2296, "question": "Many trees ______ down by the strong wind during the typhoon last week.", "options": ["blew", "are blown", "were blown", "have blown"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 233 題）", "explanation": "過去被動 → were blown。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2297, "question": "(18-20)\nOne Thursday morning in Blue Town, I noticed a lot of people going to the church. Later, all the people in the streets stopped and just stood where they were. All of them __(18)__ quiet for two minutes. Everyone looked serious.\nI found this strange and asked a woman what was happening. She said that they were commemorating the birthday of St. George, who __(19)__ for helping the farmers of the town to get back their land from the king. Later, I saw some people wearing and selling flowers on the streets. They told me the money would be used to help poor farmers.\nSince that trip, I ______(20) about Blue Town a lot. I often tell my friends about this experience and show them some pictures I took there.\n(commemorate 紀念)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["thought", "was thinking", "have thought", "will think"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】since + 過去時間點（since that trip）+ 現在完成式。\n【分析】Since that trip 表從那次旅行到現在，後句 I often tell my friends… 也是現在式 → have thought。\n【其他選項】(A) thought 只表過去；(B) 過去進行式不和 since 連用；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】Since the summer camp, I have kept in touch with my new friends.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2298, "question": "Since that day, Sandy ______ about her dream a lot.", "options": ["talked", "has talked", "was talking", "will talk"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "since → has talked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2299, "question": "Since the accident, Mr. Wang ______ more carefully.", "options": ["has driven", "drove", "was driving", "will drive"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "since → has driven。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2300, "question": "Since our trip to Japan, my sister ______ Japanese food very much.", "options": ["loved", "was loving", "has loved", "will love"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 237 題）", "explanation": "since → has loved。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2301, "question": "(19-21)\nDate: Wednesday, Oct. 24　Weather: sunny\nThis evening before dinner, Mom asked Kevin to go to the supermarket to buy some eggs. He ______(19) my jacket without asking me first. When he was putting his keys into the jacket, he found some cigarettes and showed them to Mom and Dad.\nBoth of them were very surprised. They said smoking was bad for my health. I told them that I just tried it once. In fact, I did not like it at all. I promised I __(20)__ again. Right now my mouth __(21)__ quite dry, and the smell of smoke is still in my hair and clothes. I think I need a lot of water and a hot bath.\n(cigarette 香煙　not . . . at all 一點也不　promise 承諾)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["put on", "is putting on", "has put on", "would put on"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去簡單式描述過去發生的事；put 三態同形 put-put-put。\n【分析】This evening before dinner, Mom asked…（過去式），Kevin 沒問就「穿了」我的外套，後文 he was putting…, found 也是過去 → put on（過去式）。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在進行式、(C) 現在完成式與過去敘事不合；(D) would put on 表過去習慣或假設，不合單次事件。\n【例句】Yesterday my sister put on my shoes without asking me.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2302, "question": "This morning my brother ______ my hat and went out.", "options": ["puts on", "put on", "is putting on", "has put on"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "this morning 已過 → put on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2303, "question": "Last night Dad ______ his glasses and read the newspaper.", "options": ["put on", "puts on", "has put on", "would put on"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "last night → put on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2304, "question": "Before she left, Grandma ______ her coat because it was cold.", "options": ["puts on", "is putting on", "put on", "will put on"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 241 題）", "explanation": "left 過去 → put on。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2305, "question": "(19-21)\nDate: Wednesday, Oct. 24　Weather: sunny\nThis evening before dinner, Mom asked Kevin to go to the supermarket to buy some eggs. He __(19)__ my jacket without asking me first. When he was putting his keys into the jacket, he found some cigarettes and showed them to Mom and Dad.\nBoth of them were very surprised. They said smoking was bad for my health. I told them that I just tried it once. In fact, I did not like it at all. I promised I ______(20) again. Right now my mouth __(21)__ quite dry, and the smell of smoke is still in my hair and clothes. I think I need a lot of water and a hot bath.\n(cigarette 香煙　not . . . at all 一點也不　promise 承諾)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["am never smoking", "never smoked", "have never smoked", "would never smoke"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去式的 promise/say/tell 後，子句表未來用 would + V。\n【分析】I promised（過去）「我以後再也不會抽」，是承諾未來的事 → would never smoke again。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在進行式時態不一致；(B) never smoked 表過去從未抽過，與 I just tried it once 矛盾；(C) have never smoked 同樣矛盾。\n【例句】Tom promised he would never lie to me again.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2306, "question": "After the fight, Ryan promised he ______ his sister again.", "options": ["never hits", "would never hit", "has never hit", "never hit"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "promised 過去 → would never hit。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2307, "question": "I told my teacher that I ______ late again.", "options": ["would never be", "am never", "have never been", "was never"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "told 過去 → would never be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2308, "question": "Amy promised her mom that she ______ her room every weekend.", "options": ["cleans", "has cleaned", "would clean", "cleaned"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 245 題）", "explanation": "promised → would clean。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2309, "question": "(19-21)\nDate: Wednesday, Oct. 24　Weather: sunny\nThis evening before dinner, Mom asked Kevin to go to the supermarket to buy some eggs. He __(19)__ my jacket without asking me first. When he was putting his keys into the jacket, he found some cigarettes and showed them to Mom and Dad.\nBoth of them were very surprised. They said smoking was bad for my health. I told them that I just tried it once. In fact, I did not like it at all. I promised I __(20)__ again. Right now my mouth ______(21) quite dry, and the smell of smoke is still in my hair and clothes. I think I need a lot of water and a hot bath.\n(cigarette 香煙　not . . . at all 一點也不　promise 承諾)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["feels", "felt", "was feeling", "will feel"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】Right now 表示寫日記的「現在」；feel（感覺起來）為連綴／狀態動詞，用現在簡單式。\n【分析】Right now…, and the smell of smoke is still in my hair（現在式）→ 現在嘴巴「感覺」很乾 → feels。\n【其他選項】(B) felt、(C) was feeling 為過去，與 Right now 不合；(D) will feel 表未來。\n【例句】Right now my legs feel very tired.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2310, "question": "Right now my head ______ hot. I think I have a fever.", "options": ["feels", "felt", "will feel", "was feeling"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "Right now → feels。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2311, "question": "This soup ______ delicious. Can I have some more?", "options": ["tasted", "tastes", "is tasting", "will taste"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "現在嚐起來 → tastes。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2312, "question": "Your new sweater ______ soft. Where did you buy it?", "options": ["felt", "is feeling", "feels", "will feel"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 249 題）", "explanation": "現在摸起來 → feels。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2313, "question": "(19-21)\nDad left us several months ago. He ______(19) a man who loved his family and his life a lot. He liked to help others, and everyone around him liked him very much.\nLast year, Dad got very sick and had to stay in the hospital. Mom __(20)__ very busy running between the house and the hospital. Six months later, Dad died. I couldn't believe I __(21)__ him again.\nToday is Dad's 50th birthday. I really want to tell him how much I miss him....\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["was", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】描述已不在世的人，用過去式。\n【分析】Dad left us several months ago（已過世），後句 loved, liked 都是過去式 → He was a man who…。\n【其他選項】(B) is 現在式，但父親已過世；(C) has been 表延續到現在，不合；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】My grandfather was a kind man who loved to read.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2314, "question": "My grandma died last year. She ______ a great cook.", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "已過世 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2315, "question": "Mr. Lin left our school two years ago. He ______ a funny teacher.", "options": ["was", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "過去 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2316, "question": "Our old dog died in May. He ______ always happy to see us.", "options": ["is", "has been", "was", "will be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 253 題）", "explanation": "已過世 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2317, "question": "(19-21)\nDad left us several months ago. He __(19)__ a man who loved his family and his life a lot. He liked to help others, and everyone around him liked him very much.\nLast year, Dad got very sick and had to stay in the hospital. Mom ______(20) very busy running between the house and the hospital. Six months later, Dad died. I couldn't believe I __(21)__ him again.\nToday is Dad's 50th birthday. I really want to tell him how much I miss him....\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["became", "becomes", "has become", "is becoming"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】Last year + 過去簡單式；become + adj. 表「變得」。\n【分析】Last year, Dad got very sick（過去），媽媽「變得」很忙 → became。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在式、(C) 現在完成式、(D) 現在進行式都不能和 Last year 連用。\n【例句】After the baby was born, Mom became very busy.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2318, "question": "Last winter, the weather ______ very cold.", "options": ["becomes", "became", "has become", "is becoming"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "last winter → became。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2319, "question": "When Jim moved to a new school, he ______ shy.", "options": ["became", "becomes", "has become", "is becoming"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "過去 → became。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2320, "question": "After she won the contest last month, Sara ______ famous in our town.", "options": ["becomes", "has become", "became", "is becoming"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 257 題）", "explanation": "last month → became。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2321, "question": "(19-21)\nDad left us several months ago. He __(19)__ a man who loved his family and his life a lot. He liked to help others, and everyone around him liked him very much.\nLast year, Dad got very sick and had to stay in the hospital. Mom __(20)__ very busy running between the house and the hospital. Six months later, Dad died. I couldn't believe I ______(21) him again.\nToday is Dad's 50th birthday. I really want to tell him how much I miss him....\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["did not see", "have not seen", "am not seeing", "would not see"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】主要子句為過去式（couldn't believe）時，子句表未來用 would + V。\n【分析】父親過世時，我不敢相信我「以後將再也見不到」他 → would not see him again。\n【其他選項】(A) did not see 表過去沒看到，與 again 表未來不合；(B) 現在完成式、(C) 現在進行式與 couldn't believe 時態不一致。\n【例句】I couldn't believe I would never go back to that school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2322, "question": "When my best friend moved away, I couldn't believe I ______ her every day anymore.", "options": ["won't see", "wouldn't see", "didn't see", "haven't seen"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "過去的未來 → wouldn't see。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2323, "question": "Tom didn't know he ______ his wallet on the bus.", "options": ["would leave", "leaves", "has left", "is leaving"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "過去的未來 → would leave。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2324, "question": "We never thought the old store ______ forever.", "options": ["closes", "has closed", "would close", "is closing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 261 題）", "explanation": "thought 過去 → would close。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2325, "question": "(19-21)\nOne day after dinner, Lois went to the park for a walk. On her way there, she was stopped by a man who ______(19) his fingernails. \"Somebody took my bag,\" he said, \"and I have no money to get home.\" He asked Lois if she could lend him some money. Lois was afraid and said \"no\" to him in a polite way. The man did not listen and kept asking for money. Lois did not change her mind. The man got angry and cried out, \"You __(20)__ a cold person. I hate you!\" Lois felt so bad that she ran home quickly.\nEven today, Lois is still wondering whether what she __(21)__ to that man was right or wrong.\n(fingernail 指甲　wonder 疑惑)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["bites", "has bit", "was biting", "would bite"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去進行式 was/were + Ving：過去某時正在進行。\n【分析】故事為過去（went, was stopped），攔住她的那個男人「當時正在」咬指甲 → was biting。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式、(B) 現在完成式與過去敘事不合；(D) would bite 表過去習慣或假設，不合當下動作。\n【例句】I saw a boy who was crying at the bus stop.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2326, "question": "Yesterday I met a girl who ______ for her lost cat.", "options": ["looks", "was looking", "has looked", "would look"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "過去當時正在找 → was looking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2327, "question": "At the park, Ted saw an old man who ______ the birds.", "options": ["was feeding", "feeds", "has fed", "will feed"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "當時正在餵 → was feeding。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2328, "question": "The woman who ______ next to me on the train was reading a book.", "options": ["sits", "has sat", "was sitting", "will sit"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 265 題）", "explanation": "當時正坐著 → was sitting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2329, "question": "(19-21)\nOne day after dinner, Lois went to the park for a walk. On her way there, she was stopped by a man who __(19)__ his fingernails. \"Somebody took my bag,\" he said, \"and I have no money to get home.\" He asked Lois if she could lend him some money. Lois was afraid and said \"no\" to him in a polite way. The man did not listen and kept asking for money. Lois did not change her mind. The man got angry and cried out, \"You ______(20) a cold person. I hate you!\" Lois felt so bad that she ran home quickly.\nEven today, Lois is still wondering whether what she __(21)__ to that man was right or wrong.\n(fingernail 指甲　wonder 疑惑)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["are", "were", "will be", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】引號內的直接引述，依說話者當時的「現在」用現在式。\n【分析】男人當面對 Lois 說「你是個冷漠的人。我恨你！」，同句 I hate you 是現在式 → You are…。\n【其他選項】(B) were 表過去，不合直接引述；(C) will be 表未來；(D) would be 表假設。\n【例句】She said, \"You are my best friend.\"", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2330, "question": "The teacher smiled and said, \"You ______ a very good student.\"", "options": ["were", "are", "will be", "would be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "直接引述 → are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2331, "question": "My little brother shouted, \"I ______ hungry! When is dinner?\"", "options": ["am", "was", "will be", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "直接引述現在 → am。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2332, "question": "The old man said to us, \"This park ______ my favorite place.\"", "options": ["was", "will be", "is", "would be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 269 題）", "explanation": "直接引述 → is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2333, "question": "(19-21)\nOne day after dinner, Lois went to the park for a walk. On her way there, she was stopped by a man who __(19)__ his fingernails. \"Somebody took my bag,\" he said, \"and I have no money to get home.\" He asked Lois if she could lend him some money. Lois was afraid and said \"no\" to him in a polite way. The man did not listen and kept asking for money. Lois did not change her mind. The man got angry and cried out, \"You __(20)__ a cold person. I hate you!\" Lois felt so bad that she ran home quickly.\nEven today, Lois is still wondering whether what she ______(21) to that man was right or wrong.\n(fingernail 指甲　wonder 疑惑)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["says", "said", "will say", "would say"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】what + S + V 名詞子句；說的話發生在過去，用過去式。\n【分析】她對那男人說話是那天晚上的事（過去），子句後面 was right or wrong 也是過去式 → what she said。\n【其他選項】(A) says 現在式、(C) will say 未來式不合；(D) would say 表假設或過去的未來，但話已經說了。\n【例句】I still remember what my teacher said on the first day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2334, "question": "Kevin still thinks about what his coach ______ to him after the game last week.", "options": ["says", "said", "will say", "would say"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "last week → said。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2335, "question": "I don't know if what I ______ yesterday hurt my friend.", "options": ["did", "do", "will do", "would do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2336, "question": "Mom asked me whether what I ______ at the party was true.", "options": ["say", "will say", "said", "would say"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 273 題）", "explanation": "已說過 → said。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2337, "question": "(20-22)\nWhen Marcy was a little girl, her parents were always worried about not having enough money. Their sad faces made her decide to help, so she left school and ______(20) to work at the age of fifteen. Since then, she has done many different jobs. Most of the jobs did not pay well, but she tried her best in all of them and learned a lot.\nMarcy is now thirty years old, and her family has a better life. But Marcy's friends keep telling her that she should learn to make more money. They __(21)__ her several ways, but she has not tried any of them. She is not interested in anything risky. What she wants most now is to go back to school. She knows she __(22)__ really happy if she can be a student again.\n(risky 有風險的)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["starts", "started", "has started", "will start"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】and 連接的動詞時態一致；at the age of + 數字（過去的年紀）用過去式。\n【分析】她 left school（過去式）and「開始」工作，at the age of fifteen 是過去的時間點 → started。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式、(C) 現在完成式、(D) 未來式都和 left、at the age of fifteen 不一致。\n【例句】My dad left home and started his own business at the age of twenty.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2338, "question": "Kelly finished high school and ______ to study in Japan at the age of eighteen.", "options": ["goes", "went", "has gone", "will go"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "與 finished 一致、過去年紀 → went。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2339, "question": "At the age of six, Leo ______ to play the violin.", "options": ["began", "begins", "has begun", "will begin"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "at the age of six → began。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2340, "question": "My grandpa sold his farm and ______ to the city in 1980.", "options": ["moves", "has moved", "moved", "will move"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 277 題）", "explanation": "in 1980 → moved。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2341, "question": "(20-22)\nWhen Marcy was a little girl, her parents were always worried about not having enough money. Their sad faces made her decide to help, so she left school and __(20)__ to work at the age of fifteen. Since then, she has done many different jobs. Most of the jobs did not pay well, but she tried her best in all of them and learned a lot.\nMarcy is now thirty years old, and her family has a better life. But Marcy's friends keep telling her that she should learn to make more money. They ______(21) her several ways, but she has not tried any of them. She is not interested in anything risky. What she wants most now is to go back to school. She knows she __(22)__ really happy if she can be a student again.\n(risky 有風險的)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["are teaching", "were teaching", "have taught", "will teach"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在完成式 have/has + p.p.：到目前為止已經做過的事。\n【分析】後半句 but she has not tried any of them（現在完成式），朋友「已經教了」她好幾種方法（到現在為止）→ have taught。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在進行式表正在教，與「已經提過幾種方法、她都沒試」不合；(B) 過去進行式不合；(D) will teach 表還沒教，與 has not tried any of them 矛盾。\n【例句】My teacher has given us many tips, but I haven't used any of them yet.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2342, "question": "My parents ______ me many times to go to bed early, but I still stay up late.", "options": ["tell", "have told", "will tell", "were telling"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "到目前已說很多次 → have told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2343, "question": "Our coach ______ us several ways to run faster, but we haven't tried them yet.", "options": ["has shown", "is showing", "was showing", "will show"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "與 haven't tried 呼應 → has shown。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2344, "question": "Doctors ______ Mr. Chen to stop smoking, but he hasn't listened.", "options": ["are asking", "will ask", "have asked", "were asking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 281 題）", "explanation": "到目前已要求 → have asked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2345, "question": "(20-22)\nWhen Marcy was a little girl, her parents were always worried about not having enough money. Their sad faces made her decide to help, so she left school and __(20)__ to work at the age of fifteen. Since then, she has done many different jobs. Most of the jobs did not pay well, but she tried her best in all of them and learned a lot.\nMarcy is now thirty years old, and her family has a better life. But Marcy's friends keep telling her that she should learn to make more money. They __(21)__ her several ways, but she has not tried any of them. She is not interested in anything risky. What she wants most now is to go back to school. She knows she ______(22) really happy if she can be a student again.\n(risky 有風險的)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】If + 現在式（條件）, S + will + V；knows (that) 後接主要子句。\n【分析】if she can be a student again 表示還沒發生的條件，她知道「到時會」很快樂 → will be。\n【其他選項】(A) is 表現在已很快樂；(B) was 過去式；(C) has been 現在完成式，都與條件句不合。\n【例句】I know I will feel better if I get more sleep.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2346, "question": "Jack knows he ______ the game if he practices harder.", "options": ["wins", "will win", "won", "has won"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "if 條件 → will win。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2347, "question": "Mom thinks we ______ late if we don't leave now.", "options": ["will be", "are", "were", "have been"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "條件句 → will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2348, "question": "I'm sure Grandma ______ very happy if you visit her this weekend.", "options": ["is", "was", "will be", "has been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 285 題）", "explanation": "if 條件 → will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2349, "question": "(21-23)\nShu-fen is in her third year of junior high school. She has many tests every day, but she does not even want to look at her books. Shu-fen was not like this before. In fact, she ______(21) studying during her first two years of high school and always got high grades on tests. She was happy then.\nBut these days Shu-fen always feels tired and bored. There __(22)__ so many tests that Shu-fen cannot relax and do the things she likes. But what can she do? She can only tell herself that things __(23)__ better after she starts senior high school.\n(relax 放鬆)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["enjoys", "enjoyed", "has enjoyed", "will enjoy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去時間 during her first two years（國一、國二）+ 過去式；enjoy + Ving。\n【分析】前句 Shu-fen was not like this before，後半 always got high grades / She was happy then 都是過去式 → enjoyed。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式，但她現在不想看書；(C) has enjoyed 表延續到現在，與現況矛盾；(D) 未來式不合。\n【例句】In elementary school, I enjoyed reading comic books.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2350, "question": "When Jerry was a child, he ______ playing in the rain.", "options": ["enjoys", "enjoyed", "has enjoyed", "will enjoy"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "過去 → enjoyed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2351, "question": "During her first year in Taipei, Amy ______ alone in a small apartment.", "options": ["lived", "lives", "has lived", "will live"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "過去時段 → lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2352, "question": "Last summer, we ______ swimming in the river every day.", "options": ["go", "have gone", "went", "will go"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 289 題）", "explanation": "last summer → went。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2353, "question": "(21-23)\nShu-fen is in her third year of junior high school. She has many tests every day, but she does not even want to look at her books. Shu-fen was not like this before. In fact, she __(21)__ studying during her first two years of high school and always got high grades on tests. She was happy then.\nBut these days Shu-fen always feels tired and bored. There ______(22) so many tests that Shu-fen cannot relax and do the things she likes. But what can she do? She can only tell herself that things __(23)__ better after she starts senior high school.\n(relax 放鬆)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["are", "were", "would be", "are going to be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜There be／代名詞 it, they", "explanation": "【句型】There be + N：be 動詞依時態與後面名詞單複數決定。\n【分析】these days 表現在，後面 so many tests 為複數，且同句 cannot relax 是現在式 → There are。\n【其他選項】(B) were 過去式不合 these days；(C) would be 表假設；(D) are going to be 表未來，但考試現在就很多。\n【例句】There are too many people on the bus today.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2354, "question": "These days there ______ a lot of homework, so Ted goes to bed late.", "options": ["is", "was", "will be", "would be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "these days + 不可數 homework → is。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2355, "question": "There ______ two new students in our class this year.", "options": ["is", "are", "was", "has"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "this year + 複數 → are。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2356, "question": "Last night there ______ a big storm in our town.", "options": ["is", "are", "was", "were"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 293 題）", "explanation": "last night + 單數 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2357, "question": "(21-23)\nShu-fen is in her third year of junior high school. She has many tests every day, but she does not even want to look at her books. Shu-fen was not like this before. In fact, she __(21)__ studying during her first two years of high school and always got high grades on tests. She was happy then.\nBut these days Shu-fen always feels tired and bored. There __(22)__ so many tests that Shu-fen cannot relax and do the things she likes. But what can she do? She can only tell herself that things ______(23) better after she starts senior high school.\n(relax 放鬆)\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["get", "got", "have got", "will get"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜副詞子句與名詞子句的時態", "explanation": "【句型】主要子句 will + V + after/when + 現在式（時間副詞子句以現在式代替未來）。\n【分析】after she starts senior high school 是未來的事（時間子句用現在式），主要子句要用未來式 → things will get better。\n【其他選項】(A) get 現在式不能表示將來的改變；(B) got 過去式；(C) have got 現在完成式，都不合。\n【例句】You will feel better after you take this medicine.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2358, "question": "We ______ dinner after Dad comes home.", "options": ["have", "will have", "had", "have had"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "after + 現在式，主句用未來 → will have。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2359, "question": "Call me when you ______ at the station.", "options": ["arrive", "will arrive", "arrived", "have arrived"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "when 子句用現在式代替未來 → arrive。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2360, "question": "The weather ______ warmer after spring comes.", "options": ["got", "gets", "will get", "has got"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 297 題）", "explanation": "主要子句用未來 → will get。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2361, "question": "(17-19)\nMs. Li: A-fu, why were you late every day this week?\nA-fu: I'm sorry, Ms. Li, but there ______(17) a traffic jam on Monday morning.\nMs. Li: How about Tuesday and Wednesday?\nA-fu: I missed the bus.\nMs. Li: Why did you miss the bus?\nA-fu: I __(18)__ very hard and went to bed late.\nMs. Li: If you keep being late, I __(19)__ you dump garbage for the class for one month!\nA-fu: But Ms. Li, I was NOT late this morning!\nMs. Li: No, you weren't. But why are you still wearing your slippers?\nA-fu: What? I...!?\n(traffic jam 塞車　dump 倒　slipper 拖鞋)\n\n▶ 請選出第 17 格的答案", "options": ["was", "is", "has been", "will be"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 17 格｜There be／代名詞 it, they", "explanation": "【句型】There be + N；過去時間 on Monday morning 用 There was。\n【分析】on Monday morning 是本週已過去的時間，老師問 why were you late（過去式）→ there was a traffic jam。\n【其他選項】(B) is 現在式、(C) has been 現在完成式不和明確過去時間連用；(D) will be 未來式不合。\n【例句】There was a big fire near my house last night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2362, "question": "There ______ a lot of people at the night market last Saturday.", "options": ["are", "were", "have been", "will be"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "last Saturday + 複數 → were。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2363, "question": "Sorry I'm late. There ______ an accident on the road this morning.", "options": ["was", "is", "will be", "has"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "this morning 已過 → was。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2364, "question": "There ______ a basketball game at our school tomorrow.", "options": ["was", "has been", "will be", "were"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 301 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow → will be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2365, "question": "(17-19)\nMs. Li: A-fu, why were you late every day this week?\nA-fu: I'm sorry, Ms. Li, but there __(17)__ a traffic jam on Monday morning.\nMs. Li: How about Tuesday and Wednesday?\nA-fu: I missed the bus.\nMs. Li: Why did you miss the bus?\nA-fu: I ______(18) very hard and went to bed late.\nMs. Li: If you keep being late, I __(19)__ you dump garbage for the class for one month!\nA-fu: But Ms. Li, I was NOT late this morning!\nMs. Li: No, you weren't. But why are you still wearing your slippers?\nA-fu: What? I...!?\n(traffic jam 塞車　dump 倒　slipper 拖鞋)\n\n▶ 請選出第 18 格的答案", "options": ["studied", "am studying", "have studied", "will study"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 18 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】and 連接的動詞時態一致；說明過去原因用過去式。\n【分析】回答 Why did you miss the bus?（過去式），後半句 and went to bed late 是過去式 → studied。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在進行式、(C) 現在完成式、(D) 未來式都與 went 不一致。\n【例句】I played games and went to bed late last night.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2366, "question": "A: Why are you so tired? B: I ______ a scary movie and couldn't sleep last night.", "options": ["watch", "watched", "have watched", "will watch"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "last night → watched。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2367, "question": "A: Why did you miss breakfast? B: I ______ up late and had to run to school.", "options": ["got", "get", "have got", "will get"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "與 had to 一致 → got。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2368, "question": "A: Why didn't you come to the party? B: I ______ a fever and stayed in bed.", "options": ["have", "will have", "had", "am having"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 305 題）", "explanation": "與 stayed 一致 → had。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2369, "question": "(17-19)\nMs. Li: A-fu, why were you late every day this week?\nA-fu: I'm sorry, Ms. Li, but there __(17)__ a traffic jam on Monday morning.\nMs. Li: How about Tuesday and Wednesday?\nA-fu: I missed the bus.\nMs. Li: Why did you miss the bus?\nA-fu: I __(18)__ very hard and went to bed late.\nMs. Li: If you keep being late, I ______(19) you dump garbage for the class for one month!\nA-fu: But Ms. Li, I was NOT late this morning!\nMs. Li: No, you weren't. But why are you still wearing your slippers?\nA-fu: What? I...!?\n(traffic jam 塞車　dump 倒　slipper 拖鞋)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["was making", "make", "have made", "will make"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜使役動詞", "explanation": "【句型】If + 現在式, S + will + V；使役動詞 make + 受詞 + 原形動詞（make you dump）。\n【分析】If you keep being late（條件），老師警告「我將會叫你」倒垃圾一個月 → will make you dump。\n【其他選項】(A) 過去進行式、(C) 現在完成式不合條件句；(B) make 現在式不能表示「如果…就會…」的未來結果。\n【例句】If you don't finish your homework, Mom will make you stay home.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2370, "question": "If you keep talking in class, I ______ you stand at the back.", "options": ["made", "will make", "have made", "was making"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 309 題）", "explanation": "條件句主句用 will → will make。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2371, "question": "My dad always makes me ______ my room on Sundays.", "options": ["clean", "to clean", "cleaning", "cleaned"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 309 題）", "explanation": "make + O + 原形V → clean。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2372, "question": "If the dog breaks the vase again, Mom ______ it sleep outside.", "options": ["makes", "made", "will make", "has made"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 309 題）", "explanation": "條件句 → will make。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2373, "question": "(20-22)\nLast night I had a bad dream. In my dream, I ______(20) to a room by three strange-looking people. They talked to each other in a language I didn't understand. I didn't know what they __(21)__ to me. Would they do anything bad? I was so afraid that I started to cry. Suddenly, one of them came up to me and tried to hurt me with a knife. I cried out loudly and then I __(22)__ up. Luckily, there were no people around--I was in my own bed!\n(strange-looking 長相奇怪的　suddenly 突然地)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["am taken", "was taken", "have been taken", "would be taken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜主動與被動語態", "explanation": "【句型】被動語態 be + p.p. + by + 動作者；過去式被動 was/were + p.p.。\n【分析】有 by three strange-looking people，「我被帶到」房間（被動）；Last night 夢是過去 → was taken。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式被動、(C) 現在完成式被動與過去敘事不合；(D) would be taken 表過去的未來或假設。\n【例句】The little boy was taken to the hospital by his parents.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2374, "question": "Yesterday the lost dog ______ to the police station by a kind girl.", "options": ["is taken", "was taken", "takes", "has taken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 313 題）", "explanation": "過去被動 → was taken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2375, "question": "This picture ______ by my father last summer.", "options": ["was painted", "painted", "is painted", "has painted"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 313 題）", "explanation": "last summer 被畫 → was painted。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2376, "question": "The students ______ to the museum by bus last Friday.", "options": ["take", "were taking", "were taken", "have taken"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 313 題）", "explanation": "學生被帶去，過去被動 → were taken。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2377, "question": "(20-22)\nLast night I had a bad dream. In my dream, I __(20)__ to a room by three strange-looking people. They talked to each other in a language I didn't understand. I didn't know what they ______(21) to me. Would they do anything bad? I was so afraid that I started to cry. Suddenly, one of them came up to me and tried to hurt me with a knife. I cried out loudly and then I __(22)__ up. Luckily, there were no people around--I was in my own bed!\n(strange-looking 長相奇怪的　suddenly 突然地)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["are doing", "did", "have done", "would do"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】主要子句過去式（didn't know），子句表「接下來會做」用 would + V。\n【分析】我不知道他們「將會」對我做什麼，下一句 Would they do anything bad? 也用 would → what they would do to me。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在進行式時態不一致；(B) did 表已經做了，但當時還沒發生；(C) 現在完成式不合。\n【例句】I didn't know what my parents would say about my test.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2378, "question": "Amy didn't know what her friends ______ for her birthday.", "options": ["will plan", "would plan", "have planned", "plan"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 317 題）", "explanation": "didn't know + 未來 → would plan。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2379, "question": "We had no idea how the movie ______.", "options": ["would end", "ends", "has ended", "is ending"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 317 題）", "explanation": "過去不知未來 → would end。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2380, "question": "Ben wasn't sure what the teacher ______ about his late homework.", "options": ["says", "has said", "would say", "is saying"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 317 題）", "explanation": "過去不確定未來 → would say。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2381, "question": "(20-22)\nLast night I had a bad dream. In my dream, I __(20)__ to a room by three strange-looking people. They talked to each other in a language I didn't understand. I didn't know what they __(21)__ to me. Would they do anything bad? I was so afraid that I started to cry. Suddenly, one of them came up to me and tried to hurt me with a knife. I cried out loudly and then I ______(22) up. Luckily, there were no people around--I was in my own bed!\n(strange-looking 長相奇怪的　suddenly 突然地)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["wake", "woke", "was waking", "was going to wake"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去連續動作用過去簡單式；wake 的過去式為 woke。\n【分析】I cried out loudly and then I woke up：「大叫然後醒來」是先後發生的兩個過去動作，與 cried 一致 → woke。\n【其他選項】(A) wake 現在式不合；(C) 過去進行式表正在醒，不合 and then 的接續；(D) was going to wake 表本來要醒，不合，因為他真的醒了（I was in my own bed）。\n【例句】The alarm rang, and then I woke up.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2382, "question": "I heard a loud noise and then I ______ up.", "options": ["wake", "woke", "was waking", "have woken"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 321 題）", "explanation": "與 heard 接續 → woke。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2383, "question": "Jim opened the door and then ______ into the room.", "options": ["ran", "runs", "was running", "has run"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 321 題）", "explanation": "接續動作 → ran。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2384, "question": "The baby cried for a while and then ______ asleep.", "options": ["falls", "was falling", "fell", "has fallen"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 321 題）", "explanation": "接續動作 → fell。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2385, "question": "(21-23)\nLast Saturday, I decided to go to a movie in the evening. My little sister said that she wanted to go with me because she was bored at home. When we got to the theater, a lot of people ______(21) there to buy tickets. I saw a friend in the crowd, so I walked up and talked to him for a while. When we finished talking, I found my sister was gone! I __(22)__ her name loudly and looked for her for thirty minutes. Everyone was looking at me. Finally, I found my sister in a toyshop near the theater. She was playing happily there.\nWe __(23)__ the movie that night and went home early. I have learned from this experience to be more careful if I have to take my sister out with me again.\n(crowd 人群)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["wait", "have waited", "will wait", "were waiting"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】When + 過去式, S + was/were + Ving：某事發生時，另一事正在進行。\n【分析】When we got to the theater（過去），當時很多人「正在」排隊等買票 → were waiting。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在式、(B) 現在完成式、(C) 未來式都與過去敘事不一致。\n【例句】When I got home, my parents were watching TV.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2386, "question": "When we arrived at the station, many people ______ for the train.", "options": ["wait", "were waiting", "have waited", "will wait"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 325 題）", "explanation": "到達時正在等 → were waiting。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2387, "question": "When the bell rang, the students ______ their lunch.", "options": ["were eating", "eat", "have eaten", "will eat"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 325 題）", "explanation": "鈴響時正在吃。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2388, "question": "When I walked into the gym, my classmates ______ basketball.", "options": ["play", "have played", "were playing", "will play"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 325 題）", "explanation": "進去時正在打球。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2389, "question": "(21-23)\nLast Saturday, I decided to go to a movie in the evening. My little sister said that she wanted to go with me because she was bored at home. When we got to the theater, a lot of people __(21)__ there to buy tickets. I saw a friend in the crowd, so I walked up and talked to him for a while. When we finished talking, I found my sister was gone! I ______(22) her name loudly and looked for her for thirty minutes. Everyone was looking at me. Finally, I found my sister in a toyshop near the theater. She was playing happily there.\nWe __(23)__ the movie that night and went home early. I have learned from this experience to be more careful if I have to take my sister out with me again.\n(crowd 人群)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["have called", "will call", "called", "was calling"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】and 連接的動詞時態一致，過去發生的連續動作用過去式。\n【分析】I ___ her name loudly and looked for her for thirty minutes：後半句 looked 是過去式，前面也用過去式 → called。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式、(B) 未來式與過去敘事不合；(D) was calling 表當時正在叫，與並列的 looked 時態不一致，且這是一連串完成的動作。\n【例句】I called my dog and looked for him everywhere.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2390, "question": "Mia ______ her mom and told her the good news.", "options": ["calls", "called", "has called", "was calling"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 329 題）", "explanation": "與 told 一致 → called。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2391, "question": "The boy ______ his ball and ran home.", "options": ["picked up", "picks up", "has picked up", "will pick up"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 329 題）", "explanation": "與 ran 一致 → picked up。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2392, "question": "Yesterday I ______ my room and washed the dishes.", "options": ["clean", "will clean", "cleaned", "have cleaned"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 329 題）", "explanation": "與 washed 一致 → cleaned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2393, "question": "(21-23)\nLast Saturday, I decided to go to a movie in the evening. My little sister said that she wanted to go with me because she was bored at home. When we got to the theater, a lot of people __(21)__ there to buy tickets. I saw a friend in the crowd, so I walked up and talked to him for a while. When we finished talking, I found my sister was gone! I __(22)__ her name loudly and looked for her for thirty minutes. Everyone was looking at me. Finally, I found my sister in a toyshop near the theater. She was playing happily there.\nWe ______(23) the movie that night and went home early. I have learned from this experience to be more careful if I have to take my sister out with me again.\n(crowd 人群)\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["have not seen", "will not see", "did not see", "were not seeing"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】明確的過去時間（that night）+ 過去簡單式；否定 did not + 原形V。\n【分析】找妹妹花了三十分鐘，所以那晚「沒看」電影就回家了；that night 是過去時間，後半 went home early 也是過去式 → did not see。\n【其他選項】(A) 現在完成式不和 that night 連用；(B) 未來式不合；(D) 過去進行式不適合描述整件事「沒發生」。\n【例句】We did not go out that night because it rained.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2394, "question": "It rained hard, so we ______ to the beach last Sunday.", "options": ["don't go", "didn't go", "haven't gone", "won't go"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 333 題）", "explanation": "last Sunday → didn't go。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2395, "question": "I was too tired, so I ______ my homework that night.", "options": ["did not finish", "have not finished", "will not finish", "am not finishing"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 333 題）", "explanation": "that night → did not finish。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2396, "question": "Kevin was sick yesterday, so he ______ to school.", "options": ["doesn't come", "hasn't come", "didn't come", "won't come"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 333 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → didn't come。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2397, "question": "(19-21)\n(Doris sees Carol on her way to school.)\nDoris: Hi, Carol. Would you like to go to the movie The Doll World with me tonight?\nCarol: I'd love to, but I have to take care of my sister Kelly. My parents ______(19) home tonight.\nDoris: You can take her to the movie with us.\nCarol: I don't think so. I __(20)__ taking her to a movie with me once. She kept talking during the movie, and even cried loudly. I was so embarrassed.\nDoris: That's too bad. But I've heard this movie is really popular with young children. Maybe she __(21)__ it.\nCarol: Well, let me think about it. I'll tell you later when I see you at lunch.\nDoris: Sure. See you then.\n(take care of 照顧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["don't be", "weren't", "won't be", "haven't been"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】未來時間 tonight + will (not) + V；be 動詞未來否定 won't be。\n【分析】對話在早上上學途中，tonight 是之後的時間，父母「今晚不會在家」→ won't be。\n【其他選項】(A) don't be 是否定祈使句，不能接主詞；(B) weren't 過去式；(D) haven't been 現在完成式，都不合 tonight（未來）。\n【例句】My brother won't be home for dinner tonight.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2398, "question": "I'm sorry, but I ______ at school tomorrow. I have to see a doctor.", "options": ["am not", "won't be", "wasn't", "haven't been"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 337 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow → won't be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2399, "question": "Mom ______ back until nine tonight, so we'll cook dinner ourselves.", "options": ["won't be", "wasn't", "isn't being", "hasn't been"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 337 題）", "explanation": "tonight 之後 → won't be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2400, "question": "Don't call Mr. Lin this weekend. He ______ in Taipei.", "options": ["wasn't", "hasn't been", "won't be", "doesn't be"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 337 題）", "explanation": "this weekend → won't be。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2401, "question": "(19-21)\n(Doris sees Carol on her way to school.)\nDoris: Hi, Carol. Would you like to go to the movie The Doll World with me tonight?\nCarol: I'd love to, but I have to take care of my sister Kelly. My parents __(19)__ home tonight.\nDoris: You can take her to the movie with us.\nCarol: I don't think so. I ______(20) taking her to a movie with me once. She kept talking during the movie, and even cried loudly. I was so embarrassed.\nDoris: That's too bad. But I've heard this movie is really popular with young children. Maybe she __(21)__ it.\nCarol: Well, let me think about it. I'll tell you later when I see you at lunch.\nDoris: Sure. See you then.\n(take care of 照顧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 20 格的答案", "options": ["try", "tried", "will try", "am trying"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 20 格｜動詞形式（to V / Ving / 祈使句）", "explanation": "【句型】try + Ving：試試看做某事；once（曾經一次）+ 過去式。\n【分析】後句 She kept talking…, and even cried loudly. I was so embarrassed. 都是過去式，表示過去曾經「試過」帶她去一次 → tried taking her。\n【其他選項】(A) try 現在式、(C) 未來式、(D) 現在進行式都與 once 及後面的過去經驗不合。\n【例句】I tried cooking dinner for my family once, but it was terrible.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2402, "question": "I ______ eating stinky tofu once. I didn't like it at all.", "options": ["try", "tried", "will try", "am trying"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 341 題）", "explanation": "once + 過去經驗 → tried。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2403, "question": "Lily ______ making cookies by herself last week, and they were delicious.", "options": ["tried", "tries", "will try", "is trying"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 341 題）", "explanation": "last week → tried。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2404, "question": "If the door doesn't open, try ______ the key the other way.", "options": ["turn", "turned", "turning", "turns"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 341 題）", "explanation": "try + Ving（試試看）→ turning。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2405, "question": "(19-21)\n(Doris sees Carol on her way to school.)\nDoris: Hi, Carol. Would you like to go to the movie The Doll World with me tonight?\nCarol: I'd love to, but I have to take care of my sister Kelly. My parents __(19)__ home tonight.\nDoris: You can take her to the movie with us.\nCarol: I don't think so. I __(20)__ taking her to a movie with me once. She kept talking during the movie, and even cried loudly. I was so embarrassed.\nDoris: That's too bad. But I've heard this movie is really popular with young children. Maybe she ______(21) it.\nCarol: Well, let me think about it. I'll tell you later when I see you at lunch.\nDoris: Sure. See you then.\n(take care of 照顧)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["loves", "loved", "will love", "was going to love"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】Maybe + S + will + V：對未來的推測。\n【分析】Doris 說這部片很受小孩歡迎，推測 Kelly 今晚去看「也許會喜歡」→ will love。\n【其他選項】(A) loves 現在式，她還沒看過電影；(B) loved 過去式；(D) was going to love 是過去的未來，不合。\n【例句】Try this cake. Maybe you will like it.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2406, "question": "This book is about dinosaurs. Maybe your son ______ it.", "options": ["likes", "liked", "will like", "was going to like"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 345 題）", "explanation": "對未來的推測 → will like。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2407, "question": "Take a jacket with you. Maybe it ______ cold tonight.", "options": ["will get", "got", "gets", "was going to get"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 345 題）", "explanation": "tonight 推測 → will get。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2408, "question": "Ask Ms. Wu for help. Maybe she ______ the answer.", "options": ["knew", "will know", "was knowing", "has known"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 345 題）", "explanation": "推測 → will know。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2409, "question": "(17-19)\nDate: 01/21/2002　weather: sunny\nToday is the first day of winter vacation. I'm very excited because Chinese New Year is coming. Mom told me this morning that we ______(17) Grandmother's place for the new year. Dad won't be back from Tokyo before the holidays are over. It has been two weeks since Dad left. I miss him so much.\nMom went shopping for food and presents, so I took Lucy and Annie to the library. We __(18)__ at the Children's Reading Room all the afternoon. We found some books about animals we were interested in. After we left the library, we went to Mendy's to buy hamburgers and fries. I was hungry, but I didn't eat much. I __(19)__ two kilos in the last two weeks. I hope I can lose six kilos before summer comes.\n(library 圖書館)\n\n▶ 請選出第 17 格的答案", "options": ["go to", "went to", "have gone to", "are going to"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 17 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】be going to + 地點（go to 省略 go）／be going to + V：已安排好的未來計畫。\n【分析】過年 is coming（還沒到），媽媽說「我們要去」奶奶家過年，是未來計畫 → are going to Grandmother's place。\n【其他選項】(A) go to 現在式不能表示這次的未來計畫；(B) went to 表已經去了；(C) have gone to 表已經去了（人在那裡），都與「新年還沒到」不合。\n【例句】We are going to Kenting for summer vacation.\n備註：be going to 屬未來式；Mom told me 為過去式，但「新年」仍在未來，故不需時態後移。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2410, "question": "Dad told us that we ______ Hualien next weekend.", "options": ["went to", "are going to", "have gone to", "go to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 349 題）", "explanation": "next weekend 計畫 → are going to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2411, "question": "Look at those dark clouds! It ______ rain soon.", "options": ["is going to", "went to", "has gone to", "goes to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 349 題）", "explanation": "跡象推測未來 → is going to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2412, "question": "Lucy ______ visit her aunt in Tainan tomorrow.", "options": ["went to", "has gone to", "is going to", "goes to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 349 題）", "explanation": "tomorrow → is going to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2413, "question": "(17-19)\nDate: 01/21/2002　weather: sunny\nToday is the first day of winter vacation. I'm very excited because Chinese New Year is coming. Mom told me this morning that we __(17)__ Grandmother's place for the new year. Dad won't be back from Tokyo before the holidays are over. It has been two weeks since Dad left. I miss him so much.\nMom went shopping for food and presents, so I took Lucy and Annie to the library. We ______(18) at the Children's Reading Room all the afternoon. We found some books about animals we were interested in. After we left the library, we went to Mendy's to buy hamburgers and fries. I was hungry, but I didn't eat much. I __(19)__ two kilos in the last two weeks. I hope I can lose six kilos before summer comes.\n(library 圖書館)\n\n▶ 請選出第 18 格的答案", "options": ["stayed", "will stay", "have stayed", "were going to stay"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 18 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】描述今天已經發生（過去）的事用過去簡單式。\n【分析】日記中 Mom went shopping…, so I took…（過去式），之後 found, left, went 也是過去式，我們整個下午「待在」閱覽室 → stayed。\n【其他選項】(B) will stay 未來式不合；(C) 現在完成式不和已結束的「整個下午＋後續動作」敘述連用；(D) were going to stay 表本來要待（可能沒待），與後文找到書矛盾。\n【例句】We stayed at the park all afternoon yesterday.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2414, "question": "Yesterday Tom ______ at home all day because of the rain.", "options": ["stays", "stayed", "has stayed", "will stay"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 353 題）", "explanation": "yesterday → stayed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2415, "question": "Yesterday morning we ______ at the beach for three hours.", "options": ["played", "play", "have been playing", "will play"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 353 題）", "explanation": "Yesterday morning → played。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2416, "question": "After dinner, my family ______ TV in the living room.", "options": ["watch", "will watch", "watched", "have watched"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 353 題）", "explanation": "過去敘述 → watched。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2417, "question": "(17-19)\nDate: 01/21/2002　weather: sunny\nToday is the first day of winter vacation. I'm very excited because Chinese New Year is coming. Mom told me this morning that we __(17)__ Grandmother's place for the new year. Dad won't be back from Tokyo before the holidays are over. It has been two weeks since Dad left. I miss him so much.\nMom went shopping for food and presents, so I took Lucy and Annie to the library. We __(18)__ at the Children's Reading Room all the afternoon. We found some books about animals we were interested in. After we left the library, we went to Mendy's to buy hamburgers and fries. I was hungry, but I didn't eat much. I ______(19) two kilos in the last two weeks. I hope I can lose six kilos before summer comes.\n(library 圖書館)\n\n▶ 請選出第 19 格的答案", "options": ["lose", "have lost", "am losing", "was going to lose"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 19 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】in the last/past + 時間 + 現在完成式：過去一段時間到現在的結果。\n【分析】in the last two weeks（最近兩週到現在），已經瘦了兩公斤 → have lost；後句 I hope I can lose six kilos 也顯示是到目前的成果。\n【其他選項】(A) lose 現在式不和 in the last two weeks 連用；(C) 現在進行式不能表示「已達成兩公斤」；(D) was going to lose 表本來要瘦，不合。\n【例句】I have read three books in the last month.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2418, "question": "My brother ______ five centimeters in the past year.", "options": ["grows", "has grown", "is growing", "was going to grow"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 357 題）", "explanation": "in the past year → has grown。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2419, "question": "We ______ a lot of rain in the last few days.", "options": ["have had", "have", "are having", "were going to have"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 357 題）", "explanation": "in the last few days → have had。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2420, "question": "Jenny ______ three new friends in the past two weeks.", "options": ["makes", "is making", "has made", "was going to make"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 357 題）", "explanation": "in the past two weeks → has made。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2421, "question": "(21-23)\nBilly is one of my classmates in junior high school. Three years ago, he was very heavy, but he looks wonderful now. Here is his story about how he lost weight.\nBilly ______(21) a lot of snacks and fast food in his elementary school days. Besides, he did not do much exercise. So he kept putting on weight. He became so heavy that one day he broke the chair he was sitting on when he was in class.\nAfter this experience, Billy decided to lose some kilos. First, he went to see a doctor and __(22)__ to avoid fast food. Also, the doctor said he should start exercising. Billy followed the doctor's advice: he __(23)__ away from fast food for one year, and most important of all, he jogged every day.\nThat is how Billy lost 20 kilos before he entered junior high school.\n(advice 建議)\n\n▶ 請選出第 21 格的答案", "options": ["eats", "has eaten", "ate", "was going to eat"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 21 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去時間 in his elementary school days + 過去簡單式；eat 的過去式 ate。\n【分析】小學時期是過去，後句 did not do, kept putting on 都是過去式 → ate。\n【其他選項】(A) eats 現在式，他現在已經瘦了；(B) 現在完成式不和明確過去時段連用；(D) was going to eat 表本來要吃，不合。\n【例句】In my childhood, I ate candy every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2422, "question": "In her high school days, my mom ______ in the school band.", "options": ["plays", "played", "has played", "was going to play"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 361 題）", "explanation": "過去時期 → played。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2423, "question": "When he was young, Grandpa ______ to school on foot.", "options": ["walked", "walks", "has walked", "is walking"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 361 題）", "explanation": "When he was young → walked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2424, "question": "In his college days, Mr. Ho ______ in Kaohsiung.", "options": ["lives", "has lived", "lived", "will live"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 361 題）", "explanation": "過去時期 → lived。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2425, "question": "(21-23)\nBilly is one of my classmates in junior high school. Three years ago, he was very heavy, but he looks wonderful now. Here is his story about how he lost weight.\nBilly __(21)__ a lot of snacks and fast food in his elementary school days. Besides, he did not do much exercise. So he kept putting on weight. He became so heavy that one day he broke the chair he was sitting on when he was in class.\nAfter this experience, Billy decided to lose some kilos. First, he went to see a doctor and ______(22) to avoid fast food. Also, the doctor said he should start exercising. Billy followed the doctor's advice: he __(23)__ away from fast food for one year, and most important of all, he jogged every day.\nThat is how Billy lost 20 kilos before he entered junior high school.\n(advice 建議)\n\n▶ 請選出第 22 格的答案", "options": ["is asked", "was asked", "will be asked", "would be asked"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 22 格｜主動與被動語態", "explanation": "【句型】被動 be asked to V（被要求做…）；過去式被動 was + p.p.；and 前後時態一致。\n【分析】他去看醫生並「被（醫生）要求」避免速食；與前面 went 一致用過去式，且 Billy 是被要求的一方 → was asked to avoid。\n【其他選項】(A) is asked 現在式與 went 不一致；(C) will be asked 未來式不合；(D) would be asked 表過去的未來或假設，但事情當場就發生了。\n【例句】Tom was asked to clean the classroom after school.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2426, "question": "Yesterday Jenny went to the office and ______ to help the teacher.", "options": ["is asked", "was asked", "will be asked", "asks"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 365 題）", "explanation": "與 went 一致＋被動 → was asked。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2427, "question": "All the students ______ to wear uniforms on Monday last week.", "options": ["were told", "told", "are told", "tell"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 365 題）", "explanation": "last week 被告知 → were told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2428, "question": "Ben went to the doctor and ______ to rest for three days.", "options": ["tells", "will be told", "was told", "told"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 365 題）", "explanation": "被告知，過去 → was told。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2429, "question": "(21-23)\nBilly is one of my classmates in junior high school. Three years ago, he was very heavy, but he looks wonderful now. Here is his story about how he lost weight.\nBilly __(21)__ a lot of snacks and fast food in his elementary school days. Besides, he did not do much exercise. So he kept putting on weight. He became so heavy that one day he broke the chair he was sitting on when he was in class.\nAfter this experience, Billy decided to lose some kilos. First, he went to see a doctor and __(22)__ to avoid fast food. Also, the doctor said he should start exercising. Billy followed the doctor's advice: he ______(23) away from fast food for one year, and most important of all, he jogged every day.\nThat is how Billy lost 20 kilos before he entered junior high school.\n(advice 建議)\n\n▶ 請選出第 23 格的答案", "options": ["has stayed", "is staying", "will stay", "stayed"], "answer": 3, "answerLabel": "D", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 23 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】and 連接的動詞時態一致；stay away from 遠離。\n【分析】Billy followed the doctor's advice（過去），後半句 he jogged every day 也是過去式，而且整件事在他上國中前就結束了 → stayed away from。\n【其他選項】(A) has stayed 表延續到現在，但這件事已經結束（for one year, before he entered junior high school）；(B) 現在進行式、(C) 未來式不合。\n【例句】Last year, Kim stayed away from sugar and walked to school every day.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2430, "question": "Last summer, Ray ______ away from video games and read many books.", "options": ["stays", "stayed", "has stayed", "will stay"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 369 題）", "explanation": "與 read（過去）一致 → stayed。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2431, "question": "During the test week, Lisa ______ off her phone and studied hard.", "options": ["turned", "turns", "has turned", "will turn"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 369 題）", "explanation": "與 studied 一致 → turned。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2432, "question": "For two months, my dad ______ drinking soda and lost five kilos.", "options": ["stops", "will stop", "stopped", "has stopped"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 369 題）", "explanation": "與 lost 一致 → stopped。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2433, "question": "(16-18)\nTed sat next to me when we were in elementary school. He had serious problems communicating with people. One always had to guess what he was saying. Besides, most of my classmates did not like to be with him because his hands and shirts were always dirty. I ______(16) let him know the importance of being clean by telling him several times a day to wash his hands. But he just could not understand.\nOne day, our teacher Miss Hsieh walked up to Ted. Without saying anything, she took Ted to the washroom. Slowly, Miss Hsieh washed his hands and told him that he should keep himself clean. She __(17)__ that every day for one month. Finally, Ted understood.\nMiss Hsieh's love has given me a good example to follow when I __(18)__ my job. I always remember to teach my students by showing them the right ways to do things. And most important of all, I always remember to give them more time to learn and to grow up.\n(guess 猜測　washroom 盥洗室　finally 終於)\n\n▶ 請選出第 16 格的答案", "options": ["tried to", "am trying to", "have tried to", "will try to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 16 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】過去敘事用過去簡單式；try to V（試著做…）。\n【分析】小學時的事（when we were in elementary school），後句 But he just could not understand 也是過去式 → tried to。\n【其他選項】(B) 現在進行式、(C) 現在完成式、(D) 未來式都與過去敘事不合。\n【例句】I tried to help my friend with math, but he didn't listen.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2434, "question": "When I was in third grade, I ______ teach my little brother to read.", "options": ["try to", "tried to", "have tried to", "will try to"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 373 題）", "explanation": "過去 → tried to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2435, "question": "Last night, Amy ______ call you, but your phone was off.", "options": ["tried to", "tries to", "has tried to", "will try to"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 373 題）", "explanation": "last night → tried to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2436, "question": "In elementary school, Ted ______ make friends, but it was hard for him.", "options": ["tries to", "will try to", "tried to", "is trying to"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 373 題）", "explanation": "過去 → tried to。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2437, "question": "(16-18)\nTed sat next to me when we were in elementary school. He had serious problems communicating with people. One always had to guess what he was saying. Besides, most of my classmates did not like to be with him because his hands and shirts were always dirty. I __(16)__ let him know the importance of being clean by telling him several times a day to wash his hands. But he just could not understand.\nOne day, our teacher Miss Hsieh walked up to Ted. Without saying anything, she took Ted to the washroom. Slowly, Miss Hsieh washed his hands and told him that he should keep himself clean. She ______(17) that every day for one month. Finally, Ted understood.\nMiss Hsieh's love has given me a good example to follow when I __(18)__ my job. I always remember to teach my students by showing them the right ways to do things. And most important of all, I always remember to give them more time to learn and to grow up.\n(guess 猜測　washroom 盥洗室　finally 終於)\n\n▶ 請選出第 17 格的答案", "options": ["did", "was doing", "has done", "was going to do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 17 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】do that 代替前面提過的動作；過去重複一段時間的事用過去簡單式。\n【分析】謝老師把洗手、提醒這件事「做了」一個月（every day for one month），之後 Finally, Ted understood（過去式）→ did。\n【其他選項】(B) 過去進行式表某時正在做，不和 for one month 的完整動作搭配；(C) 現在完成式不合過去敘事；(D) was going to do 表本來要做，但她真的做了，Ted 也懂了。\n【例句】Grandma walked me to school. She did that every day for six years.", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2438, "question": "Dad drove me to the bus stop. He ______ that every morning last year.", "options": ["does", "did", "has done", "was going to do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 377 題）", "explanation": "last year → did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2439, "question": "My teacher read us a story after lunch. She ______ that every day last semester.", "options": ["did", "does", "has done", "will do"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 377 題）", "explanation": "last semester → did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2440, "question": "Mom hugged me before I left. She ______ that every time I went on a trip when I was little.", "options": ["does", "has done", "did", "will do"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 377 題）", "explanation": "when I was little → did。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2441, "question": "(16-18)\nTed sat next to me when we were in elementary school. He had serious problems communicating with people. One always had to guess what he was saying. Besides, most of my classmates did not like to be with him because his hands and shirts were always dirty. I __(16)__ let him know the importance of being clean by telling him several times a day to wash his hands. But he just could not understand.\nOne day, our teacher Miss Hsieh walked up to Ted. Without saying anything, she took Ted to the washroom. Slowly, Miss Hsieh washed his hands and told him that he should keep himself clean. She __(17)__ that every day for one month. Finally, Ted understood.\nMiss Hsieh's love has given me a good example to follow when I ______(18) my job. I always remember to teach my students by showing them the right ways to do things. And most important of all, I always remember to give them more time to learn and to grow up.\n(guess 猜測　washroom 盥洗室　finally 終於)\n\n▶ 請選出第 18 格的答案", "options": ["did", "am doing", "have done", "am going to do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜會考歷屆｜克漏字第 18 格｜時態＋整句結構", "explanation": "【句型】現在式／現在進行式描述「現在」的情況；when 子句說明作者目前做這份工作時。\n【分析】同段 has given、I always remember to teach my students 都是現在，作者現在是老師，正在「做」這份工作時以謝老師為榜樣 → am doing my job。\n【其他選項】(A) did 過去式，但作者現在仍在教書；(C) have done 表已完成；(D) am going to do 表還沒開始，但他已經有學生了。\n【例句】Mr. Lee always smiles when he is working in his garden.\n備註：最自然說法是 when I do my job；選項中只有 am doing 符合「現在」時態。", "explanationSource": "source", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2442, "question": "My mom listens to music when she ______ her housework these days.", "options": ["did", "is doing", "has done", "is going to do"], "answer": 1, "answerLabel": "B", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 1（對應第 381 題）", "explanation": "現在一段時期 → is doing。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2443, "question": "Ms. Chen always thinks of her old teacher when she ______ with her own students now.", "options": ["is working", "worked", "has worked", "was working"], "answer": 0, "answerLabel": "A", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 2（對應第 381 題）", "explanation": "now → is working。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}, {"id": 2444, "question": "Leo is a nurse now. He always tries to be kind when he ______ care of sick people.", "options": ["took", "has taken", "is taking", "was taking"], "answer": 2, "answerLabel": "C", "source": "綜合（克漏字）｜類似題 3（對應第 381 題）", "explanation": "現在 → is taking。", "explanationSource": "supplemental", "section": "綜合（克漏字）"}]};